window.FWN_MARTIAL_GOD_ASURA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MARTIAL_GOD_ASURA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":6201,"title":"Chapter 6201: Chapter 6199: The Identity of the Woman In a White Dress","paragraphs":["Chapter 6199: The Identity of the Woman In a White Dress","The woman in a white dress and the black-robed woman were still standing in the same spot, their eyes locked on an observation formation that now showed Chu Feng and Eggy.","“Chu Feng is brave to not be intimidated by that. Milord, do you think he knows this is a trial, and that we aren’t truly after his life?” the black-robed woman asked.","If she was in the same position, she would have given up as that would have guaranteed both their survival. For that reason, she found Chu Feng’s decision illogical.","“Chu Feng is a bold man. There are many things he doesn’t hesitate to gamble on, but this is the one thing he dares not to gamble on,” the woman in a white dress replied.","“Milord, does this mean Chu Feng has cleared the trial?” the black-robed woman asked.","She had no idea whether the woman in a white dress would continue the trial.","“Of course. It was a gamble back then to choose Jie Ranqing’s son over her, but it looks like it was the right call. Eggy might not have displayed such conviction if it had been Jie Ranqing, and the fusion of the energy might not have proceeded as smoothly. We approached her back then as her kin, but...”","The woman in a white dress suddenly thought of something and bitterly shook her head.","She had witnessed Eggy’s aversion before, which was why she knew it wasn’t easy for Eggy to persevere with such conviction. And this was all Chu Feng’s credit.","She turned to the black-robed woman and said, “Sometimes, I have no choice but to believe in the power of love. It can grant someone incredible bravery and turn them into a different person. But only with the right person can they change for the better. Falling in love with the wrong person can cause one to descend into the abyss instead.”","The black-robed woman suddenly thought of something and chuckled. “I know milord has met the right person.”","“What makes you say so?” the woman in a white dress asked.","“I have heard about milord’s story. That is the kind of love all women crave for.”","The woman in a white dress laughed. “The rumors are out of hand. Don’t take it for real.”","A faint smile lingered on her face despite her words.","The rumors might have evolved beyond control, but that experience remained firmly etched in her mind even though a long time had passed.","“Milord, has the Asura Sword recognized Chu Feng?” the black-robed woman asked.","“It isn’t that easy. The Asura Sword harbors wild ambitions. It isn’t as easy to tame as it looks,” the woman in a white dress replied.","“Based on what I have heard about the Asura Sword, it has only revealed its prowess twice before. One was in that lord’s hand, and the other was in Chu Feng’s grasp. Am I mistaken?”","“No, you are right. That’s why Chu Feng has gained the Asura Sword’s preliminary recognition.”","The woman in a white dress looked at the black-robed woman with eyes filled with apology and gratitude. “Much time has passed in the blink of an eye. You have worked hard maintaining this place all these years. You may return after they leave.”","“Don’t say that, milord. You granted me a new life. Besides, I only have enemies in the Asura Spirit World. My life feels more worthwhile working for you,” the black-robed woman replied.","“Those are history now. No one will be after you if you return now. You can live however you wish. Come back after Chu Feng and the others leave this place,” the woman in a white dress said.","The black-robed woman was grateful. She had her reasons for doing what she did, but that didn’t change how terrible her sins were. There was no lack of powerful and influential figures among those after her life.","There weren’t many people in the Asura Spirit World who could absolve her of her crimes.","...","Eggy spent a while crying in Chu Feng’s embrace.","Chu Feng had never seen her so fragile. She was like a lost little girl who was just found by her family.","He related to her feeling of indignation and fear, for he felt the same too. He wasn’t sure whether he could meet Eggy earlier as well. It wasn’t an easy decision, but he still chose to drink the water inside the bottle because he couldn’t accept losing Eggy.","A surge of energy flowed into his body, significantly recovering his bloodline.","His fighting prowess was still weaker than before, but it was stronger than when he was crossing blows with Shahun Haotian.","Yet, this water didn’t destroy Chu Feng’s martial cultivation; it instead permanently healed his bloodline, though his bloodline remained much too impaired for him to use his bloodline ability. Nevertheless, it was only a matter of time before he regained his bloodline ability.","And it was all thanks to the black bottle’s contents.","Other than that, Chu Feng also received a black scroll, and he had to concede that it was worth even more than the black bottle’s contents.","His impaired bloodline would eventually heal like any injuries, even if it would have taken far longer to heal without the black bottle’s contents. The scroll, on the other hand, could potentially become an indispensable means for him to deal with enemies in the future.","It turned out that the final trial was a test of conviction, and he would be rewarded as long as he was willing to challenge it.","Chu Feng had no idea what the purpose of this trial was, but he understood this was the master of the Immemorial Massacre Sea showing him goodwill.","Eggy remained in Chu Feng’s embrace until she calmed down. At which, she raised her head and asked, “Chu Feng, can we leave now?”","“Of course. I cleared the trial,” Chu Feng replied.","“Why are you dawdling?” Eggy immediately got up. “Hurry up and establish the contract and become mine once more.”","“Understood, Milady Queen,” Chu Feng replied.","He began earnestly constructing the contract formation with a cheerful smile.","Eggy looked at him with gentle eyes. Despite his current liveliness, she still remembered how frail he had been back then. It was thanks to the Immemorial Massacre Sea that he was able to make a recovery.","All of a sudden, she widened her eyes in realization.","She suddenly turned around, her instincts driving her to look in a certain direction. It was where the woman in a white dress was.","The woman in a white dress initially thought it was a coincidence till Eggy pointed at her dantian and mouthed two words with a smile—”Thank you.”","The black-robed woman anxiously turned to the woman in a white dress as she realized that Eggy might have discovered them. The woman in a white dress, on the other hand, revealed a gentle smile.","“She’s a smart one; I’m not surprised that she saw through us. But I am surprised that she doesn’t blame us for putting her through so much suffering. She has truly matured,” the woman in a white dress said with a chuckle.","“Milord, are you going to meet her?” the black-robed woman asked.","“I am tempted to, but I’ll pass. She might try to squeeze benefits out of me for Chu Feng’s sake,” the woman in a white dress replied with a smile.","All of a sudden, her smile froze up.","She manifested a spirit formation gate with a flick of her wrist, and a person emerged from it. This person was not a true entity but a projection conjured by the formation.","The projected person hurriedly half-kneeled on the ground.","“What happened?” the woman in a white dress asked.","“Milord, the Sacred Hell Clan has rebelled. Lord Xing Jue has headed over to suppress them. There is no one holding the fort in our clan now,” the projected person said."]},{"number":6202,"title":"Chapter 6202: Chapter 6200: The One Who Witnessed a Legend’s Birth","paragraphs":["Chapter 6200: The One Who Witnessed a Legend’s Birth","“Got it.”","The woman in a white dress dissipated the projection with a wave of her hand.","“Looks like the Asura Spirit World is still as chaotic as ever,” the black-robed woman remarked.","“Where there is life, there will never be true peace. However, there can be relative peace if someone relatively fair calls the shot,” the woman in a white dress replied.","“The Asura Spirit World may find peace if Lord Xing Jue conquers it,” the black-robed woman said.","The woman in a white dress neither affirmed nor denied those words. “I’ll be heading back first. I’ll leave this place to you. There wouldn’t have been the Massacre Sea if not for your capability. You have worked hard over the years. Have a good rest when you return.”","The black-robed woman suddenly spoke up, “Milord, I told you I had a regret when I first agreed to come here.”","“Yes, I remember asking if there is anything I can do to help you, but you replied that you’ll tell me after accomplishing your mission at the Massacre Sea. Are you planning to tell me what it is now?” the woman in a white dress asked.","“My regret was not having met the two lords earlier and serving you two since your time in that realm, just like the Blood Clan. I can’t make up for that regret, but I can decide the future. I want to continue serving milord, regardless of who is in control of the Asura Spirit World and whether it is at peace or not.","“Milord, even though I have accomplished my mission here, I wish to continue serving you in the Asura Spirit World. Please entrust me with your most dangerous mission. I won’t let you down,” the black-robed woman said.","The woman in a white dress smiled. “I understand. The Asura Spirit World welcomes you back.”","She took a deep look at Chu Feng and Eggy before stepping into the spirit formation gate.","After Chu Feng and Eggy re-established their contract, they left this realm and returned to the Immemorial Massacre Sea. Instead of returning to Chu Feng’s World Spirit Space, Eggy chose to fly alongside Chu Feng above the sea as they headed out.","Even though Chu Feng’s fighting prowess had taken a dip and Eggy was injured, both of them were in excellent moods.","Eggy, in particular, was very satisfied with the outcome. She had some guesses about the earlier situation, and while she couldn’t confirm her conjecture, she thought there was a good chance her guess was on the mark.","“Eggy, are you truly fine?” Chu Feng asked.","The Asura Sword had told him earlier that Eggy was in terrible shape, but she looked unharmed right now. He had inspected her body, but he couldn’t find any anomalies in her.","Her cultivation had also risen from rank one True God to rank two True God level. This matter appeared to be a blessing in disguise for her.","“I am fine. Worry about yourself instead. Are you sure your bloodline can make a full recovery?” Eggy asked.","“You don’t need to worry about my bloodline; it’s only a matter of time before I make a full recovery. Eggy, this Immemorial Massacre Sea seems to be connected to the Asura Spirit World. Its master must be a formidable world spiritist, but I wonder what their goal is since they didn’t reveal their identities. Did they create this place just to benefit the later generations?”","“I don’t know. You should try asking that black metal lump instead. It might know something,” Eggy replied.","“Black metal lump?” Chu Feng was confused.","“I’m talking about the Asura Sword. Oi, black metal lump, why don’t you say something? Why are you acting all cold and lofty again? You were so talkative earlier,” Eggy shouted.","But the Asura Sword didn’t answer. It was as if it was just a normal sword.","Chu Feng felt a little gleeful when he thought about the Asura Sword. He wouldn’t have been able to free the Immortal Sea Fish Clan if not for the help he had received from the Asura Sword when dealing with the God Clan.","It was his first time experiencing the Asura Sword’s prowess, and it was beyond his imagination.","That slash he unleashed had decimated the God Mother, but from what he had felt from the Asura Sword in that instant, that was only a fraction of its power. To draw an analogy, it was similar to how tsunamis could wreak havoc, but even that was just a glimpse of the vast ocean.","The Asura Sword lived up to its reputation as the Asura Spirit World’s strongest sword. How could Chu Feng not feel gleeful when he had such a weapon with him?","“I received unexpected gains this time, and it’s all thanks to Milady Queen,” Chu Feng said as he took out a scroll emanating a black aura—Bloodline Soul Puppet.","Meanwhile, the black-robed woman was still observing Chu Feng and Eggy.","Regret flickered across her eyes when Chu Feng took out the Bloodline Soul Puppet scroll, knowing how valuable it was. Its value was nowhere compared to the Asura Sword, but the Asura Sword did not belong to Chu Feng, whereas the scroll would be Chu Feng’s if he used it.","Bloodline Soul Puppet was a Shahun Clan’s secret skill that had never been taught to an outsider. Even within the clan, it could only be obtained by highly talented clansmen who had cleared an arduous test.","The criteria were extremely strict because this secret skill couldn’t be passed down verbally.","The special energy contained inside the scroll was the key to learning the secret skill, and each scroll could only be used once regardless of whether the individual grasped the secret skill or not.","But there was a limited number of scrolls, and the Shahun Clan didn’t have many left. That prompted them to be even more prudent about giving out the scroll, making it hard to acquire even one.","Both her lords could have taken this scroll for themselves—and it would have been beneficial to them too—but the woman in a white dress gave it to Chu Feng.","This pained her heart.","“Is this the scroll you obtained from clearing the trial?” Eggy took the scroll from Chu Feng’s hands and tried to unfurl it, but it refused to open. “Why can’t it be opened?”","“Indeed.” Chu Feng nodded in affirmation.","“How do you know it’s beneficial to your bloodline if you can’t open it?” Eggy asked.","The black-robed woman’s eyes gleamed in surprise.","Chu Feng took the scroll back. “That’s just the tip of the iceberg. Once I fuse it with my bloodline, with sufficiently potent materials, I can construct a soul puppet out of my bloodline. That is the true worth of this secret skill.”","“Oh? Is that the same as constructing a clone?” Eggy was slightly confused.","“Not just any clone. You’ll know how incredible it is in the future,” Chu Feng replied.","“Keeping me in suspense? Well, it’s all good as long as it’s useful,” Eggy replied with a smile.","The black-robed woman, on the other hand, was flabbergasted.","What Chu Feng had just divulged was the scroll’s contents, but it should have been impossible to decipher the scroll’s contents before inheriting its energy. She only knew about Bloodline Soul Puppet’s true prowess after gaining some understanding of the Shahun Clan.","How did Chu Feng learn all these details?","Surely Shahun Haotian couldn’t have secretly told Chu Feng while they were crossing blows?","...","Eggy stared at Chu Feng’s scroll in curiosity. “So, you already know its cultivation method?”","“Only the rough idea. I’ll have to assimilate the scroll to know the details,” Chu Feng replied.","“Assimilate the scroll? Is it some kind of hereditary martial skill?” Eggy asked.","“You can think of it that way,” Chu Feng replied.","He placed the scroll in front of him while making his way out of the Immemorial Massacre Sea. The scroll turned into a black aura that surged into Chu Feng’s head.","The black-robed woman widened her eyes in shock. She continued to look dumbfounded even after Chu Feng completely absorbed all the black aura. It was a long time later before she finally snapped out of it and came to terms with reality.","“I wonder how many Shahun Clansmen will believe me if I tell them about this.”","She knew how difficult it was to assimilate with the black scroll, yet Chu Feng pulled it off with ease. This was unheard of in the Shahun Clan.","This prompted her to look at Chu Feng with expectant eyes.","“Can a new legend truly emerge in the world of cultivation? Will we usher in an unprecedented existence in this era? Doesn’t that make me a witness of a new legend’s birth? Chu Feng, could that person be you?”"]},{"number":6203,"title":"Chapter 6203: Chapter 6201: The Bloodline Soul Puppet’s Materials","paragraphs":["Chapter 6201: The Bloodline Soul Puppet’s Materials","Chu Feng didn’t slow his speed of advancement even after absorbing the black aura, but he fell silent for a short while.","Eggy didn’t disturb him, knowing he had gone into a special state. She could tell as much from Chu Feng’s excitement that Bloodline Soul Puppet was an extraordinary means.","But Chu Feng didn’t remain in that state for too long.","As soon as he snapped out of it, Eggy asked, “How is it? Have you grasped the skill yet?”","“I have grasped it. This secret skill is indeed beneficial to the recovery of my bloodline. It will still take time to make a full recovery, but it will be much faster than before. It’s only a matter of time before I regain what I have lost.","“What I look forward to more is the clone, the Bloodline Soul Puppet, but I’ll have to first gather materials for it,” Chu Feng replied.","“You grasped it so quickly? I guess it isn’t as formidable as I thought,” Eggy replied.","“No, this secret skill isn’t weak by any measure. It shouldn’t have been that easy to grasp it. Perhaps I am fated with it?” Chu Feng remarked with a tinge of glee.","He could tell how complicated the secret skill was, but for some reason, he was able to grasp it with ease. Other than fate, he could find no other reason to explain this anomaly.","“What materials do you require?” Eggy asked.","“I need something extremely sturdy,” Chu Feng replied.","“You can begin forging once you have the materials?”","“That’s right.”","The black-robed woman, who had been secretly observing them, shook her head. She hadn’t expected Chu Feng to be a braggart.","Chu Feng might have assimilated the black aura in record time, but understanding the secret skill was a whole new matter. This was no ordinary secret skill. He would need to study the secret skill over a long time to comprehend the intricacies of forging a Bloodline Soul Puppet.","Just then, Chu Feng suddenly stopped. He took out a God Armament and placed it before him.","“God Armaments are made out of sturdy materials too. Let me see if I can use it for the forging.”","Chu Feng placed his palms together and formed a hand seal. He closed his eyes, and his body began to tremble, especially his hands. He pointed a finger at the God Armament and released a surge of black aura mixed with nine-colored lightning.","“It can’t be! Has he already grasped the basics of the forging process?”","The black-robed woman rubbed her eyes in disbelief.","When the black aura mixed with nine-colored lightning enveloped the God Armament, the God Armament immediately melted.","The black-robed woman felt goosebumps all over. This proved that Chu Feng had truly grasped the Bloodline Soul Puppet’s forging method.","It had taken the Shahun Clan’s Clan Chief, Shahun Haotian’s grandfather, ten thousand years before he grasped Bloodline Soul Puppet. Yet, Chu Feng pulled it off in a matter of moments.","Chu Feng might be talented, but the Shahun Clan’s Clan Chief was also a prodigy who awed the Asura Spirit World back in his time! Could there be such a huge gap between prodigies?","“Is this a failure?” Eggy asked.","Energy had dissipated from the melted God Armament, reducing it to a heap of scrap metal. Clearly, something had gone wrong.","“Yes, it’s a failure. I didn’t expect even a God Armament to be insufficient.”","Chu Feeng was surprised too. Only a material that could withstand the black aura tinged with nine-colored lightning could be used for the forging of the Bloodline Soul Puppet.","Next, he whipped out a God Armament spear.","This was the spear he had taken from Huangyu Shengyu. This God Armament contained a ‘True’ character, which was a testament to its superior quality.","He had previously refrained from using this spear to conceal his ties with Huangyu Shengyu, but now that he had the Frenzied Tsunami Saber and the Dragonflame Divine Blade, he had no use for this spear anymore.","So, he decided to try using it.","He followed the same steps as before, and soon, the God Armament spear was enveloped in a surge of black aura tinged with nine-colored lightning.","However, the God Armament spear quickly melted too.","“This doesn’t work either. Just what kind of materials do you need?” Eggy was astonished.","This God Armament was already made out of incredibly sturdy materials. If even that didn’t work, she couldn’t imagine what kind of materials would work.","“I’m not sure. I only know the materials have to be sturdy. Ha, I thought I could flaunt my skills after grasping this secret skill, but it looks like I was too optimistic. The secret skill might be easy to master, but it’s no easy feat to find a material that works,” Chu Feng replied with a sigh.","The black-robed woman shook her head.","“The Shahun Clan will be infuriated to hear those words. You should already be satisfied with mastering their secret skill so easily!”","...","Seeing the disappointed Chu Feng, Eggy thought of something and asked, “Chu Feng, that skill of yours is potent enough to melt a God Armament. Can’t you use it against cultivators?”","“It doesn’t work on cultivators, though I can melt their God Armament if I can get in reach. However, I need to be fully focused to invoke this skill, making it impractical in battle,” Chu Feng replied.","Other than healing his bloodline, this secret skill was only good for forging a clone, but that couldn’t be done with materials.","“It’s already good enough that this secret skill accelerates the healing of your bloodline. We can take our time searching for materials,” Eggy consoled.","“You’re right, Milady Queen.” Chu Feng nodded with a smile.","He was disappointed at not being able to forge a Bloodline Soul Puppet right away, but Eggy was right. Just the accelerated healing of his bloodline was already a huge boon.","“All right, I’m getting tired. I’ll head back now,” Eggy said.","She wasn’t fond of crowds, and they were nearing the Immemorial Massacre Sea’s entrance.","Chu Feng opened a gate into his World Spirit Space for her.","Eggy entered the World Spirit Space and made her way toward her Asura Sword with her hands behind her. She lightly knocked the Asura Sword, saying, “Black metal lump, you did well.”","The Asura Sword didn’t reply, but neither did it blow her off as it used to."]},{"number":6204,"title":"Chapter 6204: Chapter 6202: The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Prowess","paragraphs":["Chapter 6202: The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Prowess","At the Immemorial Massacre Sea’s entrance, Little Fishy stood before the spiraling black fog with a lowered head.","She dared not to raise her head despite her usual bravery. The thought of seeing Chu Feng’s world spirit returning alone terrified her.","She had felt Chu Feng’s condition—he had been so feeble that he was as good as dead. She couldn’t imagine any way of resuscitating her.","“Yu’er, what are you thinking?” a voice echoed from the Immemorial Massacre Sea.","Little Fishy reflexively raised her head to take a look. Her eyes immediately widened.","Chu Feng stood before her, safe and sound.","“Big brother!!!”","Tears brimmed in Little Fishy’s eyes. After a brief daze, she dashed toward him.","But before she could reach him, another figure overtook her and plunged into Chu Feng’s chest.","“Brother Chu Feng, I am so glad you’re fine!”","Xianhai Shaoyu hugged Chu Feng tightly, weeping as if he were his wife.","“You skunk.” Little Fishy walked up and bashed Xianhai Shaoyu’s head.","But Xianhai Shaoyu paid her no heed. He took a step back, grabbed Chu Feng’s arms, and examined him from head to toe.","“Brother Chu Feng, are you all right?” Xianhai Shaoyu asked.","“Don’t worry, I am fine. You can check if you don’t believe me.”","Chu Feng rolled up his sleeves and offered his pulse to them.","Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy didn’t hesitate to grab his wrist to conduct a more thorough examination. Upon realizing his vitals were stable, they breathed a sigh of relief.","“As expected of the Immemorial Massacre Sea!” Xianhai Shaoyu remarked.","“Kneel!!!” a resounding voice suddenly echoed.","It was from the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief.","All the Immortal Sea Fish Clansmen were standing in a neat formation not far away, and at their clan chief’s command, they kneeled to Chu Feng. This included Little Fishy’s father, mother, and grandfather.","Chu Feng rushed forward to pull the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief up to his feet, but he was unable to do so due to the disparity in their cultivation.","“Elder, please get up. I am good friends with Yu’er and Shaoyu. I can’t accept this from you as a junior!” Chu Feng exclaimed.","“Chu Feng, I know you are good friends with Yu’er and Shaoyu, and our Immortal Sea Fish Clan would have been doomed if not for that. Huge favors are not repaid with simple words of gratitude, but you have saved our lives. The least we should do is to show our gratitude.","“From this day onward, our Immortal Sea Fish Clan will be your family and your most ardent backer. If you don’t mind, we will immediately send out an announcement to the world of cultivation to tell everyone you have our full backing. We will not turn a blind eye to anyone who shows hostility to you,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief said.","“Elder, please get up first,” Chu Feng urged.","But the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief refused to get up. It was as if he would remain kneeling if Chu Feng didn’t agree to his proposal.","Seeing how he couldn’t move the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief, Chu Feng tried to support Little Fishy’s grandfather instead. “Elder, please get up. This is too much for me.”","Little Fishy’s grandfather was a hearty man. He had met Chu Feng before; in fact, the Frenzied Tsunami Saber was a gift from him.","He knew Chu Feng better compared to Little Fishy’s father and mother, so he stood up and turned to the Immortal Sea Fish Clansmen behind him. “This should be enough. We ought to relay our gratitude, but let’s not put young friend Chu Feng in a spot over it. Get up.”","His words held great weight despite not being the clan chief. Even Little Fishy’s parents got up after hearing his words.","Little Fishy’s mother walked up to Chu Feng, stuffed a Cosmos Sack into his hand, and said, “Take this, Chu Feng. These are the treasures we collected from the God Clan. You were the one who destroyed the God Clan, so these rightfully belong to you.”","Before Chu Feng could say a word, Little Fishy’s grandfather quickly added, “You have to accept it, young friend Chu Feng. These are rightfully yours. You’ll be putting me in a spot if you don’t accept it.”","To emphasize that, he even got into the motion of doing a huge kowtow.","“Please don’t! I’ll accept it.”","Chu Feng quickly took the Cosmos Sack.","The God Clan didn’t have many treasures despite their incredible ability. The items inside were mostly average God Armaments.","God Armaments were invaluable treasures, of course, and the old Chu Feng would have been overjoyed to receive them. It was just that he was not lacking God Armaments at the moment.","Boom!","The Immemorial Massacre Sea suddenly shook.","The black fog billowed.","A glowing name appeared on the previously blank stone monument at the entrance—Chu Feng. The name glowed so brightly that it pierced through the black fog, such that anyone with decent observation means could clearly see it.","It announced to the world that Chu Feng had cleared the Immemorial Massacre Sea.","“Elder, let’s find somewhere else to talk,” Chu Feng told the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief, sensing the Immemorial Massacre Sea’s imminent destruction.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief nodded. “All right.”","Thus, Chu Feng left the area with the Immortal Sea Fish Clansmen.","No one had dared to approach the Immemorial Massacre Sea after Shen Bai’s massacre, but the Immortal Sea Fish Clan had still made sure to conceal themselves. Thus, even those who had been keeping an eye on the Immemorial Massacre Sea didn’t know about their arrival.","After leaving the Immemorial Massacre Sea, Chu Feng and the Immortal Sea Fish Clansmen boarded humongous floating warships and began making their way to the Totem Galaxy.","This incredible spectacle would have awed most cultivators if not for them being concealed.","Along the way, Chu Feng re-established his contract with the Asura World Spirit Army and stowed them back in his World Spirit Space. He also told the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief about the Totem Dragon Clan’s alliance with the Dragon Breath Clan.","He advised the Immortal Sea Fish Clan not to announce their backing for him. During such tumultuous times, it was wiser to stay in the shadows rather than to be in the center of attention.","He proceeded to ask if the Immortal Sea Fish Clan was interested in joining their alliance.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan, being much stronger than the Totem Dragon Clan, would be a huge asset to the alliance.","Fortunately, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief and upper echelons agreed to join the alliance.","After having decided to join the alliance, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief divulged their strength to Chu Feng.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan was indeed a powerhouse. They had many True God level cultivators, with quite a number of them having reached pinnacle True God level. They even had three Heavenly God level cultivators.","Little Fishy’s father and mother were at rank one Heavenly God level, whereas Little Fishy’s grandfather was at rank two Heavenly God level.","Little Fishy’s grandfather had reached Heavenly God level a long time ago, just that he had been concealing his strength.","As for Little Fishy’s parents, they only recently reached Heavenly God level. However, their advancement to Heavenly God level triggered their bloodline awakening, allowing them to raise their cultivation by two ranks to rank three Heavenly God level.","That made them even stronger than Little Fishy’s grandfather!","This was why they dared to forge an alliance with the God Clan despite knowing there was something amiss about them. They thought they could suppress the God Clan even if they tried something.","Little did they expect the God Clan to possess such bizarre powers.","If not for Chu Feng, they would have been wiped out."]},{"number":6205,"title":"Chapter 6205: Chapter 6203: The Middle-aged Red-cloaked Man","paragraphs":["“Our Immortal Sea Fish Clan has a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist too, though he also just made a breakthrough not too long ago,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief said.","That world spiritist was not an Immortal Sea Fish Clansman. The Immortal Sea Fish Clan met him by chance and invited him to be their guest elder. They believed that he was trustworthy.","This guest elder didn’t enter the God Clan with them because he had other matters to attend to, thus averting this crisis.","“That guest elder is at a cultivation spot in the Totem Galaxy. Now that I think about it, that place should be ready now. You might be able to make a breakthrough there,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief said.","“A cultivation spot? What kind of cultivation spot is it?” Chu Feng’s interest was piqued.","The allure of making a breakthrough was too great for him to resist.","From the clan chief, Chu Feng learned the Immortal Sea Fish Clan didn’t head to the Totem Galaxy to forge an alliance with the Totem Dragon Clan at the start. Instead, they were planning to visit the cultivation spot.","The cultivation spot contained potent energy that couldn’t be absorbed directly; it had to be specially refined first.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan had devoted a lot of resources into developing the cultivation spot for Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu’s cultivation, but because of the debt they owed Chu Feng, they decided to bring him along.","Chu Feng would never turn down such an opportunity. His desire to grow more powerful was stronger than anyone else’s.","“Elder, do you know how strong Jie Tianran is?” Chu Feng suddenly asked.","He had many experts on his side now, especially with the addition of the Immortal Sea Fish Clan into the alliance, but the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion still felt like an insurmountable mountain. He still knew next to nothing about them.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan was only second to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion among present-day cultivators, so they might know more about them.","“I don’t know how strong Jie Tianran currently is, but he has been concealing his strength. I once crossed blows with him, or to be more exact, he was the one who challenged me to spar, probably to probe my strength. I was at rank nine True God level then, but I had already partially awakened my bloodline and could raise my fighting prowess by a cultivation rank.","“This might not be much to your generation’s cultivators, but very few in our generation can further raise their cultivation at True God level,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief said.","“Father, you aren’t old,” Little Fishy said.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief chuckled. “I am young compared to Jie Tianran, but not when compared to you. Your generation is unprecedented in the world of cultivation. Someone who can raise their cultivation by a rank in True God level easily counts as one of the top figures in other generations, but in your generation, that barely qualifies them as a prodigy.”","He turned to Chu Feng before continuing, “That’s why I confidently accepted Jie Tianran’s challenge. I didn’t exert my full strength in that battle, but I could sense that Jie Tianran was not just any normal rank nine True Dragon World Spiritist. He has been hiding his strength, and probably to a greater extent than me too. Now that he has finally revealed that he is a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, I doubt he would only be at rank one Heavenly Dragon.","“But that’s not all to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. They have a terrifying formation far surpassing that of other powers, and above all, there is a rumor that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has a hidden expert. No one knows who that person is, but he is said to be extremely powerful, possibly an old ancestor who has been around since the inception of the present era. There is no telling whether the rumor is true or not though.”","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is truly not to be underestimated.”","Chu Feng had known for the longest time that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was formidable, or else his father would have long rescued his mother.","“Our Immortal Sea Fish Clan owes you a huge favor. If you wish to, we will aid you in your assault against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. However, if I am to be candid, putting aside whether that old ancestor exists or not, just the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s protective formations are too much for us to handle. It is beyond us to breach the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief said with a sigh, lamenting his inability to help Chu Feng. ṝά𐌽ôΒËS̩","“Elder, I’ll deal with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion myself.”","Chu Feng didn’t blame them. He, too, knew that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was not to be trifled with, and he was nowhere strong enough to challenge them yet.","“Jie Tianran, that old coot, must have had his head kicked by a donkey. Elder Jie Ranqing had given him such an outstanding grandson. If he has any brains, he should have spared Elder Jie Ranqing on account of how exceptional you are!","“Brother Chu Feng is not an unreasonable person. As long as Elder Jie Ranqing is safe, he won’t pursue the matter on his mother’s account. Given Elder Jie Ranqing’s capabilities and Brother Chu Feng’s incredible talent, the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion could have reached unprecedented heights. Why does that old thing not heed common sense?” Xianhai Shaoyu angrily spat.","Chu Feng laughed. He couldn’t care less about what Jie Tianran was thinking.","But Xianhai Shaoyu was right about one thing.","He could spare Jie Tianran on his mother’s account if his mother was safe, but if anything were to happen to his mother, Jie Tianran would have to pay the price for it.","Suddenly, Chu Feng recalled something and asked, “Elder, where’s that red-cloaked man?”","Back in the God Clan, when he unleashed Descent of Lightning Punishment to massacre the God Clansmen, he noticed the imprisoned red-cloaked man and avoided bombarding the area.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clansmen would have cleaned the battlefield afterward, and given their means, there was no way they would have missed that red-cloaked man.","Little Fishy’s mother waved her sleeves and manifested a sealed formation realm. A person was imprisoned inside. It was the red-cloaked man whom Shen Yi rode on as a mount.","However, this red-cloaked man had been relieved of his shackles and his metal mask, revealing a soulful middle-aged man beneath.","“Chu Feng, do you know him?” Little Fishy’s mother asked.","“I don’t know him. Elder, do you know anything about him?” Chu Feng asked.","“I have heard about a group of red-cloaked men hunting the Ancient Era’s races. Any Ancient Era’s race whom they set their eyes on is doomed to die. This guy must have found the God Clan’s trail and tried to eliminate them, only to find himself outmatched and end up becoming their prisoner. We’re also curious to know their goal and why they hate the Ancient Era’s races so much.","“This is our first time meeting one of them, but he refuses to answer any of our questions. He is not mute, but he is stubborn. We don’t have a grudge against him, so we have no reason to torture him for information. Chu Feng, how do you think we should deal with this?” Little Fishy’s mother asked.","Since Chu Feng had spared this red-cloaked man’s life back then, whether out of kindness or other reasons, she thought she should leave the red-cloaked man for him to deal with.","“Let him out. I’ll have a chat with him,” Chu Feng said."]},{"number":6206,"title":"Chapter 6206: Chapter 6204: The Old Ancestral Martial Realm","paragraphs":["Chapter 6204: The Old Ancestral Martial Realm","Little Fishy’s mother changed her hand seal, and the formation realm imprisoning the red-cloaked man dissipated, freeing him.","The red-cloaked man surveyed his surroundings, but he still refused to utter a word. He kept his head up, maintaining a dignified front despite being a captive.","“Elder, let me chat with him in private,” Chu Feng said.","The others heeded his words and backed off.","With a wave of his sleeves, Chu Feng constructed an isolation formation around him and the red-cloaked man. Then, he conjured two figures, one tall and one short, with his spirit power. Both wore identical red cloaks, and their faces were obscured by red bamboo veils.","These two figures spoke in the same tongue as Chu Feng remembered them to have.","Chu Feng had conjured them, thinking the person before him might recognize them.","“Do you know them?” Chu Feng asked.","There was no answer.","“They saved me,” Chu Feng added.","There was still no answer.","“I bear no malice. I know you are from the same organization. I saved you to return the favor to them.”","Chu Feng waved his sleeves once more, first removing the two formation figures before dissipating the isolation formation. Now that they were in public view, Chu Feng turned to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief, Little Fishy’s mother, and the others and asked, “Elder, may I release him?”","“Of course,” Little Fishy’s parents answered in unison.","“You may go,” Chu Feng said.","The red-cloaked man didn’t leave right away. Instead, he stared at Chu Feng.","Suddenly, Chu Feng received a voice transmission.","“They have all entered the Ninth Galaxy. All the galaxies in the current world of cultivation, except the Ninth Galaxy, are completely different from how they used to be in the Ancient Era, despite there being ancient remnants around.","“The Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s Ancestral Martial Lower Realm, for instance, wasn’t called that back in the Ancient Era because it was not a Lower Realm. Back in the Ancient Era, it was one of the largest realms, spanning a size larger than the current Ancestral Martial Galaxy. It was the brightest star in space.”","It was from the red-cloaked man. He had decided to speak.","“How did the Ancestral Martial Lower Realm become so small? What happened in the Ancient Era?” Chu Feng asked.","But the red-cloaked man didn’t answer those questions. Instead, he said, “Enter the Ninth Galaxy if you wish to grow faster, but know that there is no way out of the Ninth Galaxy right now. Do what you want first lest you have regrets.”","He whipped out a red bamboo veil, placed it on his head, and left.","Only Chu Feng heard those words, but he didn’t share it with the others.","The red-cloaked man must have chosen to speak via voice transmission because he didn’t want to publicize the information, and Chu Feng decided to respect his decision.","Eggy, however, overheard what he heard via voice transmission, so she asked, “Does that mean that the Ancestral Martial Lower Realm, or rather, the eight galaxies have shrunk? Otherwise, it wouldn’t make sense for the ancient remnants to still be around.”","“That’s possible.” Chu Feng thought Eggy’s analysis was on point.","Some time later, the group arrived at the cultivation spot mentioned by the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief.","It was a beautiful realm covered in flowers, but the Immortal Sea Fish Clansmen halted their footsteps here. Only Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather advanced with Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, and Chu Feng.","“There’s something amiss with this realm,” Chu Feng remarked.","“How so? Did you notice something?” Eggy asked.","“The natural energies here are exceptionally thin, but I can’t trace the cause of it. No wonder there are no cultivators here, and it doesn’t look like the native species have evolved either,” Chu Feng said.","“Indeed.” Eggy nodded.","They didn’t see any cultivators along the way, though there were many small animals. It was as if this was a place forgotten by cultivators.","“It probably has something to do with the cultivation spot, right?” Eggy asked.","“I think so too. There must be something special about the cultivation spot. Even my Heaven’s Eyes can’t see through it,” Chu Feng said.","His current observation means was potent enough to see through most remnants, yet he couldn’t find any traces of a cultivation spot, despite knowing that there was one here.","Finally, Chu Feng and the others stopped in the middle of a flower field.","A spirit formation gate manifested from the ground, and a world spiritist flew out from within.","It was a gray-haired old man with lush hair but an old face.","“Paying respect to milords.”","The world spiritist first bowed to Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather before lifting his head. “It’s wonderful to see milords, young master, and young miss. I noticed the happenings at the Immemorial Massacre Sea and thought the God Clan pulled some tricks.”","“Something did happen, but it has been resolved,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief replied. He turned to Chu Feng and introduced to him, “Chu Feng, this is our Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s guest elder, Elder Liu.”","He then turned back to the guest elder and said, “Elder Liu, I shouldn’t need to introduce Chu Feng to you, right?”","“Of course. Who hasn’t heard about young friend Chu Feng? I saw young friend Chu Feng’s name appearing on the stone monument before the Immemorial Massacre Sea disappeared. Young friend Chu Feng, did you conquer it?” Elder Liu asked.","The Immemorial Massacre Sea’s fog began to dissipate shortly after Chu Feng and Eggy left the area, making the name on the stone monument even more apparent.","Shortly after, the entire Immemorial Massacre Sea vanished.","Everyone observing the Immemorial Massacre Sea knew it had been conquered by Chu Feng.","“You can say so,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","They quickly brought Elder Liu up to date about the situation. The latter also learned why the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief brought Chu Feng here.","“I’m almost done with the preparations, so it should be possible to enter right now to cultivate. Lord Clan Chief, you should make the call,” Elder Liu said.","“We can’t let Chu Feng make a wasted trip here. Let them enter,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief replied.","Elder Liu took out a couple of talisman papers.","World spiritists often used talisman papers as a medium for their formations, but Chu Feng could immediately tell something was amiss with Elder Liu’s talismans.","These talismans didn’t harness spirit power. Rather these were talismans used by mortals to expel malevolent entities and suppress ghosts."]},{"number":6207,"title":"Chapter 6207: Chapter 6205: Haunted?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6205: Haunted?","Elder Liu sensed Chu Feng’s gaze and explained with a smile, “There is a ghost inside.”","“A ghost?” Chu Feng was perplexed.","‘Ghost’ was a term more commonly used by mortals, but it often referred to a cultivator’s soul. Elder Liu, as a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, should be aware of that. It was perplexing that he would use the term ‘ghost’ here.","“Brother Chu Feng, Elder Liu isn’t joking with you. This place is haunted.” Xianhai Shaoyu walked over and wrapped his arm around Chu Feng’s shoulders. “You can ask my parents and grandfather if you don’t believe it.”","“Well...” Xianhai Shaoyu’s parents smiled.","Xianhai Shaoyu’s grandfather, on the other hand, looked a little awkward. Upon meeting Chu Feng’s gaze, he flashed a mischievous smile and said, “Grandson-in-law, you should put more talismans on. Someone with your talent is bound to meet with the ghost.”","“Grandfather, you’re talking nonsense again!” Little Fishy harrumphed.","“There are no outsiders here anyway. My grandson-in-law is worthy of you, and he has just saved our clansmen’s lives. Shouldn’t you marry him to repay the debt our Immortal Sea Fish Clan owes him?” Little Fishy’s grandfather teased.","“Grandfather, you...” Little Fishy’s face turned red. Powerless to retort, she directed pleading eyes at her parents. “Look at what grandfather is doing! Stop him!”","But Little Fishy’s parents merely smiled.","Little Fishy’s grandfather guffawed. “You think the two of them dare to stop me?”","In truth, Little Fishy’s parents currently had a very high opinion of Chu Feng. Not only did they witness Chu Feng destroying the God Clansmen despite being only at rank one True God level, but they had also seen him destroy the terrifying God Mother with a black sword.","Only the foolish Jie Tianran would continue to make light of Chu Feng.","“What’s going on?” Chu Feng asked.","Those present quickly shared the details with Chu Feng.","The cultivation resources here had to be refined first before they could be assimilated, and they couldn’t be moved to another location either.","However, there was a steep cost to refining the cultivation resources. Most powers couldn’t shoulder the cost even if they discovered this place. Doing so burned a hole even through the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s deep pockets.","There was no age limit to assimilating the cultivation resources, which was why many Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s experts, including Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather, had cultivated here.","But even after the cultivation resources were refined, there remained a bizarre quality to them. There were cases where people were transported to a peculiar realm, where they came face to face with a female ghost.","After analyzing the cases, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan realized that those who encountered the female ghost were their top prodigies.","So far, only a handful of people had met the female ghost.","Little Fishy’s parents encountered the female ghost each time they cultivated here, but Little Fishy’s grandfather had never met her, which suggested that his talent might be inadequate. That was also why he looked a little awkward.","It was also for the same reason he was certain Chu Feng would encounter the female ghost.","“Did you all meet the same female ghost?” Chu Feng asked Little Fishy’s parents.","“Mmhm.” Little Fishy’s parents nodded.","“The same ghost...” Chu Feng was intrigued. He turned to Xianhai Shaoyu and asked, “What does the female ghost look like?”","“I don’t know. It’s my first time here,” Xianhai Shaoyu replied.","“It’s your first time here?” Chu Feng was surprised to hear that.","“You see, there are different ways to refine the cultivation resources here. Elder Liu came up with a special refinement method that maximizes a junior’s cultivation efficiency. So, we decided to reserve the cultivation resources here for our juniors. It has been decades since we last came here,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief answered the question.","Chu Feng didn’t expect the Immortal Sea Fish Clan to have been preparing this place for decades.","“What does the female ghost look like?” Chu Feng asked once more.","“She has blurry features, making her face hard to distinguish. What’s more frightening about her is her eerie disposition. I can’t put it in words well, but it’s bad enough to affect your cultivation. However, you have nothing to worry about. The talisman papers work. We have never met the female ghost again since we started plastering on the talisman papers,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief replied.","Xianhai Shaoyu burst into laughter. “I don’t intend to use the talisman paper. I’m going to meet the female ghost.”","He turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Brother Chu Feng, why don’t you give it a try too since you’re so curious?”","“Sure. I’m interested in meeting the female ghost too. A tragedy may have happened here, and the buildup of malice gave rise to a vicious ghost. Perhaps the female ghost is seeking someone to redress her grievances.","“It’s also possible that the female ghost is looking to siphon a man’s soul to take him as her husband. Brother Shaoyu, you have to be careful. Female ghosts are particularly into guys like you,” Chu Feng said as he patted Xianhai Shaoyu’s shoulder.","“Stop pulling my leg, Brother Chu Feng. You must have read too many novels to even think of such a thing,” Xianhai Shaoyu retorted with a smile, though his smile looked a little stiff.","“I’m not pulling your leg. The world is large enough for anything to be possible. There could be a ghost in there. I have heard many stories. Some encountered a ghost and had their yang energy siphoned to death. Some suffer from nightmares every night till they are scared to death. And there is no lack of formidable cultivators and world spiritists among these people! Many mysteries in this world can’t be explained by common sense,” Chu Feng said grimly.","Xianhai Shaoyu’s expression further stiffened. “Brother Chu Feng, stop scaring me. Are you saying that ghosts truly exist?”","By this point, his excitement had already eroded to fluster.","“What’s wrong, brother? Your face looks pale. Are you afraid?” Little Fishy snickered.","“Afraid? Me? How’s that possible? I’m just intrigued by Brother Chu Feng’s words.” Xianhai Shaoyu awkwardly scratched his head.","He didn’t believe in ghosts, which was why he dared say those words. But Chu Feng’s words planted a seed of doubt in him, making him wonder if ghosts truly existed. That, in turn, made him panic.","Chu Feng had accomplished so many unbelievable feats that his words carried weight, no matter how much they defied common sense.","Xianhai Shaoyu was so flustered that he didn’t notice Chu Feng’s mischievous smile.","Chu Feng was indeed teasing him. He, too, didn’t believe in ghosts."]},{"number":6208,"title":"Chapter 6208: Chapter 6206: The Stumped Female Ghost","paragraphs":["Chapter 6206: The Stumped Female Ghost","It was then that Elder Liu spoke up, “Young hero Chu Feng is right. The world is huge enough for anything to happen, but there must be some kind of logic to it. Perhaps our three prodigies here can unravel the mystery behind this place. Follow me.”","Elder Liu brought Chu Feng and the others into the spirit formation gate.","The teleportation passageway was old but not ancient. It contained Elder Liu’s aura, indicating that it was opened by him.","As soon as Chu Feng stepped out of the teleportation passageway, he felt a gush of cold air. Everyone, regardless of their cultivation level, shuddered.","This coldness chilled not just their bodies but their souls too, instilling unease in their hearts. They already had an ominous feeling in their guts despite not having met the female ghost yet.","“Elder Liu, give me a few talismans,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","Elder Liu divided the talisman papers in his hand into three stacks and handed them to Chu Feng, Xianhai Shaoyu, and Little Fishy.","Xianhai Shaoyu immediately pasted the talisman papers on his clothes and forehead, which made him look like a talisman entity.","“What’s wrong, brother? I thought you wanted to meet the female ghost?” Little Fishy asked with a teasing smile.","“Forget it. I’m here to cultivate anyway, not to meet the female ghost. Why don’t you hand me your talisman papers if you’re planning to meet the female ghost? You won’t be using them anyway,” Xianhai Shaoyu said as he reached for Little Fishy’s talisman papers.","“Dream on.” Little Fishy didn’t give him a chance to swipe her talisman papers. “Scaredy little cat.”","“I’m not scared. I’m merely taking precautions in case that female ghost is a pervert. I need to remain chaste for my Brother Chu Feng!” Xianhai Shaoyu exclaimed.","His parents and grandfather were rendered speechless.","“You have a screw loose,” Little Fishy spat.","But Xianhai Shaoyu was undeterred. He turned to Chu Feng and winked. “Just give the word, and I’ll be yours.”","Chu Feng laughed. He had long gotten used to Xianhai Shaoyu’s line of jokes.","But Little Fishy couldn’t take it. She pinched Xianhai Shaoyu’s cheek and roared, “You pervert! Continue talking nonsense and I’ll rip your mouth open!”","Xianhai Shaoyu’s cheek was stretched so far that he quickly begged for mercy. “I was wrong! I was wrong!”","Everyone else was already used to the siblings’ antics.","Chu Feng started to survey their surroundings.","They were in a humongous, naturally-formed cavern spanning the size of an underground realm. The cavern walls were covered in a thin layer of ice, making them exceptionally sturdy. The ice was where the coldness originated, and it was also the cultivation resource they were here for.","The layer of ice should have been thicker, but it had been refined and assimilated by others.","“How did you find this place?” Chu Feng asked.","He had paid close attention to his surroundings since arriving at this realm, but up to this point, he hadn’t found any sign there was a cultivation spot here. Given his keen eyes, his inability to find this place despite knowing about its existence showed just how well-hidden this place was.","That was why he was curious to know how the Immortal Sea Fish Clan found this place.","“It’s this.”","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief took out an old goatskin parchment and passed it to Chu Femg.","Chu Feng unfurled the scroll.","It required some observation prowess, but he quickly realized it was a hidden map through Heaven’s Eyes. The map detailed the location and the way to enter the destination.","“Our Immortal Sea Fish Clan bought this map at a high price at an auction, and we quickly noticed something exceptional about it. We quickly made our way here, but we found that someone else had been here not too long ago. We deduced that the person who sold us the scroll might have cultivated here first before selling it at a high price.","“We investigated the matter and learned that the scroll was sold by a duo, but both had disguised themselves, so we have no way of knowing their background. We quickly found that the ice can be used as a cultivation resource, but the cost of refinement is high as well,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief told Chu Feng.","“I see. Thank you for telling me, elder.”","That explained the situation. It was someone else who discovered this place.","The goatskin parchment was old, but it didn’t carry the Ancient Era’s aura. This meant that the person who found this place was a present-era cultivator.","Chu Feng and the others ventured deeper into the cavern.","Some parts of the ice looked brighter than others, and they emanated richer natural energies too. On top of that, they contained concentrated martial enlightenment that would be highly beneficial to one’s cultivation.","These were the cultivation resources Elder Liu had refined at a high price.","“Elder Liu, can we start cultivating right away? Is there anything we need to take note of?” Xianhai Shaoyu asked.","He was teeming with excitement. As a cultivator, he could tell how potent the cultivation resources were.","“The refinement might not be perfect, but it can be assimilated. You can just cultivate normally,” Elder Liu said.","Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu walked over and sat down.","“Here.” Chu Feng passed his talisman papers to Xianhai Shaoyu.","Seeing that, Little Fishy also passed her talisman papers to Xianhai Shaoyu.","“The two of you aren’t afraid? That female ghost will affect your cultivation,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","“Actually, I have been wondering if the female ghost is a fortuitous encounter instead of an obstacle. Those who can overcome the female ghost might benefit more from here, though I have no basis behind this,” Elder Liu suddenly spoke up.","“Elder Liu’s words make sense. There must be a reason behind everything. I don’t believe in ghosts, so I’m curious to meet the female ghost,” Chu Feng said before he began assimilating the cultivation resources.","Little Fishy followed suit.","“Haaa! Doesn’t that make me a coward?”","With a sigh, Xianhai Shaoyu took off the talisman papers he had plastered on and began cultivating.","Everything was normal at first.","A gush of natural energies flowed into Chu Feng’s body, and he directed the energies toward bombarding the gate that was standing in the way of his breakthrough. However, it would take more than brute force to open the gate.","Chu Feng had to find the right method to open the gate to make a breakthrough.","The cultivation resources the Immortal Sea Fish Clan had invested heavily in and spent decades preparing were indeed no joke.","It didn’t take long for Chu Feng to gather sufficient natural energies, but even so, he continued to assimilate more natural energies in hopes of gathering more martial enlightenment to find the impetus for a breakthrough.","All of a sudden, Chu Feng felt a wave of cold intent that caused him to shudder. He vaguely sensed a pair of eyes staring at him.","He opened his eyes right away, but found himself unable to move.","He was still in the cavern, but Xianhai Shaoyu and the others were nowhere to be seen.","A silhouette could be spotted in the fog ahead of him.","It was a woman dressed in a white dress with her hair scattered messily. She was slowly approaching him with her back against him, but it turned out that she was facing him, just that her hair was covering her face.","Even so, he could still see a pair of empty eye sockets.","The gaze was from her.","“Cut the act and get straight to the point,” Chu Feng said.","The female ghost vanished, only for her ghastly pale face to appear before Chu Feng the next moment. She stared at Chu Feng with her empty eye sockets, and blood started to gush forth.","“Haa!” Chu Feng sighed. “Elder, I might be young, but I have killed many people. I have witnessed all sorts of horrors in the world. You can’t scare me like this. Why don’t you get straight to the point?”","That stumped the female ghost for good."]},{"number":6209,"title":"Chapter 6209: Chapter 6207: The True Treasure?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6207: The True Treasure?","After a moment of silence, the female ghost said, “You have guts. All right, I’ll give up on the other two and choose you.”","Chu Feng thought the female ghost would get to the point, but she stared at Chu Feng, opened her huge mouth, and let out a piercing scream.","This was no ordinary scream. A sonic wave visibly wrapped around Chu Feng. It had the power to shake a person’s mind, drive them berserk, and even disintegrate their soul.","Yet, Chu Feng remained unfazed.","His mental resilience far surpassed others. He didn’t fear such attacks. Despite the sonic wave furiously tugging at Chu Feng’s clothes and hair, ripping spatial rifts around him, he continued to stare at the female ghost unflinchingly.","The female ghost was stunned.","She stopped her scream and asked, “Are you deaf?”","“Elder, you are a world spiritist. You should be able to tell that I’m not deaf; I merely have high mental resilience. That scream was a test, right? Have I cleared the test now? Is there anything I can help you with?” Chu Feng asked.","“Can’t you leave something for me to say?” the female ghost retorted in annoyance. “Fine, you’re right. That was a test, and you have cleared it. You must have been to many remnants to be familiar with these tricks.","“I have been to quite a few,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“What’s your name?”","“Chu Feng.”","“I’m asking for your real name.”","“Chu Feng is my real name.”","“Your family name is not Jie or Ling?”","Chu Feng realized that the female ghost had misunderstood that he was from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, so he clarified, “I am not from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.”","“Such an outstanding junior isn’t from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion? Has the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion fallen from grace?”","The female ghost shook her head. She looked regretful and melancholic.","“Elder, are you from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion?” Chu Feng asked.","“I used to be,” the female ghost replied.","“Elder, what is this place? Why are you testing us? I am cultivating and am on the verge of a breakthrough, so let’s not beat around the bush and get straight to the point,” Chu Feng said.","“All right, I will get to the point. There is an extraordinary treasure here; the ice you see is just the tip of the iceberg. There are more goatskin parchments out in the world aside from the one you have. One of them fell into my hands, and that’s how I found this place.","“After days of observation, I became certain that a greater treasure lies in the depths of this place. I found the treasure's location, but that place was sealed off by a formidable power. I’m unable to construct a passageway into there alone.","“So, I thought of using an ancient, forbidden treasure to breach that place. Back then, I was still too weak to fully control the forbidden treasure, but I was so curious about the treasure here that I decided to go through with it.","“I succeeded in opening a passageway, but a powerful energy immediately gushed out from within. The energy can erode one’s mind. It is similar to the means I used on you, but many times stronger.","“That energy shook my mind, and I lost control over the forbidden treasure and was consumed by it. I didn’t die, but I was trapped in the forbidden treasure. Fortunately, the forbidden treasure weakened over time, and eventually, I was able to project my consciousness out via a secret art and communicate with others in this manner,” the female ghost said.","“Chu Feng, that female ghost must be extremely powerful to be able to influence even Little Fishy’s grandfather. Saving her is a double-edged sword. It would be the best if she repays your favor, but we mustn’t forget she is from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. She could be an enemy,” Eggy voiced out her worry.","“We shouldn’t stereotype everyone in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but Milady Queen is right. We should at least first verify her character. Let me probe her a little more before making my decision,” Chu Feng replied.","“How obedient,” Eggy replied with a satisfied smile.","Thus, Chu Feng asked, “Elder, what do I need to do to save you?”","“The forbidden treasure’s energy has mostly dissipated, and it’s barely keeping me in now. In the forbidden treasure’s vicinity is a staff used for destroying the forbidden treasure. I had taken it out in advance in case something went awry, but I was consumed by the forbidden treasure before I could use it. If you destroy the forbidden treasure with the staff, I’ll regain my freedom.","“However, that area is still suffused with the formidable energy that had leaked out from the treasure room, and that energy hasn’t weakened in the least. Only someone with a sufficiently resilient mind can withstand it. It will be best if that person has a powerful psyche too. I will frankly tell you that it’s going to be extremely dangerous. Even so, are you willing to help me?” the female ghost asked.","“I’m willing to help you,” Chu Feng replied.","“You’re offering to help me when I haven’t offered you any rewards?” the female ghost asked.","“Didn’t you say that the ice is just the tip of the iceberg compared to the real treasure here, and you have already opened a path into the treasure room? I am very interested in the treasure here too, and I have many experts with me. Elder, if you’re fine with it, I’d like to explore the treasure room with you after I rescue you,” Chu Feng replied.","“The people you came with are useless. I’ve told you that only someone with a resilient mind or powerful psyche can withstand that energy. The two juniors you came with might still be able to pull it off, but those old folks don’t stand a chance at all,” the female ghost replied."]},{"number":6210,"title":"Chapter 6210: Chapter 6208: Jie Shanxian","paragraphs":["Chapter 6208: Jie Shanxian","One’s ability to withstand mental attacks was also a measure of one’s talents. Even cultivators needed to have a strong mind to progress far in their martial cultivation.","And Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu were extremely talented. They were known to be the most talented juniors in the world of cultivation before Chu Feng’s rise to fame.","Yet, this female ghost evaluated them as only having a chance. The energy that emanated from the treasure room must have been formidable.","To be safe, Chu Feng asked, “Elder, do you think I can withstand the energy?”","The female ghost assessed Chu Feng before replying, “Your earlier performance is incredible, but I still have to say that the energy from the treasure room comes nowhere close to what you have just experienced. So, I can’t say for sure whether you can withstand the energy. I can only say that you’re the likeliest to withstand it of all the people I have met so far.”","“I’ll give it a try. Elder, can you tell me where the forbidden treasure is?” Chu Feng asked.","“Later, head into the cavern and walk to the end. It might look like there’s a dead end, but that’s because I blocked off the road with a treasure to prevent others from seeing what I’m doing. On the bright side, it is also thanks to the blockade that the energy wasn’t able to spread out here.","“I’ll impart to you the method to activate the treasure and clear the blockade. Beyond the blockade, you should be able to find the forbidden treasure trapping me inside. However, you should first tell your friends to go out before opening the blockade. The energy is not to be scoffed at; your friends won’t be able to take it, especially the older ones.","“That’s why I test those who come here. If they don’t meet the requirements, I won’t ask them to risk their life in vain for me,” the female ghost said.","Chu Feng was moved.","The female ghost was still fairly powerful despite being trapped.","Those who had reached the level of Little Fishy’s parents and grandfather were able to break free of her secret art, but it would be beyond the weaker ones to do so. She had the means to force others to rescue her.","But according to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan, she did nothing of that sort.","The female ghost suddenly thought of something and hesitantly murmured, “Chu Feng, you possess an extraordinarily resilient mind. You must have gone through much suffering to have tempered your mind to this extent at your age. Even though it’s our first time meeting, and I don’t know much about you, I can tell you’re an incredible prodigy.","“I don’t want to lie to you. The energy emanating from the treasure room might be beyond your means to deal with. From the moment you open the blockade, the energy will start eroding your mind. Your life will be in danger. Thus, you might want to reconsider this matter. I won’t blame you if you choose not to help me.”","Chu Feng chuckled. “Elder, you know my name, but I still know nothing about you. If I may, could I ask for your name and the reason you left the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion?”","The female ghost did a twirl on the spot.","By the time she was facing Chu Feng once more, she looked completely different from before. She had transformed from a paled-faced, bloodied-eyed ghost into a middle-aged woman.","She was beautiful with an amazing figure, with ample bust and bottom, though she was on the chubbier side. Her delicate facial features and her chubby face accentuated her feminine charm. Not even her loose robes could conceal her incredible body.","It was as if she had two watermelons hanging in front.","But what caught Chu Feng’s attention was her fan-shaped birthmark on her forehead.","Even though it was just an avatar in an illusion, Chu Feng could tell there was something special about the birthmark.","“Chu Feng, I am Jie Shanxian. I am old now, so I reckon very few people in the world know about me, but there should be people in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion who remember me. As for why I left the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion... I can only say that I left because I am not fond of some people,” the woman replied.","“Elder, how long have you been trapped here?” Chu Feng asked.","“It has been a very long time. I have lost track of time, but it should have been at least tens of thousands of years now,” the woman replied.","“So long?” Chu Feng was appalled.","She was extremely pitiful to have been trapped in a place like this for so long.","“Have you decided yet?” Jie Shanxian asked with a careful voice.","In truth, she wanted to be freed from her imprisonment, and she was afraid Chu Feng would refuse to help her. She could have fooled Chu Feng, but she was afraid he would die in there, knowing how dangerous it was.","And that was what moved Chu Feng and made up his mind.","“I’m willing to give it a try,” Chu Feng replied.","“Really?” Jie Shanxian could hardly believe her ears. She was overjoyed.","“Yes, I am willing to give it a try.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Aren’t you worried I’m lying to you? This might be a huge lie I spun to convince you to save me. There might be no treasure at all,” Jie Shanxian asked.","“I am no saint, but elder, I can tell you are a good person. There’s no reason for you to warn me about the danger otherwise. That being said, I won’t hesitate to leave if the energy is beyond my means to deal with. I hope you can understand that,” Chu Feng said.","“I do. There’s no way I would blame you.”","All of a sudden, Jie Shanxian burst into tears. The more she cried, the more agitated she became. It reached a point where she bawled like a child.” Chu Feng, why didn’t you come earlier?”","“This is someone who lived for tens of thousands of years?”","Even Eggy was stunned by Jie Shanxian’s reaction. She was practically a child!","Chu Feng stepped forward to console her, “Calm down, elder. Please impart the method to me. I’ll give it a try.”","“Chu Feng, I feel so much regret,” Jie Shanxian said as she wiped off her tears.","“Regret?” Chu Feng was confused.","“When I first arrived here, I started by refining the cultivation resource in the ice. The best cultivation resources have already been refined by me. The remaining ones are hard to refine because they are inferior goods. However, I got trapped before I could use the cultivation resources I refined.","“A hundred years ago, two people came here. I tested them—one of them possessed a strong mind, and the other possessed a strong psyche. I saw them as my savior and promised to bring them to the treasure if they saved me. As a show of sincerity, I even told them where I hid the cultivation resources I refined.","“Both their eyes shone when they saw the cultivation resources, especially the older one. He promised to save me and not let down my trust in him. So, I told them the method to unseal the blockade.","“But as soon as they unsealed the blockade and the energy gushed out, their faces changed. The one with the strong psyche tried his best to make his way toward the forbidden treasure, but he quickly reached his limit and fled. The one with the strong mind didn’t even bother trying. He apologized, saying he wasn’t proficient in world spiritist techniques, before running away.”","Jie Shanxian gritted her teeth indignantly as she recounted the matter.","“It’s understandable for the one with the strong psyche to give up after realizing the feat is beyond him, but it’s too much that the one with the strong mind refused to even give it a try,” Chu Feng said.","“They are in cahoots. Neither of them is a good person,” Jie Shanxian exclaimed with her arms akimbo. She was so angry that her chests were puffing in and out.","“They took away all the cultivation resources?” Chu Feng asked.","He would have probably also taken the cultivation resources with him if he failed, but he would have at least left some behind out of apology. This way, Jie Shanxian could at least use them to get someone else’s help.","“Of course they did! Why else would I be so mad? That was a huge amount of cultivation resource. If only I left some for you... I paid a hefty price to refine it!” Jie Shanxian huffed.","“They are indeed too much,” Chu Feng said with a sigh.","“Right?! Chu Feng, these are the two dog things who stole my cultivation resource! Make sure to stay away from them and don’t get duped by them!”","Jie Shanxian conjured two figures with a wave of her sleeves.","Chu Feng and Eggy were stunned.","They were familiar faces. One was his master, and the other was his father."]},{"number":6211,"title":"Chapter 6211: Chapter 6209: Rank Two True God","paragraphs":["Chapter 6209: Rank Two True God","“Hahahaha...”","Eggy rolled around the World Spirit Space, laughing her head off.","“Chu Feng, I don’t think you have a choice but to help her. This is a debt left by your master and your father. Hahahaha!”","Chu Feng was also at a loss for words. He would have never thought the scammers would be his master and his father. At least his master had given it a try, but his father gave up right away.","“Hm?” Jie Shanxian suddenly narrowed her eyes.","She stared at the face of Chu Feng’s father before looking at Chu Feng. “Somehow, the two of you resemble each other.”","“Do we?”","Chu Feng dared not admit that person was his father. Now that he thought about it, he had never dared to admit their relationship before anyone who knew his father, for all of them always had a conflict with his father.","“There is some resemblance, but you look much better,” Jie Shanxian said. “Chu Feng, look closely.”","She began forming a series of hand seals.","Chu Feng breathed a sigh of relief. Fortunately, Jie Shanxian only saw the similarities between the two of them and didn’t think any deeper into it. He quietly thanked his mother for her passing down her looks to him.","He carefully studied Jie Shanxian’s movements.","After Jie Shanxian was done with her demonstration, she turned to Chu Feng and said, “What I have just shown you is the tempo for the hand seals’ transformations. Next, I will decipher each hand seal for you, so make sure to listen well.”","“Elder, I have remembered all the hand seals,” Chu Feng interjected.","“Ah?” Jie Shanxian was taken aback. She wasn’t too sure what Chu Feng was saying.","So, Chu Feng began forming the hand seals.","Jie Shanxian’s mouth fell agape.","Not only did Chu Feng change his hand seals at the same tempo as her, but his movements were precise even in the complicated portions. It was a perfect replica of her demonstration!","Memorizing the transformation of the hand seals was important, but so was understanding how to utilize each hand seal. This was a very complicated series of hand seals. Even talented world spiritists would take at least a month to master it.","Yet, Chu Feng pulled it off flawlessly without her guidance.","“You are an incredible talent,” Jie Shanxian remarked.","“Elder, there’s something I’d like to ask. I don’t want to lie to my friends about what I am going to do. If my friends ask about you, may I tell them your true identity?” Chu Feng asked.","“You may tell them what you are going to do, but I’ll have to ask you to withhold my identity. Don’t let them know my name or my appearance,” Jie Shanxian replied.","“I understand.” Chu Feng nodded.","“All right, you should focus on your cultivation. Your two friends have made a breakthrough and are waiting for you,” Jie Shanxian said.","“As expected of Little Fishy and Brother Shaoyu.”","Chu Feng wasn’t surprised to hear about their breakthrough.","His surroundings suddenly changed. His eyes were closed, and he was still amid his cultivation, but he could sense the changes in his surroundings without opening his eyes.","Jie Shanxian had dispelled the illusion.","He noticed a massive formation shrouding the cavern; it was puffing out a thick aura as if it were in an intense battle. It was an isolation formation, designed specifically to isolate phenomena.","Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu’s breakthroughs would have induced phenomena, so the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief prepared an isolation formation to conceal them lest they catch the attention of others.","Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu had stopped cultivating, but there were still some cultivation resources lying around. They had intentionally left them for Chu Feng.","Chu Feng hadn’t stopped cultivating while conversing with Jie Shanxian in the illusion, but that distracted him from grasping the martial enlightenment he had absorbed.","To Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu, it looked like he had been cultivating all this while, and the reason he hadn’t made a breakthrough was that he needed more cultivation resources to overcome his bottleneck.","Chu Feng did require more cultivation resources than them to make a breakthrough, but he had already absorbed enough natural energies. He was merely distracted.","So, he changed his hand seal and focused on his martial enlightenment. He soon found the impetus for a breakthrough.","Boom!","Thunder rumbled in the isolation formation.","Nine-colored lightning started settling in, which caused cracks to appear on the strained isolation formation as well.","Elder Liu quickly whipped out ten talisman papers imbued with the Ancient Era’s aura and fused them into the isolation formation, reinforcing it. Even so, the cracks continued to widen.","“Lord Clan Chief!” Elder Liu turned to the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief.","This isolation formation was already reinforced so that it could contain the phenomena from Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy’s breakthroughs, yet it was cracking now even though Elder Liu had just further reinforced it.","The phenomenon Chu Feng induced was stronger than they had imagined. They would have to pay a hefty price to contain this phenomenon.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief understood what Elder Liu was driving at and said, “No matter the cost, we can’t let this phenomenon show.”","Elder Liu whipped out hundreds of Ancient Era’s talismans with a wave of his sleeves. Even so, he still looked at the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief with reluctant eyes as he said, “Lord Clan Chief, this is all we have.”","“Use them,” the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief replied without hesitation.","Elder Liu gritted his teeth.","Instead of throwing all the talisman papers into the isolation formation in one shot, he tossed them in one by one. Even so, it didn’t take long before he tossed a hundred in.","It pained his heart so much that he winced.","Each of these talisman papers was an Ancient Era treasure. It wouldn’t be a stretch to call them limited edition, priceless treasures.","Fortunately, after tossing two hundred more talisman papers in, the isolation formation finally stabilized. Elder Liu breathed a sigh of relief.","He only had around fifty of them left, but that was better than nothing.","“My grandson-in-law is formidable. To think that it would be this hard to contain his breakthrough phenomenon!” Little Fishy’s grandfather exclaimed.","“I would have been shocked to see such a powerful phenomenon before, but I’m hardly surprised now after what happened at the God Clan,” Little Fishy’s mother said.","Little Fishy’s father and grandfather smiled.","Soon, the nine-colored lightning fused into a single lightning bolt that zapped down on Chu Feng. Its prowess was weaker compared to a normal breakthrough, but the outcome was the same.","Chu Feng’s aura rose to rank two True God level."]},{"number":6212,"title":"Chapter 6212: Chapter 6210: It is a New Era","paragraphs":["Chapter 6210: It is a New Era","After his breakthrough, Chu Feng opened his eyes and glanced at Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu.","“You don’t have to leave them for me. Let’s cultivate together, or else I’ll stop cultivating too.”","Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu had stopped cultivating to leave more cultivation resources for Chu Feng. Their goal for bringing him here was to repay the debt they owed to him.","Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu were delighted to see Chu Feng’s breakthrough, and they happily accepted Chu Feng’s proposal. The three of them continued assimilating the remaining cultivation resources.","However, even after finishing the cultivation resources, none of them was able to make another breakthrough.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief walked up to Elder Liu and patted his shoulder with a smile, saying, “Elder Liu, you have worked hard.”","He was satisfied with this outcome.","It was previously unheard of for a junior to reach True God level, and this was not due to a lack of cultivation resources. Those from the previous generations had access to ample cultivation resources too, but they failed to achieve this feat.","Cultivation resources were supplementary; what was more important was the cultivator’s talent. Talented cultivators could build the foundation required for a breakthrough faster, allowing them to advance than others.","While the Ancient Era’s races were likely to have even more monstrously talented juniors, from the current looks of it, Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu weren’t lagging by too much.","For that reason, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief thought it was worth investing so much into these cultivation resources.","“Brother Chu Feng, did you meet the female ghost?” Xianhai Shaoyu asked.","“I met her. What about you?” Chu Feng asked.","“Me too.” Little Fishy nodded.","“Same, but she left shortly later,” Xianhai Shaoyu added.","“It’s the same for me too,” Little Fishy vehemently nodded.","The two siblings turned to Chu Feng, curious to know what he had faced. They had a feeling Chu Feng’s encounter was different from theirs.","“She’s not a ghost.”","Chu Feng quickly filled them in on the details. As per Jie Shanxian’s request, he didn’t divulge her identity and instead opted to introduce her as a skilled world spiritist.","“Is there truly another treasure in there? I knew there was something special about this place, and that what we saw was not its true face. I have examined the ice’s formation and found that they are coming from the ground, but I couldn’t investigate further due to how sturdy the ice is.”","Elder Liu was the most excited one. As a world spiritist, he was exceptionally curious about the mysteries of the world. He found satisfaction in unraveling mysteries, even if there was nothing to be earned from them.","“Big brother, are we unable to withstand that energy?” Little Fishy asked.","“Can’t we give it a try?” Xianhai Shaoyu added.","Little Fishy’s parents, grandfather, and Elder Liu looked at Chu Feng too. The mention of a treasure had sparked their excitement. If there was truly a treasure here, it would most likely be at a level where it would expand their horizons.","Naturally, they were curious about it.","“All right, but you should stand around the exit formation to be safe. Do not hesitate to leave if it gets too much to bear. Don’t push yourself,” Chu Feng said.","Little Fishy and the others agreed.","Elder Liu handed Chu Feng a teleportation talisman paper. “Young friend Chu Feng, activate this talisman if you find yourself at your limit.”","Chu Feng could tell that the talisman paper would transport him to his current location, so he gratefully accepted it.","Following that, he ventured into the cavern alone.","He noticed that the cultivation resources he had just assimilated might be the last few in the cavern. There was still ice remaining that could be refined, but doing so would be exorbitant, and the returns were minuscule.","Furthermore, from the remains, he could tell that the person who refined these cultivation resources was more skilled than Elder Liu, so needless to say, their returns were much greater than the Immortal Sea Fish Clan.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan was the last group to join the feast, so all they got was a sip of cold soup. The meat had already been all gobbled up.","Chu Feng couldn’t help but think about his father and his master, and he murmured, “There’s so much here. Shouldn’t you leave some for me?”","Anyway, Chu Feng hastened his footsteps after confirming there was nothing else he could get from the cavern. He soon arrived at the end of the cavern.","He formed a series of hand seals. The wall before him morphed into a bundle of spirit power, and shortly after, the spirit power dissipated.","Boom!","A shockwave rippled from the opened passageway. Even Chu Feng was knocked several steps back before he regained his balance.","As the shockwave died down, Chu Feng soon verified Jie Shanxian’s words.","He couldn’t see or hear anything at all. The energy was invisible, but he felt inexplicably irritated. Something was interfering with his mind, and if he allowed it to wreak havoc, he might lose his rationality and go berserk.","With the blockade removed, the true cavern unfolded before his eyes.","The cavern was extremely deep, but Chu Feng didn’t make a move right away. He first extended his senses over to check on Little Fishy and the others.","Little Fishy’s grandfather and Elder Liu reached their limit right away and hurriedly left, leaving behind just Little Fishy’s parents, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu.","“Big brother, are you all right?” Little Fishy shouted over.","She had already extended her senses over to check on Chu Feng, but she was still worried about him.","“I’m fine. How are you faring?” Chu Feng replied.","He could already tell that Little Fishy’s parents were quickly approaching their limits, and it was only a matter of time before they had to leave.","Little Fishy was faring much better. Even though she was bearing less energy than Chu Feng, judging from her composure, she should be able to explore the cavern with him. And she would have rushed to his side if not for her being worried about her parents.","Xianhai Shaoyu, on the other hand, was frowning. His tolerance level was above his parents, but the energy was still causing a strain on him.","Chu Feng couldn’t tell whether Xianhai Shaoyu could explore the cavern with him.","“Looks like this is the end of an era. The world of cultivation belongs to the younger generation now!” Little Fishy’s parents remarked with a smile.","Those words were filled with relief and lamentation.","They used to be prodigies others looked up to, achieving feats others could never hope to. In the path of martial cultivation, they had been the ones running ahead, and others struggled to keep pace with them.","Yet, the juniors in this era were outpacing them. It was only a matter of time before they were surpassed.","Their only relief was that their son and daughter were the ones standing at the forefront of this generation.","Little Fishy’s mother looked at her children and said, “Yu’er, Shaoyu, leave right away if you can’t bear it anymore. Your safety is the priority. Don’t lose sight of that.”","Leaving those words behind, Little Fishy’s parents left via the exit spirit formation gate.","Only Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu were left in the cavern."]},{"number":6213,"title":"Chapter 6213: Chapter 6211: Anyway, I Have Gotten Used To It","paragraphs":["Chapter 6211: Anyway, I Have Gotten Used To It","“Brother, are you sure you’re fine? You should go out if you can’t make it. Big brother is waiting for me.”","Despite Little Fishy’s disdainful words, her eyes were filled with worry. She was worried that her older brother couldn’t withstand the energy, and she didn’t want him to push himself.","“You go ahead first. I’ll wait a little longer.”","Cold sweat trickled down Xianhai Shaoyu’s back. Despite his best attempt to look fine, his body was showing that he was strained.","Little Fishy didn’t leave. She often bickered with Xianhai Shaoyu, but that didn’t mean she was any less concerned about him.","“Brother Shaoyu, we are in no rush. You slowly adapt to it,” Chu Feng said, but his voice was nearer than expected.","He had walked over out of worry about Xianhai Shaoyu.","“Brother Chu Feng, I’m fine. You go ahead first.”","Xianhai Shaoyu squeezed out a smile to reassure Chu Feng, not wanting to delay the latter.","“No rush. That elder has already waited tens of thousands of years. A while more won’t hurt,” Chu Feng smiled.","Xianhai Shaoyu smiled too. He understood that Chu Feng was worried about him.","Fortunately, he was a prodigy among prodigies, despite not to the extent of Chu Feng and his little sister. It didn’t take him long to adapt to the energy. His face was drenched in cold sweat, but he had stopped perspiring, and his face wasn’t that pale anymore.","He wiped off his sweat, and the trio headed deeper into the cavern.","The further they ventured, the stronger the shockwaves. A weird noise could also vaguely be heard in the background.","“Brother Chu Feng, little sister, do you hear that?” Xianhai Shaoyu asked.","“You heard that too? I thought it was my imagination,” Little Fishy replied.","The two siblings turned to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng, as a world spiritist, was much more discerning when it came to such matters.","“This energy is filled with resentment, almost as if it is a manifestation of resentment,” Chu Feng replied.","“Resentment? How could there be such terrifying resentment?” Xianhao Shaoyu exclaimed.","“I don’t know. It’s a guess,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“Brother Chu Feng, your guesses are scaring me.”","Xianhai Shaoyu’s clattering teeth betrayed his fear.","An entity whose resentment harnessed such tremendous prowess must be a formidable figure. The thought of it sent shivers down his spine.","Grar!","Whoosh!","The sounds grew increasingly high-pitched. They sounded reminiscent of wails and growls, but in truth, they were just the sounds of the wind.","As they went in deeper, the energy morphed into a whirlwind that raged at the trio while letting out unnerving screeches. The cavern was extremely deep. The deeper they went, the stronger the shockwaves.","It took Xianhai Shaoyu longer than the other two, but he managed to cope with it even though it still took a strain on him.","The energy didn’t just attack their minds; it also hindered their vision. Under such circumstances, they dared not to hasten their footsteps. Every step they took was done with utmost prudence.","It was a distance that would have otherwise taken them an instant to travel, but they took six hours before finally arriving at the cavern’s end.","There, they saw a massive hole that resembled a volcano’s crater. That was where the energy disrupting their minds was coming from.","Above the hole floated a copper item covered in rust. It emanated the Ancient Era’s aura.","On the ground near the hole was a copper staff. The copper staff was also covered in rust, and it emanated the Ancient Era’s aura as well.","That was the forbidden treasure and the staff that could destroy it, as Jie Shanxian mentioned.","“Big brother, can you pick it up remotely?”","Little Fishy was worried that there would be danger if they went too close.","The forbidden treasure looked extraordinary at first glance. Even after depleting half of its energy, its ability to imprison someone of Jie Shanxian’s caliber suggested that it was far more powerful than them.","Chu Feng directed his hand toward the staff and exerted both his martial power and spirit power, but he was unable to remotely pick up the staff.","“It doesn’t look like I can do it remotely. It’s fine. Wait here for me.”","Chu Feng wasn’t sure if it would be dangerous, so he decided to approach alone.","He was able to pick up the staff with his hand, and he proceeded to violently smash it down on the forbidden treasure.","Clang!","The copper staff instantaneously shattered like glass.","Cracks swiftly crept all over the forbidden treasure before it crumbled apart.","Uwa!","A woman’s scream of agony sounded from the cavern’s corner. Looking over, a woman was squatting there. She was the one who made that noise.","She wasn’t there before.","Her hair was unkempt. It was the female ghost Jie Shanxian disguised as.","There was no doubt she was Jie Shanxian, just that she had disguised herself to prevent Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy from seeing her true appearance.","“What’s wrong, elder? Is it the energy here?” Chu Feng asked.","“Stow away the treasure! Stow away the treasure!” Jie Shanxian urged.","Chu Feng released his spirit power with a wave of his sleeve and formed a small spatial formation. He stowed away the shattered forbidden treasure and staff in it, along with the treasure that was previously blocking the entrance of this passageway.","The formation contracted until it was the size of a bead.","Chu Feng handed the bead to Jie Shanxian.","“I’ll need time to adapt to the energy. It’s too strong,” Jie Shanxian said as she took the bead.","Chu Feng was right. She was in pain because she was unable to withstand the energy here. While hissing in pain, she glanced at Chu Feng, followed by Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu, and asked, “Are all of you all right?”","She was surprised as she hadn’t expected Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy to make it this far. Their performance far exceeded her expectations.","“Elder, the two of them are fine, but it took me some time to adapt to the energy, and even so, I only barely made it here,” Xianhai Shaoyu replied.","Jie Shanxian clenched her jaws to stop herself from groaning in pain, but Chu Feng could tell from her warped expression and increased intensity of trembling that her pain wasn’t lessening in the least.","Moments later, Jie Shanxian turned to Xianhai Shaoyu and asked, “Is it possible to adapt to this energy?”","Her pained expression showed that she was unable to adapt to the energy.","“I managed to do it somehow.” Xianhai Shaoyu shrugged with a smug grin.","As much as others viewed him as a prodigy, Xianhai Shaoyu himself knew that he was a prodigy too. In his view, it was only normal for others to fail at what he could do."]},{"number":6214,"title":"Chapter 6214: Chapter 6212: Ancient Era’s War Clan","paragraphs":["Chapter 6212: Ancient Era’s War Clan","“Elder, you can’t withstand it?” Chu Feng got straight to the point and asked.","The hole was the formation passageway opened by the forbidden treasure. Once they jumped in, they would fall so quickly that it would no longer be their choice to advance or retreat.","The energy inside the hole was much stronger. If Jie Shanxian couldn’t even withstand the energy pouring out, she would die if she entered the hole.","“Chu Feng, put me inside the formation and bring me with you.”","Jie Shanxian passed the formation bead she had just received back to Chu Feng. She intended to enter the formation space.","“Elder, are you sure you want to do this?”","Chu Feng thought that it was a risky move.","Jie Shanxian was planning to circumvent the energy through Chu Feng, but Chu Feng wasn’t sure if this method would work. Under normal circumstances, it shouldn’t work.","“I have to go in. Bring me in,” Jie Shanxian insisted.","She opened the formation space and entered it on her own accord. But even after doing so, her face remained as distorted as before. The energy could still seep into the formation space.","Even so, she still urged, “Bring me in.”","“I shall give it a try then.”","Chu Feng grasped the formation bead and absorbed it into his palm.","But Jie Shanxian’s pain didn’t lessen. Not even this could stop the energy from seeping in.","“Elder, it isn’t working,” Chu Feng said.","But Jie Shanxian urged him, “Stop waiting and go in.”","Letting out a sigh, Chu Feng leaped into the hole.","As he had expected, the raging spirit power inside the hole caused him to swiftly plummet. There was no way to turn back at this juncture.","At the same time, the concentration of the energy suddenly spiked severalfold. Even Chu Feng was alarmed. At this rate, he would soon reach his limit.","Fortunately, the energy quickly disappeared, but Chu Feng continued to plummet. He still hadn’t reached the bottom of the passageway.","He realized he had passed by the origin of the energy; the origin of the energy wasn’t at the end of the passageway.","He raised his head out of curiosity, but couldn’t see anything. He couldn’t stop falling either and could only go with the tides.","Finally, he reached the end of the passageway and fell into a boundless palace. He raised his head once more, but he couldn’t see the formation passageway where he entered from. There was no hole or formation in the ceiling as if he had appeared out of nowhere.","This sparked Chu Feng’s worry. He knew Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy would follow him, so he was worried that they would be transported elsewhere.","A spirit formation gate suddenly appeared above Chu Feng, and Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu fell into the palace as well. The gate closed right after the two of them appeared.","Chu Feng was impressed by the prowess of Jie Shanxian’s forbidden treasure.","This formation passageway was opened with the forbidden treasure. Even now, when the forbidden treasure had been destroyed, he still couldn’t find the spirit formation gate once it was hidden.","But now wasn’t a good time to be thinking about this. Chu Feng noticed that Xianhai Shaoyu wasn’t in good condition.","“Are you fine?” Chu Feng rushed forward and asked.","“I’m fine. I just need to rest a while.”","Xianhai Shaoyu waved his hand. His complexion was terrible, and his voice was feeble.","It wasn’t surprising since the energy in the formation passageway had been so powerful that even Chu Feng felt strained. Fortunately, Xianhai Shaoyu’s body was still faring fine; he would swiftly recover after a bit of rest.","Chu Feng turned his attention to Jie Shanxian.","Jie Shanxian was not faring well too, but she had survived the worst. It could be because they were plummeting so fast that it deceived the energy, but this meant that he could bring others in.","“Elder, did you know about this?” Chu Feng asked.","“I didn’t. I just felt indignant and wanted to push ahead,” Jie Shanxian replied.","“Elder, are we able to return?” Chu Feng asked.","He thought of bringing Little Fishy’s parents, grandfather, and Elder Liu in.","This palace was old, but it didn’t carry the Ancient Era’s aura, which meant that it was constructed in the present era. The palace was so vast that he couldn’t see its ends except for the ceiling. It was eerily quiet; all he could see were massive pillars that spanned over fifty meters in diameter.","His mind would be more at ease if they had Little Fishy’s parents here as well.","“We can’t head back the same way. Even if we can, they will have to first withstand the energy before entering the passageway. Are you sure they can withstand it?” Jie Shanxian asked.","Chu Feng didn’t harp on this matter.","Since Jie Shanxian said it was impossible to return the same way, whether it was the truth or not, there was no point fussing over it anymore.","If she was speaking the truth, it would mean they were trapped and had to find another way out. If she was lying, it would mean she didn’t want Little Fishy’s parents here, and it was unlikely Chu Feng could pressure her into getting his way.","Jie Shanxian was likely to be very strong.","“Elder, how strong are you?” Chu Feng asked.","Jie Shanxian would be their biggest backing in the absence of Little Fishy’s parents.","“Being trapped in the forbidden treasure for so long has caused my spirit power to deteriorate; I’m currently at rank one Heavenly Dragon. Either way, I’m just glad to be alive,” Jie Shanxian replied.","“Elder, how strong were you before?” Chu Feng asked.","Jie Shanxian didn’t reply.","The cultivators of the present era were unaware of the existence of Heavenly God level cultivators and Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists, but Jie Shanxian was already a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist tens of thousands of years ago.","This meant the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion had been concealing their strength all this while.","“The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has been concealing their strength since a long time ago,” Chu Feng thought.","“Chu Feng, Jie Shanxian must have been a formidable figure in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. You should get on close terms with her; you might be able to fish out the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s secret from her. Who knows? She might even be able to help you save your mother,” Eggy advised.","“Mm.” Chu Feng agreed.","“Elder, do you want to come out?” Chu Feng asked.","“No need. I’m fine with staying here,” Jie Shanxian replied.","Chu Feng didn’t insist on it, knowing Jie Shanxian could still perceive their surroundings even from within his body. So, he began assessing their surroundings.","“This pillar is extremely sturdy. It’s made out of no ordinary material.”","Chu Feng soon realized that the pillars in the palace were exceptionally sturdy, capable of bearing an extraordinary amount of weight.","“It looks like the treasure is above us.”","Chu Feng started observing the palace’s ceiling.","The energy origin was above them, and these pillars appeared to be bearing the weight of something. Even the ceiling was made out of a special material that prevented one from peering through it. It felt like the palace was designed to prevent one from seeing what was above.","Suddenly, Chu Feng and the others turned their gaze in the same direction.","They sensed a large group of people swiftly approaching them. Although they were extremely far away, it didn’t take long before their silhouettes came into sight.","Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu were taken aback.","There were thousands of people, and every single one of them had reached True God level. However, the reason the three of them were shocked was because of their waist token.","Ancient Era’s War Clan."]},{"number":6215,"title":"Chapter 6215: Chapter 6213: The Disappeared War Clan","paragraphs":["Chapter 6213: The Disappeared War Clan","“Ancient Era's War Clan?” Eggy exclaimed in astonishment.","Back when Chu Feng left the Holy Land of Martialism to enter the Hundred Refinements Ordinary Realm, he learned about a legendary figure from 50,000 years ago known as Zhan Haichuan.","With a silver spear and silver armor, he swept through his opponents without suffering a defeat, swiftly rising to become the strongest person in the Hundred Refinements Ordinary Realm.","However, he vanished shortly after. Only Sunset Cloud Valley’s second-generation Valley Master knew about his later reappearance.","Zhan Haichuan knew he was approaching his limit, and he chose to construct his tomb in the Sunset Cloud Valley’s forbidden land before his death.","Later, his tomb disappeared, and the incumbent Sunset Cloud Valley’s Valley Master requested Chu Feng to find the tomb. It was there he met Old Cat.","Chu Feng had now surpassed Old Cat, but back then, there was not a single person in the Ancestral Martial Starfield who was a match for him, let alone in the Hundred Refinements Ordinary Realm.","Yet, even the powerful Old Cat found himself trapped in Zhan Haichuan’s tomb for many years. If not for Chu Feng falling for Old Cat’s ploy, he would have probably still been imprisoned there.","Even though Zhan Haichuan originated from the Hundred Refinements Ordinary Realm and later returned there, his strength was not to be scoffed at.","And he was from the Ancient Era’s War Clan.","Later, Chu Feng stumbled upon the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s territory in the Hundred Refinements Ordinary Realm and obtained Ancient Era’s War Sword and Ancient Era’s War Axe, two of their nine great secret skills.","These two secret skills were initially a huge help to Chu Feng, but their usefulness diminished as his cultivation advanced. It eventually reached a point where he stopped using them.","Later on, he learned that the Hundred Refinements Ordinary Realm’s Ancient Era’s War Clan was just a branch, and the Ancient Era’s War Clan was far more than that.","When he was discussing secret skills with Song Yuwei, he learned some clues about the Ancient Era’s War Clan from the latter.","Song Yuwei said an elder in the Golden Dragon Flame Sect had previously met an Ancient Era’s War Clansman, claiming that the clansman was powerful and had a hearty personality.","From that, Chu Feng deduced that the Ancient Era’s War Clan was far stronger than he had initially thought, and their secret skills shouldn’t be that weak. He speculated the secret skills he had learned were either incomplete or inauthentic.","That being said, powerful was relative. What was powerful to the Golden Dragon Flame Sect might not be truly powerful.","Much time had passed since, and Chu Feng finally met the Ancient Era’s War Clan once more. This time, he could tell that they were truly powerful. The number of True God level cultivators they had spoke volumes.","However, these Ancient Era’s War Clansmen looked vigilant as if they were up against a terrifying foe. They stopped a distance away from Chu Feng and assessed them in wariness and fury.","“Who are you? Why did you barge into our Ancient Era’s War Clan’s forbidden ground? What are you scheming?” the white-haired old man leading the army questioned.","He was the strongest one in the group, emanating the aura of a rank seven True God level cultivator.","“Elder.” Xianhai Shaoyu greeted the old man as he flicked his wrist and took out his Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s token.","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen widened their eyes. They recognized the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s token.","The white-haired old man even asked, “You’re from the Immortal Sea Fish Clan?”","“Elder, I am Xianhai Shaoyu, and this is my little sister, Xianhai Yu’er. We’re both from the Immortal Sea Fish Clan. This is our friend. We don’t know what is this place; we were exploring a remnant when we unknowingly stumbled in here,” Xianhai Shaoyu explained.","Meanwhile, Little Fishy secretly informed Chu Feng of a matter.","It turned out that the Immortal Sea Fish Clan once had a partnership with the Ancient Era’s War Clan many years back, but for some reason, the Ancient Era’s War Clan suddenly disappeared at one point.","Even so, they used to be on very close terms, which was why Xianhai Shaoyu opted to reveal their identity.","Barging into someone else’s forbidden ground was a huge thing; any power in the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s place would surely turn hostile.","Xianhai Shaoyu was hoping to diminish the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s hostility toward them by revealing his identity as an Immortal Sea Fish Clansmen. His plan worked, as the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen didn’t look as agitated anymore.","But one of them still voiced his doubt, “You said you got here through a formation passageway? Why don’t we see any traces?”","“We don’t know much about the formation passageway either, but it harnesses extraordinary powers. Elder, you should have means to observe this place since it is your forbidden ground, right? Can you inspect that place? There should be a formation passageway there.”","Xianhai Shaoyu pointed to the place where they landed.","“This place was constructed by our ancestors. What you see is what we see. There are no special observation means,” an Ancient Era’s War Clansman replied.","Most of the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen doubted Xianhai Shaoyu’s story.","“I swear that it is the truth. Otherwise, you can also follow us out and re-enter the remnant. It’s just that the remnant is enveloped by bizarre energy that erodes one’s mind, so I fear you might not be able to enter the passageway,” Xianhai Shaoyu replied.","They should not have been divulging the cultivation spot to outsiders, but from the looks of it, the Ancient Era’s War Clan might have some ties to it. Given the current situation, he thought that they should be honest about it.","Boom!","The palace suddenly shook intensely as if a terrifying power was pulsating above.","If not for the sturdy pillars, the palace might have collapsed there and then.","Chu Feng closed his eyes. Since he couldn’t see it, he thought he could try perceiving with his psyche instead. He was certain the trembling was coming above them, at a far distance away, and the cause was likely the origin of that terrifying energy.","That was likely where the treasure lay.","In contrast to Chu Feng and the others’ intrigue, the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen looked unnerved by the tremor.","“These three young friends, this place is ultimately our Ancient Era’s War Clan’s forbidden ground. I can’t blindly take your words as the truth. We have to investigate the matter. Come with us first,” the white-haired old man said as he led Chu Feng and the others away.","Walking out of the palace, Chu Feng was met with a blue sky filled with white clouds and lush green mountains. The entrance to the palace was located in a vast mountain range.","“This formation realm has existed since the Ancient Era,” Jie Shanxian told Chu Feng via voice transmission.","Chu Feng could also tell as much that he was in a formation realm, one that was created by a powerful world spiritist from the Ancient Era. This formation realm was beautiful, and it looked indistinguishable from the real world.","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen didn’t make a move on Chu Feng and the others along the way. If anything, they were courteous.","They brought them to a palace located amidst the lush mountain range and told them to rest there, though this was akin to imprisonment judging from the guards they had stationed around.","However, this was only normal as they needed to investigate their claims.","Xianhai Shaoyu paced around the palace as he exclaimed via voice transmission to Chu Feng and Little Fishy, “It looks like the treasure belongs to the Ancient Era’s War Clan. I didn’t expect them to have such a formidable treasure.”","“How long has it been since the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen last appeared?” Chu Feng asked.","“It has been a very long time. Probably at least 2000 years. We thought they met with a mishap, but it looks like they went into isolation instead,” Xianhai Shaoyu replied."]},{"number":6216,"title":"Chapter 6216: Chapter 6214: The Nine Secret Skills Inheritance Ground","paragraphs":["Chapter 6214: The Nine Secret Skills Inheritance Ground","“Yu’er, Brother Shaoyu, how much do you know about the Ancient Era’s War Clan?” Chu Feng asked.","Through Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu’s explanation, Chu Feng got a deeper understanding of the situation.","There was little information about the Ancient Era’s War Clan even in the early years of the present era, when most powers were vying for supremacy. It had always been a mysterious power.","Later on, an Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s elder got to know an Ancient Era’s War Clan’s elder named Zhan Lianyue by coincidence. The latter knew about a remnant in the Immortal Sea Galaxy, so he wanted to work with the Immortal Sea Fish Clan to conquer it.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan accepted the offer and worked with the Ancient Era’s War Clan to clear the remnant.","Since then, the Ancient Era’s War Clan worked with the Immortal Sea Fish Clan many more times, with Zhan Lianyue serving as the link between the two. It was a pleasant partnership for both clans.","Even so, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan knew little about the Ancient Era’s War Clan. They knew the Ancient Era’s War Clan had a few bases, but they didn’t know where most of their clansmen dwelled.","In fact, they had never met the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief.","“How strong is the Ancient Era’s War Clan?” Chu Feng asked.","“The strongest Ancient Era’s War Clansman our clan has met is Elder Zhan Lianyue. He’s a rank seven True God level cultivator,” Xianhai Shaoyu replied.","“Rank seven True God? That doesn’t seem like much,” Eggy said.","Chu Feng looked out and examined the formation realm. “But it looks like the Ancient Era’s War Clan is far stronger than that.”","Even from the formation realm, Chu Feng could already sense the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s strong foundation.","“Big brother, what do you think about the current situation?” Little Fishy asked via voice transmission.","She was feeling nervous.","Even though the Immortal Sea Fish Clan had been on good terms with the Ancient Era’s War Clan, they were merely in a mutually beneficial partnership. Things could be different now that they had stumbled upon a secret place that appeared to be very important to the latter.","None of them could know for sure how the Ancient Era’s War Clan would react to this.","Xianhai Shaoyu understood that too, which was why he immediately flashed his identity to let the Ancient Era’s War Clan know that they had backing. Even so, Little Fishy was still worried.","“That elder is a rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, and she seems trustworthy. I don’t think she’ll leave us to the lurch is the Ancient Era’s War Clan tries to pull something,” Chu Feng told Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu.","“Rank one Heavenly Dragon? That’s weaker than I thought,” Xianhai Shaoyu giggled.","“That elder’s spirit power is impaired. She was stronger before,” Chu Feng replied.","“Ah, I see. Either way, having a rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist here with us is very reassuring. Based on our clan’s deduction, the Ancient Era’s War Clan is not weak, but it hasn’t reached a level comparable to the galaxy overlords. Back when we were in a partnership, the Ancient Era’s War Clan maintained a respectful attitude toward us. Based on that, it’s unlikely that they have a Heavenly God level cultivator among them,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","“Let’s hope that’s the case.”","Chu Feng thought that things weren’t that simple, considering the formidable formation realm and the treasure they had yet to see. If someone as powerful as Zhan Haichuan could rise from a weaker branch in the Hundred Refinements Ordinary Realm, it shouldn’t come as a surprise if the Ancient Era’s War Clan had immensely talented individuals here too.","Chu Feng posed some questions to Jie Shanxian, but the latter refused to divulge anything.","Many figures suddenly appeared in the distant horizon. It looked as if a silver cloud was swiftly approaching them. It was an army of ten thousand silver-armored soldiers, but its leader was a young woman wearing a red dress.","The young woman had a curvaceous figure that drew attention, but her ferocious facial features would have intimidated those who were interested in her.","The silver-armored army quickly encircled the palace.","The woman in a red dress descended on the mountain before strutting toward the palace with two old men behind her.","“Miss Mudan.”","The ones guarding the palace initially tried to stop her, but they quickly backed off when she glared at them and told them to scram.","Bam!","She kicked down the palace door before entering with the two old men.","None of them were concealing their cultivation—the woman in a red dress was at rank four True God level, whereas the two old men behind her were at rank five True God level.","“Which of you two are from the Immortal Sea Fish Clan?”","The woman in a red dress eyed Chu Feng and the others as if they were criminals.","“Who are you?” Xianhai Shaoyu asked.","She displayed none of the courtesy and the manners of the old man they had met earlier, so Xianhai Shaoyu also brought out his airs as the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s young master.","The two old men narrowed their eyes. From experience, they knew that it was impossible for someone to imitate that disposition. There was no doubt in their mind that Xianhai Shaoyu was from a lofty background.","But the woman in a red dress remained unfazed. “You aren’t qualified to know who I am. Speak! Why did you barge into our Ancient Era’s War Clan? What are your motives? Don’t even dream about leaving this place alive if you can’t give me a convincing explanation!”","“You aren’t qualified to speak with me. Call your clan chief over,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","“You think you’re qualified to meet my father? Men, take him down.”","The two old men, despite their hesitation, were prepared to obey the command.","“Stop,” a voice echoed outside.","Three more figures flitted over.","It was a young woman wearing a white dress accompanied by two old men.","Her physique was not as eye-catching as the woman in a red dress, but her facial features were more delicate. She had a high nose bridge, big eyes, and a fair, oval face. She gave off a strong impression.","There were some resemblances between the two women, which hinted at them being sisters.","“Big sister, don’t be disrespectful. They are esteemed guests of our clan.”","The woman in a white dress immediately stood in front of the woman in a red dress, stopping her from doing anything else.","“Esteemed guests? Moli, they barged into our forbidden ground; that’s a crime that warrants death. How could you call them esteemed guests?” the woman in a red dress replied.","“Big sister, the elder has already verified their tokens, and they have explained how they got there. The Immortal Sea Fish Clan is our ally. They won’t deceive us,” the woman in a white dress said.","“The token might be real, but they could have stolen it. Even if they are Immortal Sea Fish Clansmen, how can we know for sure they are trustworthy? It’s hard to believe even your own clansmen these days, let alone outsiders,” the woman in a red dress said.","Just then, the woman in a white dress took out a golden token. Inscribed on the front was ‘Ancient Era’s War Clan’, and behind ‘Proxy of the Clan Chief’.","The woman in a red dress frowned in displeasure. “Moli, are you using father’s token to suppress me now?”","“Big sister, that is not my intention. The Immortal Sea Fish Clan is indeed an esteemed guest, and so far, we haven’t found any lies in their claims. Father will get to the bottom of the matter, and till then, we shouldn’t be discourteous to them,” the woman in a white dress said.","“Fine. I shan’t bother with this.”","The woman in a red dress was so angry that her face turned red. She flung her sleeves and furiously marched off with the silver-armored army.","The woman in a white dress glanced at the two old men behind her. The two of them retreated from the palace and closed the doors behind them.","Only then did the woman in a white dress greet Chu Feng and the others with a bow, saying, “Allow me to introduce myself. I am Zhan Moli. The woman in a red dress you just met is my big sister, Zhan Mudan. The incumbent clan chief is our father. My big sister can be over the top at times, but she isn’t a bad person. I hope you won’t hold it against her.”","“Don’t worry about it. We understand,” Xianhai Shaoyu replied.","“How can I address the three of you?” Zhan Moli asked.","Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu revealed their names to Zhan Moli.","“Miss Moli, there is a simple way to verify our words. You just have to send someone to the place I mentioned. There must be a way out of the formation realm, right?” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","“Young master Shaoyu, there has been an incident recently. We can no longer leave the formation realm,” Zhan Moli replied.","Xianhai Shaoyu realized that things might have been trickier than he had expected.","“You don’t have to be too worried about it. We will thoroughly investigate the matter lest we wrong you. Since it’s your first time here, why don’t I bring you around?” Zhan Moli offered.","Curious about the mysterious Ancient Era’s War Clan, Chu Feng and the others accepted Zhan Moli’s invitation.","So, Zhan Moli brought Chu Feng and the others around the formation realm.","The palace they were stationed at was far from the center of the Ancient Era’s War Clan, though there were still many formations and patrolling guards. It was their forbidden ground, after all, so its defenses were bound to be tight.","It took some time before they arrived at a grand city. This was the living area of the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen.","The first thing they saw upon entering the city were nine towering sculptures. Chu Feng’s interest was immediately piqued.","The nine sculptures were comprised of saber, spear, sword, halberd, hatchet, battle-ax, hook, fork, and hammer, and each of them harnessed extraordinary energy within.","Noticing Chu Feng’s interest, Zhan Moli explained, “This is our clan’s Nine Secret Skills Inheritance Ground.”"]},{"number":6217,"title":"Chapter 6217: Chapter 6215: Lost Inheritance","paragraphs":["Chapter 6215: Lost Inheritance","“The Nine Secret Arts Inheritance Ground?”","Both Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy looked at the nine sculptures with gleaming eyes.","“Is it still possible to receive the inheritance now?” Chu Feng asked.","He deduced that the energy inside the nine sculptures was likely the energy required to learn the secret skills, but the energies were already waning.","“Before talking about the Nine Secret Skills, I must first talk about our founder. Our founder is a discreet but powerful cultivator. He was the creator of the Nine Secret Skills. However, he couldn’t pass them down because of their immense power, so he constructed the Nine Secret Skills Inheritance Ground.","“What lies here isn’t the real Nine Secret Skills but their weakened versions. Clansmen who meet the criteria can undergo the inheritance of the secret skill, but what they take away from the inheritance may differ depending on the extent of their talent.","“Over time, the secret skills in this inheritance ground have grown weak, so none of our clansmen would come here to inherit them anymore. Elders who have already acquired the secret skills can pass them down to others, so we’re no longer reliant on the inheritance ground. Instead, we left a bit of energy inside the sculptures as a commemoration.","“Quite a few of our clansmen have grasped the Nine Secret Skills. For instance, I have grasped three of the Ancient Era’s secret skills.”","Zhan Moli released her martial power toward the sky, and it manifested into a 10,000-meter-tall halberd. Seconds later, a blade and sword of the same height also manifested as well.","Zhan Moli beckoned the three weapons over. The three weapons descended from the sky, contracting as they made their way down until they were the size of a normal weapon, before floating next to her.","Chu Feng eyed the Ancient Era’s War Sword.","It was identical to the one he had grasped, but there was a difference in its aura. Even though Zhan Moli was only at Half-God level, he sensed that her Ancient Era’s War Sword was stronger than his.","“Young master Chu Feng, you seem interested in the Ancient Era’s War Sword?” Zhan Moli noticed Chu Feng’s gaze.","“I just think the sword looks suave,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“You have a good eye, young master Chu Feng. The Ancient Era’s War Sword is ranked third among the Nine Secret Arts. In first place is the Ancient Era’s War Halberd, followed by the Ancient Era’s War Blade,” Zhan Moli replied.","“So, Miss Moli has grasped the three strongest secret skills?” Chu Feng asked.","“I inherited these secret skills from a clan elder for commemoration. They aren’t particularly powerful. The strongest secret skills in our clan are currently with my father,” Zhan Moli said.","“All nine of them?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes, the strongest nine secret skills are with him, but that’s only including those still within our clan. Many of our elders left with the more powerful secret skills in the early years of the present era, though those secret skills are still weaker than our founder’s. Only our founder has the true Nine Secret Skills,” Zhan Moli explained.","“Does the Ancient Era’s War Clan no longer have the true Nine Secret Skills?” Chu Feng asked.","“Our founder left after constructing the Nine Secret Skills Inheritance Ground. Many years have passed since. I don’t think he’s in the world anymore. It wouldn’t be a stretch to say our Ancient Era’s War Clan’s true Nine Secret Skills are no longer around,” Zhan Moli said in lamentation.","Eggy murmured contemplatively, “That means the version you received is just a replica, and it’s possibly one of the weaker ones among the many.”","“That seems to be the case,” Chu Feng replied.","“Chu Feng, this Zhan Moli seems easygoing. Why don’t you ask her about the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s branches?” Eggy asked.","“I was thinking the same too,” Chu Feng replied Eggy. he turned to Zhan Moli and said, “Miss Moli, there’s something I’d like to ask.”","“Feel free, young master Chu Feng,” Zhan Moli replied.","“I have a friend who stumbled upon Ancient Era’s War Clansmen by coincidence. Those clansmen are friendly, but they don’t seem to be particularly powerful. Some of them wield the Ancient Era’s secret skills, and according to my friend, they greatly resemble yours. So, I’m curious to know if those people are impersonators or true Ancient Era’s War Clansmen?”","Chu Feng chose to ask in an indirect way to avoid trouble.","“They could be impersonators, but they could also be one of our branches. Something happened in the earlier years of the present era, prompting many of our clansmen to leave and never return,” Zhan Moli explained.","“I see. My friend said that the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen he met are currently lying low. Judging from your words, they might be a branch of the Ancient Era’s War Clan,” Chu Feng remarked.","“Did your friend mention where he met them?” Zhan Moli asked out of curiosity.","“He didn’t mention it,” Chu Feng replied.","“Did your friend say how those Ancient Era’s War Clansmen are faring?”","“They seem to be faring decently.”","“That’s good to hear.” Zhan Moli breathed a sigh of relief. Even though it was just a branch that had left many years back, she was still concerned about them.","Boom!","Suddenly, there was a loud noise.","Spirit power was raging on the plains outside the city. Powerful shockwaves rippled through the clouds; they could be seen even from a distance away.","“My apologies. Something has happened. Please wait for me here. I’ll be right back. Otherwise, you can also accompany me,” Zhan Moli said.","“Don’t worry about it. Let’s head there together,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","All of them could tell that a problem had cropped up.","Despite the ruckus, it wasn’t a particularly threatening situation. The raging spirit power was only at the level of an early True Dragon World Spiritist.","“All right. Please come with me.”","Zhan Moli brought the three of them over.","The commotion was coming from an empty clearing. The shockwaves had mostly dissipated by the time they arrived, but the clearing was in a mess. Countless natural oddities were scattered around the clearing, and quite a few people were injured.","These people were all world spiritists, but none of them were carrying the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s waist tokens.","“I hope everyone is fine. Let’s continue. We’ll start with organizing the materials,” an old voice echoed.","The crowd glanced over and saw a yellow-haired, ugly old man.","While issuing orders, he constructed a recovery formation to heal himself. He had sustained some injuries from the earlier impact. Just by looking at his formation, one could tell that he was just a rank one True Dragon World Spiritist.","He looked to be the leader of the group, judging from how the others obeyed his orders.","“Elder Li, are you fine?” Zhan Moli rushed to the old man’s side.","“Miss Moli, what brings you here? Did the commotion disturb you? I’m sorry for my incompetence,” Elder Li said apologetically.","“It’s fine, Elder Li. I’m glad you’re fine. You’re the hope of our clan now,” Zhan Moli said.","Elder Li breathed a sigh of relief. He was terrified that Zhan Moli would blame him for his failure.","“What’s happened? Yet another failure? How useless. We wasted our resources raising fools!” another voice echoed from the horizon.","An army of people were heading in their direction. It was Zhan Moli’s big sister, Zhan Mudan."]},{"number":6218,"title":"Chapter 6218: Chapter 6216: Flaunting","paragraphs":["Chapter 6216: Flaunting","Zhan Mudan led her people over. As she approached, she cast her eyes on Chu Feng and the others before finally turning to Zhan Moli.","“Why did you bring them here? Is this a place they can visit? You must be out of your mind, Zhan Moli!” Zhan Mudan roared in anger.","“I’ll bear all responsibility.” Zhan Moli took out that token again.","Zhan Mudan’s face darkened at the sight of the token. “This matter concerns our clan’s safety. How can you take responsibility for that?”","“You don’t have to worry about that, big sister. With this token, I can take responsibility even if something goes wrong,” Zhan Moli replied.","“Zhan Moli, you’re siding with outsiders over me, your big sister? Did water get into your brain?!”","Zhan Mudan was so angry that her face turned red, but she was unable to do anything about Zhan Moli. So, she turned her glare to Elder Li and berated, “Elder Li, our clan has provided you with the best resources and the blueprint. Aren’t you a True Dragon World Spiritist? Why can’t you accomplish something that simple?”","“Miss Mudan, I am only a rank one True Dragon World Spiritist. My skills are limited. This formation is beyond my means. I have already said that I can’t do it from the start, but Lord Clan Chief promised not to blame me whether I succeeded or not, so long as I give it a try.","“I am also ashamed to have squandered so many precious resources. Miss Mudan, I will stop here if you find my work lacking. Please seek someone else’s help,” Elder Li said before rising into the air to leave.","But oppressive might fell from the sky and enveloped Elder Li, holding him in place.","It was the doing of one of the two old men behind Zhan Mudan.","“Don’t be disrespectful,” Zhan Moli hurriedly intervened.","“Shut up, Zhan Moli,” Zhan Mudan roared.","Before Zhan Moli could reply, Elder Li remarked with a sigh, “I am just a small fry. I only happened to stumble into here. If not for your Ancient Era’s War Clan not having any world spiritist and being unable to head elsewhere to find someone more competent, I would have never been qualified to interfere in something as important as this, and none of you would have addressed me as elder either.","“I understand that you have no choice but to do this, but my strength is limited. I am but a mere ant before the Ancient Era’s War Clan. My life is in your hands. Go ahead and kill me since I am no longer of use to you.”","Elder Li closed his eyes, looking like he was ready to accept death.","But Chu Feng could tell from the trembling hands in his sleeves that he was afraid of death, just that he was putting on an act.","Zhan Mudan’s anger deepened, but she didn’t make a move. Instead, she took a deep breath and gestured for the two elders to retract their oppressive might before descending to Elder Li’s side.","“I apologize for my insolence, Elder Li, but our clan is in a critical position. We urgently require you to construct it. I was too worried that I went overboard earlier, and I ask for your forgiveness for that. Please help our clan. We’ll handsomely reward you if you succeed.”","Elder Li was delighted by Zhan Mudan’s change in attitude. He didn’t want to die either, so he didn’t hesitate to defuse the situation when the opportunity arose.","“I’ll give it another try,” Elder Li said before he continued making preparations.","“You know what Elder Li is doing. Are you sure you want them to watch?” Zhan Mudan glanced at Zhan Moli.","Zhan Moli turned to Chu Feng and the others, “Miss Yu’er, young master Shaoyu, and young master Chu Feng, I apologize for holding up your time. Let’s head elsewhere since the matter here has been resolved.”","But Chu Feng asked, “May I take a look?”","“Is young master Chu Feng interested in formations?” Zhan Moli asked.","“My Brother Chu Feng is currently the most talented world spiritist in the world of cultivation!” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","“Most talented world spiritist? What a joke!” Zhan Mudan sneered in disbelief.","“You might not have heard of my Brother Chu Feng because you aren’t up to date with current news, but surely you must have heard of Jie Ranqing? My Brother Chu Feng is Jie Ranqing’s son,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","“My apologies, but I have never heard of Jie Ranqing either,” Zhan Mudan coldly replied.","“Wow. You truly are... ignorant.” Xianhai Shaoyu was rendered speechless.","He could tell from Zhan Mudan’s expression that she was telling the truth. The Ancient Era’s War Clan must have been trapped here for a long time now.","Chu Feng turned to Zhan Moli and said, “Miss Moli, I don’t know what problems the Ancient Era’s War Clan is facing, but I can tell from your earlier conversation that this item you are trying to forge is of vital importance to your clan. I might be able to help you.”","Before Zhan Moli or Zhan Mudan could reply, Elder Li sneered, “Young man, you are still a junior, right? I know youngsters like you brag a lot, but this matter is of grave importance. It’s beyond the means of someone who has barely grasped the basics. I won’t stop you from observing, but you should drop the idea of getting involved. We don’t have much materials left here to squander.”","Those words irked Little Fishy.","“Old man, why are you acting so arrogant? I was sympathizing with you earlier, but I see you deserve it now. You have quite the ego despite your incompetence. Do you think that all world spiritists in the world are as useless as you? Open your eyes wide and take a good look—he is Chu Feng, a world spiritist whom you can never match up to!”","She didn’t hold back on her words.","But her words merely deepened Elder Li’s derision. He shook his head and lamented, “Youngsters nowadays are getting increasingly arrogant, but there should be a limit to bragging.”","That further fanned Little Fishy’s anger. She wanted to march up to Elder Li to thrash things out, but Chu Feng held her back.","Chu Feng unleashed his spirit power, causing his clothes to flutter.","Everyone, except for Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu, was taken aback. Even Zhan Mudan was flabbergasted, and her mouth opened the widest of all.","“Y-you are a rank one True Dragon World Spiritist? You aren’t a junior?” Elder Li asked grimly.","“Young master Chu Feng is a rank one True Dragon World Spiritist too?” Zhan Moli reassessed Chu Feng in astonishment.","“Miss Moli, may I have a look at the blueprint?” Chu Feng asked.","“All right.” Zhan Molin nodded. She took out a scroll and passed it to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng unfurled the scroll and took a look at the blueprint before turning to the world spiritists making preparations in the clearing.","“Everyone, please stop what you’re doing and leave the rest to me,” Chu Feng said.","“This...”","The world spiritists turned to Elder Li.","“Listen to him,” Zhan Moli said.","All the world spiritists stopped what they were doing. Given Zhan Moli’s standing, her words held far greater weight than Elder Li’s.","Chu Feng waved his sleeves, and the natural oddities scattered around swiftly fell back into position. Then, he began the forging process.","“Miss Moli, Miss Mudan, do you intend to leave it to him? You must know how complicated the blueprint is. I struggle with it despite having studied it for months. He is a rank one True Dragon World Spiritist too, yet he seeks to forge the item with just a mere glance at the blueprint. That is a recipe for failure; we are just wasting resources in vain!” Elder Li exclaimed.","All of a sudden, a brilliant light shone.","Chu Feng had completed his formation construction.","The formation contracted, and the light receded. A faintly glowing copper sphere, spanning the size of a watermelon, emerged from the formation.","The crowd fell silent.","Elder Li’s expression stiffened up. The copper sphere was the item he had failed to construct over the past few months."]},{"number":6219,"title":"Chapter 6219: Chapter 6217: Familiar","paragraphs":["Chapter 6217: Familiar","Shoosh!","Before Zhan Moli could examine it, Elder Li reached out and grabbed the copper sphere. He examined it over and over again with all his senses, but the more he inspected it, the deeper his astonishment.","This copper sphere perfectly met the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s requirements.","“Young master Chu Feng, you aren’t a junior?” Zhan Moli looked at Chu Feng with eyes filled with respect.","“Miss, I understand where you are coming from, but my Brother Chu Feng is a junior,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","“How can there be a True Dragon World Spiritist junior?”","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen were taken aback. Even though Chu Feng felt like a junior to them, they found it hard to believe that he was indeed a junior. It was unthinkable for a junior to possess such spirit power.","Their common sense told them that only top prodigies could hope to reach Half-God level or God-cloak as a junior. Those of Zhan Mudan or Zhan Moli’s caliber could easily tower over the masses.","They believed that if not for the Ancient Era’s War Clan being in isolation, Zhan Mudan and Zhan Moli’s names would have been praised throughout the world of cultivation.","With such underlying beliefs, they found it hard to believe that Chu Feng had reached True Dragon as a junior.","This was at odds with their belief.","Bam!","A dull thud suddenly echoed from Zhan Mudan.","She had raised a treasure high up with her right hand. The treasure emanated waves of spirit power that shrouded the surroundings.","The others were unaffected, but Zhan Mudan, Zhan Moli, Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu glowed with faint lights.","This surprised everyone, including Zhan Mudan, for the treasure served to verify whether one was a junior or not.","“You truly are a junior?” Zhan Mudan asked Chu Feng with reddened cheeks.","She was embarrassed at having determinedly asserted a claim, only to have it overthrown.","“You must find it hard to believe, right? I don’t blame you. It’s for a reason that my brother is celebrated as the greatest world spiritist prodigy in the world. I don’t know why you lost touch with the outside world, but if you go out now, you will find the world of cultivation talking about my brother’s feats,” Xianhai Shaoyu said in glee.","“Young master Chu Feng, I didn’t expect you to be a hidden expert. Could I request you to help us forge more of these items?” Zhan Moli asked.","“Should I forge all the remaining materials into copper spheres?” Chu Feng asked.","Zhan Mudan interjected, “Yes, all of them.”","But Chu Feng ignored her and continued looking at Zhan Moli. It was only when Zhan Moli nodded that he formed a hand seal and reactivated his formation.","In an instant, all the natural oddities were forged into copper spheres. All in all, there were twelve of them, including the one Chu Feng had already forged.","“This... He even managed to save on the materials?” the older Ancient Era’s War Clansmen exclaimed in awe.","Even though they weren’t world spiritists and thus couldn’t forge the copper spheres, they had seen other world spiritists forging them. From that, they knew how much materials were typically needed to forge a single copper sphere.","With the materials they had remaining, Chu Feng should have only been able to forge ten more copper spheres at most, yet he produced twelve of them.","Despite saving on the materials, the quality of the copper spheres still met the requirements.","This was a clear display of Chu Feng’s superior skills as a world spiritist.","“Heaven must have sent this young friend to our Ancient Era’s War Clan to save us!” The older Ancient Era’s War Clansmen looked at Chu Feng with heated eyes.","Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu exchanged looks. They had long realized that the Ancient Era’s War Clan was facing a crisis, though they didn’t know the details of it. Chu Feng had just provided invaluable aid to them in their time of need, and that should be beneficial to their case.","“Young hero, I was blind.” Elder Li walked up to Chu Feng with a fawning smile and bowed deeply to him.","Chu Feng responded with a polite smile, but it was a gesture of nonchalance rather than forgiveness. He had met so many such people that he wouldn’t take them to heart anymore.","“Not only are you blind, but you are incompetent too. We are fortunate to have young master Chu Feng here, else I doubt you could have forged a single one.”","Zhan Mudan shoved Elder Li aside before directing a sweet smile at Chu Feng. “Young master Chu Feng, you have done us a huge favor.”","Her ravishing smile paired with her voluptuous figure made it hard for most men to resist her charm, yet Chu Feng merely responded with the same smile he gave Elder Li.","Zhan Mudan failed to notice the coldness behind Chu Feng’s polite smile. Thinking Chu Feng had forgiven her, she smiled even more radiantly.","She took another two steps toward Chu Feng before turning to Zhan Moli and saying, “Moli, deliver these over. I’ll take young master Chu Feng around.”","“Big sister, you should deliver the spheres instead,” Zhan Moli replied as she passed the copper spheres to Zhan Mudan.","Before Zhan Mudan could reply, she turned to Chu Feng and the others and said, “Let’s go.”","Chu Feng and the others followed Zhan Moli out of the clearing. None of them wanted to stay here with Zhan Mudan.","Zhan Moli brought Chu Feng and the others around the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s main city and to their known scenic spots, sharing with them her culture and the events that had transpired at those places.","But Chu Feng and the others were so busy thinking about what had happened to the Ancient Era’s War Clan that they weren’t too interested in those scenic spots.","Despite their curiosity, they chose not to ask about it.","Zhan Moli would have told them on her own accord if she wanted to talk about it. Otherwise, they wouldn’t receive satisfactory answers even if they asked about it.","“Miss Moli, I have finally found you,” an old man said as he flew over.","He was one of the two old men who followed Zhan Mudan around.","“What’s wrong, Elder Yin?” Zhan Moli asked.","The old man fell silent, but Chu Feng and the others could tell that he was still communicating with Zhan Moli via voice transmission.","After a brief silence, the old man finally spoke out loud once more, “We can’t embed the copper spheres into the formation. We might need young hero Chu Feng’s help on that.”","“Young master Chu Feng, may I trouble you with that?” Zhan Moli asked.","“Of course. Lead the way,” Chu Feng said.","“All right.”","The old man led the way for them.","“My apologies. I should have told you a long time ago about it, but I find it hard to raise the matter as it isn’t anything good.” Zhan Moli finally decided to break the silence.","“I understand. What happened?” Chu Feng asked.","“My clan is currently under attack, and the attack has been ongoing for some time now. The enemy is formidable, and he has inflicted considerable damage on my ancestor’s protective formation. The copper spheres forged by Chu Feng were intended to strengthen the protective formation.”","“Who is attacking the Ancient Era’s War Clan?” Chu Feng asked.","“All we know about that person is that he is a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist,” Zhan Moli said as she brought out a painting.","Chu Feng looked at the painting and was stunned. The person in the painting looked familiar."]},{"number":6220,"title":"Chapter 6220: Chapter 6218: A Junior Heavenly Dragon?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6218: A Junior Heavenly Dragon?","The portrait depicted a young man with black hair and masculine features that gave off an air of coldness, yet his eyes were gentle.","Chu Feng found him oddly familiar, but upon closer examination, he didn’t recognize the other party at all. His memory was so good that he could remember everyone he had met before, so it was perplexing that someone he had never met would look familiar.","Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu also examined the painting too. The more Xianhai Shaoyu looked at it, the tighter his frown became.","He noticed something and asked Zhan Moli, “Is he the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist who attacked your clan?”","“Yes, that’s him,” Zhan Moli replied.","“Why does he look so young? Almost like a junior,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","The man in the portrait looked extremely young, almost around the same age as Chu Feng and Xianhai Shaoyu.","“He can’t be a junior, right?” Little Fishy asked.","Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy weren’t saying these words for no reason. Cultivators tended to have superb intuition honed through their experiences. It could be a wild guess, but there had to be an underlying reason why such a thought surfaced in their mind in the first place.","And this person had spurred such a thought in all three of them.","“Rest assured, he’s not a junior despite his young appearance. It is already unheard of for someone as young as young hero Chu Feng to reach True Dragon, let alone Heavenly Dragon. If that man can reach Heavenly Dragon as a junior, the power behind him must be overwhelmingly powerful, capable of crushing our Ancient Era’s War Clan with a touch. They would not have to go through so much trouble,” the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s elder said.","“That’s not necessarily the case. My Brother Chu Feng will become Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist in just a few years, and given his talent, Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist won’t be the cap for him as a junior,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","“...”","The Ancient Era’s War Clan’s elder first looked at Chu Feng, followed by Xianhai Shaoyu. He had no idea how he should respond to those comments.","He would have usually refuted those words immediately, but something made him hesitate.","It should have been impossible for someone of Chu Feng’s age to be a True Dragon World Spiritist; that was a height many failed to reach despite having spent tens of thousands of years training, but Chu Feng reached it in just decades.","But again, talent was everything in cultivation.","Since time immemorial, powerhouses whom others lauded were all extremely talented individuals. They were considered prodigies because they easily achieved feats that others failed at despite having devoted their lives to it.","Looking at it from that angle, it was not that unthinkable for Chu Feng to achieve what he would have usually deemed impossible.","Records were there to be broken. Common sense was meant to be shattered.","He looked at Chu Feng once more, and he found himself wondering if Chu Feng would truly reach Heavenly Dragon as a junior. That would be a splendid sight to behold. Such a feat would surely go down in history!","“I can see young hero Chu Feng reaching Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist as a junior, but his talent is one-of-a-kind. I don’t believe that someone else can match him in terms of talent,” the elder remarked.","“You are right; Brother Chu Feng’s talent is indeed one-of-a-kind. But the world is a huge place. There must be plenty of talented people in the world. While there might not be anyone who surpasses Brother Chu Feng’s talent, there could be a few who come close to him.”","That was Xianhai Shaoyu’s true thought.","He was confident in his talent, but he didn’t make light of others just because of that. He believed that if he possessed such talent, it should be possible for someone out there to have talent on par with him too.","The birth of his little sister verified his conjecture. Chu Feng’s appearance further reinforced it.","The world was too big for them to fully explore, so who could say for sure that there wouldn’t be more monstrously talented prodigies around?","“Young master Shaoyu, Miss Yu’er, you must be formidable cultivators considering you’re from the Immortal Sea Fish Clan, but I haven’t had a chance to witness your prowess. Could you give me a glimpse of your cultivation?” Zhan Moli asked.","The elder also looked curious. He wanted to know how strong these two from the Immortal Sea Fish Clan were.","Zhan Moli and Zhan Mudan were the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s strongest juniors, praised as prodigies who would usher in an era of greatness for their clan. Who could have thought that they would be outshone by Chu Feng?","But even if they couldn’t outmatch Chu Feng, it would be a consolation if they could at least outmatch these two.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan was one of the greatest powers in the world of cultivation, after all.","“It’s our habit to conceal our cultivation. We don’t mean to intentionally conceal it. It’s not a problem if Miss Moli wants to know,” Xianhai Shaoyu said with a smile before revealing his cultivation.","“Young master Shaoyu, you...” Zhan Moli and the elder were flabbergasted.","They would have never thought that Xianhai Shaoyu was at rank two True God level, surpassing even Chu Feng. It turned out that he was a monster too.","“I am only second in my clan.” Xianhai Shaoyu glanced at Little Fishy.","Little Fishy glared at her older brother before telling Zhan Moli, “Don’t listen to his nonsense. I’m at the same cultivation level as him.”","Zhan Moli was at a loss for words.","Little Fishy’s humility made it seem as if reaching rank two True God level as a junior was nothing to make a fuss about, yet Zhan Moli was lauded as a prodigy despite failing to reach True God level as a junior.","Zhan Moli couldn’t help but think she wasn’t qualified to be a prodigy.","“This... Is the current world of cultivation that terrifying?”","The elder felt his common sense shatter.","It turned out that Chu Feng wasn’t the exception here; none of these three juniors were ordinary.","“Miss Moli, I overheard your conversation, and it sounds like your Ancient Era’s War Clan has lost touch with the world for a long time now. Is your clan currently trapped in here?” Chu Feng asked.","“That’s right. Our founder left the Nine Secret Skills Inheritance Ground and a powerful protective formation for us. Two thousand years ago, a problem occurred with the protective formation, resulting in our clansmen being trapped here. Not only are we unable to leave, but we can’t see what’s happening outside via the formation either.","“You met Elder Li and the others. They were cultivating in the vicinity of our clan back then and were unaware of our existence. They were caught inside our protective formation and ended up getting trapped here too. We later revealed ourselves to them because we needed their help,” Zhan Moli said.","“If it’s a protective formation, shouldn’t it be impossible for outsiders to get in here too?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes, that would usually be the case. But the fact you’re here now shows otherwise, young hero Chu Feng,” Zhan Moli said.","“Does that mean that only your clansmen are trapped here, but outsiders are still able to enter?” Xianhai Shaoyu asked.","“There are people residing in the surrounding area too, but we have never seen any strangers stumbling in here till that Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist appeared. That was why we were vigilant when you appeared. We thought you were in cahoots with that Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","“That being said, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan is our long-time ally, and I don’t believe you would do anything like that. What we’re thinking is that the formation can stop outsiders from entering, but it is still possible to enter under specific circumstances,” Zhan Moli said.","“Do you know what the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist is after?” Chu Feng asked.","“We have tried communicating with him, but he didn’t answer us as if he’s unable to speak,” Zhan Moli said.","“You said he’s a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. Do you know exactly how strong he is?”","“I’m afraid we can’t tell. We only know his spirit power surpasses that of True Dragon World Spiritists.”","“Does your Ancient Era’s War Clan have any enemies?”","“How could a cultivator clan not have any enemies? We have considered that possibility, but no one in particular comes to mind.”","Chu Feng was rendered speechless. The Ancient Era’s War Clan knew nothing at all except that the invader was a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","“Brother Chu Feng, there is more than meets the eye. My gut feeling tells me that Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist is a junior. If so, the chances are that he’s from an Ancient Era’s race. Our encounter with the God Clan taught me that Ancient Era’s races can’t be underestimated, especially since the God Clan might not even be the strongest Ancient Era’s race. We should tread carefully,” Xianhai Shaoyu reminded via voice transmission."]},{"number":6221,"title":"Chapter 6221: Chapter 6219: The Other Party’s Attack","paragraphs":["Chapter 6219: The Attack","“Rest assured, Brother Shaoyu. I know what I’m doing,” Chu Feng replied via voice transmission.","Zhan Moli and the elder led them to a black city wall inscribed with runes that pierced into the sky, sealing off the entire formation realm. It harnessed spirit power, and every single brick of it was incredibly sturdy.","Chu Feng could tell just from the runes that it contained a huge amount of spirit power.","This was the wall that had been protecting the Ancient Era’s War Clan all this while, and it was indeed formidable.","“The Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist still poses a threat to you despite the wall?” Chu Feng asked.","Someone who could breach this wall wouldn’t just be at rank one or rank two Heavenly Dragon.","“Young hero Chu Feng, this is our Ancient Era’s War Clan’s final layer of protection. There is another wall outside, and that’s the one under attack,” Zhan Moli said as she gestured for the elder to open the city wall.","It was peaceful outside the city wall.","Chu Feng and the others advanced further outward, and it didn’t take them long to hear explosions.","After traveling a little more, they found their path blocked again, this time by a copper wall. There was a light flowing through the wall, an indication that it was reinforced by spirit power.","Yet, it was still shaking nonstop due to the explosions outside.","There was a round cavity in every section of the wall, and it was filled with the copper spheres Chu Feng had forged earlier. These copper spheres were supplying spirit power to the wall.","But as far as Chu Feng could see, almost a hundred of the copper spheres had started to crack, and these cracked copper spheres released far less spirit power than the intact ones.","What was even more terrifying was the presence of empty cavities in the wall. They indicated that either the formation was incomplete in the first place, or that the copper spheres that were previously slotted in there had shattered.","The copper wall’s defensive prowess should have been formidable, but it was greatly discounted now due to the missing or cracked copper spheres.","Just then, a group of people approached Chu Feng and the others.","Zhan Mudan was leading the group, but she was accompanied by two True God level elders and many other foreign faces. These were the elders stationed here to guard the copper wall.","They must have heard about Chu Feng as they were looking at him with eyes of respect or wariness.","“Young hero Chu Feng, please help us. The copper spheres aren’t emanating spirit power despite having slotted them in,” Zhan Mudan said.","Chu Feng flew up to a section of the wall. He could tell which copper spheres were the ones he had just forged.","He infused his spirit power into them and changed his hand seal. The copper sphere fused into the wall and unleashed a powerful surge of spirit power. It had been activated.","He proceeded to make his way to the other copper spheres and activated them.","This powerful influx of spirit power greatly reinforced the copper wall, so much so that it even reduced the wall’s shaking.","This further verified Chu Feng’s guess.","This copper wall should have been even sturdier than the black city wall, just that its prowess was discounted due to the missing or cracked copper spheres.","“We’re truly grateful to you, young hero Chu Feng.”","The elders walked up to Chu Feng and bowed to him in gratitude.","“There’s no need to thank me. It’s not much,” Chu Feng said.","“Young master Chu Feng, it might not be much to you, but it is immense to us. You don’t know how important this protective formation is to us. If it were to be breached, we would lose much of our territory to the enemy,” Zhan Mudan said.","Her attitude toward Chu Feng had completely changed after learning he was a True Dragon World Spiritist.","“Can I see the situation outside?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course.”","Zhan Mudan took out an ancient copper token, infused her bloodline power into it, and formed a series of hand seals, before finally pointing her finger at the copper wall.","A section of the copper wall turned transparent.","Over ten thousand war chariots were floating in the air, each towering at over ten thousand meters tall. They were all slaughter formations, and they were striking the copper wall with beams of spirit power.","It looked as if a giant’s army was invading the Ancient Era’s War Clan.","“Young master Chu Feng, you are a world spiritist. Can you tell how powerful the enemy is through the formations?” Zhan Mudan asked.","“The formations appear to be from a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist,” Chu Feng replied.","“Rank two Heavenly Dragon? That explains why our ancestor’s protective formation is unable to stop him,” someone exclaimed.","“He amplified each of his slaughter formations with treasures, making them stronger than usual. Where is the world spiritist you mentioned?” Chu Feng asked.","“Did he go into hiding to channel the formations from the shadows?” someone asked.","Chu Feng shook his head. “No one is channeling the formations. The formations are being sustained by the treasures inside them.”","“No one is channeling them?”","The crowd was surprised.","“You have seen the world spiritist, right? How long has he been missing?” Chu Feng asked.","“It has been ten days since we last saw him,” an elder replied.","“Is he attacking any other sections of the wall?”","“No, he has been focusing his attack here from the start.”","“My advice is to be more vigilant. Keep a close eye on every section of the copper wall.”","Chu Feng’s words piqued unease among the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s elders.","“Young friend Chu Feng, what do you mean by that? Did you notice something?” Zhan Mudan asked.","“These formations are formidable even when channeled by treasures, and they would only be more potent when channeled by the enemy world spiritist. On top of that, there is a limit to the energy contained in the treasures. The treasures will only grow weaker over time, and so will the formations. So, there is no reason for the enemy world spiritist not to personally channel the formations,” Chu Feng explained.","“Now that you mentioned it, the slaughter formations were much more powerful before. Is he intentionally drawing our attention here while preparing an attack elsewhere?”","Zhan Moli was the first to grasp what Chu Feng was driving at.","The other Ancient Era’s War Clansmen were horrified to hear that.","“That is likely to be the case,” Chu Feng answered."]},{"number":6222,"title":"Chapter 6222: Chapter 6220: Meeting An Acquaintance","paragraphs":["Chapter 6220: Meeting An Acquaintance","“Young hero Chu Feng, can a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist determine the weakest spot in our clan’s protective formation?” Zhan Mudan asked with an awful complexion.","“It is extremely difficult, but the other party came prepared. I wouldn’t exclude such a possibility,” Chu Feng replied.","“That isn’t good.” Zhan Mudan’s complexion darkened. “Young hero Chu Feng, it takes us significant time to remove the copper spheres from the protective formation. Do you have a way to hasten the process?”","“I can find a faster way to do it, but why do you want to remove the copper spheres? Are you hoping to relocate it to the weaker spots?” Chu Feng asked.","“We moved the copper spheres from other parts of the protective formation here, thinking the intruder would only focus on this spot, so this is the sturdiest part of the protective formation. There are many weaknesses elsewhere for him to exploit.","“There is one particularly weak spot. It is extremely discreet and outsiders typically wouldn’t target it, so we removed almost all the copper spheres in that area. If the other party can see through our formation, that spot is the most likely to be targeted,” Zhan Mudan said.","“Young master Chu Feng, do you think our barrier can hold on if we remove some copper spheres here?” Zhan Moli asked.","The copper wall was shaking earlier, and it only stabilized after Chu Feng drew out the copper spheres’ spirit power.","“This copper wall isn’t as brittle as you think. An attack of this level shouldn’t pose a problem,” Chu Feng said.","“Young hero Chu Feng, we’ll be troubling you to retrieve the copper spheres then,” Zhan Mudan said.","“All right.”","Chu Feng constructed a formation with a wave of his hand and swiftly retrieved the copper spheres.","All of a sudden, everything fell silent. The ten thousand slaughter formations simultaneously halted their attack and began relocating elsewhere as if having received an order.","The crowd was baffled.","“What’s going on?”","The Ancient Era’s War Clan’s upper echelons looked at Chu Feng in confusion, hoping to get some answers from him. Before Chu Feng could answer, all their waist tokens lit up.","The formation is breached. Evacuate the clansmen.","These were the words that appeared on their waist tokens.","All the clansmen anxiously flitted to the black city wall. Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu followed them too.","“Looks like you’re right, Chu Feng. The copper wall was breached elsewhere,” Xianhai Shaoyu whispered.","All of a sudden, they sensed quakes coming from the black city wall.","“Has the black city wall been breached too?” Xianhai Shaoyu anxiously turned to Chu Feng and asked.","He was more concerned about their safety than the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s safety.","Chu Feng replied via voice transmission, “Let’s wait and see first.”","They soon arrived at the black wall. As they passed through it, it dawned upon them that the quakes were coming from the sky. Layers of energy descended from the sky like clouds and flowed in the same direction.","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen realized something, and their complexions turned even more awful.","Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu exchanged looks. Despite the sky being obscured by energy, they could tell that the energy was coming from the place where they had come from.","It was where the forbidden ground and the treasure were.","They hadn’t forgotten that they were in an underground formation realm, located beneath the treasure they sought.","“Where is the energy flowing toward?” Xianhai Shaoyu was curious.","“It is likely flowing toward where the protective formation was breached. I’m guessing it has something to do with the intruder,” Chu Feng deduced.","“Big brother, is the intruder after the treasure too?” Little Fishy asked via voice transmission.","Xianhai Shaoyu could hear the voice transmission too, and he replied, “Does that need to be said, my silly little sister? That has to be the case.”","“I’m asking big brother, not you.” Little Fishy glared at Xianhai Shaoyu. She cast a sweeping glance at the nervous-looking Ancient Era’s War Clansmen and continued asking, “The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen can’t possibly not know that the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist is after the treasure. They must be withholding the truth from us.”","“The situation looks complicated. Elder, what do you think?” Chu Feng asked Jie Shanxian, though Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu could hear those words too.","“It’s a mere Ancient Era’s War Clan and a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. You have nothing to fear. I’m here to back you,” Jie Shanxian replied.","Only Chu Feng could hear those words.","“Elder, have you regained your cultivation?” Chu Feng asked.","“Not yet,” Jie Shanxian replied.","“Wouldn’t a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist pose trouble to you?” Chu Feng was confused.","“Why can’t I beat a rank two Heavenly Dragon as a rank one Heavenly Dragon? You aren’t the only prodigy here,” Jie Shanxian asked in displeasure.","Chu Feng was excited to hear that. “That’s wonderful, elder. I have nothing to fear then.”","“Big brother, what did that elder say?” Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy asked via voice transmission.","“The elder says that she’ll back us, and we need not fear the rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist or the Ancient Era’s War Clan,” Chu Feng replied.","Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy breathed a sigh of relief.","The situation was getting messy now, the Ancient Era’s War Clan didn’t seem trustworthy, and their strength was limited. The only one they could fall back on now was Jie Shanxian.","“What’s with that energy?” Chu Feng asked Zhan Moli, feigning ignorance.","“Young master Chu Feng, I’ll fill you in on the details later, but from the current looks of it, the intruder might be more cunning than we have thought. We will likely require your help. Can you follow us to take a look at the situation?” Zhan Moli looked at Chu Feng with pleading eyes.","The other Ancient Era’s War Clansmen did the same too. It was evident from their gazes that they were in a tough spot.","“All right,” Chu Feng agreed.","On the one hand, he wanted to get to the bottom of the situation. On the other hand, he was much more confident now after hearing Jie Shanxian’s words.","Soon, they arrived at the spot along the black wall where the energy was flowing toward.","The energy had gathered in one spot, threatening to tear down the black wall like a raging tsunami. In response, the black wall and the runes inscribed on it glowed brilliantly it emitted waves of spirit power to stop the energy.","Even so, bits of the energy still managed to seep out.","Zhan Mudan took out her waist token and formed a hand seal. A portion of the black wall turned transparent, allowing one to see the scenery outside.","All energy that had seeped out of the black wall flowed in the same direction as if something was absorbing it. Two silhouettes could be vaguely seen amidst the flood of energy.","One was the young world spiritist depicted in Zhan Moli’s painting. The other was a cat smoking a pipe.","“Old Cat?”","The latter was the old cat who plundered Zhan Haichuan’s tombstone, but he looked different. His eyes were blood-red like a ferocious beast, and his aura was chilling.","His cat paws were joined together in a special hand seal as the energy surged into his body."]},{"number":6223,"title":"Chapter 6223: Chapter 6221: Old Cat and Zhan Haichuan","paragraphs":["Chapter 6221: Old Cat and Zhan Haichuan","“That Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist has an accomplice. Why does that cat demon look so familiar?” Xianhai Shaoyu discreetly murmured. Only Chu Feng and Little Fishy could hear his monologue.","“Big brother, do you recognize that cat?” Little Fishy asked.","“I don’t recognize it, but I can’t shake off the feeling I have met it somewhere before.” Xianhai Shaoyu pondered for a long while before suddenly turning to Chu Feng. “Chu Feng, isn’t that the cat you’re acquainted with?”","“Yes, that’s him,” Chu Feng replied.","“Who is it?” Little Fishy was curious.","“The God Bestowment Bamboo Slip.”","Little Fishy widened her eyes in realization before furiously glaring at Old Cat. “So that darned cat demon was the culprit!”","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan had previously bought a God Bestowment Bamboo Slip at a hefty price. By the time it fell into their grasp, it had already gone through many hands.","Curious to know the origin of this God Bestowment Bamboo Slip, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan did some digging and learned that the very first seller was a cat. When Chu Feng heard about it, he told Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy that Old Cat had stolen that God Bestowment Bamboo Slip from him back in the Hundred Refinements Ordinary Realm.","It was for that reason Little Fishy hated Old Cat despite having never met him. Who could have thought they would meet here?","Chu Feng also didn’t expect Old Cat to be here.","The last time he met Old Cat, he interrogated the latter for Xue Ji’s whereabouts. When he learned that Xue Ji had been gifted to an evil world spirit named the Demon Spirit King, he forced Old Cat to head to the Demoncoffin Ordinary Realm with him to find her.","Later, the demon coffin opened.","Old Cat and Chu Feng ended up working together to take advantage of this fortuitous encounter.","There, he met one of Qin Jiu’s world spirits, Taowu. Taowu approached Chu Feng and Old Cat and requested an alliance, concealing his true strength and taking on the alias of Tao Wu.","He also met the Totem Nine Daoist’s Daoist Seventh Dragon, Daoist Eighth Dragon, and Daoist Ninth Dragon there, but they were enemies competing for the treasure then.","Taowu later revealed his true form and strength, and that prompted the Totem Nine Daoists to quickly change their attitudes.","Old Cat feared the Totem Nine Daoists and didn’t want to offend them, so he chose to leave before Taowu revealed his true form.","That was Chu Feng’s last time meeting Old Cat.","He thought they would never meet again, but they ended up crossing paths once more.","Old Cat was now attacking the Ancient Era’s War Clan and devouring the energy emitted from the treasure. He possessed incredible strength.","This surprised Chu Feng. The Old Cat then dared not even cross Daoist Ninth Dragon, so why was he challenging the Ancient Era’s War Clan now?","“It’s that cat! It has returned!”","Many Ancient Era’s War Clansmen exclaimed in horror. Some even took out paintings and unfurled them, revealing Old Cat’s portraits.","“You know that cat?” Chu Feng asked.","“That cat has been after our clan’s treasures for a long time now. Many years ago, it colluded with our clan’s traitor to steal our treasure,” a voice suddenly boomed from afar.","Looking over, a white-haired old man with a powerful disposition was making his way over.","“Lord Father.”","“Paying respect to Lord Clan Chief.”","Everyone present bowed to the old man. This was the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief, the elusive individual whom no one in the Immortal Sea Fish Clan had ever seen before.","“Young friends, there’s no need for the ceremony.” The Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief descended before Chu Feng and humbly said, “My apologies. We should have welcomed you as guests into our Ancient Era’s War Clan, but not only did we fail as hosts, we even got you involved in our mess. I am truly ashamed.”","“Lord Clan Chief, you are too courteous. Our Immortal Sea Fish Clan and your Ancient Era’s War Clan are allies. We will not turn a blind eye if there is anything we can do to help you,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","Before the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen could say a word, Little Fishy glanced at her brother and scoffed, “What have you done to help? It’s my big brother who has been doing things here.”","“Brother Chu Feng and I are closer than real brothers. I take credit for what he has done.”","Even though the crowd was initially rendered speechless by Xianhai Shaoyu’s words, his words did make sense upon careful thought.","“Lord Clan Chief, you mentioned that this old cat has been coveting your clan’s treasure. Can you share more details with us?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course.”","The Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief shared their history with Old Cat.","40,000 years ago, they learned that a man named Zhan Haichuan was searching for them. They realized that Zhan Haichuan was an Ancient Era’s War Clansman too, just that he was from a fallen branch family.","Zhan Haichuan possessed incredible talent, and he was searching for the main family because he wanted to return to them.","After a series of tests on his strength and character, he received the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s acknowledgment and was welcomed back into the main family. He swiftly grew and quickly became a core member of the clan.","The Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief even thought about entrusting his position to Zhan Haichuan. This proposal was firmly rejected by the elders, but he did consider this possibility.","At this juncture, the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief let out a sigh.","“What happened afterward showed how naive I was. He is an outsider. He shares the same blood as us, but he grew up elsewhere. Even after cultivating with us for tens of thousands of years, Zhan Haichuan is still not of the same heart and mind as our clansmen.”","The clan chief’s gaze fell on Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu.","“I’ll be frank with you. There is indeed a treasure where you came from, and it was left there by our founder. However, that treasure has been sealed away and can’t be used by our clansmen anymore. We can only unseal it after some time.","“However, Zhan Haichuan wanted that treasure unsealed as soon as possible. He knows our clansmen won’t agree to it, so he colluded with an outsider to pull it off. His accomplice is none other than that cat.”","The clan chief looked at the old cat devouring the energy outside.","Chu Feng was astonished.","He had only heard that Zhan Haichuan left the Hundred Refinements Ordinary Realm shortly after he made his name, and when Zhan Haichuan later returned, he did it discreetly and built his tombstone in advance, knowing his days were numbered.","Old Cat raided his tomb and stole Zhan Haichuan’s legacy and treasure.","Little did he know that the two of them knew each other right from the start!"]},{"number":6224,"title":"Chapter 6224: Chapter 6222: Old Cat’s Strength","paragraphs":["Chapter 6222: Old Cat’s Strength","The Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief was unaware that Chu Feng was acquainted with Old Cat, so he didn’t know about Chu Feng’s thoughts. He continued the story...","According to him, Old Cat was a special cat demon. It was unknown where Zhan Haichuan found this cat demon, but it possessed special powers. With Zhan Haichuan’s help, Old Cat took in the treasure’s energy and obtained the method to unseal it.","Old Cat’s absorption of the energy was part of the process of unsealing the treasure.","Back then, the Ancient Era’s War Clan stopped Old Cat and Zhan Haichuan with the power of the formation. They thought they had killed Old Cat, though the severely injured Zhan Haichuan managed to make his escape.","Little did they expect Old Cat to be alive and return to haunt them.","“Lord Clan Chief, could the person beside the cat demon be Zhan Haichuan?” one of the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s elders asked.","“It can’t be. Zhan Haichuan is a talented cultivator, but he doesn’t have the same aptitude for world spiritist techniques. There is no way he could have reached such heights,” the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief said.","“Lord Clan Chief, do you know how strong the cat demon was back then?” Chu Feng asked.","Supposing the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief was speaking the truth, it would mean Old Cat had survived the ordeal. Most likely, he had suffered a severe injury that impaired his spirit power, resulting in his subsequent weakness.","“That cat demon has never revealed his spirit power, but he should be around the same level as Zhan Haichuan, late True God level,” the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief replied.","Just then, the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist beside Old Cat took out a copper coin. The copper coin swiftly expanded to over ten meters tall before falling in front of Old Cat.","At the same time, Old Cat changed his hand seals. His eyes turned white, and he opened his mouth and breathed out a stream of energy.","The Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist formed a series of hand seals, and the copper coin began revolving.","The energy channeled through the copper coin unleashed a light beam that gushed toward the black wall.","Boom!","Deafening rumbles echoed clearly through the city as the black wall shook. The intensity of the shaking lessened after a while, but it didn’t cease entirely. It resembled the copper wall when it was being sieged earlier.","“That old cat is using the energy he absorbed from the treasure to attack the black wall?” Eggy asked.","“Yes. That formation is also a special one.”","The copper coin formation that the energy passed through played an important role in the conversion of energy too. For that reason, Chu Feng was more focused on the copper coin.","The copper coin itself was an Ancient Era’s treasure, but the formation was even more amazing. Chu Feng couldn’t see through it even with his current observation prowess.","“Lord Father.”","“Lord Clan Chief.”","Zhan Mudan, Zhan Moli, and the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen looked at their clan chief with worried eyes. This black wall was their final layer of protection. If it collapsed too, they would have to directly confront their enemies.","“All Ancient Era’s War Clansmen, follow me to subdue our enemies!”","The clan chief whipped out of a token and relayed his instructions through it. Then, he rose to the sky and headed up to the black wall. He formed a hand seal, and the sky shook.","Chu Feng could sense that the clan chief was at rank eight True God level.","Xianhai Shaoyu was right. The Ancient Era’s War Clan had no Heavenly God level cultivator.","Energy visibly manifested in their surroundings and surged inside the clan chief. Golden runes appeared on the clan chief’s body and the space around him. These golden runes were infused with the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s bloodline, which bestowed them with a dominating nature.","The clan chief’s disposition changed. He felt like a war god towering over the masses.","In terms of auras, he felt even stronger than the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist and Old Cat outside, as if he could easily crush them with his fingers.","At the same time, the clan chief’s cultivation swiftly rose to rank nine True God level. Moments later, he overcame his bottleneck and reached rank one Heavenly God level.","His white hair turned black once more, and half of his facial wrinkles vanished. He transformed from an old man to a middle-aged man.","His cultivation further advanced to rank two Heavenly God level, but that seemed to be the limit. The energy had stopped manifesting.","The clan chief took out a token and grasped it tightly between his palms. He thrust the token forward, and a light pillar gushed forth. The light pillar fused into the black wall. increasing the energy in it.","The other Ancient Era’s War Clansmen took out identical tokens and released light pillars too to reinforce the black wall’s defensive prowess.","“Lord Father.”","More Ancient Era’s War Clansmen arrived in groups. They must have rushed here to reinforce the black wall after receiving the clan chief’s instructions. The leaders of these groups called the clan chief ‘father’ and ‘grandfather’.","A handful of those who called the clan chief ‘grandfather’ looked aged.","The clan chief had many offspring, and Zhan Moli and Zhan Mudan were his younger daughters. It wasn’t too surprising to Chu Feng and the others as it was already revealed that the incumbent clan chief was already the clan chief back when Zhan Haichuan first came here.","The clan chief had to be much older than Zhan Haichuan. Given his age, it wasn’t surprising for him to have many offspring.","In the blink of an eye, tens of millions of Ancient Era’s War Clansmen were already gathered around the black wall. All of them were fusing energy into the black wall via their tokens. It was an incredible sight.","The black wall became much stabler under their efforts. It was no longer on the verge of collapse.","“Looks like the Ancient Era’s War Clan has a solid foundation,” Xianhai Shaoyu remarked as he eyed the clan chief.","He was more impressed by the clan chief’s prowess than their clan’s unity. Even though all the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen were doing their best to reinforce the black wall, the only one who was making a difference was the clan chief.","Boom!","Suddenly, there was a loud explosion.","The black wall shook intensely as thick smoke puffed from it. Taking a closer look, countless cracks had appeared on the wall, and the smoke was the dust blowing out from the cracks.","It was Old Cat’s doing.","His copper coin formation transformed once more, and the energy he released became even stronger. The black wall that had just stabilized was on the verge of collapse once more.","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen panicked. Without the city wall, they stood no chance against the cat demon.","“Is that cat that strong?” Xianhai Shaoyu discreetly asked Chu Feng.","The energy released by Old Cat must have exceeded rank two Heavenly God, reaching rank three Heavenly God or even beyond. Otherwise, it couldn’t have shaken the black wall."]},{"number":6225,"title":"Chapter 6225: Chapter 6223: Lord Zhenlong, Ancient Era’s Treasure","paragraphs":["Chapter 6223: Lord Zhenlong, Ancient Era’s Treasure","Shoosh!","With a wave of his hand, the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief delivered three tokens before Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu. “Young friends, I’m embarrassed to ask this of you, but can you lend us a helping hand?”","It was a request coming directly from the clan chief; it wouldn’t be good for Chu Feng and the others to turn him down. Thus, they took the tokens.","With their talent, they had already figured out how to use the tokens by the time they lay their hands on them. They were supposed to channel it with their bloodline power.","This was a bloodline formation infused with spirit power, so Chu Feng’s world spiritist bloodline was the ideal medium to channel it.","Their participation greatly strengthened the formation.","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen sensed the sudden addition of three powerful, foreign bloodlines in the formation and reflexively turned to Chu Feng and the others.","However, Chu Feng paid no heed to the attention on him.","Old Cat was a cunning, selfish individual, but Chu Feng had been through a fair bit with him. Naturally, he wouldn’t just listen to the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s one-sided story. He wanted to ask Old Cat what was going on and get to the bottom of this matter.","Through the token, he found a chance to do so.","The token channeled his bloodline power into the black wall, and it happened that Old Cat was also channeling his energy to attack the black wall. This meant that he could use the black wall as a medium of communication between them.","Since the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen were not skilled in world spiritist techniques, Chu Feng was confident of sending voice transmissions to Old Cat without them noticing. Still, he opted for a more convoluted method to be doubly safe, so it took him some time and effort.","“Old Cat, it’s me. I’m Chu Feng. I’m currently in the Ancient Era’s War Clan. What brings you here? What grudges do you have with the Ancient Era’s War Clan?”","Chu Feng finally succeeded in sending a voice transmission to Old Cat, but there was no response. It was as if Old Cat had been stripped of his thoughts and feelings, rendering him unable to answer.","So, Chu Feng assessed Old Cat via the formation.","Old Cat was overflowing with killing intent; he was not his usual self. His body was still insignificantly small, but he gave off a terrifying aura.","“Is this not the Old Cat I know? But that’s the smoking pipe he usually carries,” Chu Feng murmured.","The other party looked exactly like Old Cat, but the feeling he gave off was different from the Old Cat he knew.","Old Cat felt like a scheming scum, whereas the cat demon before him felt like an exceedingly dangerous feral beast.","“Young friend Chu Feng?”","Chu Feng suddenly heard a youth’s voice. It was from outside the black wall. Taken aback, he quickly turned his gaze from Old Cat to the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","“You are?” Chu Feng asked.","It sounded like the other party recognized him.","“Have you already forgotten about me?” the voice echoed once more, but this time, it was a familiar old man’s voice rather than a youth’s.","Chu Feng widened his eyes. It finally dawned on him why that Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist had looked so familiar to him. He replied probingly, “Lord Zhenlong?”","Lord Zhenlong used to be the Totem Dragon Clan’s honorary grand elder. That position was later taken over by Bai Yunqing’s master, Taishi Xingzhong, when he left the Totem Dragon Clan due to his advanced age.","This happened a long time ago. Since his retirement, Lord Zhenlong had never appeared in public, so most people assumed he was dead.","Later, Chu Feng stumbled upon Lord Zhenlong’s remnant.","It was there he first met Bai Yunqing, and together with Old Cat, the three of them competed over Lord Zhenlong’s legacy. Chu Feng eventually acquired the clue to Lord Zhenlong’s legacy, and it was while searching for the legacy that he met Yue Ling.","The legacy was of tremendous help to Chu Feng.","His world spiritist techniques and control of spirit power were lagging far behind his peers then, so much so that he was weaker than Bai Yunqing when they first crossed blows.","It was because of Lord Zhenlong’s legacy that his world spiritist techniques and control of spirit power improved by leaps and bounds, reaching an unprecedented height.","The Lord Zhenlong he met back then was just a formation entity, so he assumed that the real Lord Zhenlong was already dead. Who could have thought that he was still alive, not to mention he had become much younger?","“I already knew you were an unpolished gem back then, but your rapid growth astounds me nevertheless. It truly is God’s Era,” the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist remarked.","This further verified he was Lord Zhenlong.","“What’s going on, Lord Zhenlong? How did you end up with Old Cat? Is this Old Cat?” Chu Feng asked.","“The remnant you stumbled upon back then was my hiding spot. I was in closed-door training there in hopes of being born anew. I succeeded, and my cultivation grew by leaps and bounds. The cat demon beside me is indeed Old Cat. He told me about his encounters with you, so I know that you have some ties. However, he is in a peculiar state at the moment and is unable to communicate with you. What about you? How did you get here?” Lord Zhenlong asked.","Chu Feng told Lord Zhenlong about how he ended here. He thought Lord Zhenlong was more credible than the Ancient Era’s War Clan.","“I see. Chu Feng, I presume the Ancient Era’s War Clan painted Old Cat to be the villain, right?” Lord Zhenlong asked with a chuckle.","“Indeed. They told me he colluded with Zhan Haichuan to steal their treasure. Lord Zhenlong, can you tell me why the two of you are attacking the Ancient Era’s War Clan?” Chu Feng asked.","“Since you came here for the treasure, we should start by talking about the treasure. The Ancient Era’s War Clan isn’t an Ancient Era’s race. They are from the present era. They name themselves the Ancient Era’s War Clan because they obtained an Ancient Era’s treasure that allows them to cultivate much faster than other cultivators.","“The Ancient Era’s War Clan might look weak now, but they were one of the powers who wielded the potential to dominate the world of cultivation back then. Do you know why there isn’t much news about them despite their overwhelming strength?","“That’s because their clansmen spent most of their time in closed-door training all this while. When their founder thought they were strong enough to dominate the world of cultivation, he led their elites out to the strongest galaxy then, the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, hoping to make a name for themselves right away.","“Yet, when they arrived at the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, before they could challenge any of its major powers, they stumbled upon a little-known, mysterious sect. Their founder thought they could start by sinking their blade into this sect, but they were utterly decimated by that sect.","“The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen lost their faith and scattered all over the universe. Their founder went back into closed-door training, and his descendants thought that they would exact vengeance on the Ancestral Martial Galaxy once he returned.","“When their founder finally broke out of his closed-door training, he constructed this protective formation and led his clan’s elites into the Ninth Galaxy. There were rumors within their clan that their founder benefited greatly from the treasure, and he received an epiphany about the Ninth Galaxy.","“No matter the reason, if one thing can be certain, the Ancient Era’s War Clan reached their current heights thanks to that Ancient Era’s treasure. Even the bloodline they are so proud of originated from it. And that treasure belongs to Old Cat,” Lord Zhenlong said."]},{"number":6226,"title":"Chapter 6226: Chapter 6224: Old Cat is the Treasure?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6224: Old Cat is the Treasure?","“Old Cat’s? Old Cat is from the Ancient Era?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes,” Lord Zhenlong replied.","“But why can’t I see it?” Chu Feng looked at Old Cat once more, but he couldn’t sense any Ancient Era’s aura from the latter.","“What you see isn’t Old Cat’s main body. That is just his avatar; his main body is the treasure,” Lord Zhenlong replied.","“Old Cat is the treasure?” Chu Feng was even more surprised.","“That’s right,” Lord Zhenlong replied.","Wu!","Just then, Old Cat halted his attack. He let out a deep groan, and his killing intent began to recede. His eyes brimmed with indignation as he collapsed to the ground.","It happened so quickly that even the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen were taken aback, but it showed that Old Cat was shouldering a great burden from absorbing the treasure’s energy to attack them, and he was reaching his limit.","“Chu Feng, I’ll leave you with a formation. You can come out through it. Come out and meet me at this location, and I’ll tell you the truth,” Lord Zhenlong said via voice transmission as he took out a copper sword, fused a formation in it, and passed it through the copper coin formation.","The copper sword disintegrated as it transformed into a green pillar of light and struck the black wall, causing it to shake once more.","The Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief harrumphed. “A mere rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist dares to act so arrogantly? You must think our Ancient Era’s War Clan has fallen from grace!”","He channeled his bloodline power into the black wall via his token.","This time, the other clansmen didn’t need to do a thing. Just the clan chief’s prowess was enough to stabilize the shaking wall.","Cheers broke out within the Ancient Era’s War Clan.","Without Old Cat, not even a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist could pose a threat to them. Naturally, they were excited to have survived this ordeal.","“Why didn’t he use that earlier?” Xianhai Shaoyu was confused.","He couldn’t understand why the clan chief allowed the copper wall to collapse when he could have stopped the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist with this power. There was no reason to wait till the enemy reached the black wall before making a move.","“My silly brother, that skill probably has an area restriction. He couldn’t use it because the copper wall was too far away.” Little Fishy looked at Xianhai Shaoyu in disdain.","“Really?” Xianhai Shaoyu looked at Chu Feng. He was more inclined to trust the latter’s judgment.","“There’s no other reason to explain it,” Chu Feng replied via voice transmission.","“That sounds right. Ey, looks like I am getting dumb.” Xianhai Shaoyu nodded. He also thought Little Fishy’s deduction made sense.","The cheers grew louder as Lord Zhenlong grabbed the unconscious Old Cat and retreated.","Chu Feng could tell that Lord Zhenlong’s earlier attack was formidable even though it was quickly suppressed. He was attempting to create an opening in the black wall, and this opening could only be exploited from the inside.","Chu Feng could use the opening to modify the black wall’s formation and slip out.","However, Lord Zhenlong and Old Cat would also be able to enter the black wall using the opening, rendering the black wall useless.","Even though Lord Zhenlong had once helped him, Chu Feng was not inclined to undermine the Ancient Era’s War Clan just like that. Old Cat’s earlier killing intent was so overwhelming that he might go on a massacre if he slipped in.","“Chu Feng, who do you think is more credible?” Eggy asked.","“What does Milady Queen think?” Chu Feng returned the question.","“You speak first.”","“Old Cat is unreliable, and I don’t know Lord Zhenlong well either, but I find Lord Zhenlong’s words more credible. What do you think, Eggy?”","“I concur. That Zhenlong old man looks more trustworthy. I don’t think the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief is a good person.”","“What makes you say so?”","“I noticed that the people leading the reinforcement earlier are all the descendants of the clan chief. I initially thought the True God level cultivators were subservient to Zhan Mudan and Zhan Moli because the clan chief made special arrangements for them because of their young age, but that seemed to be the norm instead of the exception.","“The clan chief’s offspring are monopolizing all the important posts. I find it offputting how power-hungry the clan chief is. He may be qualified to be the clan chief, being a rank eight True God level cultivator, but he has many offspring occupying important positions. How good could someone who practices such blatant nepotism be?” Eggy said.","“Your words make sense.” Chu Feng nodded.","“But that doesn’t mean Old Cat and Lord Zhenlong are trustworthy. Old Cat can’t be trusted. Lord Zhenlong might have passed down his legacy to you, but birds of the same feather flock together. Now that he’s with Old Cat, who knows if they are the same type of people? Chu Feng, keep your guard up and don’t be exploited by them. Our goal is not to side with anyone but to obtain the treasure,” Eggy reminded.","“I know,” Chu Feng replied as he glanced at the clan chief.","Even though Old Cat and Lord Zhenlong had halted their attack and left the area, the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen continued to stay vigilant. They had begun repairing the black wall under their clan chief’s instructions.","“Lord Clan Chief, may I offer my help?” Chu Feng stepped forward and offered his service.","“That would be wonderful, young friend Chu Feng.” The clan chief was overjoyed to hear that.","The other Ancient Era’s War Clansmen also welcomed Chu Feng’s help, having witnessed the feats he had achieved thus far. Even though Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy’s bloodline powers were formidable too, they thought that Chu Feng’s help was more valuable.","...","Meanwhile, Lord Zhenlong finally stopped after fleeing a far distance away from the black wall. The sleeping Old Cat in his arms suddenly opened his eyes.","“It is Chu Feng. I didn’t sense wrongly,” Old Cat said as he got to his feet. He was weakened, but not so much that he would pass out. He was pretending to faint earlier. “Lord Zhenlong, do you think Chu Feng would come out?”","“You know him better than me. What do you think?” Lord Zhenlong returned the question.","“That fellow is sharp-witted; I doubt he’ll fall for it so easily. If he refuses to help, we’ll just follow our original plan. This is a rare opportunity. I won’t let it slip through my fingers even if I have to put my life on the line,” Old Cat said.","“What if Chu Feng sides with the Ancient Era’s War Clan?” Lord Zhenlong said.","A vicious glint flashed across Old Cat’s eyes. “Then we’ll kill him too.”"]},{"number":6227,"title":"Chapter 6227: Chapter 6225: The Most Important Clan-protection Treasure","paragraphs":["Chapter 6225: The Most Important Clan-protection Treasure","Chu Feng had requested to repair the black wall formation to alter the formation using the opening left by Lord Zhenlong. The black wall was now fully repaired, and he also did what he wanted to do.","All he had to do was to form a hand seal and the opening in the formation would expand, allowing him to escape through the black wall.","Of course, he didn’t do this to let Old Cat and Lord Zhenlong in. Rather, it was a backup plan in case things went awry.","The Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief could reach rank two Heavenly God level using his ancestor’s bloodline formation, but that might not be his limit. He could have more tricks up his sleeves too. It would be wise for Chu Feng to prepare an escape route.","“Young friend Chu Feng, your world spiritist bloodline is formidable,” the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief exclaimed with gleaming eyes.","Chu Feng initially thought the clan chief was excited because he helped them fix the black wall, and that made him feel embarrassed as he had secretly expanded the opening in it. It was only when the clan chief spoke up once more that he realized he was mistaken.","“Young friend Chu Feng, that cat demon shouldn’t have been able to breach even the copper wall, let alone the black wall, but our founder’s protective formation has been weakening each year and is nowhere as strong as it used to be. I don’t know if we can stop the cat demon the next time he attacks.”","The clan chief took out countless shattered tokens with a wave of his sleeves—these were life tokens. Chu Feng could tell that these life tokens had shattered very recently.","“These are the clansmen whom we failed to evacuate in time when the cat demon breached the copper wall. The cat demon is vicious. It still remembers the grudge from back then. If the black wall crumbles too... Ha...”","The clan chief sighed before he could finish his words. The other clansmen also looked distressed. They knew the calamity that would befall them if the cat demon breached the black wall.","“Our clan knows of a way to deal with the cat demon. We were only able to curb it back then because we found its weakness and forged a treasure to subjugate it. But times have changed. We are only a step away from completing that treasure. We need the help of a world spiritist with either formidable spirit power or a world spiritist bloodline, but we have been trapped here. Young friend Chu Feng, you have an incredible bloodline. Can you help us complete the treasure?” the clan chief raised his request.","“I am not confident of pulling it off, but I’m willing to give it a try,” Chu Feng accepted the request.","The clan chief was overjoyed. He brought Chu Feng, Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, and the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s experts to one of their forbidden grounds.","The forbidden ground harnessed incredible spirit power and contained many extraordinary materials. The spirit power had fused with most of the materials, and the treasure was only one step away from completion.","Chu Feng knew right away the clan chief wasn’t lying.","The formation contained an aura identical to Old Cat’s. If it was completed, it could curb and even kill Old Cat.","Shoosh!","The clan chief retrieved his Cosmos Sack from his waist, and countless bundles of light scattered from it. These bundles of light were treasures, including God Armaments, invaluable materials, and boxes containing rare treasures.","Even Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu, despite their wealthy background, were excited.","Chu Feng surveyed the surroundings before his gaze fell on an item. It was a lump of black metal spanning around 30 centimeters. It had an odd shape, resembling a fragment that had fallen off some kind of item.","It was placed inside an exquisite golden box. Just the box itself made it clear that the item inside was invaluable.","“Young friend Chu Feng, these are our Ancient Era’s War Clan’s clan-protection treasures. You may take anything you desire if you vanquish that cat demon,” the clan chief said.","“Elder, what is that?” Chu Feng pointed to the black metal lump.","“Young friend Chu Feng, you have a good eye,” the clan chief complimented. “This metal lump is from the Immemorial Era. I don’t know its name, but it has unmatched sturdiness. Our founder once requested the strongest world spiritist in his era to forge a God Armament out of the metal lump, but the latter couldn’t melt it despite having exhausted all his means. Even though we are unable to draw out the metal lump’s true prowess, its sturdiness speaks for itself. It is our most valuable clan-protection treasure.”","Chu Feng was moved. That was also why he was fixated on the black metal lump of all things. He currently needed an incomparably sturdy material, and this black metal lump might meet that criterion.","“Young friend Chu Feng, I can give it to you if you’re interested in it. As long as you aid us in completing the treasure and subjugating the cat demon, we will give you any three of our clan’s nine strongest secret skills.”","The clan chief waved his sleeves, and nine weapons appeared out of thin air. These secret skills were on a different level from what Zhan Moli had previously displayed. They could serve Chu Feng well if he could properly grasp them.","“Lord Clan Chief!”","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen looked troubled. These were the nine strongest secret skills in their clan; it wouldn’t be a stretch to say they were their clan’s foundation. Their legacy would be incomplete if they gave three to Chu Feng.","“Our clan is on the brink of destruction. Young friend Chu Feng will be our savior if he completes the treasure. There is nothing we can’t give him.”","The clan chief was resolute about it, and his words made sense too. The clansmen fell silent. Everyone turned to look at Chu Feng.","“All right, I’ll give it a try.”","Chu Feng began channeling his spirit power into the formation. He quickly confirmed that his bloodline power was indeed able to complete the treasure, but he was aiming to do more than just that.","Up to this point, he still couldn’t tell for sure who was lying to him, so he wanted to prepare as many means as possible.","“Elder, can you help me? I wish to exert complete dominance over the treasure,” Chu Feng discreetly asked Jie Shanxian.","“I didn’t expect you to be this cunning.”","Jie Shanxian was surprised. She thought Chu Feng was earnestly helping the Ancient Era’s War Clan; she hadn’t expected him to leave a hand here. That being said, she still accepted his request.","“It is a wise move, so I’ll help you this once.”"]},{"number":6228,"title":"Chapter 6228: Chapter 6226: He Knows the Cat Demon","paragraphs":["Chapter 6226: He Knows the Cat Demon","Given Jie Shanxian’s ability and Chu Feng’s assistance, it was easy enough for them to alter the formation’s structure without any amateur world spiritists noticing.","Everything went smoothly; the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen didn’t notice anything amiss despite watching the process from the start to the end. They would have never known that they were no longer calling the shots by the time the copper cauldron emerged from the formation.","“Young friend Chu Feng, did you succeed?” The Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief looked at the copper cauldron with gleaming eyes.","“It should be. Give it a try, Lord Clan Chief.” Chu Feng passed the meter-tall copper cauldron over to the clan chief with a wave of his hand.","Without any hesitation, the clan chief formed a hand seal and infused his bloodline power into the copper cauldron, causing it to glow. A powerful aura emanated from the cauldron.","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen weren’t worried as the aura didn’t hurt them. The copper cauldron’s energy served only to neutralize Old Cat’s powers.","“It worked!”","“There is hope for our clan!”","“It will be the end of the cat demon if he dares return!”","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen were overjoyed, but the clan chief pointed out with a frown, “Young friend Chu Feng, the forging seems to be a failure.”","“A failure? May I give it a try?” Chu Feng asked.","“Go ahead.”","The clan chief carefully pushed the copper cauldron over to Chu Feng, a sign of how much he cherished it.","Chu Feng formed a hand seal and fused his bloodline power into it. The copper cauldron glowed so brightly in response that the crowd was forced to squint their eyes. On top of that, runes emerged from the copper cauldron and swiftly revolved around it.","The cauldron expanded to over a hundred meters tall and unleashed a powerful suction force that devoured everything in the vicinity, except for cultivators and the treasures they protected.","And this wasn’t the copper cauldron’s full prowess.","Soon, the light surrounding the copper cauldron scattered, and the revolving glowing runes seeped back into the cauldron. At the same time, the copper cauldron buzzed aloud and grew even larger instead of contracting back to its original size.","In the end, the cauldron shot out a green light beam covered in runes. This light beam was formidable, on par with the phenomenon induced when a prodigy made a breakthrough in their cultivation.","Fortunately, the green light beam didn’t hurt anyone or damage the surroundings.","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen were overjoyed.","“It worked!”","It was evident the treasure forging was a success, for the earlier green light beam was an energy that countered Old Cat’s.","Chu Feng changed his hand seal, and the copper cauldron reverted to its original size.","“Lord Clan Chief, why don’t you give it another try?” Chu Feng asked.","Eggy burst into laughter. “Hahaha! Chu Feng, you’re terrible! You could have told the old man straight you’re the only one who can use the cauldron. You’re shattering his hope time and time again!”","“Milady Queen, it’s best if he discovers it himself. Besides, I doubt he’ll believe me even if I tell him that. He’d still try it anyway,” Chu Feng replied.","The clan chief took the copper cauldron. He activated his clan-protection formation to raise his cultivation to rank two Heavenly God level once more before unleashing his bloodline power, but it was still to no avail.","“Young friend Chu Feng, your bloodline power is so strong that it may have altered the treasure’s core. You are the only one who can activate this treasure now,” the clan chief said.","“Only I can activate it? But I didn’t sense any issue when I was forging the treasure,” Chu Feng exclaimed in a fluster, sounding incredibly innocent.","“It’s normal for mutations to occur when a powerful bloodline is involved. Young friend Chu Feng, we’ll have to trouble you to channel the treasure against the cat demon when he invades again,” the clan chief said.","Chu Feng frowned. “That may be difficult.”","The clan chief was stunned. Fearing that Chu Feng didn’t want to help them, he quickly added, “Young friend Chu Feng, this matter concerns the survival of our clan. You may take more treasures if you wish.”","Chu Feng shook his head. “It’s not about the treasures... Haaa, I think I should come clean now. I am acquainted with that Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.”","“What? You’re acquainted with that Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist?”","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen were shocked. Many eyed him in wariness. Some even secretly reached for their weapons.","The clan chief, however, remained calm. He first glanced at his clansmen, a gesture for them to calm down first, before turning to address Chu Feng, “Young friend, you recognize the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist?”","“I once entered a remnant and benefited greatly from it, and that Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist is the remnant’s master. I don’t know his identity, but I am indebted to him. Furthermore, he felt like a righteous person based on my previous encounter with him. Why don’t I go out and talk with him? I’ll tell him the truth about the cat demon and ask him to hand him over,” Chu Feng proposed.","Since the Ancient Era’s War Clan needed him, he thought he could use this opportunity to have them open the city gates so that he could head out, meet Lord Zhenlong and Old Cat, and get to the bottom of the story via them.","Old Cat shouldn’t pose a threat as long as he wasn’t close enough to absorb the treasure’s energy. As for Lord Zhenlong, while he was a formidable world spiritist, Chu Feng had nothing to fear with Jie Shanxian backing him.","Chu Feng should be able to make a safe retreat even if they were lying. Even if they attacked the black wall again, Chu Feng would have nothing to fear now that he had the copper cauldron to subdue Old Cat.","“Young friend Chu Feng, you don’t have to take such a huge risk. Since you are indebted to the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, all you have to do is subjugate the cat demon. We won’t hurt the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. What do you think?” the clan chief proposed.","“Young master Chu Feng, my father is right. You are doing this out of goodwill, but the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist might use this opportunity to hurt you. It’s too dangerous!” Zhan Moli added.","“I know this matter is of grave importance, but I owe that elder too much. I trust his character. He must have fallen for that cat demon’s deception,” Chu Feng said.","“Young friend Chu Feng, you’re still young. You may know a person’s face, but you will never know their heart. Humans can do terrible things for their interests.","“How about this? It’s only a matter of time before they return. I’ll open the city gate so that you can have a talk then. That way, I can use our founder’s formation to protect you if the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist insists on siding with that cat demon, but you must harden your heart and vanquish the cat demon. I’ll also slay the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist,” the clan chief said,","“All right.” Chu Feng accepted the offer.","His goal was to get to the bottom of the matter, so it would be best to confront them in person. Thus, he added, “To be honest, I am acquainted with that cat demon too.”","“Ah?”","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen put up their guard once more."]},{"number":6229,"title":"Chapter 6229: Chapter 6227: Ancient Era’s Saint Beast","paragraphs":["“You’re acquainted with that cat demon?”","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen looked at Chu Feng with eyes brimming with hostility. Even their clan chief couldn’t maintain his previous composure. He stowed away the copper cauldron and pulled his clansmen behind him.","“Calm down, Lord Clan Chief and elders. I know a cat demon who looks identical to the one I saw today, but we aren’t close. He even scammed me once. On top of that, the cat demon I know is far weaker and has a different disposition from the one who attacked the Ancient Era’s War Clan today. So, I can’t be sure if they are the same cat demon. I’m thinking that they might just be from the same clan.","“In any case, please put your hearts at ease. I’ll help you vanquish the cat demon regardless of whether it is the one I know or not,” Chu Feng explained.","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen breathed a sigh of relief, though they continued to keep their guards up against Chu Feng. What he had just divulged was too shocking, after all.","“Young friend Chu Feng, that cat demon is cunning. You mustn’t pity him. Any opening you reveal may spell the end of not just our Ancient Era’s War Clan but the three of you too. If he ever escapes from here, he will become a disaster for the world of cultivation!” the clan chief reminded.","“Don’t worry, Lord Clan Chief. I’m only seeking to persuade the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. I won’t show mercy to that cat demon,” Chu Feng promised.","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen remained fully vigilant in the time to come, knowing that the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist and the cat demon would soon return. No one left to cultivate or to rest.","The following day, Old Cat and Lord Zhenlong appeared in the same place they attacked.","By the time Chu Feng and the others rushed to the scene, Old Cat had already begun absorbing the treasure’s energy. It could be because Old Cat figured out a more efficient method, but he was absorbing the energy much faster than yesterday.","“Young friend Chu Feng, must you have a talk with the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist?” the clan chief asked.","“Let me give it a try,” Chu Feng said.","“All right.”","The clan chief took out his token and turned the section of the black wall before them transparent. This time, those outside could peer in too. They could now talk freely and exchange voice transmissions.","Chu Feng sent a voice transmission to Old Cat and Lord Zhenlong right away to inform them about the situation. He told them to pretend that it was their first time seeing him here.","Lord Zhenlong’s acting was surprisingly good. His shock looked genuine as he exclaimed, “Young friend Chu Feng, why are you here?”","“Elder, it’s a long story. I have some ties with the Ancient Era’s War Clan. May I know why you have joined hands with the cat demon to attack them?” Chu Feng asked.","Old Cat suddenly stopped absorbing the treasure’s energy and berated, “Chu Feng, who are you insulting? Your head must be getting big for you to dare call me a demon!”","“It is you, cat demon! So what if I insult you? Have you forgotten how you scammed me? Hmph, you hid your strength well. I didn’t expect you to be this formidable,” Chu Feng sneered.","“I could say the same for you too. I didn’t expect you to be Jie Ranqing’s son. And those two behind you are the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s young master and young miss, right? The rumors that you can close with them are indeed true. But Chu Feng, you won’t be able to save anyone here. Surrender, and I’ll consider sparing your lives. Otherwise, I’ll kill you no matter who your backing is!” Old Cat sneered domineeringly.","His killing intent was so intense that it didn’t seem to be a lie.","This lent credence to Chu Feng’s previous claim that he was not on good terms with Old Cat, and the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen finally loosened some of their tension.","“Young friend Chu Feng, are you here to help the Ancient Era’s War Clan? You mustn’t be fooled by them. This old cat might have done you injustice in the past, but he is here to reclaim his possession. The Ancient Era’s War Clan has done many evil deeds and deserves to die a thousand times over!” Lord Zhenlong said.","Those words provoked infuriated responses from the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen. Their words were as awful as one could imagine. In gist, they were criticizing Lord Zhenlong and Old Cat for besmirching them even though they were the invaders.","Amidst the furious exchange of words, Old Cat slowly fell silent as his killing intent flared.","Lord Zhenlong impassively spoke aloud, “In the early years of the present era, the War Clansmen stumbled upon a severely wounded Ancient Era’s saint beast. That saint beast was restrained by a treasure and was unable to move, but he still gave cultivation pointers to them. To accelerate their growth, he gave them his flesh and blood to consume and taught them how to assimilate them. He hoped that the War Clan could one day grow strong enough to free him.","“The War Clan grew swiftly under the saint beast’s help, but instead of finding ways to free the saint beast, they severed more of the saint beast’s flesh and blood without his permission. When they learned that the saint beast couldn’t stop them, they feasted on his flesh, gulped his blood, tore his skin, and ripped his tendons. They stole his everything and used them as cultivation resources. They refused to spare the saint beast even after it breathed its last. They researched ways to squeeze whatever they could from his remaining carcass.”","At this point, Lord Zhenlong turned to Old Cat and declared, “Old Cat is that Ancient Era’s saint beast.”"]},{"number":6230,"title":"Chapter 6230: Chapter 6228: The Wall Collapses","paragraphs":["Chapter 6228: The Wall Collapses","“Utter nonsense! You have no shame to be able to utter such falsehoods!”","“Lord Clan Chief, let’s not hesitate anymore. Let’s eradicate those invaders!”","Many Ancient Era’s War Clansmen couldn’t withstand the insult anymore and turned to implore their clan chief. The clan chief, however, was staring at Chu Feng, so the others turned to look at Chu Feng too.","The only one who could vanquish Old Cat was Chu Feng.","In contrast to the agitated Ancient Era’s War Clansmen, Lord Zhenlong calmly added, “Think about it, Chu Feng. How do you think Old Cat was able to absorb the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s treasure? Isn’t it clear who the true owner of that treasure is?”","The Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief sneered, “What a joke. That thieving cat demon coveted our founder’s treasure, so he colluded with our traitor to obtain the treasure’s power. Yet, you have the cheek to claim that you are the treasure itself now and sully our good name. How can anyone be this shameless?”","Those words were spoken through gritted teeth as his body trembled. His rage was palpable.","“Traitor? Are you talking about Zhan Haichuan? He is indeed a traitor, but the one he betrayed isn’t you but me! I would have long eradicated your Ancient Era’s War Clan had that weak-willed fool not turned his back on me in that critical moment! But it doesn’t matter anymore. You won’t have a chance. Zhan Fengdan, I’ll first massacre your descendants before settling the scores with you in the Ninth Galaxy!”","The treasure’s energy began furiously surging toward Old Cat like a tsunami. It was such a powerful surge of energy that even the black wall started to shake. At this rate, the black wall would collapse even before Old Cat launched his attack.","The bulk of the energy was blocked by the black wall, but a significant amount of it still leaked out. At this rate, Old Cat would become ridiculously powerful.","“Young friend Chu Feng, that cat demon is spouting rubbish! I’ll take you to the treasure right now so that you can see its true form. It is truly a treasure and not some Ancient Era’s saint beast,” the clan chief said as he grabbed Chu Feng’s arm to drag him away.","Boom!","A massive cloud of dust suddenly puffed into the air. The black wall had collapsed!","A golden light harnessing the power of a rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist gushed in from outside the wall. It was from Lord Zhenlong!","Without any hesitation, the clan chief activated his clan-protection formation and raised his cultivation to rank two Heavenly God level before stepping forth to deal with Lord Zhenlong’s attack.","But Lord Zhenlong’s attack was not just an ordinary surge of spirit power; it contained a slaughter formation.","The clash raised such a powerful shockwave that no one dared to approach them. It was hard to tell who came up above in that clash.","Lord Zhenlong proceeded to manifest the copper coin formation in front of Old Cat with a wave of his sleeves.","Old Cat opened his mouth and spewed the treasure’s energy through the copper coin formation at the clan chief.","The clan chief hurriedly whipped out his God Armament and activated the Nine Secret Skills.","Nine pillars of light gushed into the sky. These were the humongous weapons manifested from the Nine Secret Skills. They flew forth and formed a wall of weapons to block Old Cat’s attack.","Yet, Old Cat’s energy blast easily shattered the Nine Secret Skills.","The sheer shockwave knocked the clan chief back to Chu Feng’s side. He felt like his bones had been all fractured, and he spurted blood. Not even a rank two Heavenly God level cultivator could rival Old Cat.","Enduring the pain, the clan chief tossed the copper cauldron to Chu Feng. With pleading eyes, he shouted, “Young friend Chu Feng, you need to make a move now, or else we will all die!”","By this point, Old Cat and Lord Zhenlong had already passed through the black wall.","Most people realized the disaster was upon them and frantically escaped, but there were also fearless Ancient Era’s War Clansmen who drew their weapons and attacked Old Cat.","However, they suddenly froze up before they could even get close to Old Cat before abruptly exploding right after.","Old Cat didn’t spare those clansmen a glance when he killed them. It was as if he was just trampling on ants along the way. His gaze remained fixated on the sky, where the treasure was.","Now that the black wall had been breached, the energy descending from the sky surged into Old Cat’s body with greater fervor. At this rate, he would become unstoppable. To make things worse, his killing intent was becoming increasingly fearsome.","It was clear to Chu Feng that Old Cat was going to massacre everyone here.","“Chu Feng, things don’t look good. I don’t think the cat demon will spare any of us,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","Little Fishy didn’t say a word, but her eyes looked flustered. Both of them could feel death encroaching on them.","Chu Feng cast aside his hesitation and fused his bloodline power into the copper cauldron, causing it to emanate a blinding light. Then, he hoisted the gigantified cauldron up into the air with him and pointed its opening at Old Cat.","Both Old Cat and Lord Zhenlong sensed something was amiss, so they simultaneously launched their attacks on the copper cauldron and Chu Feng.","Lord Zhenlong had at least held back in his attack, but Old Cat was seeking to decimate Chu Feng together with the copper cauldron.","The clan chief quickly stepped forward to neutralize Lord Zhenlong’s attack. He couldn’t stop Old Cat’s attack, but it dissipated as soon as it came within range of the copper cauldron.","Old Cat was stunned.","A green light beam gushed from the copper cauldron toward Old Cat.","Old Cat tried to dodge, but the green light beam was too fast. It enveloped both Old Cat and Lord Zhenlong.","Lord Zhenlong was unharmed, but Old Cat collapsed to the ground in pain. His body began unraveling as if something was burning his skin to ashes. At this rate, he would be destroyed.","Lord Zhenlong wanted to drag Old Cat to safety, only to find the latter firmly pinned to the ground. He was unable to move the latter no matter what he tried."]},{"number":6231,"title":"Chapter 6231: Chapter 6229: The Treasure’s True Form","paragraphs":["“Stop, Chu Feng! Do you intend to kill Old Cat?” Lord Zhenlong asked Chu Feng.","Chu Feng didn’t say a word, but his determined eyes answered that question. His hands maintained a firm grip on the copper cauldron as he channeled his bloodline power into it. The green light beam restraining Old Cat changed, and Old Cat was sucked into the cauldron.","Unable to stop Chu Feng, Lord Zhenlong could only watch helplessly as Old Cat disappeared into the cauldron. From his viewpoint, he saw Old Cat swiftly disintegrating inside the cauldron.","“You scoundrel, Chu Feng! How dare you help those ingrates? I won’t spare you even as a ghost!” Old Cat’s initial miserable cries turned into furious howls, but soon, his voice weakened till there was no more sound.","Lord Zhenlong shook his head in regret. Knowing no words could change the situation now, he looked at Chu Feng and sighed, “You’re a fool, Chu Feng.”","With that, he took his leave.","Chu Feng descended to the ground as the cauldron reverted to its original size.","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen, including their clan chief, rushed to his side. The clan chief snatched the copper cauldron over and carefully examined it. Other than the remnants of Old Cat’s aura, splatters of blood, and bits of clothes, there was nothing inside it.","The copper cauldron had completely broken down Old Cat.","Upon confirming their victory, the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen exhaled in relief.","“Lord Clan Chief, what do we do about that Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist?” the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen asked.","“We’ll let it go since he is young friend Chu Feng’s acquaintance. We won’t pursue this matter as long as he doesn’t attack us anymore,” the clan chief said as he eyed Chu Feng.","Chu Feng was staring at the copper cauldron in a daze. He looked conflicted, unsure whether he had done the right thing or not.","“Young friend Chu Feng, I sense your dilemma, but there’s nothing to worry about. That cat demon claimed he was our treasure, but the truth will be evident once I show you our treasure. Young friends, come with me.”","The severely wounded clan chief brought Chu Feng, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu toward the treasure, and the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s experts followed suit.","It didn’t take long before they returned to the palace.","The clan chief stopped not far from where Chu Feng and the others landed when they first arrived in this formation realm. He formed a hand seal, and a glowing talisman emerged from his soul.","“A bloodline formation hidden in the soul; it must be a hereditary formation,” Eggy remarked.","The clan chief activated the talisman, and a faint golden light enveloped him. He directed his palm toward the ceiling and roared, “Open!”","A spirit formation gate appeared.","Cu Feng and the others entered the spirit formation gate, where they found themselves in a passageway leading upward. Terrifying energy suffused the passageway. It was the energy that Jie Shanxian struggled to overcome.","However, the golden light emanating from the clan chief protected Chu Feng and the others from the energy’s terror.","“Follow me.”","The clan chief glanced at Chu Feng and the others before flying upward.","The passageway felt like a pathway to heaven, though the illusion was swiftly shattered when Chu Feng and the others reached the end of the path. There, they were met with a huge gate that towered over ten thousand meters.","The gate was locked. The lock was a formation more formidable than the black wall, and it was in perfect condition.","The clan chief conjured a glowing rune and fused it into the lock.","The lock opened.","The rune was the key to the formation. It was likely a means passed down from the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s founder through generations of clan chiefs.","On the other side of the gate was a formation realm.","This formation realm was filled to the brim with that terrifying energy. It was hard to tell how big the realm was because the surroundings were shrouded in a thick fog. This fog must have been produced by a formation as Chu Feng couldn’t see through it with his means.","Still, he spotted a faint light pillar in the fog connecting the ground to the sky. It was a formation passageway. It seemed to be the formation passageway Jie Shanxian opened with her treasure.","The clan chief formed a hand seal, and the fog receded. It didn’t take long before Chu Feng and the others got to see the formation realm in its full glory.","The formation realm was humongous; its scale was comparable to the formation realm where the Ancient Era’s War Clan resided. However, this place didn’t feel suitable for anyone to live in, not just because of the terrifying energy but the surroundings too.","The sky was covered in dark clouds. The ground was withered and cracked. There was no life to be seen. It felt empty and stifling.","In the distance, countless massive mountains rose above the dark clouds, making it impossible to see their full forms. These mountains occupied the bulk of this formation realm.","Chu Feng and the others were taken aback, for they could tell that those mountains were, in fact, bones.","The terrifying energy suffusing the formation realm came from none other than the bones. Now that the fog was no longer around, the energy became stronger than ever. Resentful voices that sounded like they were from vengeful spirits could be vaguely heard from the energy.","It was clear as day that the energy was the manifestation of resentment.","Chu Feng and the others turned to the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief. The latter looked back at them with a smile.","“As you can see, the cat demon was telling the truth. This is his carcass.”"]},{"number":6232,"title":"Chapter 6232: Chapter 6230: The Master Returns","paragraphs":["Chapter 6230: The Master Returns","“The cat demon should have died when our founder was still around, but for some reason, it is still alive and morphed into a cat demon. It fooled Zhan Haichuan into working with him, but fortunately, Zhan Haichuan realized that the cat demon wouldn’t spare anyone in our clan if he got his way.","“He was a fool. He wouldn’t have been able to return to our clan if not for that cat demon’s aid, yet he chose to side with us. In the end, the cat demon died, and there was no way I would spare Zhan Haichuan either. He got away, but I dealt a severe blow to him. I reckon he should be dead by now.","“I didn’t expect that even though the traitor Zhan Haichuan is dead, the cat demon is still alive and more powerful than ever.”","The Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief finally told the truth with a gleeful smirk. The way he shared the story was much more maddening than when Lord Zhenlong did it.","“I didn’t expect your clan to be so despicable, and you don’t feel a morsel of regret for what you have done. How can anyone be so shameless?” Chu Feng asked.","The clan chief was unfazed. He looked at Chu Feng with greedy eyes as if the latter was prey.","“Young friend Chu Feng, that cat demon is indeed pitiful, but our founder has extracted everything of value in him. We, his descendants, didn’t get anything from the cat demon. If that cat demon wants to exact vengeance, he should go after our founder. We feel indignant too.","“Fortunately, you came. You have not just the Ruler’s Bloodline but the legendary Genesis Bloodline too. Your appearance marks a new start for our clan.”","Chu Feng was startled. “You knew who I am? You can see the outside world?”","“Of course. This is the formation realm we inherited from our founder. Do you think we wouldn’t be able to peer outside? We are aware of what’s happening outside. Your reputation as the most talented prodigy in God’s Era is resounding. You conquered even the legendary Genesis Bloodline.”","Those words were from Zhan Moli. Her attitude had also changed, just like her father. Her previous dignified demeanor vanished, and she became yet another venomous-hearted woman like her older sister.","“It was a ploy. You coveted my bloodline,” Chu Feng said.","“Did you think we would have a fallout over an outsider? It’s all my father’s will. I only provoked you so that my younger sister could win your trust and convince you to lower your guard. That way, you would construct that copper cauldron and vanquish that cat demon for us,” Zhan Mudan said.","The Ancient Era’s War Clan’s elders encircled Chu Feng. They knew about this too.","“My father knows we are here. Our Immortal Sea Fish Clan won’t spare you if anything happens to us,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","“Hahaha!”","The clan chief suddenly burst into laughter. Zhan Mudan, Zhan Moli, and the other Ancient Era’s War Clansmen did the same too. They were mocking Xianhai Shaoyu.","“Do you take me for a fool? Your father would be here if he could enter. Besides, our clan is going to ascend through the ranks now that we have Chu Feng. It won’t be long before your Immortal Sea Fish Clan means nothing to us!”","The clan chief then turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Isn’t that so, young friend Chu Feng?”","“Haa...” Chu Feng let out a deep sigh. “I was acquainted with one of the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s branches, which was why I had a high impression of you people. I didn’t expect the main lineage to be filled with scum. No wonder your ancestors left you. Ah, I nearly forgot. You are just the War Clan, not the Ancient Era’s War Clan. It’s far-fetched to claim you are an Ancient Era’s clan when you have merely assimilated the flesh of an Ancient Era’s saint beast.”","Chu Feng’s eyes were filled with disdain.","“Chu Feng, a sharp tongue won’t change your fate. The world of cultivation has always been a place where the strong prey on the weak. Those who preach values are merely courting death. History is always written by the victors.","“Don’t blame me for this. Blame your greed. You came here because you coveted this treasure. Little did you know the treasure is a heap of useless bones that emanated resentment. Rather, your arrival benefited us. This must be heaven’s will. The cat demon had become stronger than ever, and we would have lost if not for you. Yet, you came at this timely moment. Heaven must have sent you here to help our Ancient Era’s War Clan return to its former glory!”","Not wanting to wait anymore, the clan chief reached out and grabbed Chu Feng, but a formidable gush of spirit power shoved him aside.","“You’re underestimating me too much.”","A figure flitted forth and stood in front of Chu Feng. Her body was enveloped in a radiant glow, obscuring her appearance. It was Jie Shanxian!","“You brought a helper? No wonder you’re so fearless.”","The clan chief summoned his Ancient Era’s War Halberd and attacked Jie Shanxian with the might of a rank two Heavenly God level cultivator.","“Hmph!”","Jie Shanxian took out a loop of Buddhist beads and hurled it forth. It unleashed a blast of spirit power sent the clan chief and the others toppling over.","“Hahaha! Interesting!”","Yet, the clan chief remained calm. He wiped off the blood seeping from the corner of his mouth and revealed a frenzied smile.","“Chu Feng, I admit that I have underestimated you. No wonder you can stand your ground against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Someone this powerful was protecting you all this while. But you aren’t the only one with tricks up your sleeves.”","The clan chief changed his hand seal, and the glowing rune enveloping Chu Feng and the others dissipated. The terrifying energy from the formation realm immediately rushed in.","“Chu Feng, you and your help can’t withstand this energy no matter how powerful you are. Without my protection, your only fate is...”","His words suddenly trailed to a halt and he stiffened up. Much to his horror, he realized Chu Feng and the others were unfazed by the energy gnawing at them.","“How is this possible? How are you unaffected by that cat demon’s resentment?”","The clan chief and his clansmen were bewildered. They knew how overwhelming the cat demon’s resentment was; their founder had to pay a heavy price to construct this hereditary formation to counteract it.","Faced with the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen’s confusion, Chu Feng replied with a chuckle, “I already said you are underestimating me.”","A spirit formation gate manifested with a wave of his palm, and a figure emerged from it.","The Ancient Era’s War Clansmen went pale as if they had seen a ghost, for it was none other than Old Cat.","Not only was he unharmed, but the formation realm even shook at his presence. The killing intent he emanated was more terrifying than ever.","He wasn’t just a mere cat.","He was the master of this formation realm."]},{"number":6233,"title":"Chapter 6233: Chapter 6231: A Stalwart Comrade","paragraphs":["Chapter 6231: A Stalwart Comrade","“Y-y-you deceived us?” the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief angrily questioned Chu Feng, though his face was marked with fear more than anything.","He understood the consequences of Old Cat being here.","“Yes, I deceived you. Did you think I would help you kill him? Do you think we would foolishly walk into your trap? Let me tell you that Old Cat and I are stalwart comrades!” Chu Feng replied.","“You...” The clan chief trembled in fury.","Old Cat frowned at Chu Feng. “Stalwart comrades?”","“Shush.” Chu Feng glanced at Old Cat before turning back to the clan chief. “First, that black wall should have been strong enough to withstand the energy. You secretly weakened it to let Old Cat in. You wanted to cause a panic so that I would be forced to decide on the spot without seeing the treasure. I would have no choice but to activate the copper cauldron and kill Old Cat to resolve the imminent crisis.","“But you forget that I’m a world spiritist. Your tricks can’t fool me,” Chu Feng said.","“Chu Feng... I’ll kill you!”","The clan chief invoked his clan-protection formation and flitted up to Chu Feng. His cultivation had further risen to rank three Heavenly God level. He did have more tricks up his sleeves.","But before he could reach Chu Feng, he froze in place. He clutched his neck in pain as he struggled frantically in mid-air.","It was Old Cat’s doing.","No one else sensed Old Cat’s maneuver except for Chu Feng. He had tapped into the terrifying energy suffusing the land to unravel the power protecting the clan chief.","Old Cat was the ruler of this place. A mere rank three Heavenly God level cultivator was nothing to him.","“Spare us! Spare us, please!”","Some Ancient Era’s War Clansmen tried to escape, whereas others pleaded for mercy, but they were all dragged into the air like the clan chief.","Instead of killing them right away, Old Cat rose into the air and formed a hand seal. A furious storm swirled, and the earth tremored intensely.","The mountainlike bones shattered, transforming into auras that surged into Old Cat’s body along with the terrifying energy. It didn’t take long for the terrifying energy and the bones to disappear.","Everything fell silent.","Old Cat stood quietly in mid-air.","No one knew how strong he currently was, but the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen, who were still hanging mid-air, knew for certain they were no match for him. Despite being a cat, he emanated the airs of a top-notch expert.","“Brother Chu Feng, will the cat demon take our lives too?” Xianhai Shaoyu asked via voice transmission.","He was nervous because Old Cat looked even more frightening than the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen.","“Old Cat is not a bad person at his core. I don’t think he’ll return kindness with ingratitude now that we have helped him,” Chu Feng replied discreetly.","In truth, he wasn’t sure how Old Cat would respond either. Old Cat had never been a reliable one, not to mention he had just absorbed a tremendous amount of resentment and unknown energy. Those might have induced changes in his personality.","All of a sudden, Old Cat disappeared.","“Chu Feng, is that cat demon reliable? If not, I can bring us out through the passageway,” Jie Shanxian said via voice transmission. The passageway she was referring to was the one she previously created with her treasure.","“Chu Feng, come with me,” Old Cat’s voice suddenly echoed.","At the same time, Old Cat appeared next to Chu Feng. He had returned.","Before Chu Feng could reply, the scenery around him suddenly changed. Old Cat was taking him somewhere, though this only lasted for a second. By the time they stopped, Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy were nowhere to be seen.","Chu Feng had once reached Heavenly God level too, albeit through desperate means, so he understood the power wielded by Heavenly God level cultivators. Thanks to that, he could tell that Old Cat’s cultivation had reached a frightening level.","“Brother Chu Feng, can you take a look at this for me?” Old Cat asked with a grin. He seemed to have reverted into the Old Cat that Chu Feng knew.","He was pointing at a formation around the size of a face basin. The formation was not emanating any aura, and it eluded one’s senses too. To put it in other words, it couldn’t be sensed with martial power or spirit power; it could only be seen with one’s physical eyes.","“It is a martial power formation,” Chu Feng replied.","“A martial power formation? Can you tell what kind of formation it is?” Old Cat asked.","“Can you breach it?”","“I tried. It doesn’t work.” Old Cat shook his head.","“It doesn’t work for you too?”","“Those scoundrels have siphoned away my blood and flesh’s origin energies. It is already amazing for my cultivation to be restored to its current level with just these bones. I should cultivate much faster now that I have partially recovered my bloodline though. You will have to work hard. You might have the Ruler’s Bloodline and the Genesis Bloodline, but you might still never catch up with me in your lifetime,” Old Cat said gleefully.","Chu Feng could sense Old Cat’s glee, though that was only to be expected. He had been through a lot before this.","“What’s your current cultivation level?” Chu Feng asked.","“Why are you asking that? Study that formation and tell me what’s going on with it!” Old Cat urged.","“How do you know there’s a formation here?”","“Of course I’d know! Someone placed it in my bones. Wouldn’t you know if someone planted something in your bones too?”","“When was it placed here?”","“I don’t know. I only sensed it when I entered this place.”","“You don’t even know when someone placed something in your bones?”","“Y-y-you... I-I-I... You also know I was... Argh!” Old Cat didn’t want to bother explaining it anymore and exclaimed, “Stop beating around the bush and tell me what’s going on with this formation.”","Chu Feng grimly looked at Old Cat and asked, “Old Cat, let’s put our grudges aside for now. Would you have been able to absorb your bones if not for me?”","“Of course not.”","“Does that make me your savior?”","“Rest assured, Brother Chu Feng. I don’t need anything from the Ancient Era’s War Clan. You can have all their treasures and their Nine Secret Skills.”","“I’m not talking about that. Can we be considered stalwart comrades after everything we have been through?”","“Of course, of course.” Old Cat nodded.","“If that’s the case, you should tell me the truth. Do you truly know nothing about this formation?” Chu Feng asked Old Cat.","He could tell that Old Cat was extremely afraid of the formation."]},{"number":6234,"title":"Chapter 6234: Chapter 6232: The Martial Power Formation’s Aura","paragraphs":["Chapter 6232: The Martial Power Formation’s Aura","“There’s nothing to hide. Zhan Haichuan’s feats are a legend in the Hundred Refinement Ordinary Realm, so you should have already heard about them. Needless to say, I am the reason why he possesses such great talent.","“I was severely injured back then. I don’t remember why I was injured and who did that to me, but I was indeed helpless against those ungrateful Ancient Era’s War Clansmen. So, I had no choice but to feign death and preserve a sliver of my soul. It took many years to transfer that sliver out of my carcass using a secret skill.","“But I didn’t have a body then, so what I could do alone was limited. To recover my power, I’ll have to first repair my carcass and fuse it into my main body. That was no easy feat. Fortunately, an opportunity soon presented itself.","“The Ancient Era’s War Clan created a treasure that strengthened one’s bloodline in hopes of tapping into my energy. My strength was limited then, but that treasure was tailored just for me. So, I found a way to seep into that treasure and make it mine. It took 50,000 years to incubate that treasure, and in that time, I gained full control over it.","“However, that treasure can only be used by the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen; I am unable to channel it myself. Thus, I planted a binding contract inside that treasure to slowly alter the minds of those who obtain the treasure and turn them into my puppets. But an incident happened while those fools were channeling the treasure, and the treasure left this formation realm.”","Chu Feng widened his eyes in realization.","50,000 years ago, a brilliant silver light enveloped the Hundred Refinement Ordinary Realm’s sky. A humongous silver spear of inestimable proportions appeared amidst the silver light, almost like a divine weapon that could destroy the entire world.","This weapon descended from the sky as a surge of silver light and landed inside a child’s body. That child was none other than Zhan Haichuan.","It turned out Zhan Haichuan’s talent was Old Cat’s credit.","“That treasure flew to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy and happened to fall into the newly-born Zhan Haichuan’s body?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes. I thought I had failed until Zhan Haichuan went to the War Clan many years later. Everything went smoothly at the start; Zhan Haichuan successfully returned to the War Clan under my tutelage and obtained the materials I required. We secretly repaired my carcass and strengthened my soul before fusing the two.","“It was easier said than done. We prepared for many years before finally pulling it off. But just as the fusion was about to take place Zhan Haichuan suddenly turned against me because he was afraid I would massacre the War Clan. That was the only chance I had because the energy and treasures all came from me. There is no way to find more once they are depleted, making it nigh impossible to pull it off anymore.","“When I went to the Hundred Refinement Ordinary Realm to look for Zhan Haichuan, I wasn’t coveting his treasure but seeking him for vengeance. I didn’t expect him to be dead because of the injuries the War Clan’s Clan Chief inflicted on him.","“He deserved it, but his death does little to assuage my hatred. So I dug his grave to vent my frustration, but that despicable Zhan Haichuan set up a formation before his death to imprison me. I was only freed later when you arrived.”","Old Cat gritted his teeth in anger.","“Why didn’t you tell me the truth then?” Chu Feng asked.","“Hmph.” Old Cat clicked his tongue. “Do you think I’d trust you after my ordeal with the War Clan and Zhan Haichuan? I’m not going to get bitten by a snake twice.”","Chu Feng thought those words made sense. Anyone who had been through so much wouldn’t easily trust others once more.","“I had already given up on everything, but in the last two years, I suddenly sensed my carcass summoning me. Somehow, I regained connection with my bones. My carcass has regained its powers. It was much stronger than when Zhan Haichuan repaired it, and this reparation is permanent. This should have been impossible, but a miracle happened.","“I sought ways to return here, but I couldn’t breach the War Clan’s formation. It was then you made a name for yourself. I learned you were Jie Ranqing’s son and the most talented world spiritist in the present era. However, you were too elusive for me to track down, so I eventually gave up on that. I returned to Zhenlong’s remnant to see if I could find anything there.","“You can figure out what happened next. Zhenlong was still alive, and he made a breakthrough to Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. I thought it was heaven’s will. What were the odds stumbling upon a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist just like that? Knowing this was a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity, I kneeled and told everything to Zhenlong, hoping my sincerity would move him.","“Little did I expect him to be moved by my sincerity. He came here to help me. You know what happened afterward,” Old Cat said.","Chu Feng fell into deep thought,","Old Cat thought Chu Feng didn’t believe him, so he added, “Brother Chu Feng, you can ask Zhenlong if you don’t believe me. Everything I said is the truth.”","“Old Cat, you have changed,” Chu Feng said.","“Changed? How so?” Old Cat asked.","“The way you address Lord Zhenlong changed. I bet you previously called him Lord Zhenlong. Fusing with your bones might not have fully restored your cultivation, but it must have partially restored your bloodline. You’re no longer the scared Old Cat now but an indomitable Ancient Era’s saint beast, so you stopped calling him Lord Zhenlong and instead addressed him directly by name.","“Similarly, you’re calling me Brother Chu Feng because you need my help, but you’ll go back to calling me Little Feng once things are over, right?” Chu Feng asked.","“Do I seem like that kind of person? I’m only saying that because we’re close! I’ll still address Zhenlong as ‘Lord Zhenlong’ when I meet him again. I might be more senior than even your ancestors, and Zhenlong is indeed unworthy of me addressing him as ‘Lord Zhenlong’, but I’ll never forget the favor I owe you two.”","Perhaps to show their close ties, Old Cat even levitated up and grabbed Chu Feng’s shoulders with his cat paws.","“Fine, I’ll give it a try.”","Chu Feng had been observing this martial power formation all this while and had already devised a method to decipher it. He swiftly constructed a formation, and it only took him moments to decipher the martial power formation.","“Chu Feng, you are too humble. Look, you succeeded in a single try! You live up to your reputation as Jie Ranqing’s son!” Old Cat lavished compliments on Chu Feng.","But Chu Feng fell into a daze.","A palm-sized metal tool emerged from the dissipated martial power formation. Inside the metal tool was a stronger martial power formation. To top it off, Chu Feng sensed a familiar aura from it.","It was his father’s aura.","“Damn.”","Chu Feng realized something."]},{"number":6235,"title":"Chapter 6235: Chapter 6233: Your Benefactor’s Son Is In Front Of You","paragraphs":["Chapter 6233: Your Benefactor’s Son Is In Front Of You","The aura was so discreet that it could have eluded Old Cat’s notice even though Chu Feng had discovered it.","More importantly, the metal tool resembled a crossbow, and it was pointing in the direction of where Jie Shanxian was previously trapped. The martial power formation contained powerful breaching prowess; it was prepared for Jie Shanxian.","This martial power formation should have already activated, but the crossbow arrow didn’t fire, possibly because it noticed that Jie Shanxian had already been freed. It was a highly ingenious formation; most world spiritists wouldn’t have been able to create such a precise formation.","“What fortuitous encounter did my father stumble upon to be able to construct such formidable martial power formations?” Chu Feng murmured.","Old Cat didn’t hear those words, but Eggy did.","“What? Your father is behind this formation?!” Eggy widened her eyes in astonishment.","“I think so. I sense my father’s aura. This formation is designed to rescue Jie Shanxian. I can’t think of anyone else who would do this other than my father,” Chu Feng said.","“Right, your father did promise to save Jie Shanxian. I guess he had to flee back then because he couldn’t withstand the energy, but he returned after becoming stronger. But why didn’t he save Jie Shanxian straight? That’s a roundabout way of doing things. Or does this have something to do with the energy infused inside Old Cat’s carcass?","“That is plausible. The timeline fits. Old Cat started sensing his carcass around the same time your father planted the protective formation inside your body. Considering how powerful that protective formation is, your father must have reached a high cultivation level. He should have been capable of pulling it off.","“He entered this formation space in search of the treasure, only to stumble upon a pile of bones emanating overwhelming resentment. Given your father’s personality, he would investigate the matter to uncover the truth. He probably learned about the secrets between the Ancient Era’s War Clan and Old Cat, so he decided to give Old Cat a helping hand.","“He probably thought it was better for Old Cat to regain his powers first before freeing Jie Shanxian, so he opted to construct this martial power formation here. What do you think about my conjecture, Chu Feng?” Eggy asked.","“My thoughts alike. I also think my father is behind everything.” Chu Feng nodded.","“But if your father has decided to help Old Cat, why doesn’t he see it all the way through and bring Old Cat here? What if Old Cat never makes it here to recover his powers? The martial power formation would have never triggered, and Jie Shanxian would never be freed,” Eggy asked.","“I don’t know. My father might have secretly made some arrangements,” Chu Feng replied.","“Your father is indeed an enigmatic man. I can’t believe someone as powerful as him is still unknown in the world of cultivation. Practically all the news we have stumbled upon about your father is related to remnants. Seriously, why is a cultivator like your father so obsessed with graverobbing?” Eggy exclaimed.","“It’s called exploring remnants, not graverobbing,” Chu Feng corrected.","Eggy rolled her eyes. “Exploring remnants is just another term for graverobbing.”","Chu Feng was rendered speechless. He couldn’t refute that. His father was indeed passionate about graverobbing.","“Chu Feng, how strong do you think your father is if he is behind this? If he still isn’t strong enough to rescue your mother, I can’t imagine what monsters are lurking in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” Eggy murmured worriedly.","Chu Feng’s greatest worry was still his mother. It was only a matter of time before he made a trip to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. But if the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion was that powerful, Chu Feng might still struggle to rescue his mother even after advancing to Heavenly God level.","“Brother Chu Feng, you have been staring at that metal tool for quite some time now. Are you unable to see through it too? It seems to be pointing in the direction where you came from,” Old Cat probed out of curiosity.","He hadn’t gotten a chance to have a proper conversation with Chu Feng yet, but he picked up many details from the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen’s earlier chatter.","Chu Feng looked at Old Cat and made up his mind. He asked, “Old Cat, under normal circumstances, you shouldn’t have been able to recover your cultivation from those bones, right?”","“Yes, that’s right,” Old Cat replied.","“Why aren’t you telling me the truth then?” Chu Feng asked.","“What truth?” Old Cat was confused.","“This formation was constructed around the same time as when you started to sense your carcass. Someone was behind all of this. You should have been able to tell as much,” Chu Feng pointed out.","Old Cat widened his eyes. He grabbed Chu Feng’s shoulders and anxiously asked, “Chu Feng, is there any lingering aura? You have to find that person for me. He is my benefactor!”","Chu Feng was flustered. He was planning to corner Old Cat into admitting that someone had helped him, but he didn’t expect the latter to concede to it so easily. This worked in his favor.","“You did sense it! Tell me the truth, Old Cat. What did you sense from the formation?”","“Fine, I’ll tell you the truth. My bones are packed with not just the martial power formation’s energy but natural oddities too. Thanks to that, my carcass regained its energy. The person behind this is my benefactor for giving me a second chance in life. I have to repay this debt.","“However, my benefactor didn’t leave any information behind. Now that I have absorbed the energy and the natural oddities, this martial power formation is the only clue left. So, Brother Chu Feng, please take a closer look and help me uncover clues about my benefactor,” Old Cat pleaded.","Chu Feng chuckled. “Search no further.”","“Huh?” Old Cat was bewildered.","“You are in the presence of your benefactor’s son.”","“You brat! I am being serious! Help me look into it...” Old Cat’s voice began to trail off as he noticed the serious look on Chu Feng’s face. He was stunned for a second before laughing in a mix of awkwardness and disbelief. “You can’t be serious... right?”"]},{"number":6236,"title":"Chapter 6236: Chapter 6234: The Son Inherits the Father’s Favor","paragraphs":["Chapter 6234: The Son Inherits the Father’s Favor","“You know that my mother is Jie Ranqing. Do you know who my father is?” Chu Feng asked.","“I don’t know.” Old Cat shook his head.","“Old Cat, I shall be honest with you too. My father is a powerful cultivator, but he is a highly elusive figure. I hardly see him too. He... wasn’t around when I was growing up, and I have only met him a couple of times.","“I sensed my father’s aura in the martial power formation, which is why I can say for certain that he is the one who restored the energy in your carcass,” Chu Feng said.","“Why did he do that? What does he stand to gain from this?” Old Cat asked grimly, his previous light-hearted attitude vanishing into thin air. The atmosphere around him changed too.","Chu Feng sensed faint killing intent from Old Cat, but he was unfazed, having expected as much. “I can’t say for sure, but I’m guessing that my father helped you knowing that we are acquainted. He has done such things before. Even though he was hardly around, he would secretly do things to help me from the shadows, such as rescuing my friends.","“You should have heard about the massive explosion that occurred in the Totem Galaxy, right? That’s the protective formation he planted inside me. It is a martial power formation too, and the Totem Dragon Clan can testify to that,” Chu Feng explained.","He was being honest in hopes that Old Cat could lend him a helping hand. He would rather rescue his mother earlier than later.","But Old Cat’s first reaction upon learning that Chu Feng’s father was his benefactor chilled him. His skepticism ran bone-deep, which was unsurprising given how he had been exploited all his life.","Chu Feng had only explained so much to let Old Cat know that his father didn’t rescue him with the intent of exploiting him. At the same time, he was indirectly telling Old Cat his father was not a pushover so that the latter wouldn’t do anything reckless.","“How can you prove this is your father’s formation? You could be lying to me,” Old Cat asked.","“This formation carries my father’s lingering aura. There will be bloodline resonance between a parent and a child. As a world spiritist, you should know how to verify that, right?”","“I don’t sense your father’s aura.”","“Your world spiritist techniques are lacking despite the advancement in your cultivation. Why don’t you call Lord Zhenlong here? He can testify to it,” Chu Feng said.","Old Cat bound Chu Feng with his energy before vanishing into thin air. The same happened to the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen, Xianhai Shaoyu, Little Fishy, and even Jie Shanxian.","“Chu Feng, isn’t this too risky? Old Cat is highly skeptical. He may appear light-hearted, but he is exceptionally guarded when it comes to matters concerning him. After his encounters with the War Clan, he might think that your father wants to take advantage of him and turn against you,” Eggy asked worriedly.","“It is possible.”","“Then you...”","“But he may also help me out of gratitude for my father. It’s a gamble. There are hardly any ties between us. I may have helped him this time, but it is far from enough to move him. Even if my father had an ulterior motive, it is a fact that Old Cat couldn’t have regained his powers if not for my father’s help. I believe Old Cat is well aware of that too.”","Chu Feng was betting that Old Cat was someone who repaid his debts.","If Old Cat was the type to stoop to anything for his interests, he would have coveted Chu Feng’s Ruler’s Bloodline and Genesis Bloodline too. Those were invaluable treasures, after all.","Soon, Old Cat returned with Lord Zhenlong.","Shockingly, Lord Zhenlong couldn’t detect the aura of Chu Feng’s father either. He only managed to sense it with the help of Chu Feng’s pointers.","Everything else was simple enough. Lord Zhenlong had his ways to verify whether the aura belonged to Chu Feng’s father or not.","It was a complicated process, but the outcome verified that Chu Feng was telling the truth.","“So he is your father.” Old Cat’s mouth fell agape. He was still surprised despite having mentally prepared himself for this possibility. It took a while before he finally recovered and rushed forth to grab Chu Feng. “Chu Feng, how strong is your father? Do you know where he is? May I visit him and thank him in person?”","“I told you earlier I hardly see him too, so I don’t know where or how strong he is,” Chu Feng replied. “I don’t think there is a need to probe deeper now that you know who your benefactor is. You should focus more on how you can repay the debt.”","“I need to find your father first to repay the debt,” Old Cat said.","“What if there’s a way to repay the debt without finding my father?”","“How do I do that?”","“The son inherits the father’s favors.”","“Ah? What does that phrase mean? I have only heard about sons repaying their fathers’ debt,” Old Cat scoffed.","“How uncultured! It means that if you want to repay a debt, you can choose to repay the son instead,” Chu Feng said.","“Bullshit! I have never heard of that phrase before. Did you invent it?” Old Cat snorted.","“That’s right, I invented it,” Chu Feng frankly admitted to it.","Old Cat was rendered speechless.","Chu Feng took this opportunity to push his case, “Old Cat, you talked about repaying your debt earlier. Do you intend to follow through with it now you know who your benefactor is?”","“Of course, of course. You are a cunning one. Given how you told me so much, I bet you already have something in mind. Stop beating around the bush and get to the point,” Old Cat said.","“I have always been worried about my mother. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is at its weakest ever now that Jie Tianran is stuck in God’s Era. I want you to accompany me to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion and investigate how my mother is faring,” Chu Feng said."]},{"number":6237,"title":"Chapter 6237: Chapter 6235: Old Cat’s Answer","paragraphs":["Chapter 6235: Old Cat’s Answer","“Why doesn’t your father rescue your mother?” Old Cat asked.","“I don’t know either. I can’t see through my father’s thoughts. No matter the reason, I need to check on my mother and verify that she’s fine. Old Cat, I don’t know what’s your cultivation level, but I can tell you are very strong now. That’s why I am making this request to you.","“I’ll remember this favor if you help me, but it is understandable for you to turn down my request too. I won’t hold a grudge over this,” Chu Feng said with sincere eyes.","Even though Chu Feng’s father had restored the energy in Old Cat’s carcass, and Chu Feng had chosen to save Old Cat despite the opportunity to take the latter’s life, Chu Feng believed that Old Cat had the right to turn down his request.","Old Cat might owe him a favor, but that didn’t mean he was obliged to do anything Chu Feng asked of him.","Besides, Chu Feng also had his considerations for sparing Old Cat. If Old Cat hadn’t survived, he would have been dead too.","Old Cat lowered his head and fell into contemplation.","Chu Feng patiently waited for his answer.","In the end, Old Cat lifted his head and replied, “I’ll give you an answer later. For now, let me deal with these ingrates first.”","Old Cat ordered the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief to gather all his clansmen via their clan-protection formation.","The clan chief, being a coward, dared not defy Old Cat. He still held onto the hope that Old Cat might spare him if he was obedient enough.","Oblivious to the danger, the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen assembled in their square. They steered clear of the elevated platform at the center of the square, reserving it for their clan chief. The mood was merry as they thought their clan chief was going to hold a celebratory banquet.","But all of them froze up when several figures suddenly crashed into the elevated platform. These were the people whom they had been waiting for—their clan chief and their clan’s top experts.","How did they land in this pitiful state?","As fear and confusion rippled through the crowd, a few more figures descended on the elevated platform. It was Chu Feng, Old Cat, and the others.","Old Cat landed on the clan chief and stomped his foot through the latter’s body, crushing his dantian. The clan chief’s wretched cry echoed resoundingly across the square.","That jolted the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen awake. All of them rose into the air, but they were visibly divided into two teams.","One team rushed to the elevated platform to attack Old Cat, in hopes of saving their clan chief. The other team fled from the square.","But regardless of their intention, they were all frozen in place shortly after they rose into the air, before they could get anything done.","Old Cat lowered his posture and swiped his claws. Blood splattered. His claws ripped through the clan chief’s head, but it didn’t claim the latter’s life.","GAH!","The clan chief screamed in agony. His body convulsed as Old Cat forcefully siphoned away the energy harnessed inside his soul.","“Something feels off, Chu Feng. That old stray cat is absorbing the clan chief’s origin energies. It’s not as if he is a world spirit, so why is he absorbing their origin energies?” Eggy asked.","“Old Cat is indeed a cunning one,” Chu Feng remarked.","“What does that mean?” Eggy was confused.","“I’m guessing all War Clansmen have that energy in them. It is rooted in their hereditary bloodline. Old Cat did help the War Clan, but his motives were not pure. He planted something equivalent to a gu in their ancestors, and this gu was passed down through the generations. This gu can be turned into energy for his use,” Chu Feng explained.","“What? That old stray cat is such a schemer! Doesn’t that mean that the War Clan’s ancestors made the right choice to leave Old Cat to the lurch? Otherwise, they would have been destroyed by now!” Eggy widened her eyes.","“There’s no way to say for sure, but it is indeed an underhanded trick,” Chu Feng replied.","Xianhai Shaoyu, Little Fishy, and Lord Zhenlong were taken aback as well. They, too, could tell that something was amiss even if their analysis wasn’t as thorough as Chu Feng’s.","Soon, the clan chief died amidst excruciating pain.","Old Cat pulled out his claws and licked them before turning his gaze to the remaining clansmen.","“War Clan, it’s time to pay your debt.”","Old Cat placed his paws together and invoked a secret skill. His tiny body swiftly enlarged till it was tens of thousands of meters tall. He didn’t look fierce no matter how he tried when he was small, but now that he was massive, he naturally commanded an air of intimidation.","Many Ancient Era’s War Clansmen peed their pants. They knew this was the end for them.","Old Cat opened his mouth, and a powerful wind brewed. Soon, a powerful suction force engulfed the square.","Shrill screams followed. All Ancient Era’s War Clansmen were experiencing the same pain their clan chief suffered earlier.","“Save me, Chu Feng! Save me!” Chu Feng vaguely heard a plea.","Looking over, he saw Zhan Moli. She had become so emaciated that her skin was clinging to her bones. She looked at Chu Feng with pleading eyes.","Anyone else would have felt sorry for her despite knowing she deserved it.","But Chu Feng merely smiled at her and mouthed, “Farewell.”","That single word seemed to contain magic in it, as Zhan Moli first widened her eyes before her head tilted to the side. She was dead.","The other Ancient Era’s War Clansmen, due to their lower cultivation, didn’t last as long as their clan chief did. Their vitals disappeared in just an instant.","Old Cat returned to his original size, but he didn’t descend to the ground. His domineering aura continued to loom over the square.","With a wave of his sleeves, all the Ancient Era’s War Clansmen’s Cosmos Sacks unraveled. Glowing treasures and natural oddities surged into the sky like brilliant stars, lighting up the surroundings.","Old Cat descended toward Chu Feng. Grabbing Chu Feng’s shoulder, he grandly gestured to the sky and said, “Brother Chu Feng, you have contributed the most to my comeback. You may take any treasure of your liking.”","Chu Feng noticed that the metal lump he desired wasn’t in the sky even though he saw the exquisite box holding it rising upward too. He felt a tinge of disappointment. If Old Cat was reluctant to give him the best treasure, it was even more unlikely for him to accompany him to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Just then, Old Cat suddenly spoke up, “Brother Chu Feng, I should give you my answer now that I am done dealing with the War Clan. About what you mentioned earlier, I’ll help you.”"]},{"number":6238,"title":"Chapter 6238: Chapter 6236: Immemorial God Armament Fragment","paragraphs":["Chapter 6236: Immemorial God Armament Fragment","Chu Feng was overjoyed, but before he could say anything, Old Cat continued, “But I’ll need your help on something, Brother Chu Feng. I wish to repair a treasure, but it’ll require a powerful world spiritist bloodline. Can you assist Lord Zhenlong in repairing it?”","Old Cat took out a box and opened it. In it was an Ancient Era’s talisman that looked ordinary but wasn’t. This box carried the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief’s aura, hinting that he cherished it.","This wasn’t one of the items that the clan chief had previously shown Chu Feng, which was more than enough to show that it was more valuable than that lump of black metal.","“A damaged teleportation talisman paper?” Little Fishy asked.","“What sharp eyes you have! It is a damaged teleportation talisman paper, but it is not ordinary teleportation talisman paper. I don’t have the means to repair a teleportation talisman paper of this tier,” Lord Zhenlong said.","“Don’t worry, Lord Zhenlong. I have the reparation method,” Old Cat said as he whipped out a formation blueprint.","Lord Zhenlong’s eyes lit up. This blueprint was so ingenious that it could realize the impossible. Nevertheless, he still soon shook his head, “It will take a huge toll on young friend Chu Feng’s bloodline.”","“That’s why I need Brother Chu Feng’s help.” Old Cat turned to Chu Feng.","“This despicable old stray cat! Chu Feng, don’t help him!” Eggy was angry.","She thought Old Cat was lying about accompanying Chu Feng to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion; he was merely trying to coax Chu Feng into repairing the teleportation talisman paper.","Instead of answering the question, Chu Feng asked, “Old Cat, you said that I can have all their treasures, so why are you hiding the good stuff?”","With a wave of his sleeve, Old Cat swooped all the treasures in the sky into a Cosmos Sack and handed it to Chu Feng. “Brother Chu Feng, all the treasures are here. You can have it all if you want. I always keep my promises.”","He handed the Cosmos Sack to Chu Feng.","“I don’t need these, and I’m willing to help you repair your damaged teleportation talisman paper either, but I have a small request. Can you hand that black metal lump to me?” Chu Feng got to the point.","“Black metal lump? Is this it?” Old Cat whipped out a black metal lump with a flick of his wrist.","That was indeed what Chu Feng wanted.","“That’s right.” Chu Feng nodded.","“This is a fragment of an Immemorial God Armament,” Old Cat said.","“Immemorial God Armament?” Chu Feng was taken aback.","“Immemorial God Armaments are nothing like the God Armaments you know; they are separate things. You’ll know it in due time.”","“Can you give it to me? I need it.”","“Brother Chu Feng, I can’t give it to you. It is mine. I promised to give you all of the War Clan’s possessions, but I ought to keep my stuff, no?” Old Cat asked.","It was a fair but shameless statement. Chu Feng figured that the chances of Old Cat double-crossing him were high, so he asked, “You don’t want to repair this talisman paper anymore?”","“Brother Chu Feng, I truly can’t give that to you. Rest assured. As long as you and Lord Zhenlong try your best to repair the talisman paper, I’ll accompany you to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Also, you should have this.” Old Cat stowed away the black metal lump and took out a bundle of aura.","It was the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Nine Secret Skills.","“These secret skills were forged out of the treasure I gave the War Clan back then, but that trash, Zhan Fengdan, could not withstand the full might of the secret skills, so he divided them into many portions. The secret skills I have put together now might pale far compared to Zhan Fengdan’s, but it is far superior to those owned by the other War Clansmen. I shall hand them to you now.","“A reminder—the energy in these secret skills is not to be underestimated. Tell me if you can’t withstand it; don’t strain yourself trying to take it in,” Old Cat said as he pumped the aura into Chu Feng’s body.","Chu Feng’s face warped. He was in great pain.","“Tell me if you can’t withstand it,” Old Cat advised.","But Chu Feng squeezed out a smile and said, “Cut the bullshit and give it all to me.”","Old Cat smiled too. He had also expected Chu Feng to be able to withstand it, so he pumped all the aura into Chu Feng’s body.","Soon, Chu Feng’s body shone. He formed a hand seal and began fusing the secret skills while erasing their consciousness, retaining only the Ancient Era War Sword and Ancient Era War Axe’s consciousness. This turned the two secret skills that had once helped him into the rulers of the Nine Secret Skills.","The light soon dissipated, and Chu Feng’s complexion returned to normal.","“The secret skills aren’t too bad, right? Did I keep my promise and give the Nine Secret Skills and all the War Clan’s treasures to you?” Old Cat asked as he handed the Cosmos Sack filled with treasures over.","Chu Feng took the Cosmos Sack. The treasures inside were worth far less than what he had, for Old Cat had already swiped everything of value. Still, there was no reason to reject it. While he still had complaints, he had to concede the secret skills were not too bad.","Thus, he said, “Fine, I’ll give it a try. I’ll be counting on you, Lord Zhenlong.”","“I can only play a supporting role here. It will come down to you, young friend Chu Feng. Try your best, but don’t strain yourself. It will be terrible if you shake your foundation. I believe Old Cat will not blame you even if this fails.” Lord Zhenlong turned to Old Cat and asked, “Right?”","“Of course, of course! Lord Zhenlong is right!” Old Cat nodded profusely.","Despite his earlier casualness in addressing Lord Zhenlong, he was showing the latter a lot of respect now. This showed that Old Cat still had some principles even though his scruples might be lacking at times.","If he was truly evil, he could have coerced Chu Feng and Lord Zhenlong into doing his bidding, given that he was now stronger than them. There was no need for him to amicably negotiate with them like this.","“But we’ll have to modify the formation blueprint,” Chu Feng said.","“What are you doing, Chu Feng? My formation is...”","Old Cat tried to stop Chu Feng, but he soon froze up. Much to his shock, the formation was much smoother after undergoing modification.","Lord Zhenlong’s mouth also fell agape in shock. Even Jie Shanxian’s eyes lit up.","They didn’t think Chu Feng could further perfect such a complicated formation blueprint.","“What’s wrong?” Chu Feng turned to Old Cat.","Old Cat shot Chu Feng a thumbs up. “I just want to give you my deepest compliment.”"]},{"number":6239,"title":"Chapter 6239: Chapter 6237: I Don’t Fear Rank Five Heavenly Gods","paragraphs":["Chapter 6237: I Don’t Fear Rank Five Heavenly Gods","“You can decipher the formation blueprint? You’re more enigmatic than I thought,” Old Cat remarked.","“It’s not about being enigmatic; we just don’t know each other well enough,” Chu Feng smiled.","“Makes sense. Hahaha!” Old Cat laughed. He could tell Chu Feng was driving at something, as he was also withholding personal information.","Chu Feng and Lord Zhenlong worked together to repair the teleportation talisman paper. It was a complicated process that took a lot of time, but nothing went wrong thanks to the modifications made to the formation blueprint.","“Lord Zhenlong, Brother Chu Feng, I don’t know how I can thank the two of you.” Old Cat held the repaired teleportation talisman paper with an unconcealable grin.","“How far can that teleportation talisman paper teleport? And why is Old Cat so excited?” Eggy asked out of curiosity.","“That teleportation talisman paper can only be fully understood and activated through a special method,” Chu Feng replied.","“I’m guessing that old stray cat is the only one who knows that method. He’s keeping so many secrets from us. Chu Feng, do you think he can be trusted? Isn’t there a chance he might betray you for treasures when the time comes?” Eggy reserved her skepticism.","“Let’s give it a try. There should be kindness in Old Cat, or else he wouldn’t have treated young master Wolf so well,” Chu Feng replied.","“That’s true.” Eggy nodded.","Old Cat swept through the Ancient Era’s War Clan and collected all their treasures. He claimed that those items were worthless, so he didn’t bother giving them to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng wasn’t bothered; he had no complaints as long as Old Cat accompanied him to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. To be fair, the Nine Secret Skills were already enough to make this a worthwhile trip for him.","Old Cat handed Lord Zhenlong a Cosmos Sack. This was probably the benefit he had promised Lord Zhenlong. Chu Feng couldn’t see through it.","After taking what he wanted, Lord Zhenlong prepared to take his leave.","“Lord Zhenlong, what do you plan to do next?” Chu Feng asked.","“I don’t have anything specific in mind yet. I’ll probably either journey around the world of cultivation or make my way to the Ninth Galaxy,” Lord Zhenlong said.","From those words, Chu Feng understood that Lord Zhenlong’s fate with the Totem Dragon Clan had come to an end. Lord Zhenlong had no intention of returning to the Totem Dragon Clan.","This was not surprising since Lord Zhenlong had now surpassed the Totem Dragon Clan. There was no reason for him to serve them anymore. In the first place, he was merely in a partnership with the Totem Dragon Clan and had fulfilled his obligations to them. He owed nothing to them.","Lord Zhenlong turned to Chu Feng and said, “Young friend Chu Feng, I heard about your conflict with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. I shan’t interfere in your family affair, but I heard from the Totem Dragon Clan that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion isn’t as simple as it seems. You should tread carefully. You’re a rare talent. I’m only going to the Ninth Galaxy to widen my boundaries, but I’m sure you will make a name for yourself there. I’m still looking forward to boasting about knowing you.”","The usually uptight Lord Zhenlong cracked a rare joke and chuckled. Behind his words carried great expectations for Chu Feng’s future.","Chu Feng clasped his fist and smiled. “I won’t let you down.”","“Good, I’ll look forward to it. Young friend Chu Feng, Old Cat, may fate bring us together in the Ninth Galaxy.”","Lord Zhenlong took his leave. He probably knew of a way out of this formation realm.","Chu Feng and the others couldn’t leave with him as the Immortal Sea Fish Clan was still waiting outside for them.","“Chu Feng, what happened between you and the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion?” Jie Shanxian asked Chu Feng via voice transmission.","She could tell from Chu Feng’s conversation with Old Cat and Lord Zhenlong that something was amiss.","“Elder, I have no grudge against the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but I do have a conflict with its incumbent mansion master.”","Chu Feng proceeded to tell Jie Shanxian about his history via voice transmission. He decided to be honest because he deduced that she was someone who could draw a line between right and wrong.","Jie Shanxian didn’t comment on the matter after hearing the full story. Instead, she said, “I’d like to go into closed-door training. Your formation space is quite comfortable. Let me stay here for a while longer. However, I won’t help you in your conflict with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.”","“Feel free to stay.” Chu Feng was more than happy to have her.","Even if Jie Shanxian didn’t intervene in his conflict with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, it was still a good thing to have a formidable world spiritist tag along with him.","Jie Shanxian entered Chu Feng’s formation space once more.","The curious Old Cat asked via voice transmission, “Who’s that, Chu Feng? I can’t see through her disguise.”","“It’s an elder I just met. I’m not familiar with her too, but I think she’s trustworthy,” Chu Feng replied.","“You think she’s trustworthy even though you just met her?” Old Cat retorted.","“Aren’t you the same too, Old Cat? You call me brother, but I don’t even know your current cultivation level,” Chu Feng pointed out.","“There’s nothing to hide. I only recovered a portion of my bloodline, so my cultivation is still greatly limited. I’ll have to cultivate from the start. I am currently at rank four Heavenly God level, but my powerful bloodline allows me to rival enemies a cultivation rank stronger. Not even rank five Heavenly Gods are beyond me.","“I have long heard that the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has an old monster in their ranks. Rest assured. As long as his cultivation doesn’t surpass rank five Heavenly God level, I’ll have my ways of dealing with him,” Old Cat said.","“Old Cat, you are the enigmatic one here. I’m curious to know how strong you were at your peak,” Chu Feng said.","“That’s a secret.”","“Do you know what happened in the final years of the Ancient Era?”","“Afraid not. I have forgotten all about that. I don’t even know who wounded me back then. It’s annoying to not even know who my enemy is when I was reduced to this state,” Old Cat cursed. “Wait a moment, Chu Feng, isn’t it time to part ways? Why did that fellow enter your body? Is she tagging along too?”","“She’ll be cultivating in my body for the time being,” Chu Feng replied.","“What the heck? You’re going to bring that world spiritist of unknown background with us?” Old Cat was unhappy to hear that.","“It’s fine. You’re stronger than her anyway,” Chu Feng replied.","Deep down, he thought that Jie Shanxian might know the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s secrets. Even though she said she wouldn’t help him, he still harbored a tinge of hope for her.","“That’s true. She’s not bad, but it isn’t worth a mention to me. Brother Chu Feng, you should be careful with who you associate with. Don’t trust anyone except for yourself. I know you’re smart, but you can be too emotional at times. I’m worried you might trust the wrong person. You can know a person but not their heart,” Old Cat advised.","“Got it.” Chu Feng smiled.","Old Cat’s advice made sense as there were many unreliable people in the world, but Chu Feng would rather believe there were reliable people in the world too, such as Eggy, Zi Ling, Su Rou, Su Mei, Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu,","He had met many conniving and underhanded rascals along the way, but he also met reliable comrades. This made him realize that even though the world could be a cold place, and human hearts were unpredictable, there was always warmth to be found in family members, friends, and lovers.","Family members were more reliable in that regard; friends and lovers would require more prudent judgment."]},{"number":6240,"title":"Chapter 6240: Chapter 6238: The Unreliable Old Cat","paragraphs":["Chapter 6238: The Unreliable Old Cat","Chu Feng and the others left via the passageway they came by and met with the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief and the others. Due to Old Cat’s urging, Chu Feng quickly filled them in about what he would do next.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief and the others wanted to follow Chu Feng to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, but Chu Feng firmly turned them down.","The Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief wanted to tag along because his clan owed Chu Feng a favor, and they wanted to do something for him, but he also understood that it was unlikely he could contribute much when there was a powerhouse of Old Cat’s caliber around.","Thus, he requested a recommendation letter from Chu Feng before leading the Immortal Sea Fish Clan to the Totem Galaxy to meet with the Totem Dragon Clan.","He knew about Chu Feng’s ties with the Totem Dragon Clan. He would be partially repaying Chu Feng’s favor if he could keep the Totem Dragon Clan safe.","Little Fishy and Xianhai Shaoyu wanted to follow Chu Feng, but Chu Feng refused to let them come along. They had no choice but to follow their clan to the Totem Dragon Clan.","On their way to the Totem Dragon Clan, Xianhai Shaoyu shared with his grandfather and his parents in greater detail what they had encountered in the Ancient Era’s War Clan.","Upon learning the full story, the faces of the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s upper echelons turned grim. Old Cat’s appearance shattered their common sense about the world of cultivation.","“If he’s already this strong after fusing with his carcass, just how powerful are the so-called Ancient Era’s saint beasts? How many more formidable Ancient Era’s races are there that we don’t know about?”","Even Xianhai Shaoyu’s grandfather, despite his usual optimism, felt a wave of pessimism. He was worried that there were more terrifying powers among the Ancient Era’s races other than the God Clan and the Ancient Era’s saint beasts.","How were the present-era cultivators supposed to cope with that?","...","On Chu Feng’s side, Old Cat took out a sword that was originally a meter in length, but it had extended to over ten meters long. It was not a weapon but a treasure intended for fast travel.","Their current traveling speed was nowhere on par with the Nine Heavens Secret Domain’s teleportation formations, but Chu Feng was hesitant to reveal that to Old Cat and Jie Shanxian.","The two of them sat on the sword as they traveled through a teleportation passageway. By now, they were already nearing the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Along the way, Old Cat engaged Chu Feng in conversations, but he would secretly nudge the subject toward Chu Feng’s father to gather more information. There were some secrets Chu Feng couldn’t say, but more often than not, he didn’t have the answer to Old Cat’s questions.","His understanding of his father was severely limited.","“Brother Chu Feng, you’re too tight-lipped. I only want to know more because I’m grateful to your father; I bear no malicious intention.” Old Cat was frustrated to see Chu Feng shaking his head at all his questions.","“It’s not that I don’t want to tell you; I don’t have the answers,” Chu Feng replied.","Old Cat didn’t believe him.","“Who don’t I share a secret with you too? Do you know why Lord Zhenlong wishes to enter the Ninth Galaxy? It’s because I told him the world of cultivation’s secret,” Old Cat said.","“What’s the secret?”","“I might have suffered a memory loss, but I still remember plenty of things. I can tell you with certainty that the current eight galaxies are different from how they were in the Ancient Era.”","“Are the current eight galaxies fake?”","“No, they aren’t fake. It’s just that many realms are gone missing, and those that remain have become smaller to different degrees. I don’t know the reason behind this phenomenon, but the natural energies have also become much thinner. It is nowhere close to the Ancient Era.","“Yet, the Ninth Galaxy remains the same. That’s why cultivators have to enter the Ninth Galaxy if they hope to make a breakthrough,” Old Cat said.","Those words were similar to what he had heard from the middle-aged, red-cloaked man he saved from the God Clan.","“Brother Chu Feng, I have already told you such a huge secret. You should tell me more about your father too. I truly bear no hostility,” Old Cat said.","“Old Cat, I truly don’t know. You can rest assured that my father likely intervened to help you; I don’t think he has any other intention. You are an Ancient Era’s saint beast. You should be able to tell if there’s anything amiss with your body, right?” Chu Feng asked.","“Look at how narrow-minded you are. Why do you think the worst of me? Why would I be skeptical of my benefactor? All I want to do is to know more about my benefactor. Forget it. I shan’t ask anymore since you’re so reluctant to speak. Just watch how I rescue your mother. I shall show the measly Seven Realms Sacred Mansion what I’m capable of!”","Old Cat took out a talisman paper; it was imbued with the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Clan Chief’s aura. It must have been stolen from him.","The talisman paper transformed into an aura that flowed into the sword beneath them. The sword swelled with spirit power before abruptly piercing through the teleportation passageway, causing them to emerge in the middle of space.","There was a massive realm not too far away from them—it was the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s headquarters. The realm was brighter than before because it was wrapped in a protective formation.","“Hoh, are they holing themselves in? Brother Chu Feng, do you have a way to breach that formation?” Old Cat asked.","Chu Feng examined the protective formation, but he was unable to see through it. “I wouldn’t have sought your help if I could do so.”","“We’ll have to brute force it then. I’ll show you what I’m capable of.”","Without any hesitation, Old Cat hurled his fist at the massive realm.","Despite his small stature, his punch rattled the void as it gushed toward the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion with a golden radiance. It felt like a realm’s worth of martial power was packed inside his fist.","Yet, this powerful attack failed to damage the protective formation or even produce a sound against it. It was almost as if Old Cat’s attack had been devoured.","“What the...” Old Cat was stunned.","He did consider the possibility that his attack might fail to shatter the protective formation; it was just a probing strike, after all. However, he didn’t think that it would fail to even scratch it.","“Old Cat, we need to run!” Chu Feng exclaimed.","Old Cat finally snapped out of his daze.","Clearly, they had underestimated the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. If they had such a powerful protective formation, who could guarantee that they didn’t have a slaughter formation of the same caliber too?","Old Cat took out a talisman paper, but a gush of energy suddenly enveloped the two of them from behind. It caused their movements to be delayed as if they were moving in viscous fluid.","Old Cat activated the talisman paper, and it transformed into a surge of aura and fused with the sword beneath them. The sword glowed brilliantly, but nothing else happened aside from that.","“Crap.” Cold sweat dripped from Old Cat’s face.","The talisman paper should have transported them into the nearest teleportation formation, allowing them to quickly retreat from this place. However, the energy binding them had not only restricted their movements but their means too.","Chu Feng activated Heaven’s Eyes to figure out a way to break free from this restraint.","Old Cat’s paws suddenly appeared before him. On one paw was the box containing the black metal lump, and on the other paw was a talisman paper. It was the talisman paper Chu Feng and Lord Zhenlong and helped him repair.","Old Cat looked at Chu Feng with apologetic eyes. “Brother Chu Feng, think of these as my gifts if you’re able to survive this ordeal. Otherwise, I’ll avenge you by destroying the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion after I advance my cultivation.”","Chu Feng was horrified to hear that. “What do you mean by that, Old Cat? Are you abandoning me?”","“Don’t blame me for this, Brother Chu Feng. It wasn’t easy for me to partially recover my bloodline. It’s my chance to return to my former glory. I can’t die a dog’s death here. That would be too sad. I owe you a favor for this, and I’ll compensate you if we ever meet again!”","Old Cat crushed a talisman paper, and the talisman paper released a powerful surge of energy.","“Old Cat, where has your loyalty gone? Take me with you!”","The talisman paper was potent enough for Old Cat to bring Chu Feng with him, but Old Cat chose to use all the talisman paper’s energy on himself, lest the energy wasn’t enough for him to break free of the restraint. With a flash of light, Old Cat vanished into thin air.","“Damn it. That cat is unreliable!” Chu Feng was rendered speechless.","He had teleportation talisman papers too, but those weren’t potent enough to overcome the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation.","A spirit formation gate appeared in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s protective formation. Warships flew out from the spirit formation gate and made their way toward Chu Feng. They had noticed his presence.","Just then, spirit power suddenly flowed out from his body and enveloped him and Old Cat’s box. This surge of spirit power rendered even the formation restraining him useless.","He quickly fled further out into space. His movement speed was far superior to the members of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Chu Feng breathed a sigh of relief. “At least there’s a reliable one here.”","It was Jie Shanxian who helped him."]},{"number":6241,"title":"Chapter 6241: Chapter 6239: Qin Jiu’s Bamboo Boat","paragraphs":["Chapter 6239: Qin Jiu’s Bamboo Boat","With Jie Shanxian’s help, Chu Feng quickly broke free of the formation. Jie Shanxian proceeded to bring him somewhere safe.","Chu Feng pulled Jie Shanxian out of his formation realm.","Jie Shanxian was in a terrible condition. Cold sweat flowed profusely from her forehead. She had become so frail that even her concealment means had been dispelled, revealing her true face.","This was caused by the token inscribed with the words ‘Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’ she held. The token was from the present era, but it harnessed an old aura Chu Feng had never seen in anyone else in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","Thanks to this token, Jie Shanxian was able to save Chu Feng from the formation when even Old Cat had his hands tied. However, she paid a heavy price invoking the token, resulting in her current weakness.","“I’m fine.” Jie Shanxian had already gulped down her pills, so she rejected Chu Feng’s.","Sitting crossed legs in space, she took out an incense stick emanating the Ancient Era’s aura and lit it with a hand seal. The smoke rising from the incense stick flowed into Jie Shanxian’s nose, healing her.","“Woah, she has a lot of valuable treasures. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion must have looted plenty of treasures back then,” Eggy remarked.","Jie Shanxian was severely injured, which also showed just how valuable the incense stick was.","Chu Feng looked at the ghastly pale Jie Shanxian and her trembling hand as it held the incense stick. It made his heart ache. She wouldn’t have landed in this state if not to save him.","“Elder, I don’t know how to thank you,” Chu Feng sighed.","Jie Shanxian suddenly opened her eyes and looked at him. “I would still have been trapped if not for you. Now that I have saved you, we are equals. But again, if not for me, you would have never entered the Ancient Era’s War Clan, met that Ancient Era’s saint beast, and obtained the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s secret skills. In that regard, you owe me more.","“How about this? You shall accompany me to retrieve an item that will recover some of my cultivation, and we will call it quits. What do you think?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“Sure.” Chu Feng accepted the offer.","Jie Shanxian’s decision to expend herself to rescue Chu Feng from the formation proved that she was trustworthy. It showed that she had her moral compass and wasn’t blindly loyal to her clan.","To the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, her actions were tantamount to a betrayal. It was a crime that would have warranted her death. Very few people would be willing to go against their clans like that.","For that reason, Chu Feng was grateful to her.","Jie Shanxian brought out a five-meter-long bamboo boat with a fling of her sleeves. This bamboo boat emanated the Ancient Era’s aura and harnessed tremendous spirit power, leaving no question it was a formidable treasure.","Shoosh!","A bamboo scroll and a map flew toward Chu Feng.","“I’ll leave the traveling since I need to treat my injuries. You may control the boat with the bamboo scroll. This boat can travel at a speed on par with teleportation formations, so you can head there directly,” Jie Shanxian said.","Her words affirmed how incredible the bamboo boat was.","Chu Feng was taken aback when he received the bamboo scroll and map.","There was nothing special about the map; it was an ordinary map indicating the location Jie Shanxian wanted him to head to. The bamboo scroll, however, emanated an aura identical to the bamboo boat, and inscribed on it were the words ‘Qin Jiu’.","“This boat is Qin Jiu’s treasure?” Eggy was startled.","“No wonder it felt familiar,” Chu Feng remarked.","On second thought, the formation on the bamboo boat felt weirdly familiar—it was designed with Qin Jiu’s flair.","Jie Shanxian noticed Chu Feng staring at the words ‘Qin Jiu’ and commented, “It looks like you know about the World Spiritist Emperor.”","“The World Spiritist Emperor’s name is Qin Jiu. He was the strongest world spiritist in the Ancient Era. I have indeed heard about him,” Chu Feng replied.","“Let’s get moving,” Jie Shanxian said as she flitted onto the bamboo boat, sat down, and continued meditating to recuperate from her injuries.","Chu Feng needed some time to channel the bamboo boat via the bamboo scroll, but once the bamboo boat was fully activated, its speed was even more exaggerated than how Jie Shanxian had described it.","While it was not as fast as traveling via the Nine Heavens Secret Domain, it had the benefit of being able to travel at incredible speeds without having to enter a teleportation formation. It was truly an amazing treasure.","“Woah, it’s able to move so quickly without entering a teleportation formation! It is good stuff indeed!” Even Eggy was impressed.","“Lord Qin Jiu is formidable,” Chu Feng complimented.","This bamboo boat shattered his common sense about what was possible with treasures.","“Chu Feng, tell me more about your grudge with that Jie Tianran,” Jie Shanxian said.","Chu Feng had previously told Jie Shanxian a summarized account of the circumstances surrounding his mother and his grudge against Jie Tianran without going into the details. Now that Jie Shanxian was asking for more details, he didn’t hesitate to share more since he didn’t think he was at fault.","“Do you know why I left the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion then?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“Does it have anything to do with Jie Tianran?” Chu Feng asked.","“You’re a smart one. Yes, it has something to do with him. Back then, an incredible prodigy had just appeared in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion—Jie Tianran. Everyone in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion harbored high expectations of him, which led to him being nurtured as the next mansion master.","“But I was not fond of him. From a young age, he has already displayed a willingness to resort to unscrupulous means to achieve his goals. I didn’t think it would be a good thing for him to take over the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. However, I didn’t have the means to overrule the decision of others, so I chose to leave.","“I have to admit he is a capable person. I have not met him for many years and don’t know how strong he currently is, but just from the protective formation itself, I can tell he is now extremely powerful. If what you said is true, I can only say that your opponent is a very dangerous one,” Jie Shanxian said."]},{"number":6242,"title":"Chapter 6242: Chapter 6240: The Eyes on Chu Feng","paragraphs":["Chapter 6240: The Eyes on Chu Feng","Chu Feng wanted to ask more, but Jie Shanxian had begun meditating to recuperate, so he had no choice but to focus on the road.","...","Meanwhile, all the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Saint-tier elders were gathered in an observation formation, including the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief.","They were observing everything in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s vicinity to locate Chu Feng, but the latter was nowhere to be found.","“Are you sure it’s Chu Feng?” The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief found it hard to believe.","The formation was unharmed, but Chu Feng must have come prepared.","“There is no mistake. It is Chu Feng. He had a cat demon with him, and that cat demon wields power comparable to a rank five Heavenly God level cultivator, according to the feedback of our formation. Lord Mansion Master said that our formation can restrain even a rank five Heavenly God level cultivator, but both Chu Feng and that cat demon still got away.”","“There has to be someone formidable behind Chu Feng. That would explain how he monopolized so many fortuitous encounters, including the Immemorial Massacre Sea. I wonder what he got from there.”","“This isn’t good news for our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Other than Lord Mansion Master, no one is a match for that cat demon once we step out of the protective formation.”","“It’s not just the cat demon who poses a threat. Chu Feng was carrying a treasure too. That treasure emanated a powerful wave of spirit power that curbed our clan’s protective formation. Who knows? He might just figure a way to breach our protective formation with it!”","The Saint-tier elders were sweating profusely. They were in charge of monitoring the protective formation, and they personally saw Chu Feng and Old Cat through the formation.","When Chu Feng was restrained, they immediately led their army out to capture him, only to see him escaping with their own eyes. Not knowing the truth, they were misled into thinking that Chu Feng was a far more troublesome opponent than he truly was.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief and the remaining Saint-tier elders revealed uneasy looks.","“It’s a good thing Lord Mansion Master should be returning soon.” The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief looked toward God’s Era via the observation formation.","When God’s Era suddenly closed back then, a humongous formation incense stick appeared. Even though it was a formation, it was lifelike and was gradually burning down. By now, it was already on the verge of going out.","Most people speculated that God’s Era would open once the incense stick was burned out, allowing those trapped inside to escape.","“Lord Mansion Master should be able to acquire the power inside God’s Era, right?”","This matter calmed the worried Saint-tier elders a little.","Even though God’s Era had closed, there was a massive mirror reflecting the situation inside. Jie Tianran had been in a leading position from the start, and he was still maintaining his lead.","If they were truly competing for the power inside God’s Era, the person most likely to acquire it was none other than Jie Tianran.","...","Chu Feng channeled the bamboo boat toward the Bloodline Galaxy.","The Seven Realms Galaxy was humongous, and God’s Era happened to be along the way. While Chu Feng was passing by God’s Era, he couldn’t help but look at what was happening inside.","“Is it about to open?” Chu Feng asked.","“Chu Feng, do you think Jie Tianran will acquire the power inside God’s Era?” Eggy asked.","“He’ll get something out of God’s Era, but it won’t be that power,” Chu Feng replied.","“What makes you so certain?”","“Have you forgotten about God’s Era’s prophecy? It’s stated that the power will be abstained by a junior.”","“I thought you don’t believe prophecies?”","“I should believe prophecies that benefit me,” Chu Feng replied.","He glanced at Jie Shanxian, who had stopped recuperating to look at God’s Era. She had only heard about God’s Era, yet it was now right in front of her. Naturally, she was extremely curious about it.","“Elder, do you know how strong Jie Tianran is?” Chu Feng asked.","“I don’t know.” Jie Shanxian shook her head.","“How could you tell from the formation that he’s extremely powerful?” Chu Feng asked.","“That protective formation was left behind by our ancestors, and it is powered by a formidable Ancient Era’s treasure. Based on what I know, the formation is minimally strong enough to ward off a rank five Heavenly God level cultivator, whereas the upper limit is determined by how strong the person controlling the formation is.","“It was only capable of warding off rank five Heavenly God level cultivators back when the previous mansion master was still alive. To put it in other words, that’s the limitation of the previous mansion master.","“But that’s only normal. Our ancestors exploited all the resources available in the earlier days of the present era, to the point where there is nothing much left for us. That is why the powerhouses from the earlier days of the present era are far stronger than us. If you ask me, I don’t think those powerhouses are any more talented than those of our generation.","“Luck is necessary everywhere, whether for martial cultivation or even just everyday life. Reincarnating into the right clan can easily go a long way. Honestly, we were also lucky to be more talented than others too.”","Chu Feng nodded in agreement. “You’re right, elder.”","Despite the tribulations he had been through, he had to admit that he had good luck, or else he would have never stumbled upon so many fortuitous encounters.","“Anyway, the protective formation has been maintained at that level since those powerhouses’ departure, and that Ancient Era’s saint beast happened to be at rank five Heavenly God level, but he was still trapped by the formation.","“This means that the protective formation has surpassed its minimum prowess under Jie Tianran’s control. From this, we can get a glimpse into Jie Tianran’s strength,” Jie Shanxian said.","“Elder, are you saying that Jie Tianran might have reached rank six Heavenly Dragon?” Chu Feng asked.","“It’s hard to say. Ability does not necessarily translate to spirit power. Your ability to improve the formation blueprint provided by that Ancient Era’s saint beast despite your low spirit power is the best proof of that. That being said, Jie Tianran should be quite powerful now. You should tread carefully. Don’t underestimate your enemy. If I wasn’t with you, you would have been captured by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion,” Jie Shanxian said.","“Elder, I heard the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is protected by an ancestor from the early days of the present era. Is that true?” Chu Feng asked.","Jie Shanxian didn’t answer the question. “Let’s get going.”","She closed her eyes and continued meditating.","Chu Feng turned his focus back on channeling the bamboo boat. It was surprisingly hard to control that even he would have to get a little serious here. Any other rank one True Dragon World Spiritist would have struggled to move the bamboo boat.","“Chu Feng, will that black metal lump be sturdy enough for your use?” Eggy asked.","“I’m not sure, but I’ll give it a try later. If even that black metal lump isn’t sturdy enough, it’ll likely be impossible to find anything suitable in the world of cultivation. I’d have to make my way to the Ninth Galaxy for it,” Chu Feng said with a sigh.","He was looking forward to the Ninth Galaxy after hearing all the stories about it.","Little did he know that even though the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion failed to find him, there was still a pair of eyes locked on him."]},{"number":6243,"title":"Chapter 6243: Chapter 6241: Forging the Clone With the Black Metal","paragraphs":["Chapter 6241: Forging the Clone With the Black Metal","It was Old Cat.","He had entered the teleportation passageway leading straight to the Ninth Galaxy; it was the route he had prepared beforehand. If any mishap happened, he would escape from the world of cultivation using a teleportation talisman paper and head to the Ninth Galaxy.","His eyes glowed golden as if he could see through everything. This was the effect of the talisman paper burning in his hand.","“Damn it. She’s from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion! She could have moved earlier and spared me from squandering such a valuable teleportation talisman paper!” Old Cat grumbled.","His burning talisman paper was locked on Chu Feng. Through it, he was able to observe Jie Shanxian too. He could decipher the content of their conversation by reading their lips.","He felt that Jie Shanxian had intentionally held back so that he would waste his treasures. He was tempted to rush over to teach Jie Shanxian a lesson, but he didn’t want to waste this invaluable teleportation talisman paper. Since he had already invoked it, he would rather not cancel it.","He didn’t want to stay in the world of cultivation anyway.","Besides, Chu Feng would stop him from teaching Jie Shanxian a lesson and perhaps coerce him into doing things for him. That would rob him of his freedom.","With such thoughts in mind, he dropped the thought of teaching Jie Shanxian a lesson, and his hostility toward her plummeted as well.","When the talisman paper burned out, the golden glow in Old Cat’s eyes receded. He was no longer able to track Chu Feng, though he continued looking in the same direction.","“Chu Feng, you have to come to the Ninth Galaxy. I’m curious to see if you can stir waves even in the Ninth Galaxy.” Old Cat’s eyes were gleamed with expectations.","...","Old Cat was no longer able to track Chu Feng, but there was another pair of eyes in space that was locked on Chu Feng, precisely tracking him no matter how fast the bamboo boat was.","Unlike Old Cat, who was limited by his talisman paper, this pair of eyes wasn’t limited by time. Furthermore, no one was able to detect its existence or discern its location.","...","Soon, Chu Feng and Jie Shanxian arrived at a larger realm in the Bloodline Galaxy.","From afar, this realm looked like a sun, with brilliant raging flames. There were no mountains, rivers, or land to be seen; only boundless lava of indiscernible depth existed.","The lava was no ordinary lava. Cultivators beneath True God level couldn’t hope to approach it. No one resided here as there were no cultivation resources to be found in this realm. It was for the same reason that there was no teleportation formation connected to this realm too.","Fortunately, they traveled here using the bamboo boat and not a teleportation formation.","Chu Feng entered the lava realm and stopped above the bubbling lava.","Massive tsunamis or at least a thousand meters in height rose from the lava, sometimes even reaching tens of thousands of meters. They looked terrifying, to say the least.","Chu Feng examined the lava. This was the location marked on Jie Shanxian’s map. He had already informed Jie Shanxian, but the latter’s eyes remained closed, seemingly still focused on her recuperation. He didn’t want to disturb her, so he chose to look around first.","He quickly found some clues—there was an ancient formation passageway hidden in the lava. He informed Eggy about what he discovered.","Both believed what Jie Shanxian desired was inside the formation passageway.","“Chu Feng, even you were only able to discover the formation passageway after confirming the location. How did Jie Shanxian find this place?” Eggy was intrigued.","“She must either possess a powerful observation means, or that she learned about this place by chance. It doesn’t matter either way since we’re here to help her.”","Chu Feng wasn’t concerned about what was hidden here. It had nothing to do with him anyway.","He took out the black metal lump. That was what he was most concerned about right now. Forging a Bloodline Soul Puppet would be greatly beneficial to him, and he needed an incredibly sturdy material for the forging.","If this black metal lump didn’t meet the cut, it was unlikely he could find anything suitable in the world of cultivation.","Chu Feng thought the black metal lump should be sturdy enough, but he was so focused on channeling the bamboo boat that he didn’t have the spare energy to try it out. Now, he finally had a chance to try tempering the black metal lump.","“Are you going to try it here? But that means Jie Shanxian would learn about your secrets too,” Eggy said.","“It’s not a problem. She doesn’t know what I’m going to do anyway. Besides, I would have already been captured by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion if not for her. I should show her some sincerity, and transparency is one way to do so,” Chu Feng said.","Eggy nodded in agreement. “That’s true. Your candidness might convince her to divulge the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s secrets. If her goodwill for you grows further, she might even bring you straight into the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to rescue your mother. Chu Feng, you are getting increasingly cunning!”","“It’s all thanks to Milady Queen’s teaching.” Chu Feng chuckled.","He formed a hand seal.","Seconds later, a black aura imbued with nine-colored lightning gushed out of his body toward the black metal lump. The box holding the black metal lump instantly melted, but the black metal lump remained intact.","Eggy was so excited that she shot to her feet in the World Spirit Space, but she held her tongue for fear of interrupting Chu Feng.","Chu Feng said in elation, “Eggy, this black metal lump is indeed extraordinary. I might be able to use it.”","“Might? Is it not certain yet?” Eggy asked.","“I’ll only know once the forging is completed, but it won’t take long.”","Chu Feng changed his hand seal, and their surroundings shook. Even the lava beneath began raging with greater fervor than before. The black aura imbued with nine-colored lightning grew visibly more powerful.","The black metal lump began to melt, but it retained its unique properties. This was a good sign.","The black aura began to fuse with the black metal lump. This was a highly complicated procedure, so much so that Chu Feng dared not to let his guard down. It took some time, but the fusion was successful.","The remaining black aura receded into Chu Feng’s body.","“Is it a success?” Eggy asked.","“Yes, it’s a success. I can use this metal now!” Chu Feng was overjoyed.","“That’s wonderful!” Eggy was exhilarated. “Does that mean you have finished forging your clone?”","“Not yet. This metal will require more tempering before I can forge it into my clone, and that will take some time. More importantly, I’ll require more metal,” Chu Feng said regrettably.","“Is it not enough?” Eggy asked.","“There are ways to forge the clone with what I have now, but it will compromise the clone’s resilience. That being said, I am already contented with what I have,” Chu Feng replied.","“That’s good to hear.” Eggy smiled.","Chu Feng turned to Jie Shanxian. He noticed that the latter had woken up and had been observing him for some time now."]},{"number":6244,"title":"Chapter 6244: Chapter 6242: Seven Realms Immortal Sect","paragraphs":["Chapter 6242: Seven Realms Immortal Sect","Jie Shanxian was drawn to Chu Feng’s method of tempering that black metal lump.","Chu Feng thought Jie Shanxian would ask about his means, but the latter didn’t. Instead, she opened her palm and revealed a formation in it. Two pills rose from the formation. One floated to Chu Feng, and she popped the other one into her mouth.","Chu Feng could tell the pill was freshly concocted.","Jie Shanxian hadn’t been talking not because she was recuperating, but because she was focused on concocting these two pills inside her body.","Chu Feng sensed that the pills contained a powerful aura concealment effect, which left him wondering why she didn’t just conceal their bodies. It would have been much easier to do that.","Sensing his doubt, Jie Shanxian explained, “The place we’re heading to is occupied by Ancient Era’s races. This pill hinders them from discerning us as intruders. You don’t have to tell them too much other than the fact you’re an unaffiliated cultivator. As long as nothing goes wrong, they would assume we’re from the Ancient Era as they don’t think present-era cultivators can get in.”","She formed a hand seal and changed her appearance into that of a middle-aged woman, and her physique became flat. She didn’t want to attract unwanted attention.","“You have your disguise means, right? Or do you require my help?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“It would be best if you could help me,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","He had ways to disguise himself, but Jie Shanxian’s disguise means were bound to be superior given she was a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","“Take this pill.” Jie Shanxian passed a pill to Chu Feng,","Chu Feng swallowed the pill, and the pill transformed into a formation that enveloped his body. He could now alter his appearance at will. He disguised himself as an ordinary man too.","“Elder, is there anything else I should pay attention to?” Chu Feng asked.","“We’re entering a huge realm where many Ancient Era’s races reside. There are many different factions there, but there are plenty of unaffiliated cultivators too. Two regions in the northern boundary and southern boundary are sealed. I once asked the cultivators there what’s in the sealed regions, but no one can say for sure what’s in there.","“The two regions are sealed by powerful barriers. The southern boundary’s barrier is from a treasure, whereas the northern boundary’s barrier is from a world spiritist’s formation. My guess is that the two regions are under the control of powerful Ancient Era’s clans, with the southern one being cultivators and the northern one being world spiritists.","“Our goal is the sealed region in the northern boundary. We are looking for a poisonous purple flower that locals call Purpledream Ascension. Its name comes from its lethal poison; anyone afflicted with the poison will enter a purple dreamscape. It’s said that the dream is beautiful, but one will quickly lose one’s life force till death.","“For that reason, locals dare not to harvest Purpledream Ascension. However, it is a world spiritist’s cultivation resource, and I have a way to refine it. The refining method requires a potent bloodline power. With your bloodline power, I should be able to quickly refine it,” Jie Shanxian said.","“Elder, have you encountered anyone powerful inside that realm?” Chu Feng asked.","“I have yet to meet anyone stronger than me, but the same can’t be said about the two sealed regions as I’m unable to breach them. I don’t know if I can deal with whoever resides there. The Ancient Era’s races have been awakening since God’s Era’s opening, so the powers residing there are unlikely to be dormant. Our target is just a poisonous flower that no one wants, but it’s best for us to lie low and avoid trouble,” Jie Shanxian said.","“Elder, I agree.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Let’s go.” Jie Shanxian stowed away the bamboo boat before pulling Chu Feng down into the bubbling lava beneath.","A layer of spirit power protected Chu Feng from the lava. Jie Shanxian brought Chu Feng to the place where he sensed earlier, opened the passageway, and entered it.","The journey was smooth sailing, and they soon landed on the ground.","Chu Feng raised his head, but the passageway was nowhere to be found. He could only see the blue sky and white clouds as if the passageway had never existed.","This place felt much larger and more vibrant than the formation realms most Ancient Era’s races resided in. He could already see several cultivators around him. Some were flying in the air, whereas others were traveling on land via chariots. Most of them were in groups.","He could tell from their clothes that the cultivators were from different powers, but they didn’t harbor hostility against one another. Many of them chatted joyously while traveling together as if close friends.","“Are they all Ancient Era’s cultivators? What a harmonious sight! It feels like a trip back in time.” Eggy was excited.","The Ancient Era’s cultivators they had met thus far were arrogant fellows whose chins were always tilted upward when talking to them. This was their first time seeing the Ancient Era’s cultivators in their daily lives.","Strictly speaking, these people were born in the present era too. It was just that they clung to their ancestor’s past glory, so they identified themselves as Ancient Era’s cultivators.","“They seem to be heading somewhere. Chu Feng, is there a commotion awaiting us? Or maybe a fortuitous encounter?” Eggy asked.","She noticed that the crowd was all heading in the same direction.","Curious, Chu Feng pricked up his ears to listen to their conversation.","It was the Huangfu Heavenly Clan. They had invited the Ancient Era’s cultivators to decipher their treasure.","Chu Feng knew about the Huangfu Heavenly Clan. Their most talented prodigy, Huangfu Shengyu, had caused quite a commotion in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith back then.","“Oh? Is this the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s base? What a coincidence!” Eggy chuckled.","Chu Feng turned to Jie Shanxian and asked, “Elder, have you heard of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan?”","“Not at all, but judging from the number of people heading there, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan might be one of the major powers hiding in this realm.” Jie Shanxian turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Are you interested in joining the commotion?”","“I’m tempted to,” Chu Feng smiled.","“Let’s deal with what we came here for first. I’ll bring you there if we can make it in time,” Jie Shanxian replied before taking Chu Feng northward.","This was at odds with where others were heading.","To not attract attention, Jie Shanxian opted not to use the bamboo boat, but their journey didn’t take long as there were teleportation formations they could use.","By the time they emerged from a teleportation formation, there was already hardly anyone around them. The number of people further decreased as they continued heading north. Soon, their surroundings were all nature, with no signs of cultivators anymore.","A while later, they encountered a visible barrier in the far distance. It extended from the earth to the sky as if it was the end of the world.","If there were truly two reclusive powers in this realm, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was probably the one occupying the south, whereas another one occupied the north.","The answer was soon revealed.","A ten thousand meters tall gate could be seen at the bottom of the barrier. This gate was manifested from a formation, but it was majestic and imposing. Four words above the gate revealed the territory’s master—the Seven Realms Immortal Sect."]},{"number":6245,"title":"Chapter 6245: Chapter 6243: Even a Powerful Dragon Can’t Suppress the Local Snake","paragraphs":["Purple flowers could be seen on the barrier’s outskirts. They were the Purpledream Ascensions that Jie Shanxian previously mentioned.","However, they were sparsely scattered around, suggesting that someone had already harvested more than half of them.","But Chu Feng was more focused on the words ‘Seven Realms Immortal Sect’.","“Seven Realms Immortal Sect? I remember there being a Seven Realms Immortal Pavilion among the Ancient Era’s races who previously attacked the Ancestral Martial Galaxy. Does that mean there is also a Seven Realms Immortal Hall, Seven Realms Immortal Mansion, Seven Realms Immortal Gate, and Seven Realms Immortal Sect? Wow, is the ultimate goal of all world spiritists to be the master of the Seven Realms? Hahaha!” Eggy teased.","Chu Feng turned to Jie Shanxian and asked, “Elder, have you heard of the Seven Realms Immortal Sect?”","“I haven’t, but it’s evident from the name that the Ancient Era’s race occupying this place are world spiritists. The gate wasn’t here before. They must have emerged from their seclusion. Furthermore, the Purpledream Ascensions left behind are all inferior products. They must have taken the good ones. We can’t look down on this Seven Realms Immortal Sect,” Jie Shanxian looked at the remaining purple flowers with regretful eyes.","Those words enlightened Chu Feng to why the Seven Realms Immortal Sect had only harvested half of the Purpledream Ascensions. It turned out the remaining ones were inferior products.","“But it seems possible to assimilate them,” Chu Feng approached one of the Purpledreams Ascensions and examined it before remarking.","“It’s possible, but I don’t know whether someone owns those flowers. Chu Feng, the Seven Realms Immortal Sect doesn’t seem to be a pushover, so it’ll be best to keep a low profile here. I’ll ask them for permission. If there’s no response, I’ll go ahead and assimilate the flowers. If they reply negatively, we’ll give up on the flowers.","“Remember, not even a powerful dragon can suppress a local snake. No matter how awful their words are, you mustn’t take it to heart. We aren’t here to cause trouble, all right?” Jie Shanxian instructed.","“Rest assured, elder. My skin is thick. I can bear being insulted, though I am vindictive as well. Should they insult me, I’ll get back at them if a chance arises in the future,” Chu Feng replied.","Jie Shanxian chuckled at those words. She walked up to the gate, bowed respectfully, and spoke aloud, “I am Shan Jie, an unaffiliated world spiritist. I came here for the Purpledream Ascensions after hearing they are rare cultivation resources, but I don’t know if they belong to anyone.”","There was an answer from the gate.","“These Purpledream Ascensions are planted by our Seven Realms Immortal Sect, but we left them outside for others to harvest them. Feel free to assimilate them if you have the means to. My only fear is that you don’t have the means to do so and instead fall for their poison. I’ll say it right now—your only fate is death if you fall for the poison. We won’t save you.”","The person who replied was a woman. Even though she allowed them to assimilate the purple flowers, her voice was filled with disdain.","“All right.” Jie Shanxian didn’t thank the woman, and she didn’t look as respectful as before too.","Chu Feng could tell she was angry.","Jie Shanxian sent a voice transmission to Chu Feng, “Chu Feng, don’t bother displaying your world spiritist bloodline. I can assimilate these inferior products by myself. You just have to wait for me by the side. I won’t take long.”","Chu Feng obediently stood by the side.","Jie Shanxian channeled a secret skill that enveloped all the Purpledream Ascensions with her spirit power. She didn’t hold back, so Chu Feng could tell how formidable her secret skill was.","“I told you that Purpledream Ascensions are poisonous, but instead of treading carefully, you choose to assimilate all of them. You must be tired of living,” the woman’s voice echoed from the gate.","Her eyes were not as sharp as Chu Feng; she couldn’t tell how formidable Jie Shanxian’s secret skill was.","“Ignorant people like to court their doom. Pay her no heed,” an old man’s voice echoed from the gate.","“Indeed. It’s a common problem among ignorant people to be greedy despite their incompetence. Forget it, she can die all she wants,” the woman sneered.","Her words sounded more like a reprimand rather than out of concern.","“These Ancient Era’s races are annoying,” Eggy snorted even though those people weren’t talking about Chu Feng.","Chu Feng had his eyes on Jie Shanxian. He noticed the change in her complexion, and her anger was beginning to surface.","The woman and old man inside the gate soon fell silent.","Jie Shanxian had revealed her prowess as a rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, and under the effects of her secret skill, the purple flowers turned into auras that converged to her.","“Elder, you’re assimilating the flowers too quickly. Do you want to consider feigning being poisoned by the Purpledream Ascensions?” Chu Feng asked via voice transmission.","He was worried that Jie Shanxian would cause a huge commotion. Even though the Seven Realms Immortal Sect had said that they could freely assimilate the flowers, they might get greedy after seeing Jie Shanxian’s secret skill.","“It’s just a mere Seven Realms Immortal Sect; what’s there to fear? I’ll show them my prowess,” Jie Shanxian replied Chu Feng via voice transmission.","Chu Feng was right. Jie Shanxian had gotten caught up in her anger after hearing the woman’s contemptuous attitude.","“Elder... didn’t you say that a powerful dragon can’t suppress a local snake? We aren’t here to stir trouble,” Chu Feng advised.","“Stop talking! The likes of them can’t even be considered a snake. Let’s see what they can do about me even if I stir trouble,” Jie Shanxian scoffed.","“Why is this Jie Shanxian so brainless? You’re saying this for her own good, yet she’s putting you down.” Eggy was displeased by Jie Shanxian’s disrespectful attitude.","But Chu Feng didn’t lose his temper. He turned to Eggy and said, “Milady Queen, you’re right. Elder Jie Shanxian, despite her age, seems to have an innocent personality. She’s usually fine, but her rationality erodes as soon as she gets angry.”","It was frustrating, though it made her look adorable too.","Humans tended to become sharper with age; the more they went through, the more lessons they learned. Wisdom naturally followed.","It was rare for people to retain their original personality even after so many years like Jie Shanxian.","Soon, Jie Shanxian forged all the Purpledream Ascensions into a single pill. With the pill in hand, she turned to the gate and said, “I guess that’s all to the Purpledream Ascensions. Plant more higher-quality, poisonous ones next time. It isn’t much of a challenge otherwise.”","She chose to provoke the Seven Realms Immortal Sect.","After saying those words, she immediately left with Chu Feng, not giving the other party a chance to retort.","“Elder, should we disguise ourselves again?” Chu Feng asked.","“Why? Do you fear them? They can come after us if they dare. I’d like to see what right their Seven Realms Immortal Sect has to plagiarize our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s name! You aren’t allowed to change your face either. Don’t worry, I’ll back you up if anything happens!” Jie Shanxian said with a warning tone.","Chu Feng felt helpless. He felt like she was the junior between the two of them instead, but he could only reply, “I’ll listen to you.”"]},{"number":6246,"title":"Chapter 6246: Chapter 6244: Chu Feng’s Great Reputation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6244: Chu Feng’s Great Reputation","Shortly after Chu Feng and Jie Shanxian left, the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s gate opened, and a group of people dressed in white world spiritist cloaks rushed out.","Three people stood at the forefront of the group—a young woman, an old man, and a middle-aged man. It could be seen from their eyes that they were old monsters who had lived for a long time.","The middle-aged man scanned the surroundings before asking the woman, “Why didn’t you stop them?”","Both the woman and the old man looked nervous. They were the ones who made disdainful remarks earlier from inside the gate. Only upon seeing how easily Jie Shanxian refined the Purple Ascensions did they rush to inform the middle-aged man.","“Milord, she left right after refining the Purple Ascensions. We didn’t have time to stop her,” the woman explained.","Before the woman and the old man could snap out of their daze, Jie Shanxian had already left with Chu Feng.","“Do you remember her appearance?” the middle-aged man asked.","The woman quickly drew them with her spirit power—it was Chu Feng and Jie Shanxian’s disguised appearances.","“They look too normal. They must have disguised themselves.”","The middle-aged man’s face grew increasingly colder, which left the woman and the old man so afraid that they dared not raise their heads. They realized that they had slipped up.","The middle-aged man didn’t lose his temper in the end. Instead, he ordered, “Look for them, but don’t cause a fuss. Report their whereabouts to me after you find them.”","The world spiritists behind him immediately scattered, including the woman and the old man.","The middle-aged man walked up to where a cluster of Purple Ascensions used to be and picked up some of the refinement residue. His eyes looked grim, but they carried a hint of delight.","...","Chu Feng and Jie Shanxian headed off to join the commotion. It wasn’t difficult for them to figure out the way as most people were headed in the same direction.","In the meantime, they also kept an ear out on the street.","They learned that the Huangfu Heavenly Clan indeed occupied the southern sealed region. It was only recently that they and the Seven Realms Immortal Sect emerged from their seclusion. They did so at the same time, almost as if it was planned.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan once left the formation realm to participate in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith, but their results were lackluster. They were mocked by the Seven Realms Immortal Sect over that, and a battle even broke out.","It was a huge battle. It ended inconclusive, but both sides revealed that they had Heavenly God level cultivators and Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists.","The others realized that these two powerhouses weren’t to be trifled with, though they didn’t know exactly how powerful their Heavenly God level cultivators and Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists were.","Recently, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan announced that they had a treasure to share with everyone, and those who came would receive a benefit. However, no one knew what the treasure and benefits were.","In other words, Chu Feng didn’t receive any useful information.","“Brother, do you know who is the strongest junior in the world of cultivation now? Do you know who defeated the juniors in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith?” a man with a sharp mouth and sunken cheeks asked Chu Feng.","Most of the useless information Chu Feng obtained was from this man.","Before Chu Feng could answer, someone else traveling alongside them replied, “Who doesn’t know that? It’s someone named Chu Feng.”","The man smiled in glee. “You might have heard of Chu Feng, but how much do you know about him? Do you know what he looks like?”","The crowd shook their heads.","They couldn’t see what was happening outside. Everything they knew about Chu Feng was leaked from the Huangfu Heavenly Clan, though there were also claims that it was the Seven Realms Immortal Sect who divulged the information.","The Seven Realms Immortal Sect, as a world spiritist sect, was likely to have means to observe the outside world too.","“It’s rumored that Chu Feng is a vicious and bloodthirsty person. He would gouge out the eyes of anyone he sees,” the man said.","“Hoh. Chu Feng, I didn’t expect you to have such a reputation among the Ancient Era’s races,” Eggy teased.","Chu Feng was rendered speechless. How am I such an unreasonable person? The Huangfu Heavenly Clan is outright trying to sully my reputation.","The man glanced at Chu Feng as he continued, “Brother, it’s only a matter of time before this formation realm opens up. There are countless remnants out there, and we will inevitably cross paths with the present-era cultivators. You have to be careful if you do meet Chu Feng. Flee if you ever hear his name. Make sure you don’t ever look at him. I happen to have his portrait with me. Would you like to take a look? You can at least avoid him if you know what he looks like.”","He took out a rolled-up portrait.","“I’ll take a look,” Chu Feng said.","The others craned their necks to take a look. Even those who hadn’t participated in the conversation came closer to get a glimpse of the portrait.","“I spent a king’s ransom to obtain this portrait. I can give you a look, but you should at least compensate me for it, right?” the man asked.","“I shan’t look then.” Chu Feng waved his hand. Why would he spend money to look at his portrait?","But a bearded, brawny man among the crowd asked how much it would cost and paid the sum.","“Brother, do you want to look at it yourself and share it with the others?” the man asked.","“I’ll let the others have a look too,” the bearded man replied.","His generosity won him cheers from the crowd.","“All right.” The man quickly unfurled the portrait.","Chu Feng was rendered speechless upon seeing the portrait.","The portrait showed a dark-skinned, hideous man with the vilest face imaginable. He was even more hideous than the sharp-mouthed, sunken cheeks man, so much so that he resembled a walking ape than a human.","“Why is Chu Feng so ugly?” the bearded man asked.","“He might be ugly, but you mustn’t underestimate him because of it. Make sure to avoid him if you ever see him!” the man exclaimed.","“He does look like a vicious person. To think that the present-era cultivators are so vile!”","The crowd criticized the Chu Feng in the portrait.","“Brother, did you draw this portrait yourself?” Chu Feng couldn’t resist asking."]},{"number":6247,"title":"Chapter 6247: Chapter 6245: The Immemorial Bloodline Tower","paragraphs":["Chapter 6245: The Immemorial Bloodline Tower","“Of course not. It’s a scroll from the Huangfu Heavenly Clan. I bought it at an exorbitant price!” the sharp-nosed, sunken cheek man replied.","“A load of bull. Chu Feng doesn’t look like that,” Chu Feng replied.","“Why don’t you tell us what he looks like then?”","“He doesn’t look like that. Why don’t we do this? You can leave your address here. He’ll come to knock on your door and beat you up when the time comes.”","“Hmph! I shall not squabble with an ignorant and black-hearted person. I haven’t even complained about you not having the money to see my portrait, yet you turned against me and tried to sully my reputation. I shall not waste my words on you,” the man said as he sped off.","He soon disappeared in the distance.","“He ran away! Is that portrait fake?”","The crowd talked among themselves.","But the bearded, brawny man thought nothing of the matter. Instead, he looked at Chu Feng.","“You were duped, brother. Aren’t you going to chase him?” Chu Feng asked.","“Don’t worry about it; it’s chump change. Let me introduce myself—I’m Li Gangtie. What’s your name?” the bearded, brawny man asked.","“My family name is Chu,” Chu Feng replied.","“Ah, it’s Brother Chu. You have the same family name as Chu Feng,” Li Gangtie said with a chuckle. “Have you really met Chu Feng before?”","“Yes, I have met him. He looks much better than that.”","“So, what does he look like?”","“I forgot.”","Chu Feng was reluctant to tell the truth to avoid trouble. The Huangfu Heavenly Clan and the Seven Realms Immortal Sect likely already knew about his Genesis Bloodline.","Both the Genesis Bloodline and the Ruler’s Bloodline were huge temptations to cultivators and world spiritists. Revealing his identity here was as good as courting his doom.","But Li Gangtie refused to let things slip. He was extremely curious about Chu Feng and kept bugging him for more information. He even offered to purchase Chu Feng’s real portrait.","Chu Feng didn’t answer his questions, but he was surprised by Li Gangtie’s interest in present-day cultivators. The latter appeared to respect Chu Feng a lot. He wondered how Li Gangtie would react if he learned that he was Chu Feng.","Soon, Chu Feng and the others were finally approaching their destination. There was still some distance to cover, but they could already spot a towering mountain peak rising into the clouds.","That mountain peak was golden. It wasn’t made out of rock or gold but something more formidable. Upon closer examination, there was a massive window on the mountain peak too. Rather than a mountain peak, it looked more like a unique tower.","Most important of all, the mountain peak emanated an aura that felt older than the Ancient Era. It was very likely to be from the Immemorial Era.","“Chu Feng, is that a mountain peak or a tower?” Eggy asked out of curiosity.","“It looked more like a tower. It must be the treasure the Huangfu Heavenly Clan mentioned,” Chu Feng said.","“Are you able to tell what’s special about that tower?” Eggy asked.","“Not yet, but I reckon something good is hidden in there, and the Huangfu Heavenly Clan requires external help to obtain it. Otherwise, they wouldn’t be so kind as to share the treasure with everyone,” Chu Feng deduced.","“That makes sense. This is an opportunity for us,” Eggy smiled.","“Indeed.” Chu Feng nodded in agreement.","Amidst their conversation, they got even closer to the mountain peak. Countless figures stood along the perimeter of the golden mountain peak, covering not just the ground but the sky too. They looked like a locust swarm from afar, but they were all cultivators and world spiritists.","This showed that there were a lot of Ancient Era’s cultivators living in this formation realm, and most of them belonged to a sect or clan. Yet, all of them chose to maintain a distance away from the mountain peak-shaped golden tower.","As they got closer, Chu Feng and Jie Shanxian finally understood why that was the case.","Millions of Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were gathered beneath the golden tower, surrounding a platform.","A white-haired, middle-aged man stood on the platform. He was dressed identical to the other Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen, and he carried a black wooden box on his back too. He gave off the aura of a rank one Heavenly God level cultivator.","The crowd was steering clear of his aura.","Soon, the crowd parted to give way to a golden war chariot bearing the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s flag. The chariot landed on a square, and tens of thousands of juniors stepped out from within. They were the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elites.","The weakest of these juniors were at rank one Half-God level, and three of them had reached rank one True God level. Of the three, there were two men and one woman.","Chu Feng recognized one of the two men—Huangfu Shangwu.","Huangfu Shangwu had accompanied Huangfu Shengyu to the Nine Heavens’ Zenith to put down the present-era cultivators, but perhaps due to his lacking ability, he didn’t appear in the final test, though that was the reason he survived at all.","Chu Feng didn’t think he would meet Huangfu Shangwu once more.","The other two were foreign faces. They were good-looking, but they gave off an air of arrogance. Even Huangfu Shangwu could only walk behind the two of them. It was evident their standing was above Huangfu Shangwu’s.","Chu Feng wasn’t surprised to learn that, as Huangfu Shangwu didn’t seem to be respected by the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s juniors back when he was at the Nine Heavens’ Zenith.","All the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s juniors made their way toward the rank one Heavenly God level middle-aged man. With Huangfu Shangwu and the other two at the forefront, the whole group bowed deeply to the middle-aged man.","“Paying respect to Lord Zhantian.”","Even though the middle-aged man, Huangfu Zhantian, was not the clan chief, he had a high standing in the Huangfu Heavenly Clan due to his outstanding talent.","“Rise.” Huangfu Zhantian casually waved his hand.","An elder from the Huangfu Heavenly Clan walked over to Huangfu Zhantian’s side and asked, “Lord Zhantian, everyone is here. May we begin?”","“Yes, let’s begin. I can’t be bothered to explain, so I’ll leave the job to you,” Huangfu Zhantian told the elder.","“Understood.”","Despite looking much older than Huangfu Zhantian, the elder maintained a respectful attitude toward him. He turned to the crowd and started with some pleasantries before explaining the situation.","“The mountain behind me is an Immemorial Era’s treasure known as the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. It can enhance bloodline powers, making it an invaluable treasure to us cultivators. Our kind clan chief believes in sharing resources with others, so we shall open this treasure we have cherished for a long time to everyone here!”","Resounding cheers broke out. The crowd went into a fervor.","If that elder was speaking the truth, the Immemorial Bloodline Tower was a treasure far surpassing their wildest imagination. Bloodlines were the cultivators’ foundation. Enhancing one’s bloodline was far more useful than raising one’s cultivation.","The elder was satisfied with the crowd’s response. There was a brief pause before he added, “But there are requirements to enter the tower.”"]},{"number":6248,"title":"Chapter 6248: Chapter 6246: The Divine Deer Wants It","paragraphs":["Chapter 6246: The Divine Deer Wants It","“We’ll only be picking cultivators with sufficiently strong bloodlines to enter the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. We have to turn down those whose bloodlines are too weak as they won’t benefit from the tower.","“A tower token is required to enter the tower, and there is a limited number of tower tokens. Each tower token can be shared by multiple people. When benefits are obtained from the tower, the tower token holder can determine how the benefits are shared. So, I’d advise those who don’t belong to any powers or came alone to look for acquainted powers to bring them in.","“Alternatively, you may also form a group with other unaffiliated cultivators, but the group must have at least ten thousand people before we will consider allocating a tower token. Individuals will not be allowed to take a tower token by themselves, no matter how powerful their bloodlines are.”","The words from the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elder sparked a huge uproar, especially among the world spiritists. They had traveled all the way here, only to be blocked at the entrance. It was no surprise that they had plenty of complaints.","However, they dared not to grumble loudly out of deference for the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","“That’s surprisingly troublesome. I bet there’s a catch,” Eggy said.","“The Huangfu Heavenly Clan isn’t that kind-hearted. There has to be a catch, though I can’t tell what it is yet.”","Chu Feng had been observing the golden tower to gather as much information about it as possible before heading in.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elders activated their treasures to construct a barrier to seal off the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.","However, there were hundreds of gates on the barrier. Those who wished to enter the tower could do so via these gates. These gates contained a test to gauge how strong a cultivator’s bloodline was.","Those whose bloodlines were too weak would be enveloped by a red light and denied entry. Furthermore, the tests also rejected world spiritists with powerful bloodlines; only those with formidable martial cultivation bloodlines were granted entry.","Doubts surfaced in Chu Feng’s mind. He wondered if this was a trap for cultivators. In the world of cultivation, it was not uncommon for the strong to exploit the weak for their interests.","“Chu Feng, I sense something is amiss. Should we pass on this? I know you believe in finding opportunities amidst risk, but it won’t be worth it if you lose your life.” Eggy smelled danger too.","Just then, a voice sounded inside Chu Feng’s body, “The Immemorial Bloodline Tower was a valuable treasure even in the Ancient Era.”","It was the Divine Deer.","Upon hearing the Divine Deer’s words, Eggy stopped talking and obediently listened.","Chu Feng hurriedly probed, “Elder, what do you know about the Immemorial Bloodline Tower?”","“The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elder speaks the truth. This tower contains energy beneficial to one’s bloodline. However, there are different types of Immemorial Bloodline Towers. The stronger ones can enrich both cultivator and world spiritist bloodlines. If he’s discouraging world spiritists from entering, it might be a poorer-quality tower. If so, it might be useless to you.","“That being said, it’s also possible that it is a misdirection. In any case, you should go in and take a look. The Immemorial Bloodline Tower is powered by an Immemorial Era’s natural oddity located at the top of the tower. If you can reach the top of the tower and obtain that natural oddity for me, it’ll greatly hasten the recovery of my powers,” the Divine Deer said.","“Looks like I’ll have to enter the Immemorial Bloodline Tower,” Chu Feng said. He still harbored reservations, but his motivation was greater than ever.","The Divine Deer’s formidable powers allowed him to escape from any enemy, but she needed to recharge after each use. If he could hasten the recovery of her powers, he would be in a much safer position. Naturally, he couldn’t miss this opportunity.","Chu Feng could sense how much the Divine Deer desired that natural oddity. He had always believed that the Divine Deer possessed means aside from those intended for escape, just that it had never shown it.","Furthermore, the Divine Deer had saved him many times before. If she wanted that natural oddity, he felt obliged to obtain it for her.","“Elder, what else do you know about the Immemorial Bloodline Towers? What should I look out for if I wish to enter?” Chu Feng asked.","“The tower token determines the allocation of resources, so you have to obtain your own. Otherwise, you’ll just become a puppet for others. Even though the Immemorial Bloodline Tower has no age restriction, powerhouses used it to test their juniors back then. So, when the tower is fully activated, it’ll become transparent, allowing those outside to see everything happening inside as if watching a play. Disguise means will be dispelled, and everyone’s true appearance will be revealed.”","Eggy was astonished to hear that. “Doesn’t that mean exposing Chu Feng’s identity?”","She was worried as Chu Feng possessed well-known powers like the Genesis Bloodline and the Ruler’s Bloodline. He was like a walking treasure chest to all powers.","Furthermore, the Ancient Era’s races harbored hostility toward present-era cultivators. Being exposed here could spell his death.","“It could indeed be dangerous for you. Also, while the way to obtain power is different in each Immemorial Bloodline Tower, there is only one strongest power in each tower. You’ll have to compete for the strongest power. Even if not for the treasures you’re carrying, as long as you’re seeking the strongest power, it is inevitable that you’ll offend the Huangfu Heavenly Clan. You should consider carefully whether to enter the tower or not,” the Divine Deer said.","“It’s fine, Eggy. I have ways to protect myself,” Chu Feng consoled Eggy before turning to the Divine Deer, “Elder, I remember all the times you have helped me. Since there is something you require at the top of the tower, I’ll obtain it for you. Is there anything else I should take note of?”","“You don’t need to fawn on me. I have already told you everything I know,” the Divine Deer said.","“Hehe, I’m not fawning on you. I’m just telling the truth as it is.” Chu Feng smiled.","He meant those words from the bottom of his heart."]},{"number":6249,"title":"Chapter 6249: Chapter 6247: Competing For People","paragraphs":["Chapter 6247: Competing For People","Chu Feng began surveying the situation.","Those from sects had started crossing the barrier to claim their tower tokens. Some sects with more people split into multiple groups to claim more tower tokens so that everyone in their sect could enter, but their ploy failed.","It turned out each sect could only claim one tower token, and each tower token could only be shared with at most 20,000 people.","The sects had no choice but to select their elites to use the tower token.","At the same time, the unaffiliated cultivators started organizing themselves into groups. The question of who to hold the tower token was a huge point of contention, and most people chose to argue based on their cultivation.","“Elder, let’s make a move too,” Chu Feng said.","Since the Divine Deer had already advised him, Chu Feng needed to gather his people too.","“My world spiritist talent is passable, but my martial cultivation talent is lacking. I’ll pass on this commotion,” Jie Shanxian said.","“Elder, you aren’t planning to give it a try?” Chu Feng asked.","On top of possessing strength rivaling a rank two Heavenly God level cultivator, Jie Shanxian also had many treasures with her. Her lack of fear for the Seven Realms Immortal Sect also suggested that she had more tricks up her sleeves.","Chu Feng would lose his greatest backing if Jie Shanxian didn’t enter.","Instead of answering, Jie Shanxian got up and flew toward one of the gates. A red light shot out from the gate and enveloped her. Before the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen could drive her back, she turned around and headed back to Chu Feng’s side.","“You see that?”","Jie Shanxian was telling Chu Feng that she couldn’t enter the tower even if she wanted to due to her lacking martial cultivation talent. Sensing Chu Feng’s worry, she added, “Don’t worry. I’ll be right here. I won’t turn a blind eye if you get into trouble. Worse comes to worst, I’ll barge in. That measly rank one Heavenly God level cultivator can’t stop me.”","She glanced at Huangfu Zhantian as she spoke.","That boosted Chu Feng’s confidence, but he still said, “Elder, I need to gather people to obtain a tower token. It’ll be more effective if you rally people on my behalf.”","“So that’s your true goal. Don’t bother entering the tower if you can’t handle such trivialities by yourself,” Jie Shanxian scoffed.","Chu Feng had to settle this matter by himself since Jie Shanxian didn’t want to get involved. Only by giving something would there be returns, so he was planning to offer some incentives to the crowd to rally them over.","He took out many Cosmos Sacks, opening some of them while he was at it so that everyone could sense the treasures inside. Every Cosmos Sack was filled with the same treasures, and that was the benefit he was offering those who followed him.","Millions of people immediately crowded around Chu Feng, wanting to get a slice of the pie. Some even stared at him with greedy eyes as if he were a fat lamb waiting to be slaughtered. They were planning to rob him.","But Chu Feng was unfazed. This bunch of ragtag wasn’t a match for him, and if he did encounter an opponent beyond his means, he had Jie Shanxian here to back him anyway.","Chu Feng couldn’t accept everyone onto his team, so he listed his requests too. He didn’t impose any age restrictions, but he demanded his team members to be at least at Half-God level.","Aside from that, they also must have a decent martial cultivation bloodline. For that, he constructed a formation to assess an individual’s martial cultivation bloodline, and those who cleared the formation would be eligible.","It was a great deal of trouble, but many people still went through with the test for the generous incentives.","Unaffiliated cultivators were bound to be lacking compared to the affiliated ones. Despite more and more people flocking to Chu Feng’s side, with the crowd reaching tens of millions, less than a thousandth of them met the criteria.","Due to the sheer number of sign-ups, Chu Feng soon gathered 20,000 people. However, he didn’t stop the recruitment despite having already met the quota.","Those who were applying also paid it no heed as they were after the incentives.","“Chu Feng, I thought you only need 20,000 people?” Eggy was confused.","“We need more so that we can further filter them,” Chu Feng explained.","“That’s true.” Eggy thought those words made sense.","Having more rounds of selections could raise the quality of the final team.","“H-h-huh? What are you d-d-doing? Do you have no s-s-shame?”","A group suddenly tore through the crowd and marched up to Chu Feng. The one leading the group was a tall, brawny man with a dashing face. He was so suave that the women couldn’t help staring at him with gleaming eyes.","His only problem was his stutter.","However, Chu Feng was more interested in the dignified old man behind the dashing man. Others might not have noticed it yet, but he could tell with a glance that the old man was an expert. He was the dashing man’s backing.","“You need something?” Chu Feng asked.","“D-d-don’t you think you’re too much? Can’t we c-c-compete fairly?” the dashing man asked.","Chu Feng had long noticed the dashing man; the latter had been using the same method to recruit people, and he did succeed in attracting a crowd. However, due to Chu Feng’s more generous incentives, many of the people he had recruited abandoned him for Chu Feng instead.","That made the dashing man angry.","“What’s unfair about this? You can offer more if you want,” Chu Feng casually replied while waving a Cosmos Sack.","“D-d-do you have too much money to burn? You already have 20,000 people, so w-w-why are you still recruiting? Are you t-t-trying to corner the rest of us?” The man glared at Chu Feng with grudging eyes.","“I need more people, but I will be eliminating some of them later. You can wait a little longer if you aren’t in a rush,” Chu Feng replied.","“L-l-like hell I’ll wait for you! Aren’t you g-g-getting ahead of yourself? Take him down!” the dashing man ordered.","At his order, the old man behind unleashed his oppressive might at Chu Feng. He was a rank nine True God level cultivator.","Uwa!","Thousands of people toppled to the ground, but it was not Chu Feng but the dashing man, the old man who unleashed his oppressive might, and those following them.","Even the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were drawn to this commotion, including Huangfu Zhantian.","Jie Shanxian had made her move, revealing herself as a rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. That naturally drew attention to her. No one expected to encounter another expert of this caliber here.","“Why? Trying to make a move?” Jie Shanxian flitted to Chu Feng’s side and glared at the dashing man.","“T-t-the hell! Why do you n-n-need this when you have such a strong b-b-backing?” The floored dashing man was speechless.","Just then, Chu Feng noticed a pendant around the dashing man’s neck. The pendant looked extremely familiar, so he quickly sent a voice transmission through the corresponding pendant, “Brother, are you in the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s territory?”","“H-h-huh? Chu Feng? A-a-are you here too? W-w-where are you?” Wang Qiang replied via the pendant.","At the same time, the dashing man began scanning his surroundings."]},{"number":6250,"title":"Chapter 6250: Chapter 6248: Is There Something Wrong With Your Friend’s Head?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6248: Is There Something Wrong With Your Friend’s Head?","Chu Feng was delighted.","He had given that pendant to Wang Qiang. It allowed them to communicate when they were within a certain range of each other without the existence inside Wang Qiang eavesdropping on their conversation.","The dashing man was Wang Qiang, just that his disguise was so impeccable that Chu Feng wouldn’t have known if not for the pendant.","“Brother, I am right in front of you,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“In front of me? I-I-I don’t see you.” Wang Qiang first looked in Chu Feng’s direction, but he quickly turned elsewhere. A second later, he turned his gaze back to Chu Feng. “T-t-the heck! Are you the one who snatched my people?”","Wang Qiang sounded delighted.","“Who else?” Chu Feng replied.","“Brother, t-t-tell that old hag to retract her spirit power!” Wang Qiang exclaimed.","“Elder, I know him. He’s my friend,” Chu Feng told Jie Shanxian with a smile.","“A friend?” Jie Shanxian was confused.","“Yes, he’s a friend. We were just fooling around.”","Chu Feng’s words surprised even the rank nine True God level old man beside Wang Qiang.","Wang Qiang quickly sent a voice transmission to the old man, informing him about Chu Feng’s identity. The old man widened his eyes in realization before looking at Chu Feng with a gentler gaze.","Jie Shanxian was skeptical, but she withdrew her spirit power.","As soon as Wang Qiang regained his freedom, he charged up to Chu Feng and hugged him. “B-b-brother, I miss you!”","The crowd realized Chu Feng and Wang Qiang were indeed acquainted, or else they wouldn’t have been this close.","Through their telepathic communication, Chu Feng quickly learned how Wang Qiang got here.","The old man behind Wang Qiang was a Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s grand elder. The Divine Body Heavenly Mansion had long discovered the way to enter this place, and they found a natural oddity here many years back.","The natural oddity needed more time to mature, so they couldn’t take it away with them yet. They could only return many years later to claim it.","Before entering the God’s Era, the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s Mansion Master told this grand elder to bring Wang Qiang here to fetch the natural oddity when it matured to compensate for the unfair skewing of resources toward Yuwen Yanri at Wang Qiang’s expense.","So, Wang Qiang followed the grand elder here.","Little did they know this was the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s territory. There was also another power here known as the Seven Realms Immortal Sect that was not to be trifled with. It was a good thing they had hidden the natural oddity at a remote location beforehand, so neither of the two powers found it.","Wang Qiang consumed the natural oddity and advanced to rank two True God level.","On top of that, the natural oddity was a violent cultivation resource that complemented his Four Fiends Divine Body. Just assimilating a small portion was enough for him to advance to rank two True God level, and he still had a large bunch of energy in his body that he needed more time to assimilate.","He should be able to advance to rank three True God level once he was done assimilating all the energy.","Wang Qiang planned to leave after obtaining the natural oddity, but he heard the news spread by the Huangfu Heavenly Clan and decided to join the commotion. He didn’t expect to meet Chu Feng here.","“B-b-brother, I heard you conquered the Immemorial Massacre Sea. What did you g-g-get from there? I also heard the so-called God Clan got m-m-massacred. Have you heard of it? A-a-also, where did you find a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist h-h-hag to protect you? What have you b-b-been through? What kind of f-f-fortuitous encounter did you have?”","Wang Qiang dropped a series of questions on Chu Feng after telling him about his affairs.","“Hold on, brother. Let’s settle this matter first.”","Now that Chu Feng and Wang Qiang had reunited, it went without saying that they were going to combine their teams. Chu Feng had recruited over 20,000 people, whereas Wang Qiang had a few thousand people. All in all, they had 30,000 people.","That was too much.","“Isn’t that simple? We’ll just k-k-kick off the weaker ones,” Wang Qiang replied.","“I have an idea.” Chu Feng turned to Jie Shanxian and said, “Elder, may I trouble you to construct an illusion formation?”","He proceeded to share the criteria of the illusion formation.","Jie Shanxian eyed him in doubt, but she still constructed the illusion formation following his request.","“I promise you’ll receive your incentives if you clear the trial and I successfully obtain a tower token. This will be the last trial. You may enter now,” Chu Feng said.","The crowd entered the formation without uttering a word of dissatisfaction.","Putting aside the generous incentives offered, Chu Feng and Wang Qiang were backed by a rank nine True God level cultivator and a rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. They were powerhouses the crowd would want to get on good terms with even if there were no incentives.","“Brother, c-c-can you speak now?” Wang Qiang asked.","Chu Feng chuckled. He shared his experiences after parting ways with Wang Qiang via voice transmission, not hiding anything at all except for Jie Shanxian’s identity.","“T-t-t-t-the heck! The heck the heck the heck! You w-w-were the one who eradicated the God Clan?!” Wang Qiang’s eyes bulged.","Despite his already high opinion of Chu Feng, he couldn’t believe that the latter could destroy the God Clan despite being only at rank one True God level. The thought of it left goosebumps all over his body.","He knew Chu Feng wasn’t the type to brag, which meant that this could only be the truth.","“Brother, are you n-n-not going to tell others? N-n-no one will dare mess with you if they know about this. E-e-even that old fart Jie Tianran might have to apologize to you,” Wang Qiang said.","“I doubt they would believe me, and that is not my true strength either. I would have been dead if not for Milady Queen,” Chu Feng replied.","“T-t-that’s true. Your world spirit is a-a-amazing. She holds the f-f-fort whenever it matters. Why don’t you b-b-bring her out? I’ll kowtow to her to t-t-thank her for saving my brother’s life,” Wang Qiang said earnestly.","“I appreciate the sentiment, but there’s no need for that. Milady Queen isn’t an outsider,” Chu Feng said.","“T-t-that won’t do! You’re my only brother in this world! She saved m-m-my only brother in this world; that’s the same as s-s-saving my life! I’d even lick h-h-her feet, let alone kowtow to her!” Wang Qiang said.","Chu Feng frowned.","Eggy exploded in anger, “Chu Feng, tell that stutterer to shut his mouth, or else I’ll come out to smash him right now! How disgusting!”","She felt revulsed, especially since she knew what Wang Qiang looked like. If the latter licked her, she would be tempted to cut off her leg and toss it away.","“Don’t be angry, Eggy. That’s what he’s like.”","While placating Eggy, Chu Feng turned to Wang Qiang and said, “Brother, how can you think about licking Milady Queen’s feet? Is that an apology? No, that’s a benefit you’ll never get even in your dream.”","“Hehe, t-t-hat’s true. Your world spirit is gorgeous.” Wang Qiang grinned. “B-b-but I don’t mean any disrespect. That was an example to show h-h-how important you are. I have my pride too! The m-m-most embarrassing thing I can think of is to lick someone’s feet. I don’t mean to make light of y-y-your woman. Even if I’m interested in a-a-all women in the world, I would never look at your woman with lecherous eyes! I-I-I swear!”","He initially spoke via voice transmission, but halfway through, he suddenly raised his hand and swore aloud, “May I become impotent if I lust for my brother’s woman!”","Those words drew countless gazes to them. Those who didn’t know the truth were confused.","Many women blushed because of how direct his words were. They thought it was a pity for someone as handsome as him to be impotent.","Jie Shanxian glanced at Wang Qiang in disdain before whispering to Chu Feng, “Is there something wrong with your friend’s head?”"]},{"number":6251,"title":"Chapter 6251: Chapter 6249: Intimidating Me?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6249: Intimidating Me?","Chu Feng also became the center of attention due to Wang Qiang’s declaration. They thought that something must have happened between them for Wang Qiang to suddenly make such a declaration.","“I trust you, brother, so stop speaking. We can settle this quietly among ourselves. Don’t do this. It’s too embarrassing.” Chu Feng quickly dragged Wang Qiang’s raised hand down.","“I-I-I’m just saying it aloud to show my sincerity,” Wang Qiang exclaimed. “Brother, you don’t doubt me, r-r-right? I don’t mean anything like that.”","“I believe you.”","Chu Feng trusted Wang Qiang’s character. The latter might be severely lacking in tact, but he was a trustworthy person.","Soon, people started stepping out from the illusion formation. Most had awful looks on their faces; only some were smiling. The illusion formation was created by a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist. As soon as they stepped in, they forgot it was a trial and thought it was reality.","All of them went through the same experience in the illusion formation.","They entered the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, and Chu Feng saved their lives. Later, Chu Feng encountered danger, and they were made to choose between betraying Chu Feng and escaping safely or risking their life by helping Chu Feng.","Those with awful looks on their faces had chosen to betray Chu Feng.","Those who were smiling had chosen to help Chu Feng.","But there were very few kind-hearted people. Of the 30,000 people who went through the illusion formation, only 37 of them had chosen to help Chu Feng.","With a wave of his sleeves, Chu Feng took out Cosmos Sacks of another color and tossed them to the 37 people. The 37 people tried to open it but to no avail.","Just as they were about to ask about it, Chu Feng said, “You have been eliminated.”","“Ah? Why? We helped you in the formation!”","The 37 people felt confused and aggrieved.","Even those who had betrayed Chu Feng were taken aback too. They didn’t expect the people who had chosen Chu Feng to be eliminated like that.","“You aren’t suited for this. Leave. Go as far as you can.” Chu Feng waved his hand.","“W-what about us?” someone who had betrayed Chu Feng in the illusion formation asked.","“You may stay,” Chu Feng replied.","Those who had betrayed Chu Feng were initially startled, but they soon revealed gleeful smiles. Some even taunted those who helped Chu Feng, saying, “The strong preys on the weak in the world of cultivation. The likes of you aren’t suited for this world. Scram as far as you can, or else it’s just a matter of time before you’re eaten up.”","Many people agreed with those words.","“Hypocrites pretending to be good people. Pui!”","“You deserve that!”","Those who were eliminated had their heads lowered a second ago, but their regret vanished without a trace upon learning they were the chosen ones, and they became extremely gleeful.","In the first place, they didn’t regret betraying Chu Feng; they only regretted failing to clear the illusion formation.","“B-b-brother, why are you doing this?” Wang Qiang asked Chu Feng in confusion.","“Ah, I forgot to tell you. The Immemorial Bloodline Tower becomes transparent when fully activated, allowing the spectators outside to see what’s happening inside. On top of that, our disguise means will unravel, revealing our true identity,” Chu Feng discreetly replied.","“I understand. You’re w-w-worried that they’ll be implicated when our identities are revealed.” Wang Qiang widened his eyes in realization.","“Mmhm. We can’t implicate the kind.” Chu Feng looked at the ones who were gleeful despite having betrayed him. “We’ll see what fate has in store for these people. I’ll count them lucky if the Huangfu Heavenly Clan doesn’t go after them. Otherwise... since their favorite catchphrase is that the world of cultivation is a place where the strong preys on the weak, they shouldn’t blame us for fooling them.”","“T-t-they deserve it,” Wang Qiang said.","“Are you sure you still want to enter? I wouldn’t advise you to,” Chu Feng said.","“W-w-what are you saying? What do you take me, W-W-Wang Qiang to be? When have I feared death?” Wang Qiang grumbled in displeasure.","“You might not fear death, but what about the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion? You might implicate them if you get revealed here,” Chu Feng said.","“It’s fine. I-I-I have already let out the news that I’m leaving the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion.”","Chu Feng was taken aback. Why would a Divine Body Heavenly Mansion’s grand elder be protecting him if he had already left them?","“It’s a feint lest I bring trouble upon the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion, especially since I have offended the Netherworld Sect. But I am still a member of the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion. I’ll tell my grand elder later not to go in,” Wang Qiang explained.","Having made up their minds, Chu Feng continued filtering the group till there were only 20,000 people left. These were the people he had meticulously chosen, so they unsurprisingly passed through the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s gates without a hitch.","Just like that, Chu Feng successfully obtained a tower token from the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","He activated it and enveloped his team members in it. The tower token could be described as a mini-contract formation; his team members could choose whether to join him or not. Needless to say, all his team members accepted his invitation.","With that, they completed the binding. Chu Feng fulfilled his promise and gave his team members the incentives he promised them.","He was examining the tower token when the surroundings suddenly quietened down. He didn’t have to lift his head to tell that someone important had just arrived—it was the juniors from the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","Huangfu Shangwu was among them too, but he trailed behind the man and the woman from earlier. They were the ones leading the group.","“What’s your name?” the man asked.","“Shouldn’t you i-i-introduce yourself first before asking for someone’s name?” Wang Qiang asked.","“Shut your mouth. I’m not talking to you.” The man glared at Wang Qiang.","A yellow-bearded Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elder suddenly descended from the sky. All of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s juniors, except for the man and the woman, bowed to him, including Huangfu Shangwu. This showed he had a high standing in the Huangfu Heavenly Clan, yet he fawned over the man and the woman like a lapdog.","“They are our clan chief’s children, young master Huangfu Jiangxing and Miss Huangfu Jiangyue,” the yellow-bearded elder said.","“I don’t care what’s your name, but let me give you some words of reminder. We’ll welcome you if you follow our rules, but we won’t hold back if you try something with us,” Huangfu Jiangxing pointed a finger at Chu Feng and said those words before turning around to leave.","“H-H-Huangfu Jiangxing and Jiangyue... Judging from their name, they probably possess General-tier Heavenly Bloodline. Does the Huangfu Heavenly Clan have no other Saint-tier Heavenly Bloodline aside from the Huangfu Shengyu whom you killed?” Wang Qiang asked via voice transmission.","Chu Feng didn’t answer, but a smile formed on his lips.","Trying to intimidate me? I’m too familiar with this.","Such situations had happened so many times that he couldn’t even remember how many people had tried this on him. But he remembered none of them having a good outcome."]},{"number":6252,"title":"Chapter 6252: Chapter 6250: Stepping Stone","paragraphs":["Chapter 6250: Stepping Stone","There were so many people that it took some time to distribute the tower tokens.","After trying to intimidate Chu Feng, Huangfu Jiangxing and Huangfu Jiangyue returned to their war chariots. The yellow-bearded elder followed them.","“Young master, miss, there is no need to lower yourself to educate an outsider. He’s merely your stepping stone,” the yellow-bearded elder said.","“Didn’t you see? That fellow has a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist as his backing,” Huangfu Jiangxing remarked.","“Of course I did. I didn’t expect there to be an expert of this caliber in this realm. But there’s nothing to fear when you have brought Lord Huangfu Zhantian here with us. With him holding the fort, what can a mere rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist hope to achieve? Even if not for him, I could have...”","A cold intent shrouded the area before the yellow-bearded elder could finish his words.","“I’m merely letting him know who is the master here lest he get over his head just because he has a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist as his backing, but what do you mean by those words? Do you think that I fear him? The likes of him posing a threat to me? What foolish words. If not for that Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, I would have thought he was a weak mortal trash!” Huangfu Jiangxing glared at the yellow-bearded elder with cold eyes.","He was the one emanating that cold intent.","“Young master Jiangxing, that’s not what I mean.” The yellow-bearded elder realized that he had misspoken and hurriedly apologized.","Huangfu Jiangxing harrumphed, his anger unabated.","Huangfu Jiangyue spoke up, “Elder Huang, my little brother and I had to spend a long time convincing my father for this. Are you certain it is feasible? I hope that our effort doesn’t go to benefiting those bumpkins.”","She knew that they could only attain greater rewards if they fully awakened the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, or else they would truly be giving out freebies to outsiders.","The yellow-bearded elder took out an ancient scroll and said, “Rest assured, Miss Jiangyue. I have examined the records—the more cultivator bloodlines there are, the likelier it is to awaken the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s true energy. With so many people here and the preparations we have made, we will surely awaken the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. The people gathered here are nothing more than your stepping stones.”","“Elder, we will remember your contribution if we truly awaken the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s true energy. For now, you should head out,” Huangfu Jiangyue said.","The yellow-bearded elder quickly left.","As soon as he stepped out of the war chariot, his earlier fawning expression vanished, and he scoffed in displeasure, “You’re throwing a tantrum at me even though I’m strategizing for you? Do you take yourself to be the clan chief’s successor? I would never fawn on wastrels on you if young master Shengyu was still around.”","...","In the war chariot, Huangfu Jiangyue turned to Huangfu Jiangxing and advised, “Little brother, you need to learn to control your temper. Elder Huang has some influence in the clan too, not to mention he just advanced to Heavenly God level not too long ago. Lord Father plans to promote him to a guardian elder.”","But Huangfu Jiangxing interjected, “He was Huangfu Shengyu’s lackey. He is only fawning on us now that Huangfu Shengyu is dead. I wouldn’t have even given him the time of my day if not for your insistence.”","“Don’t be caught in trivialities if you wish to do bigger things. If we succeed, you might be able to advance to rank two True God level,” Huangfu Jiangyue told Huangfu Jiangxing.","“So what if I advance to rank two True God level? I have already surpassed Huangfu Shengyu, but to father, I am still beneath him. Is it just because my bloodline pales in comparison? But my cultivation has already surpassed him!” Huangfu Jiangxing huffed.","Huangfu Shengyu was a thorn in his heart. He had always towered over him from a young age. Even when the Huangfu Heavenly Clan chose Huangfu Jiangxing as the clan chief’s successor after Huangfu Shengyu’s death, his father still refused to dote on him the same way as he did on Huangfu Shengyu.","Huangfu Jiangyue looked at Huangfu Jiangxing with a dissatisfied frown. “What’s the point of throwing a tantrum? It’s because of God’s Era’s prophecy that Lord Father spared no expense to help us awaken our bloodline and advance our cultivation. You and I might have advanced to True God level, but didn’t Huangfu Shangwu succeed as well? What makes you think Huangfu Shengyu wouldn’t have advanced to rank two True God level if he was still alive?”","“Do you think I’m beneath Huangfu Shengyu too?” Huangfu Jiangxing questioned.","“It’s not just me; everyone thinks the same. You’re young, so you don’t know how doted our mother was because of Huangfu Shengyu. It was because of Huangfu Shengyu that his mother became more doted than our mother. Huangfu Shengyu’s death is an opportunity for us.","“Do you know why Huangfu Shengyu’s mother is still the one our father dotes on the most even though Huangfu Shengyu is dead? I’ll tell you why—it’s because we aren’t strong enough yet. Others won’t respect you just because you throw a tantrum; you need to win it yourself.","“Why do you think our father agreed to this plan? Is it because he trusts us or Elder Huang? Not at all. It’s because Huangfu Zhantian spoke on our behalf. That’s why our father allowed us to get our way. But why did Huangfu Zhantian help us? It’s because our mother begged him.","“This is a rare opportunity. Your bloodline may metamorphose if we awaken the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. You may just surpass Huangfu Shengyu. If you expect things to be handed to you on a silver platter, you should return now. I’ll do it myself!” Huangfu Jiangyue roared.","Huangfu Jiangxing was silent for several seconds before he raised his head. “Big sister, I understand. I won’t let you and mother down. I’ll awaken the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s true energy and replace Huangfu Shengyu in the truest sense.","...","The Immemorial Bloodline Tower was activated after all the tower tokens were distributed, but the tower doors didn’t open straight away to let everyone in. Instead, a huge formation appeared around the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.","The formations divided the surrounding land into several segments; the number of segments tallied with the number of tower tokens.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan instructed the tower token holders and their teams to step into the segmented lands.","The crowd was excited, thinking that this was a free windfall.","Chu Feng, however, earnestly observed the surroundings."]},{"number":6253,"title":"Chapter 6253: Chapter 6251: Bloodline Resonance, Nine-colored Lightning Envelops the Sky","paragraphs":["Chapter 6251: Bloodline Resonance, Nine-colored Lightning Envelops the Sky","He couldn’t decipher much before the Immemorial Bloodline Tower was fully activated, but now that the formation had surfaced, he was able to gather more information.","“The first thing that has to be done before entering the tower is to awaken the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s energy. The degree of awakening will determine the benefits we can obtain inside. The process won’t be easy, but the road of cultivation has never been smooth sailing. I implore you to do your best,” the yellow-bearded elder said.","He addressed the crowd solemnly from mid-air to rouse their morale. His words motivated many people, who expressed that they would give it their all.","“Aren’t they just making use of us?” Wang Qiang murmured to Chu Feng.","The two of them were seated in the formation, where they could feel the formation. As long as they willed so, they could fuse their bloodline into the formation. This was the only way to awaken the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.","Many people had already begun fusing their bloodlines into the formation, causing the surroundings to tremor.","The base of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower began to glow, casting iridescent lights in the sky. That was many different bloodlines vying for supremacy.","Wang Qiang was tempted to unleash his Four Fiends Divine Body, but Chu Feng suddenly placed his palm on Wang Qiang’s hands and said, “Brother, I advise you to remain a spectator.”","“D-d-did you discover something?” Wang Qiang asked.","He knew Chu Feng wouldn’t say that if he hadn’t discovered something.","“Look.” Chu Feng looked at the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.","The iridescent lights in the sky looked like thousands of clans vying for supremacy, but the strongest one of all was the nine-colored lightning.","A hundred layers of halos manifested around the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. The other bloodlines hadn’t even reached the third layer, but the nine-colored lightning representing the Heavenly Bloodline had already reached the thirtieth layer and was still swiftly climbing up.","At this rate, it was likely to reach the peak.","The higher the nine-colored lightning scaled, the brighter the Immemorial Bloodline Tower glowed. The connection between the two was clear.","But what Chu Feng was more focused on was the formation’s structure.","“This formation pits cultivators against one another. Only one bloodline can emerge victorious, and I suspect that the other bloodlines will become fodder for the winner.”","Wang Qiang widened his eyes in astonishment. “Fodder? Do they intend to devour all of us?”","“Not to that extent, but it may impair your bloodline. It’s just a conjecture on my part, but that seems to be the case based on the formation’s structure,” Chu Feng said.","“T-t-the heck! I didn’t expect them to be so despicable!” Wang Qiang berated.","“Brother, I shouldn’t be advising you to give up when we are rivals. You have a formidable bloodline, and you can monopolize the final benefit if your bloodline reaches the top. However, I’m not the only one with the Heavenly Bloodline here. The presence of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan is highly advantageous to me. If I awaken the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, it’ll benefit all cultivators possessing the Heavenly Bloodline, but it will be at your expense,” Chu Feng said.","Wang Qiang understood what Chu Feng was saying. “W-w-will I not be a stepping stone as long I don’t fuse my bloodline into the formation?”","“That should be the case.” Chu Feng nodded.","While Chu Feng and Wang Qiang were brothers, they were also cultivators. It was inevitable that they would sometimes have to compete over fortuitous encounters, and it would only be fair if they competed on their own merits.","However, the presence of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan skewed the odds greatly in Chu Feng’s favor. Despite Wang Qiang’s formidable bloodline, he was doomed to lose here. The same could be said about all cultivators who didn’t possess the Heavenly Bloodline.","That was why Chu Feng dissuaded Wang Qiang from joining the competition.","“I-I-I understand, brother. I’ll just pretend to f-f-fuse my bloodline power. I’ll leave the a-a-awakening of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower to you,” Wang Qiang said with a smile.","Wang Qiang knew that Chu Feng’s Heavenly Bloodline was even more formidable than his Ruler’s Bloodline. He wasn’t confident of beating Chu Feng’s bloodline by itself, so it would be wiser for him to back down here.","Chu Feng initially refrained from fusing his bloodline into the formation, choosing to spectate instead. While all Heavenly Bloodlines would benefit if the Heavenly Bloodline emerged as the victor of this competition formation, the bulk of the reward would go to the biggest contributor.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan had come prepared, displaying tremendous prowess. Their bloodline power had already reached the seventieth layer of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, but the rate of ascension had visibly slowed down.","Chu Feng noticed strained looks on the faces of the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen, be it those in the older generations or the juniors. They were approaching their limit.","“Looks like it’s time to give them a push.”","Chu Feng was about to fuse his bloodline into the formation when the yellow-beared elder suddenly roared, “Activate your talisman!”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen took out an ancient talisman each. Upon activation, the talismans morphed into spirit power and flowed into the formation. A bizarre surge of energy suddenly appeared in the surroundings.","“B-b-brother, there’s something amiss with those talismans!” Wang Qiang exclaimed.","The energy didn’t shroud them, but it bound everyone who had fused their bloodlines into the formation and forcefully siphoned their bloodline powers, causing their faces to warp in pain.","The bloodline powers that had stopped at the lower layers of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower began fusing with the stagnated nine-colored lightning, causing the latter to continue rising once more.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen who didn’t enter the formation cheered in delight, though Huangfu Zhantian’s eyes remained closed, displaying his nonchalance.","“T-t-the heck! How shameless! How are they any different from demonic sects?!” Wang Qiang exclaimed in disbelief. He was glad Chu Feng had advised him earlier, or else he would have been suffering now too.","“Hold on, everyone. We are at a critical phase of awakening the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. You have to hold on!” the yellow-bearded elder continued to deceive them.","The majority of the crowd didn’t know that their bloodline power was being siphoned. They thought this was a natural reaction from the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, so they gritted their teeth and bore with the pain.","Soon, the nine-colored lightning reached the eightieth layer of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.","But those shrouded by the energy were reaching their limits. Some fainted, but even when unconscious, the energy still continued to siphon their bloodline powers to fuel the Heavenly Bloodline.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan showed no inclination to stop.","“Damn it, I can’t continue spectating anymore.”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan wouldn’t bat an eye even if they siphoned these people’s bloodlines dry and destroyed their future, but the crowd was already reaching their limits, including the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen.","At this rate, they wouldn’t be able to awaken the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s true energy.","Chu Feng knew it was time for him to make a move. He had been observing the situation from the start, so he knew what to do to avoid catching any attention.","He secretly fused his bloodline power into the formation, and the stagnant nine-colored lightning suddenly surged up as if something had awakened it. Soon, it reached the ninetieth layer.","“Waaaaa!”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan cheered in excitement.","This was not their first time activating the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, but they had never fully awakened it before. Their previous record was the eighty-fifth layer, but it had now reached the ninetieth level and was still going up.","Even Huangfu Zhantian opened his eyes. When he saw the brilliant nine-colored lightning, he widened his eyes in bewilderment and remarked, “This method works?”","“GAHHHH!!!”","A figure suddenly stood up and formed a hand seal—Huangfu Jiangxing. The veins popping from his body made it clear that he was exerting his full strength, and the nine-colored lightning he emanated was identical to the one scaling the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.","“I, Huangfu Jiangxing, shall be the one to awaken the Immemorial Bloodline Tower!”","Along with his roar, the nine-colored lightning surged to the peak.","All bloodlines returned to the crowd’s body. Only the nine-colored lightning was left enveloping the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, and it began fusing with the tower.","All of a sudden, a surge of lightning shot into the sky and scattered, enveloping the sky in nine-colored lighting. Everyone watched with bated breaths. Even Huangfu Zhantian also shot to his feet as he stared at the Immemorial Bloodline Tower incredulously.","The nine-colored lightning had fully fused with the Immemorial Bloodline Tower and was emanating a peerless aura. It couldn’t have been clearer that the Immemorial Bloodline Tower was fully awakened.","Everyone turned to look at Huangfu Jiangxing, and resounding cheers ensued.","“Huangfu Jiangxing!”","“Huangfu Jiangxing!”","...","The cheers started from just a few Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen, but more and more clansmen joined in. Subsequently, even outsiders began cheering as well.","They thought Huangfu Jiangxing was the biggest contributor to the full awakening of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.","Huangfu Jiangxing smiled in glee as he took in the respectful gazes directed at him. He had been waiting for this day for a long time now.","I, Huangfu Jiangxing, shall become renowned in the world of cultivation!","Even Huangfu Jiangyue also looked at her little brother with a heartened smile. She knew this wasn’t just her little brother’s credit; everyone had contributed to this, including the bumpkins. However, the truth was not important.","As long as people believed it was her little brother’s credit, it would become the truth.","From this day forth, her little brother’s name, Huangfu Jiangxing, shall go down in the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s annals!"]},{"number":6254,"title":"Chapter 6254: Chapter 6252: Claiming the Initiative in the Activated Bloodline Tower","paragraphs":["Chapter 6252: Claiming the Initiative in the Activated Bloodline Tower","Huangfu Zhantian eyed the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen inside the formation with narrowed eyes. These people might have been handpicked elites, but when it came to bloodlines, he wouldn’t pale in comparison to them.","He had participated in the Immemorial Bloodline Tower many times before back then, but not once had he ever succeeded in fully awakening it. Even though he did enter the tower, his gains from it had always been limited.","Yet, these juniors fully awakened it today. It made him, a prodigy from the older generation, a little bitter.","That being said, these people were his clansmen. He was earnestly happy for them despite his bitterness. He was curious to know who was the biggest contributor to the tower’s awakening. Those from the older generation had participated in previous tower activations, so the only new faces were the juniors.","His eyes eventually fell on three people—Huangfu Shangwu, Huangfu Jiangyue, and Huangfu Jiangxing.","Unlike others, he didn’t think it was Huangfu Jiangxing’s sole credit. He knew what their capabilities and limits were, having watched them grow up, so he was more inclined to believe it was their shared credit.","It was just that the other two weren’t taking credit for it.","“It would have been more amazing if Huangfu Shengyu and the others were still around. This generation of juniors is impressive. Has the era truly changed?” Huangfu Zhantian muttered.","Meanwhile, Wang Qiang was staring at the gleeful Huangfu Jiangxing with a disgruntled look. “W-w-why’s that little bastard acting so smug? Does he t-t-think he’s the biggest contributor to the tower’s awakening?”","He was angry because he knew it was Chu Feng’s credit, though he didn’t disturb Chu Feng over it.","That was because he noticed that while others were celebrating their success, Chu Feng continued to sit with crossed legs, focused on the formation even though its light had dimmed.","Knowing Chu Feng well, Wang Qiang realized that there might be more to the formation than what they saw, and Chu Feng was currently deciphering it.","...","The nine-colored lightning in the sky looked fearsome, but the crowd beneath displayed no fear, only excitement.","However, the excitement soon turned into confusion when the nine-colored lightning converged toward the peak of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, forming a nine-colored lightning sphere that floated at the top.","This nine-colored lightning sphere might appear less impressive than before, but the energy harnessed inside it didn’t pale in comparison. It resembled the sun, lighting up the surroundings.","Soon, pillars of nine-colored lightning shot out from the sphere and began revolving, sweeping the surroundings.","This induced shouts of horror. Many people were so frightened that they peed their pants.","The aura emanated by the nine-colored lightning was so terrifying that they had no doubt they would die if they were struck by it.","However, the crowd soon calmed down when they realized that the pillars of nine-colored lightning passed through the earth and their bodies without causing any damage. It turned out to be an empty scare.","“Observe closely! The secret of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower lies here!” Huangfu Zhantian advised upon sensing something amiss.","All the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen gathered their attention to observe the phenomenon, including Huangfu Jiangxing.","“T-t-those fools! Do they think they c-c-can understand it?” Wang Qiang scoffed.","“We’ll go in together later,” Chu Feng told Wang Qiang via voice transmission.","“Brother, did you s-s-succeed?” Wang Qiang was overjoyed.","Those who had participated in the tower activation were weakened to some extent, but Chu Feng’s complexion looked the same as before. He didn’t look injured in the least.","“Easy-peasy.” Chu Feng winked at him.","He was satisfied with the massive rewards he got.","“That Huangfu guy m-m-mentioned that the lightning sphere contains some secret. Was he wrong?” Wang Qiang asked this question because Chu Feng wasn’t observing the lightning pillars.","“It does, but I have already grasped it,” Chu Feng replied.","“When?” Wang Qiang asked.","“Just now.”","“You g-g-grasped it at a glance?” Wang Qiang was stunned.","“That’s right. I previously advised you not to enter the tower because I thought you wouldn’t get anything from it if you don’t participate in its activation, but I later realized that the benefits aren’t just exclusive to those who activated the tower,” Chu Feng replied via voice transmission.","“What b-b-benefits are there?” Wang Qiang’s eyes lit up.","“I can’t say for sure yet, but it’s located on the ninety-ninth floor. We can take a look together,” Chu Feng said.","“S-s-sure...” Wang Qiang nodded.","The nine-colored lightning sphere dissipated shortly after, and many spirit formation gates manifested at the base of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. It was finally possible to enter the tower.","Huangfu Zhantian breathed a sigh of relief. He had been observing the nine-colored lightning sphere despite not having entered the formation, but he was unable to see through it.","“Did you notice anything?” Huangfu Jiangyue asked her little brother.","“Did you?” Huangfu Jiangxing returned the question.","“I’m afraid not.” Huangfu Jiangyue shook her head.","“I didn’t notice anything too. Is Huangfu Zhantian too sensitive? It could have just been a simple display,” Huangfu Jiangxing said.","“That’s possible. He has never fully awakened the Immemorial Bloodline Tower either, so his deduction might be off the mark,” Huangfu Jiangyue agreed.","Huangfu Zhantian was an important figure in their Huangfu Heavenly Clan, not just because of his high cultivation but because of his Heavenly General-tier Heavenly Bloodline too.","According to their father, Huangfu Zhantian had been practicing a unique profound skill that slowed the advancement of his cultivation, but the moment he mastered it, his cultivation would grow by leaps and bounds.","If not for that, Huangfu Zhantian wouldn’t just be at rank one Heavenly God level. Even so, his fighting prowess was superior to ordinary rank one Heavenly God level cultivators.","But Huangfu Zhantian’s talent was only notable among the older generations. His powerful bloodline was commonplace in their generation. For instance, both Huangfu Jiangxing and Huangfu Jiangyue’s bloodlines were at Heavenly General-tier too.","Due to that, their respect for Huangfu Zhantian was only skin deep.","Let’s go, big sister,” Huangfu Jiangxing said as he made his way toward the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.","Those who were standing around began surging into the Immemorial Bloodline Tower as well, including Chu Feng and Wang Qiang.","The Immemorial Bloodline Tower was different from how the crowd expected it to be. Inside it was neither a majestic palace nor a deep cavern but a lush forest.","A mysterious power in the forest restrained their ability to fly and restricted their visibility, but the crowd still rushed into the forest because they were worried they might miss the benefits.","Initially, Chu Feng’s group advanced quickly, lagging only slightly Huangfu Jiangxing’s group, but all of a sudden, Chu Feng stopped. His body had suddenly become incredibly weak, and he coughed violently.","“What’s wrong, brother?” Wang Qiang rushed forward to support Chu Feng.","“I might have impaired my bloodline while activating the bloodline tower,” Chu Feng replied.","Those words put Wang Qiang’s mind at ease as he knew that couldn’t be true.","Oblivious to the truth, Huangfu Jiangxing sneered, “Trash.”","Despite being in the lead, he had been secretly paying attention to the crowd behind him, including Chu Feng. Thinking about the respectful gazes he received earlier and how useless Chu Feng was, suffering such severe damage just from activating the tower, he decided not to waste his effort observing Chu Feng.","He didn’t think that Chu Feng could pose a threat to him anyway.","Chu Feng’s teammates stopped to look at him anxiously. They were not worried about him but losing their lead and missing the benefits, since his delay had allowed other teams to overtake them.","They initially put up with it, but when they were the only ones left outside the forest, someone finally lost his patience and said, “Young friend, I’m sympathetic about your plight, but we are here to benefit from the tower. Why don’t you hand the tower token to me if you can’t advance any further?”","The one who had just spoken was a rank four True God level old man. He initially planned to rob Chu Feng’s tower token and treasures, but he dropped that thought upon realizing that the latter was backed by a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","That was the only reason the old man was still speaking politely now.","You old t-t-thing! You received my brother’s incentive, s-s-so just do your job and don’t think about anything else,” Wang Qiang scoffed.","“Young friend, you’re mistaken if you think you can order us around like dogs over that bit of incentives. We wish to benefit from the tower too,” the old man said.","“I’ll be fine very soon. Give me a moment. I won’t delay you by much,” Chu Feng said.","“Young friend, you’re a cultivator too. You should understand the importance of clinching the initiative. The others have already ventured into the forest; we’re the only ones left here. We will be left with nothing at this rate. How about this? I’ll return the incentive I received from you, and in return, you’ll hand the tower token to me.”","Despite the old man’s amicable tone, he didn’t take out the items at all. Instead, he unleashed his rank four True God level aura.","He was not negotiating with Chu Feng but threatening him!"]},{"number":6255,"title":"Chapter 6255: Chapter 6253: Claiming the Initiative","paragraphs":["Chapter 6253: Claiming the Initiative","“What if I refuse?” Chu Feng asked.","“Young friend, you’re being unreasonable. You should think on our behalf too. We didn’t work hard to enter the tower just to dawdle around. You can’t just throw away our future just because you have someone backing you outside,” the old man said.","“Indeed, indeed!”","“That bit of incentive you gave us can’t do much. We suffered so much to activate the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. It would be all in vain if we don’t get something from it.”","As more people voiced their support, the old man became even more brazen.","He sent a voice transmission to everyone present except for Chu Feng and Wang Qiang, telling them that they were the only ones here and that they could just murder Chu Feng and Wang Qiang, take the tower token, and split their treasures.","He said those words in a subtle manner, but to his surprise, quite a few people agreed with him.","Most people were still hesitant to make a move on Chu Feng because they were afraid of the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist; they were worried that the latter would go after them if Chu Feng disappeared here.","Nevertheless, the old man decided to go ahead with it. He would just have to kill those who disagreed with him together with Chu Feng and Wang Qiang.","Little did he know that Chu Feng’s grasp of the tower token far surpassed their wildest imagination. Not only could Chu Feng hear their voice transmission through the tower token, but he could extend the privilege to Wang Qiang too.","A cold gleam flashed across Wang Qiang’s eyes. He had already made up his mind to kill them after hearing about their ploy.","Holding the tower token, Chu Feng waved his sleeves.","What happened next stunned the majority of the crowd—Chu Feng had released them from their binding with the tower token.","“You may go,” Chu Feng said.","He had released those who dared not kill him from the tower token. Granted that they had betrayed Chu Feng during the trial, a distinction should be made between reality and illusion.","He understood that it was because of Jie Shanxian that they dared not kill him, but it was still a fact that they had refused to work with the old man. He had no qualms about taking the lives of others, but he still had a set of principles that he followed.","“Milord, we...”","Those released from the tower token were dumbstruck.","“Your refusal to kill me has made you an eyesore to the rest of them. I’m saving you by letting you go now, or else they might seek to silence you,” Chu Feng said.","The crowd was stunned.","“How dare you rat on me? The lot of you better stay put!” the old man roared in anger as he unleashed his rank four True God level oppressive might.","Chu Feng had been alerted to their plan, but how did he find out about it? Someone must have told him. But this worked in the old man's favor, as he now had a legitimate excuse to silence them.","The crowd was horrified. They could sense the rank four True God level old man’s killing intent.","Instead of attacking right away, the old man turned to Chu Feng. “I hesitated whether I should deal with you or not, but with things coming to this point, there is no reason for me to hold back anymore. Brat, I don’t give a damn about you, but I am interested in your treasures. You’re a goner in this life, so I suggest you wise up in your next. Don’t flaunt your wealth in public when you don’t have the strength to protect it, or else you’re only courting your death.”","Pu!","A formation sword pierced through the old man’s dantian. Chu Feng was still standing on the spot, but the formation sword was extended from his palm.","“Someone is courting his death, but a pity it isn’t me,” Chu Feng snickered as he looked at the old man with contemptuous eyes.","“R-rank one True Dragon! He’s a rank one True Dragon World Spiritist? But how did he defeat that old man?!”","The crowd was baffled to see a rank one True Dragon World Spiritist subduing a rank four True God level cultivator so easily.","The old man couldn’t speak. He could only stare at Chu Feng in shock as the formation sword inflicted tremendous torture on him.","“I overheard your voice transmissions, so I prepared a share for the rest of you too,” Chu Feng sneered.","The formation sword that pierced through the old man’s body suddenly extended, piercing through over three thousand bodies in the blink of an eye like a candied hawthorn, popping all of their dantians.","Those who survived the ordeal were horrified to witness Chu Feng’s brutality. Many kneeled and begged for mercy.","“Watch your mouth when you leave. You may go now.”","Chu Feng didn’t make things hard for them. To be honest, he wasn’t worried about them running their mouths outside as he knew his identity was bound to be exposed today.","The survivors quickly turned tail and fled.","Chu Feng tightly gripped the tower token as he formed a hand seal. Nine-colored lightning surfaced on his formation sword and surged through the bodies of the skewered cultivators.","Screams of agony filled the air.","Their bodies convulsed in sheer pain as their eyeballs rolled upward. White froth dribbled from their mouths. They were swiftly approaching their limits.","But Chu Feng stopped the lightning right before they were about to die.","All screams halted right away. The cultivators stood orderly on the spot like puppets.","Chu Feng constructed a small spatial formation, which exerted a suction force that took away all the cultivators’ clothes and treasures.","“Brother, w-w-what are you doing?” Wang Qiang asked.","He could tell that Chu Feng was up to something.","“While I was activating the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, I noticed that the tower token’s formation can be used to control the people bound to it like puppets, but this will result in the puppets’ deaths. Since I’m going to kill these people anyway, I thought I might as well use them as puppets,” Chu Feng said.","“They are lucky to die l-l-like that.” Wang Qiang harrumphed.","“Indeed. They are lucky to get away with this much after conspiring to kill the two of us. However, I need them to do something for me. Think of it as a way for them to make up for their sins,” Chu Feng said.","The formation sword instantly retracted into his palm.","These naked cultivators looked no different from normal people at first glance, but their consciousness had already been destroyed, making them empty shells. They were already doomed to die.","Chu Feng ordered these cultivators to enter the forest, but he had them scatter in different directions.","“What are you using them for?” Wang Qiang asked.","“To claim the initiative,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","He walked up to Wang Qiang, raised his finger, and transmitted a surge of light into the latter’s head. It was a map of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower."]},{"number":6256,"title":"Chapter 6256: Chapter 6254: Terrible Circumstances","paragraphs":["Chapter 6254: Terrible Circumstances","“The hell! Brother, y-y-you know everything about this place!” Wang Qiang exclaimed.","The map showed a secret passageway leading straight to the 99th floor.","“Well, I’m a world spiritist,” Chu Feng smiled.","This map was based on the clues from the nine-colored lightning sphere previously at the top of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. Others struggled to see through it, but Chu Feng, as the main contributor to the tower’s awakening, could see it more keenly than others.","In the first place, world spiritists like him were much more observant.","From there, he learned many important details about the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.","“Brother, why are you telling m-m-me about this place? Are you not c-c-coming with me?” Wang Qiang asked.","“You should head there first and wait for me. Remember, don’t wander around. Just stay there. If you can unravel it, go ahead and do so. There’s no need to wait for me,” Chu Feng replied.","“W-w-what about you?” Wang Qiang asked.","“I have other matters to attend to. I’ll look for you once I’m done,” Chu Feng replied.","“Let’s go together.” Wnag Qiang still wanted to stick with Chu Feng,","“Don’t worry, I’ll be fine. It’ll be more convenient for me to go alone. Wait for me there, brother,” Chu Feng said.","“A-a-all right. You must take care.”","Believing in Chu Feng’s capability, Wang Qiang turned around and entered the forest.","Chu Feng also made his move, but he headed off in a different direction. Just like that, the two of them parted ways.","This forest was the first floor of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. There were many roads and methods to reach the second floor, but the clues were hidden in the forest.","All the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s tower token holders had a map in hand. They were maps of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, created based on their predecessors’ experiences. Thanks to that, they were able to navigate much more smoothly than others.","While most people were still exploring the first floor, they had already reached the tenth floor.","This stoked the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s glee, especially Huangfu Jiangxing. He felt like he was opening a new chapter for the Huangfu Heavenly Clan, and his feats today would go down in history.","Little did they know that Wang Qiang had already reached the 99th floor while they were still in the tenth. Even the people whom Chu Feng controlled were now spread over every single level of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, from the third to the 98th.","There was a hidden formation on each floor.","Upon gathering at the hidden formations, the bodies of the people under Chu Feng’s control broke down, and the nine-colored lightning that Chu Feng fused inside their bodies surged into the hidden formations.","Chu Feng was on the second floor of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, standing between two mountain peaks. It looked like nothing was between the two mountain peaks at first glance, but there was a formation hidden there.","Holding the tower token with his right hand and pointing at the midpoint of the two mountain peaks with his right, Chu Feng released a surge of nine-colored lightning reminiscent of a little lightning snake.","The little lightning snake struck an invisible barrier, producing a series of intense ripples.","Spirit power emerged, and before long, a thousand-meter-wide formation appeared before Chu Feng’s eyes. This formation was pulsating rhythmically.","The little lightning snake fused with the formation.","Once the fusion was complete, the formation slowly disappeared as if nothing had happened.","Chu Feng sat down and formed a hand seal to control the remaining puppets. He planned to use the puppets to find the hidden formation on every level and fuse his nine-colored lightning into them.","Once the job was done, the puppets could quietly dissipate into thin air without leaving a trace. That was also why Chu Feng removed their clothes earlier.","It was troublesome to remotely control the puppet, but fortunately, Chu Feng had made ample preparations beforehand. It didn’t take long for him to complete this step.","“We can finally begin now.”","Once the puppets on the 98th floor completed their mission, Chu Feng stood up.","He formed a series of bizarre hand seals that were neither related to martial power nor spirit power at the hidden formation in front of him, and the hidden formation appeared once more.","This time, the formation was exceptionally violent, causing the surroundings to tremor with increasing ferocity. Nearby mountain peaks collapsed, and distant mountains revealed cracks. The tremors could be felt not just on the second floor but throughout the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.","The spectators outside could see it too.","This alarmed the Huangfu Heavenly Clan, including Huangfu Zhantian. They had entered the Immemorial Bloodline Tower many times, but this was the first time such a thing had happened. Even though the tremors weren’t serious, it indicated that something was happening inside.","Just then, spirit power suddenly manifested from the tower’s second floor and swiftly enveloped the entire tower. Wherever the spirit power enveloped, the tower turned transparent.","The field inside the Immemorial Bloodline Tower was much bigger than what it appeared outside, but the tower’s formation still allowed the spectators to locate everyone. However, there were still two locations that the spectators couldn’t see through.","One was a section in the 99th floor. That was where Wang Qiang was.","The other was the peak of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. The entire floor couldn’t be seen.","But none of the spectators was bothered about that. Their attention was fully drawn to the second floor.","“It’s him?”","All eyes fell on Chu Feng. They couldn’t believe what they were seeing.","A massive formation was emanating terrifying energy that caused the entire Immemorial Bloodline Tower to quake, and Chu Feng, with his small stature, was fighting against the formation.","Shockingly, the formation was weakening under Chu Feng’s opposition. As the formation contracted, nine-colored lightning began appearing within it.","“Lord Zhantian!”","All the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elders turned to Huangfu Zhantian. They could tell that the formation Chu Feng was suppressing was important, and it could determine who obtained the final power.","“What are you waiting for? Enter the tower and take control of it!” Huangfu Zhantian roared.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen rushed into the Immemorial Bloodline Tower with their tower tokens.","The crowd didn’t hear their exchange, so they thought that the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was merely sending more people into the tower.","Jie Shanxian frowned. “This isn’t good.”","She could tell that the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was going after Chu Feng."]},{"number":6257,"title":"Chapter 6257: Chapter 6255: The Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s Sectmaster","paragraphs":["Chapter 6255: The Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s Sectmaster","Jie Shanxian was right.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen split into many groups upon entering the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, but the group with the strongest members marched straight to where Chu Feng was.","The others went off to inform the other Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen.","Jie Shanxian reached into her Cosmos Sack and absorbed a talisman paper into her palm. She channeled her spirit power and began constructing a formation.","“The Huangfu Heavenly Clan is filled with sore losers.”","Jie Shanxian suddenly received a voice transmission. She turned around and saw several figures standing not too far away. They had average appearances, but she could tell at a glance that they were in disguise.","To her astonishment, she couldn’t see through their disguise.","“I am Jiang Buxiu, the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster,” another voice transmission was relayed to Jie Shanxian.","It was the voice of the middle-aged man who stood outside the Seven Realms Immortal Sect earlier. It turned out he was the Seven Realms Immortal Set’s sectmaster.","Upon learning about how easily Jie Shanxian refined the Purpledream Ascensions, he ordered his men to locate her whereabouts.","Jie Shanxian and Chu Feng headed here straight without bothering to disguise or conceal themselves, so it was an easy feat for world spiritists of the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s caliber to find them.","As soon as he received Jie Shanxian’s location, he rushed over with a group of people.","“I apologize for the disrespect my sectmembers have shown to you. What are you waiting for? Apologize to her right now!”","Two people trailed behind the sectmaster.","“Milord, we apologize for our earlier disrespect.”","The two of them bowed in unison. Their faces were disguised, but they didn’t alter their voices. They were the woman and the old man who slighted Jie Shanxian earlier.","“What do you want from me?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“I see that you’re a candid person. I shan’t beat around the bush then. Our sect placed those Purpledream Ascensions outside for others to refine, with the goal being to find someone talented enough to refine them.","“Unfortunately, we have never found anyone capable of doing so, to the point where we have almost given up on it. That’s why we opened our barrier and took back the flowers, leaving only inferior ones outside. We didn’t expect you to arrive right after.","“I don’t know your affiliation or where you learned your skills from, but we need your capability. We’ll compensate you accordingly if you work with us,” the middle-aged man said.","“You want me to help you refine Purpledream Ascensions?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“Yes, there are Purpledream Ascensions that are more difficult to refine in my sect,” the sectmaster replied.","There were suddenly loud exclamations from the crowd—Chu Feng had caused yet another commotion. He had compressed the thousand-meter-wide formation till it was less than ten meters wide, turning it from intangible into tangible.","The formation now resembled a metal piece crackling with nine-colored lightning. There were marks on the metal piece, but the metal piece was just a fragment, so the mark was also incomplete. It was impossible to decipher the mark just from this single metal piece.","Given how this metal piece had invoked a phenomenon throughout the entire Immemorial Bloodline Tower, there was no question that it could lead one to a huge fortuitous encounter. However, obtaining the metal piece was easier said than done.","Chu Feng released his hand seal, but the nine-colored lightning inside his body continued surging into the metal piece. It could be that the metal piece was absorbing his bloodline power, or that he was exerting dominance over the metal piece to become its owner.","The crowd could only speculate on the situation.","Soon, the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen arrived at Chu Feng’s vicinity. They noticed that the metal piece emanated an aura almost identical to the Immemorial Bloodline Tower; the two were clearly one entity.","The way Chu Feng infused his bloodline power into the metal piece was similar to how the tower was activated earlier. It was likely the only way to gain ownership over the metal piece.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan was appalled. Were it not for the Immemorial Bloodline Tower suddenly turning transparent, they wouldn’t even know that there was such a mechanism in the tower. The thought of them filled them with inexplicable anger.","Several surges of oppressive might simultaneously fell on Chu Feng.","Anyone else in Chu Feng’s place would have been scared out of their pants, but Chu Feng calmly asked, “Why are you exerting your oppressive might on me when there is no grudge between us? Does the Huangfu Heavenly Clan intend to kill me?”","The elder leading the group glared at those who exerted their oppressive might. People were spectating outside, and they weren’t planning to tarnish their reputation for good here.","Huangfu Zhantian had already ordered them not to go too far.","Even though the Huangfu Heavenly Clan couldn’t care less about these cultivators, especially since they had only invited them to exploit them, they had no intention of making it appear too blatant. They should at least appear fair on the surface, or else they could lose public support.","Upon the elder’s glare, the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen quickly retracted their oppressive might, though they felt aggrieved. In the first place, they were here to teach Chu Feng a lesson. They didn’t expect the latter to question them.","“I didn’t expect this young friend here to possess the Heavenly Bloodline too,” the elder said with a smile as he approached Chu Feng.","“Why? Did you think that your Huangfu Heavenly Clan is the only one with the Heavenly Bloodline?” Chu Feng asked.","Chu Feng’s discourteous attitude made the elder’s cheeks twitch in anger. How dare a junior act so arrogantly? Is it just ignorance? Or is he a fool?","The elder didn’t know that Chu Feng had already deciphered the tower’s secrets, so he knew that the tower had become transparent and that the crowd could see their interactions.","Chu Feng understood well how powers like the Huangfu Heavenly Clan operated. They still committed evil deeds, but unlike demonic sects, they were hypocrites and still wanted others to see them as good people.","Otherwise, they could have just forced the crowd to do their bidding during the activation of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. There was no need for them to come up with useless explanations to lie to the crowd.","If no one was watching, they wouldn’t have wasted their time with words. They would have just killed Chu Feng and snatched the metal piece.","“This young friend, you’re thinking too much. The Heavenly Bloodline is not exclusive to our Huangfu Heavenly Clan. I’m just asking out of curiosity. May I know how did you find this item?” the elder suppressed his anger and asked with a jolly tone.","“You’re asking the obvious,” Chu Feng replied with a chuckle.","A Huangfu Heavenly Clansman roared, “Audacious! Answer our elder’s question as it is! Stop acting so arrogantly!”","They were so used to being domineering that it was a struggle for them to feign courtesy.","Chu Feng blinked his eyes. “The nine-colored lightning sphere earlier contains information about these items. You should have seen it too. That’s why I say you’re asking the obvious.”","Chu Feng briefly paused before adding, “Or were you unable to decipher the clues in the nine-colored lightning sphere?”","All of the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen, as well as the spectators outside, were startled. Most of their complexions turned awful. Even Huangfu Zhantian coughed twice and scratched his head.","Even Huangfu Zhantian had failed to decipher the nine-colored lightning sphere, let alone the others."]},{"number":6258,"title":"Chapter 6258: Chapter 6256: Scheming Against Me? I’ll Make You Feel the Pinch","paragraphs":["Chapter 6256: Scheming Against Me? I’ll Make You Feel the Pinch","“You deciphered something from the nine-colored lightning sphere?” The elder widened his eyes in astonishment, though he remained skeptical about Chu Feng’s words.","They couldn’t make out anything at all, yet this brat deciphered something from it? There was no way he could believe that.","They might both share the Heavenly Bloodline, but there were different tiers to Heavenly Bloodlines. From his very bones, he believed that all other Heavenly Bloodlines outside of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan were subpar, and he looked down on them.","“How else do you think I found this?” Chu Feng replied.","“You have sharp eyes, young friend. Do you what’s its use?” the elder asked despite his skepticism. He needed to know the use of this item.","“Elder, you couldn’t decipher the nine-colored lightning sphere?” Chu Feng asked.","“Well... This...” The elder was at a loss for words.","He sent a voice transmission to Chu Feng, “I’m already being polite to you. You better cooperate with me and answer my question, or else I’ll massacre your family.”","A smile firmly remained on his face, but he had already revealed his true self.","Anyone else would have been intimidated by that threat, especially given that the elder was a late True God level cultivator. But those words only confirmed Chu Feng’s guess that they dared not make a move on him in public.","Still, Chu Feng decided to cooperate on the surface, “Elder, based on my observation, this item is the key to obtaining the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s energy. However, it won’t be easy to obtain it even if you find one. You’ll have to fuse a huge amount of bloodline power into it to make it yours, or else you won’t be able to take it away or decipher its content.”","“Is it? Let me give it a try.”","The elder fused his bloodline power into the metal piece the same way he did when activating the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, and it worked. His face lit up in delight. This meant that they could take over the metal piece even though they weren’t the ones who discovered it.","“Young friend, an extraordinary amount of bloodline power is needed to awaken this item. You won’t be able to accomplish it by yourself. Don’t worry, I won’t steal your credit since you were the one who found it. Why don’t you have this item to our Huangfu Heavenly Clan, and we will reward you for it,” the elder said as he handed a Cosmos Sack to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng took the Cosmos Sack and smiled.","Contained in the Cosmos Sack were ten martial power beads, but they were trashy beads that contained very little martial power. The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elder was humiliating him.","Seeing Chu Feng’s smile, the elder sent another voice transmission to Chu Feng, “Brat, you disgraced me by rambling too much earlier. It’s only out of magnanimity that I’m not pursuing the matter and even offering you compensation. You better take it and not cause any trouble.”","Chu Feng nodded, only to crush the Cosmos Sack right after. The ten martial power beads inside the Cosmos Sack floated out.","“Don’t you think your compensation is lacking?” Chu Feng asked with a faint smile.","The crowd could see the quality of the martial power beads from the martial power they emanated.","“They are giving so little? They might as well not give anything at all. Aren’t they just humiliating him?”","“Indeed. This is an important discovery. Even if he had only stumbled upon it by luck, they shouldn’t be offering him so little.”","The crowd discussed.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elder spoke as if there were great treasures inside the Cosmos Sack, and Chu Feng would have deserved it as the metal piece was an important clue to the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.","Yet, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan only gave him this bit of reward. It was almost as if they were trying to drive off a beggar.","“Haa, I should have known that we were nothing to big clans.”","“I reckon those who went in won’t be able to get anything good out of this. Lucky I stayed away.”","Countless such whispers could be heard outside. Their voices weren’t loud, but cultivators, with their far more sensitive senses, could easily pick up on them.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were infuriated to hear those words.","Huangfu Zhantian frowned. He beckoned a nearby elder and told him via voice transmission, “Enter the tower right now and tell them to stop being so stingy. Can’t they at least put on an act? They have cultivated for so many years, but it looks like their brains remain primitive!”","“Understood.”","The elder was at pinnacle True God level. He took a tower token and rushed into the tower.","In truth, the elder standing before Chu Feng was no fool. Most cultivators would have been intimidated by the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s reputation and kneeled to beg for mercy. He didn’t expect Chu Feng to be so brazen as to complain about the rewards.","“Are you tired of living?” the elder questioned seethingly.","“Elder, I’m standing right in front of you. You can speak directly. There’s no need to send voice transmissions to threaten me. There’s no one else here other than your Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen. Are you trying to keep it a secret from them?” Chu Feng got straight to the point.","“Ah? What? W-who’s threatening you?”","The elder was stumped by Chu Feng’s candidness. He knew that Chu Feng was brazen, but he didn’t expect him to be this brazen.","His face turned livid. He was convinced that the youth in front of him was a fool, for a normal person would have never dared to do something like that. He would have slapped a fool like this to death had it been on any other occasion, but unfortunately, his hands were tied here.","He understood that threats wouldn’t work here, and he could only exact vengeance in the future.","So, he suppressed his anger and awkwardly explained, “Young friend, you must have been hearing things because you were too nervous. I got the wrong compensation here. Here, let me right things.”","The elder waved his sleeves, and brilliant lights filled the surroundings. They were all martial power beads, and there were so many of them that they looked like stars in the sky. There must have been at least tens of millions of them.","These beads might not contain much martial power too, but just the sheer number of them would have made them useful. It would have been a decent compensation for most people.","But Chu Feng didn’t think it was enough. These beads weren’t enough for him to floss his teeth. Thus, he said, “It isn’t enough.”","“What did you say?” The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were stunned.","“It said it isn’t enough,” Chu Feng replied.","“Brat, you are getting ahead of yourself. Who do you think you are? This Immemorial Bloodline Tower belongs to our Huangfu Heavenly Clan! It’s out of generosity that we allowed you to enter, but instead of showing gratitude, you’re trying to extort us?” a Huangfu Heavenly Clansman lost his patience and berated Chu Feng.","The elder didn’t stop the clansman, for he was feeling so angry that he wanted to kill Chu Feng.","“Yes, the Immemorial Bloodline Tower is your possession, but you wouldn’t have known about this if not for me. I can tell you frankly that this item is present on every floor from the second to the 98th. You’ll need more than just one to obtain the final power,” Chu Feng said.","That stumped not just the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen but those outside too.","“Is that for real? That brat must be talking rubbish, right?”","They couldn’t believe what they were hearing. Could that fellow have deciphered so much about the Immemorial Bloodline Tower?","“I can see that you have failed to decipher the clues in the sphere. As long as you offer me sufficient benefits, I’ll uncover all the formations for you,” Chu Feng said.","“We will compensate you accordingly if your words are true, but if you are lying to us, the consequences are not something you can bear,” the elder said.","“You’re the Huangfu Heavenly Clan. I wouldn’t dare deceive you.” Chu Feng smiled.","“What do you want?” the elder asked.","“These cultivation resources aren’t enough. Bring out your treasures and let me pick among them,” Chu Feng replied.","“Fine, I’ll let you pick whatever you want.”","The elder didn’t hesitate to take out his treasures, and the other Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen quickly followed suit.","There were so many treasures that it made the spectators outside drool, but Chu Feng shook his head. He had so many invaluable treasures with him that very few items that could catch his interest.","“I’ll take all the cultivation resources and a God Armament on top of that,” Chu Feng replied.","“God Armament?”","“You sure are greedy!”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen thought Chu Feng was out of his mind. Even those outside thought that Chu Feng was asking for too much. God Armaments were invaluable treasures to them.","They couldn’t have imagined that Chu Feng had plenty of those with him.","Whatever God Armament they brought out was unlikely to be of a quality that could catch Chu Feng’s eye, but he wanted to make them feel the pinch. So, he pressed on, “Do you think that a God Armament is worth more than the final power here?”","The elder accepted the offer with gritted teeth. He tossed his God Armament to Chu Feng.","“Fine, you can have it.”","By this point, he had already decided to kill Chu Feng once they were outside. It didn’t matter to him what Chu Feng demanded; he was going to get everything back anyway."]},{"number":6259,"title":"Chapter 6259: Chapter 6257: Desire to Kill","paragraphs":["Chapter 6257: Desire to Kill","Chu Feng took out a Cosmos Sack and stored all the cultivation resources lying around and the God Armament the elder passed to him in it.","“I’ll accept this as compensation for this formation. Let’s go with this amount for subsequent formations too,” he said as he stowed away his Cosmos Sack.","“Are you out of your mind?” The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen couldn’t believe their ears.","“Fine, I’ll accept your offer,” the elder replied. You greedy brat. You can have all the wealth you want in the world, but you won’t have the life to spend it.","“That’s a wise decision, elder. Leave someone here to channel the formation. We’ll advance to the next floor,” Chu Feng said with a beaming smile.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan thought that Chu Feng was a fool courting his doom.","Chu Feng led the Huangfu Heavenly Clan to the third floor. News spread fast, and more Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen headed over to join the group, including Huangfu Jiangxin, Huangfu Jiangyue, and the yellow-bearded elder who had already progressed to the fifteenth floor.","“Brat, I’ll make sure you die a terrible death if you fail to find the formation,” Huangfu Jiangxing threatened.","“Oh? Aren’t you the one who activated the Immemorial Bloodline Tower? You didn’t manage to decipher it too?” Chu Feng asked with a composed smile.","“What did you say?” Huangfu Jiangxing growled.","“I’m talking about the lightning sphere. You were staring so intently at it that I thought you deciphered it. Ah, I guess that was an unnecessary question. You would have known that I’m leading you down the right path if you had deciphered it,” Chu Feng replied.","“You’re looking to die!” Huangfu Jiangxing had never been humiliated like that. He exerted his True God level oppressive might on Chu Feng.","However, that oppressive might was suppressed by many other oppressive mights before it could even get close to Chu Feng. It was not just the yellow-bearded elder and the others who intervened to stop him; even his big sister Huangfu Jiangyue did so too.","“Stop acting rashly. He’s of value to us,” Huangfu Jiangyue told him via voice transmission.","But Huangfu Jiangxing couldn’t care less and asked aloud, “Big sister, do you trust him? How can he decipher what we can’t see through? He merely got lucky and found that formation by coincidence, so he’s using this to extort benefits from us.”","Outside, Huangfu Zhantian shook his head and sighed. “Haaa... No wonder our clan chief is more fond of Shengyu. Huangfu Jiangxing might have a good bloodline, but he lacks wits.”","Huangfu Jiangxing had the right to be arrogant, but the occasion mattered too. To continue acting arrogantly despite knowing the people outside could see and hear what was going on, Huangfu Jiangxing was a complete moron.","Huangfu Zhantian turned to Chu Feng and murmured, “What’s that brat’s background?”","He was starting to feel uneasy. If that brat saw through the lightning sphere when none of them could, was there a chance that their Huangfu Heavenly Clan wasn’t the biggest contributor to the tower activation?","That brat possessed the Heavenly Bloodline too.","“No, I must be overthinking it.” Huangfu Zhantian shook his head and refuted those thoughts. How could anyone have a Heavenly Bloodline stronger than their Huangfu Heavenly Clan here?","...","Chu Feng adeptly navigated his way through the tower, showing no hesitation even when faced with a crossroad. It was as if he had been here many times before.","Both the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen and the spectators outside the tower reserved their doubts about his capabilities.","Chu Feng suddenly stopped and formed a hand seal toward empty space. The tower shook as a massive formation appeared in front of the crowd’s eyes.","Everyone looking at Chu Feng was stunned, especially Huangfu Jiangxing, Huangfu Jiangyue, and the yellow-bearded elder. They felt immense power pulsating from the formation, so much so that they had no idea how could they begin opposing it.","Yet Chu Feng single-handedly opposed that formation.","Similar to the second floor’s formation, Chu Feng didn’t take long to suppress the formation into a metal piece.","“Give me my compensation, and we’ll head to the fourth floor.” Chu Feng stretched his hand toward the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen.","“It’s all prepared for you. Is it to your satisfaction?” the yellow-bearded elder replied as he handed a Cosmos Sack to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng inspected the Cosmos Sack. There was a God Armament inside, and the cultivation resources inside was much better than what he received before.","“This elder is more generous,” Chu Feng remarked as he stowed away the Cosmos Sack.","“You’re too polite. I’m only giving you what you deserve. Young friend, I’m curious to know how you deciphered this information from that lightning sphere,” the yellow-bearded elder asked with a smile.","As expected of someone who had managed to climb to a high position, the yellow-bearded elder displayed maturity far beyond that of the previous elder and Huangfu Jiangxing. He even gave Chu Feng a bit more benefits to win his goodwill so that he could ask a question.","“I just looked at it normally. Elder, were you really unable to decipher it?” Chu Feng asked.","The yellow-bearded elder smiled at those words.","“Does this mean I’m the chosen one?” Chu Feng intentionally glanced at Huangfu Jiangxing when he said those words, only to burst into laughter right after. “I’m kidding. Let’s head to the next formation.”","He began making his way to the fourth floor.","Chu Feng also adeptly navigated the fourth floor and easily found the formation.","“That’s incredible! How is that fellow so formidable when he looks so average?”","“Is it truly his first time entering the Immemorial Bloodline Tower? What’s his background?”","“Ah, there was a Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist backing him. Is he from the Seven Realms Immortal Sect?”","“How could those from the Seven Realms Immortal Sect possess the Heavenly Bloodline? I bet there’s a third powerhouse hiding in this realm, and that fellow is from there.”","“That makes sense.”","Any doubt harbored by the crowd dissipated when Chu Feng easily found and resolved the formation on the fourth floor too. That led the crowd to speculate about Chu Feng’s identity.","Those from the Huangfu Heavenly Clan couldn’t help but glance at Jie Shanxian while observing Chu Feng. Even those from the Seven Realms Immortal Sect had begun speculating Jie Shanxian’s background. They knew that Chu Feng and Jie Shanxian had come together.","“Lord Sectmaster, how is that brat so formidable too? Could they have a powerful backing?”","The Seven Realms Immortal Sect secretly sent voice transmission to their sectmaster, but their sectmaster quietly stared at Chu Feng.","Chu Feng received a Cosmos Sack each time he resolved a formation, and in it were a God Armament and cultivation resources. Correspondingly, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan would take the metal piece from him and use their bloodline power to assimilate it.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan had planned to find the final power by themselves, but Chu Feng’s appearance convinced them to change their strategy. Most Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were gathered around Chu Feng by this point.","Finally, Chu Feng resolved the formation on the 98th floor too.","The yellow-bearded elder handed the Cosmos Sack he had prepared to Chu Feng as he asked, “Young friend, I realized I haven’t asked you for your name yet.”","“I’m Chu Feng.”","“Chu Feng?”","The yellow-bearded elder and the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were taken aback. That was a familiar name to them, but they didn’t think that he was the Nine Heavens’ Zenith’s Chu Feng.","They didn’t look like each other, and they didn’t think that Chu Feng was capable enough to find his way into this formation realm. In the first place, the world was so big that there were plenty of people with the same name. It wouldn’t be surprising to find two people without blood relations who looked identical to each other.","Two people having the same name was nothing to make a fuss over.","“I’ll be taking my leave if there’s nothing else,” Chu Feng said.","“Where are you going?” Huangfu Jiangxing asked.","“Our cooperation has ended. You have received all the formations. It’s none of your business where I go,” Chu Feng replied.","Huangfu Jiangxing had long thought that Chu Feng was an eyesore. Seeing how the latter dared to talk back to him despite having completed the mission, he made up his mind to kill the latter.","The yellow-bearded elder hurriedly interjected, “Young friend Chu Feng, what should we do after we assimilate all these formations?”","“Piece the formations together. That’s all I know,” Chu Feng replied before turning to Huangfu Jiangxing. “You’re thinking of killing me, aren’t you?”","Before Huangfu Jiangxing could reply, Chu Feng turned his gaze toward the other Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen, including the yellow-bearded elder. “It isn’t just him. The rest of you can’t wait to kill me too. After all, I’ve taken so many God Armaments from you.”","The yellow-bearded elder laughed. “Young friend Chu Feng, you’re thinking too much. Our Huangfu Heavenly Clan prides itself on its integrity. We would never do anything like that when we have already agreed to work together.”","There was no way he would acknowledge Chu Feng’s claim.","“If that’s the case, no one will stop me if I leave, right?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course not. Feel free,” the yellow-bearded elder said.","“I’ll be taking my leave then.” Chu Feng clasped his fist and left.","“Are we letting him go?” Huangfu Jiangxing asked.","The yellow-bearded elder sighed in frustration. He had already told Huangfu Jiangxing that outsiders could hear their conversation, but the latter continued to show zero discretion. If not for his bloodline talent and his background as the clan chief’s son...","The yellow-bearded elder answered via voice transmission, “Don’t worry, young master. We have left tracking talismans in the Cosmos Sacks we gave him, so he won’t be able to get away. Those outside can hear our words, so it’s best not to say some things out loud.”","“Hmph.” Huangfu Jiangxing harrumphed in disdain, but he still switched to voice transmission. “They are just a bunch of small fry. There’s no need to care too much about their opinions. We should make an example out of someone and show them the consequences of disrespecting our Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","“It’s Lord Clan Chief’s will for us not to go too far. It wouldn’t be wise for us to defy his order, especially not when Lord Huangfu Zhantian is watching outside. Of course, we won’t take this lying. That brat is audacious and greedy. How dare he extort our Huangfu Heavenly Clan?","“Once we conquer the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, I’ll capture that brat and leave his punishment to you,” the yellow-bearded elder said.","“I’ll make him suffer a fate worse than death. He shall kneel before me and beg me to end his life” Huangfu Jiangxing sneered discreetly."]},{"number":6260,"title":"Chapter 6260: Chapter 6258: Forging the Secret Skill","paragraphs":["Chapter 6258: Forging the Secret Skill","“Chu Feng, they must be seething with hatred. There’s no way they will spare you,” Eggy said.","“Definitely. Why else would they plant so many location talismans inside my Cosmos Sacks?” Chu Feng replied.","The location talismans were fused inside the cultivation resources, making them extremely discreet, but they couldn’t escape Chu Feng’s notice.","Chu Feng lingered on the 98th floor. The spectators continued to pay attention to him because they were curious what he was going to do, but he suddenly formed a hand seal and vanished into thin air.","“Where did he go?”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen outside instinctively sensed that things were about go awry. They began to quietly form an encirclement around Jie Shanxian to seal her routes of escape, knowing that she was with Chu Feng.","“The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen aren’t going to let you leave that easily,” the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster told Jie Shanxian via voice transmission.","“Let them try,” Jie Shanxian scoffed.","“Where do you think that young friend went?” the sectmaster asked.","“I don’t know,” Jie Shanxian replied curtly.","The sectmaster could tell that Jie Shanxian was not interested in discussing this matter, so he didn’t bother asking more, though he turned his eyes to the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s peak. He deduced that since Chu Feng knew how to find and resolve those formations, he likely knew more secrets about the tower.","The biggest secret about the Immemorial Bloodline Tower should be at its peak, though that was not necessarily the case since there was a section on the 99th floor blocked from outside view too.","“Have you found a way to enter the 99th floor yet?” Huangfu Zhantian asked the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elders.","His deduction coincided with the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster. He thought that Chu Feng must have entered the peak or the section of the 99th floor that was shielded from their view.","Unfortunately, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan had no idea how to enter the 99th floor despite having entered the tower many times before. This was the first time they had a chance to enter the 99th floor.","That was why they left a group of people to continue investigating the tower even though they needed as many clansmen as possible to refine the formations Chu Feng discovered.","“We haven’t found the way into the 99th floor yet,” an elder replied.","“Useless!” Huangfu Zhantian berated.","In truth, he wasn’t confident of finding a path to the 99th floor even if he entered the tower.","...","In truth, Chu Feng had entered a formation passageway.","The passageway was so short that it felt like he was stepping through a door instead. On the other side of the passageway was a majestic palace. This was the section of the 99th floor that the spectators outside couldn’t see.","“B-b-brother, what took you s-s-so long?” a familiar voice echoed from behind.","Chu Feng didn’t need to look to know that it was Wang Qiang.","“Those Huangfu fools were working as coolies for me,” Chu Feng replied.","“Oh? H-h-how did you make them do it?” Wang Qiang was intrigued.","“A huge amount of bloodline power is needed to acquire the power here. Unlike the tower activation, which is more demanding on bloodline quality, what I got the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen to do is more demanding on bloodline quantity. It would have taken me a long time to do it myself. Since they have more people, I had them help me instead.”","“A-a-and they were willing to help you?”","“Of course not. They thought I voluntarily handed the benefits to them because I was intimidated. Little do they know that I have already imprinted on all the formations. They are merely working for me now,” Chu Feng replied.","“Holy shit! Won’t they d-d-die of anger once they learn the truth? Looks like a conflict with the Huangfu Heavenly Clan is i-i-inevitable,” Wang Qiang replied.","“Not necessarily,” Chu Feng replied.","“H-h-huh?” Wang Qiang was confused.","“There are no definites in the world.” Chu Feng chuckled, choosing to keep Wang Qiang in suspense. “Brother, why didn’t you breach the formation?”","He already knew what was hidden here, and he knew that he could tell that the formation wouldn’t be too tough to breach either. What was difficult was the subsequent trial, though he was confident Wang Qiang could conquer it.","“I’m waiting f-f-for you to share the benefits. Brother, what’s h-h-hiding here?” Wang Qiang asked.","“It’s a secret skill. You can think of it as an additional benefit from the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. Brother, I shan’t beat around the bush. The power here could potentially strengthen my bloodline power, so I’m planning to take it for myself. You should take the secret skill. I’ll help you if you aren’t able to breach the formation,” Chu Feng said.","“S-s-secret skill? What kind of secret skill?” Wang Qiang asked.","“This secret skill is currently incomplete, but it will complete itself based on your traits. In other words, it is a secret skill tailored to your needs,” Chu Feng replied.","“H-h-holy! That’s some good stuff!” Wang Qiang exclaimed.","“Indeed.”","“I-I-I can’t monopolize something as good as that! Brother, let’s do s-s-scissors paper stone. Whoever loses gets the secret skill.”","“Why does the loser get the secret skill?”","“Hehe, it’s the spirit of giving. It shows h-h-how close we are.” Wang Qiang chuckled.","“Let’s cut the nonsense. I take the power; you take the secret skill. There’s also something at the peak that I covet, and it’s more important than this secret skill. Take the secret skill if you consider yourself my brother,” Chu Feng said.","“Your words make sense, b-b-but I haven’t contributed at all. I just h-h-happen to be here, or else everything would have been yours. It’s like I’m f-f-freeloading off you.” Wang Qiang felt embarrassed.","“Brothers share fortune and woes. Think of it as us stumbling upon three delicacies together. Even if I found it first, I can’t monopolize everything without leaving a dish aside for you. That would be too much, no? If I did so, it would mean that I don’t see you as my brother,” Chu Feng said.","“That k-k-kind of makes sense.”","“It’s not ‘kind of makes sense’. It makes perfect sense. Besides, sharing things with my brothers brings me a feeling of accomplishment and fulfillment. You shouldn’t rob me of my happiness just because you feel embarrassed,” Chu Feng said.","“F-f-fine, I shan’t be so indecisive. I’ll be t-t-taking the secret skill then.” Wang Qiang chuckled as he began breaching the formation.","Chu Feng thought that Wang Qiang wouldn’t have trouble with the formation, but two hours passed and there was still no response from Wang Qiang. It made him realize that the formation might be more difficult than he had anticipated.","All of a sudden, the palace shook. Countless surges of auras manifested all around the palace.","Chu Feng observed the situation vigilantly, ready to intervene if Wang Qiang encountered a hurdle. Moments later, his face lit up with delight.","“That’s the method to forging the secret skill!” Chu Feng exclaimed."]},{"number":6261,"title":"Chapter 6261: Chapter 6259: A New Ancient Era’s Secret Skill","paragraphs":["Chapter 6259: A New Ancient Era’s Secret Skill","“What? You should pay close attention to it then!” Eggy exclaimed in delight.","Chu Feng was capable of creating his secret skills and martial skills too, but what was difficult was creating skills stronger than what he had already grasped. He was confident of pulling it off given sufficient time, but he didn’t want to spend time on it.","The predecessors had created many secret skills and martial skills, and plenty were passed down through the generations.","Chu Feng had so many things to do that he would rather devote his time elsewhere. Thus, he preferred picking up ready-made secret and martial skills instead.","Eggy was well aware of that, so she could tell from Chu Feng’s current excitement that the ‘secret skill forging method’ he mentioned was a big deal. It must be a means that Chu Feng hadn’t grasped yet.","That was why she urged Chu Feng to focus and learn.","This situation didn’t last for long. The aura shrouding Wang Qiang soon seeped into his body. Then, Wang Qiang pounced up from the ground like a revived monkey. He jumped up to Chu Feng, grabbed the latter’s shoulders, and stared at him with eyes widened like bells and mouth cracked so wide open that it almost reached the back of his head.","“H-h-holy, brother... This is r-r-really good stuff!”","“You succeeded?” Chu Feng asked.","“O-o-of course. Here, I’ll s-s-show you,” Wang Qiang said.","He formed a hand seal. Four auras gushed out of his body and manifested into four incomparably massive beasts with an overwhelming presence. It was a manifestation of the Four Fiends. Each of these beasts harnessed incredible offensive prowess.","Chu Feng could tell that the secret skill was tailored to Wang Qiang’s Four Fiends Divine Body.","“How does my secret s-s-skill look, brother?” Wang Qiang asked with a grin.","“It is formidable. I’d say it is stronger than the average rank three God Taboo,” Chu Feng replied.","“You have good eyes. I-It’s all thanks to you, brother. If not for you, I couldn’t have o-o-obtained such a powerful secret skill.” Wang Qiang suddenly lowered his head in apologetically. “Brother, i-i-it’s not that I want to be wishy-washy, but I feel t-t-terrible about taking this. You’re a cultivator t-t-too. Who wouldn’t want s-s-something like that?”","“You’re mistaken. I benefited from this too, and it might be better this way,” Chu Feng replied.","“Y-y-you benefited too? How?” Wnag Qiang was confused.","“I gained more than you. You learned a secret skill, but I learned a method that can further enhance my secret skills.” Chu Feng told Wang Qiang what happened earlier.","“H-h-holy! As expected of my brother! Y-y-you were able to learn so much from the forging of my s-s-secret skill?” A smile returned to Wang Qiang’s face.","Anyone else would have thought there were two benefits here—one was the forging of a secret skill, and the other was the method of forging secret skills.","But Wang Qiang interpreted the situation differently.","He believed there was only one benefit here, just that Chu Feng happened to witness the forging of the secret skill and was intelligent enough to grasp it.","Using an analogy, it was similar to how most kids might not learn anything from seeing experts fight, but the more talented ones might remember a couple of moves and put them to good use.","Chu Feng was lucky to witness the process, but without talent, he wouldn’t have been able to grasp the secret skill forging method. Wang Qiang thought it was unlikely that anyone other than Chu Feng could have learned the secret skill forging method just by observing it.","“I recently obtained the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Nine Secret Skills. Even though they aren’t weak, I somehow feel they aren’t polished enough. This method allows me to properly polish up the Nine Secret Skills. This method came at a good time. Give me a moment, brother. Let me modify the Nine Secret Skills inside me.”","Chu Feng sat down and began forming hand seals. His martial power flowed out and swiftly coiled around his body, similar to the aura that enveloped Wang Qiang earlier.","Soon, several weapons emerged from Chu Feng’s body. They were the manifestations of the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Nine Secret Skills. However, there were more than just nine of them. He had obtained all the Nine Secret Skills from the eradicated Ancient Era’s War Clan, after all.","Countless weapons revolved around Chu Feng in unique trajectories. Amazingly, none of them bumped into one another. The trajectories changed in real time as Chu Feng made adjustments to find the perfect flow.","“This is so complicated!” Wang Qiang was dumbstruck.","He didn’t think he could learn such a complicated method despite being a cultivation prodigy himself, and it made him feel greater respect for Chu Feng.","Chu Feng remained in this state for three days before he changed his hand seal.","The martial power and weapons revolving around him suddenly surged back into his body.","“Haa!” Chu Feng sighed as he got up.","“W-w-what’s wrong? Did you fail?” Wang Qiang stared at Chu Feng with widened eyes.","“I was too confident. I didn’t grasp the crux of it. I was able to modify the secret skill, but I couldn’t raise it to the level I wanted,” Chu Feng said.","“Brother, why don’t I give my s-s-secret skill to you?” Wang Qiang offered.","“No need for that. I have another hand.” Chu Feng took out an ancient talisman paper.","This talisman paper had quite the background.","The Ancestral Martial Galaxy’s Great Chiliocosm Upper Realm had Six Great Sacred Vestiges: Primal Sea Sacred Mountain, Ethereal Sacred Gate, Darknight Sacred River, Nine Moons Sacred Domain, Purple Sun Sacred Palace, and Void Sacred Tree.","Before Chu Feng left the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, he chanced upon the opening of the Darknight Sacred River and entered it. There, he met Song Yuwei, whom his grandmother had tasked to send his father, Chu Xuanyuan, back to the Chu Heavenly Clan.","Song Yuwei chanced upon the opening of the Darknight Sacred River after sending Chu Xuanyuan back to the Chu Heavenly Clan. She thought that there was a fortuitous encounter inside and entered it. Little did she expect to be trapped in there.","Chu Feng also met a mysterious Lord Bai inside the Darknight Sacred River.","Lord Bai had once given Song Yuwei a talisman that could greatly enhance the power of Song Yuwei’s secret skill. Before Lord Bai left, he also gave Chu Feng one of those talismans.","Oblivious to Chu Feng, Lord Bai had another name—the Eight Trigram Dao Immortal.","“Elder Bai, it’s time to put the item you have given me to good use,” Chu Feng remarked as he looked at the talisman in his hand.","When he first obtained the talisman paper, he had intended to offer it to the Descent of the Demon Exalted, but the latter ignored him. He tried using it on the Ancient Era’s War Sword too, but it was too weak to fuse with the talisman paper.","He later learned why the Descent of the Demon Exalted refused to serve him. He could force the Descent of Demon Exalted to do his bidding, the Descent of the Demon Exalted was still a part of the Blood-devouring Demon Exalted.","Since the Blood-devouring Demon Exalted was now hiding in Wang Qiang’s body, Chu Feng decided not to assimilate the Descent of the Demon Exalted just yet,","He believed that his modification of the Ancient Era’s War Clan’s Nine Secret Skills had gone well, but the only problem was that these secret skills were replicas, so their prowess was still lacking.","This talisman paper was the perfect tool to strengthen the Nine Secret Skills.","Chu Feng activated the talisman paper before absorbing it into his body and fusing it into his secret skills. The Nine Secret Skills, including the Ancient Era’s War Sword and Ancient Era’s War Axe, were all fused into a new secret skill.","“This talisman paper is incredible!” Chu Feng was amazed. He was satisfied with the result.","He couldn’t help but wonder who Lord Bai was to give out such a powerful talisman paper just like that."]},{"number":6262,"title":"Chapter 6262: Chapter 6260: The Divine Deer’s Gaze Changes","paragraphs":["Chapter 6260: The Divine Deer’s Gaze Changes","“Brother, did you succeed?” Wang Qiang asked.","“Mmhm. It’s not just a success; it surpassed my expectations,” Chu Feng said.","“T-t-then how does it compare to my secret skill?”","“It’s definitely not weaker than yours.”","“Are you f-f-for real? Let’s spar!”","“Forget it. I don’t want to ruin your pride.”","“Hahaha, I like your c-c-confidence.”","Wang Qiang was even happier than Chu Feng. He felt conscience-stricken accepting the secret skill as he thought it should have belonged to Chu Feng. Only now when he saw that Chu Feng had benefited from this fortuitous encounter too did he feel ease of mind.","“Brother, there’s some energy here that enhances our bloodline, but its effects are quite lackluster. I doubt that it’ll be of much help to us. There’s no need for you to stay here anymore. You should wait for me outside,” Chu Feng said.","“What are you doing, brother? T-t-take me with you. We agreed to b-b-brave through danger together,” Wang Qiang said.","“Some things should be shouldered alone. We shouldn’t put ourselves in danger just for the sake of it, right?”","“Your words make sense, b-b-but something sounds off.”","“Don’t worry, brother. Don’t forget that I have everything within my grasp. Nothing will happen to me,” Chu Feng twirled his palm as he spoke with a smirk.","“Haha, t-t-that’s true. I’ll wait for you outside.”","Wang Qiang returned to the first floor via the secret passageway.","Chu Feng looked at the ceiling. A secret passageway was hidden there. He had to open the passageway to get to the peak of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. There, he would find what the Divine Deer wanted.","And the method to do so was the same as summoning the metal piece formations.","In truth, those who comprehended the nine-colored lightning sphere could easily navigate the tower, whereas those who failed wouldn’t even come close to this fortuitous encounter.","Chu Feng formed a hand seal and fused his bloodline power into the ceiling. A formation appeared on the ceiling, and it opened up to reveal an entrance. The entrance was so small that those who were too big wouldn’t be able to fit in.","With this gap, he could use his spirit power to scan the peak.","Boom!","Before Chu Feng could discern anything, a force gushed down from the entrance and suffused the tower. It was a powerful force that not only restricted Chu Feng’s movements but caused his bones to creak as well.","It was fortunate Wang Qiang had left, or else he would have to suffer together with Chu Feng.","Chu Feng took a moment to adapt to the force. He tried to scan the peak, only to find that his spirit power was unable to pass through the force. Thus, he leaped through the entrance and entered the highest floor of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.","He found himself in a hall smaller than that of the 99th floor. His surroundings were painted white, so much so that it was difficult to make out where the walls were. It felt boundless and a little divine.","It was due to that that his eyes were drawn to the center, where a golden blade of grass floated at the center of the hall.","“Elder, is that it?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes, but I didn’t expect it would be golden,” the Divine Deer replied.","“Is it formidable?”","“Yes, I have heard about the golden grass. To obtain it, you only have to touch it. However, it will unleash a powerful force to attack you, and the force becomes stronger the closer you are to it. You also mustn’t attempt to obtain it remotely, or else it will deem you unqualified, and you won’t be able to obtain it anymore,” the Divine Deer warned.","“Elder, it’s a relief you are here to remind me, or else I would have tried to obtain it remotely.” Chu Feng was alarmed. He had been observing the golden grass, and he didn’t find any signs that discouraged obtaining the golden grass remotely.","“Chu Feng, this item is placed here to be claimed, but it is beyond someone of your cultivation to handle. You can give it a try, but don’t force yourself if it’s too much. Don’t lose sight of what’s important over trivialities,” the Divine Deer reminded.","“Don’t worry, elder. I’ll be prudent.”","The first thing Chu Feng did was to construct a teleportation formation linked to the 99th floor. This way, he could return to the 99th floor if he reached his limit.","Weng!","But as soon as the teleportation formation was completed, the golden grass suddenly unleashed a brilliant light, as if it had read his mind. The light harnessed overwhelming destructive prowess, and it burned through Chu Feng’s skin, flesh, and bones. Even his soul was put under tremendous pressure.","“What’s wrong, Chu Feng?” Eggy and the Divine Deer asked.","They had just witnessed the instantaneous destruction of Chu Feng’s body, leaving behind just his soul.","“I’m fine,” Chu Feng replied.","“Are you sure? You lost your body!” Eggy didn’t believe him.","“Don’t force yourself, Chu Feng,” the Divine Deer advised.","“I feel some pressure, but my skin is anything but thick. If this is a test of willpower, I can only say that the golden grass is prepared just for me.” Chu Feng was in so much pain that his words didn’t come out as smoothly as they usually did, but a tenacious smile remained on his face.","He took a moment to adapt before making his way toward the golden grass.","Every step he took would cause the golden grass to emanate a brighter light, heaping even greater pressure on him.","Chu Feng had lied.","His body was far stronger than his peers, yet it was decimated by the first attack. This showed just how powerful the golden grass’ attack was. Most people’s souls would have dissipated with the attack; he had only survived due to his superior resilience.","His soul was already under tremendous strain, but the attack was continuous, and it only intensified the closer he got to the golden grass. It was as if he was inside a furnace filled with flames. Unless he left the furnace, he wouldn’t be able to avoid the heat.","Even Wang Qiang and Little Fishy wouldn’t have been able to withstand this.","It was indeed no easy feat to get the golden grass.","Chu Feng wasn’t confident in overcoming this trial, and he was ready to give up if needed. However, he was determined to hold on for as long as possible till he was at his limit.","Chu Feng took a deep breath and continued advancing.","“Chu Feng, does your teleportation formation still work?” Eggy asked.","She could tell from his ragged breathing that he wasn’t in a good condition. She knew that he was determined to give it a try and wouldn’t listen to her advice, so the least she could do was to ensure that he had a way out.","“It’s still working. I can leave anytime I want if I reach my limit,” Chu Feng replied.","He tried his best to feign normalcy, but Eggy could tell that he was severely weakened. She felt a pinch in her heart, but she didn’t persuade her to give up. Instead, she rooted for him, saying, “You can do it.”","Every step Chu Feng took was a challenge. It was a short distance, yet it felt like they were worlds apart. It reached a point where his consciousness began turning hazy, but he persisted.","Finally, Chu Feng reached the golden grass and grabbed it.","As soon as he touched the golden grass, the terrifying light vanished.","Chu Feng collapsed to the ground, unconscious.","A white light seeped out of his body and morphed into a figure. It was a beautiful woman wearing a green dress. She was so beautiful that few aside from Eggy and Little Fishy could match her appearance.","She was the Divine Deer.","She knew about this golden grass, which was why she understood how difficult it had been for Chu Feng to obtain it. The hardships he endured for her sake moved her. Not only were his face and lips pale, but even his soul was filled with cracks.","The Divine Deer couldn’t imagine the sheer willpower it had taken Chu Feng to go this far.","“No wonder your companions trust you so much. You are indeed worthy of their trust.”","The Divine Deer’s eyes had long become placid after having witnessed the vicissitudes of life, yet they flickered when looking at Chu Feng now.","She had only thought that he was a reliable person when she saw how he put his life on the line for his friends, but now that he was doing it for her, it somehow shook her to the core.","She couldn’t help but look at Chu Feng with shaken eyes."]},{"number":6263,"title":"Chapter 6263: Chapter 6261: Time to Reel In the Net","paragraphs":["Chapter 6261: Time to Reel In the Net","The golden grass cast a faint golden light on Chu Feng now that he had tamed it. The same light that previously tried to burn him to ashes was now healing his injuries. Its healing prowess was as frightening as its destructive prowess.","The Divine Deer knew that Chu Feng would soon recover under the golden light’s healing despite his severe injuries, so she wasn’t worried about him. She was only moved by his earlier valiance.","She bent down and gently stroked Chu Feng’s face with her snowy-white, slender palm. A mesmerizing smile formed on her lips as her eyes narrowed into beautiful crescents. It was a contemplative but gentle smile.","Seconds later, she morphed into a white light and returned to Chu Feng’s body.","Just as she had guessed, it didn’t take long for Chu Feng to recover under the golden grass’ treatment. Not only did his soul fully recover, but his body was restored as well. It didn’t take him long to regain consciousness.","“You’re awake, Chu Feng. How do you feel?”","Even though Eggy shared senses with Chu Feng, it only worked when he was conscious. She didn’t know that the Divine Deer had come out, and she didn’t hear her words either. Thus, she was only concerned about Chu Feng’s safety.","“I’m fine. It doesn’t hurt anymore. Instead, I feel refreshed,” Chu Feng said merrily as he leaped to his feet.","Through Chu Feng’s eyes, Eggy could tell that his body had fully recovered.","“Is it the golden grass’ doing?” Eggy asked.","“Most likely.”","Chu Feng looked at the golden grass he clutched in his hand with a gleeful smile. Only he knew how tough it had been for him to obtain it. He was on the verge of giving up.","“Can you use it for your cultivation?” Eggy asked.","“The golden grass contains martial power and spirit power, but there’s also energy in it that I’m unable to see through. It seems to be from a formation, but it could be from something else too. It is quite a peculiar thing, Anyway, I got it for Elder Divine Deer. I won’t use it for myself even if it benefits me.”","Chu Feng sent a voice transmission to the Divine Deer inside him. “Elder, I have obtained the golden grass. Do you want to come out and take it?”","The Divine Deer sent a surge of energy out from Chu Feng’s body and swiped the golden grass away.","As soon as she took the golden grass, the Immemorial Bloodline Tower shook intensely. Others might not know what happened as nothing happened after the shaking, but Chu Feng could tell that the golden grass was the cause of it.","The Divine Deer had told him that the golden grass was the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s source of energy, powering its formations. To take it away meant robbing the tower of its source of energy.","The tower was still fine at the moment because it still had reserve energy, but once that was depleted, the tower would collapse.","Chu Feng wasn’t worried about that. As a world spiritist, he could tell that the tower could last for a while longer. However, if he took away the final power too, the Immemorial Bloodline Tower would likely collapse on the spot.","“Chu Feng, I am very satisfied with your performance. I’ll impart Divine Evasion to you as soon as we leave this place,” the Divine Deer said.","Chu Feng’s face lit up with delight. “Thank you, elder.”","The Divine Deer had previously told him that she was a god skill, and she possessed three abilities, namely Divine Concealment, Divine Flitting, and Divine Evasion.","Divine Concealment didn’t physically hide a person, but it completely erased one’s aura. That made it impossible to notice one’s presence as long as one remained out of sight.","Divine Flitting greatly raised a person’s movement speed.","Chu Feng had already grasped those two abilities.","Divine Evasion allowed one to avoid a powerful attack. For instance, if he activated Divine Evasion as a rank one True God level cultivator, he could escape unscathed from even a rank seven True God level cultivator.","Against stronger cultivators, it was a powerful survival means.","Against peers, it was a powerful trick that could be used to secure victory.","Chu Feng was qualified to learn Divine Evasion now that he had reached True God level, which was why he had once asked the Divine Deer to teach him. However, the latter refused to impart the ability to him, and there was nothing he could do about it since it was her ability.","Yet, the Divine Deer was now taking the initiative to teach him.","Chu Feng thought that it was worthwhile acquiring the golden grass.","“Don’t bother flattering me with flowery words. It’s a reward for obtaining this natural oddity for me. You can be assured that I keep my promises, so you should settle whatever business you have here first. The tower might not last long,” the Divine Deer said.","“All right,” Chu Feng replied.","“Chu Feng Chu Feng, why does it feel like the Divine Deer’s tone when talking to you has changed?” Eggy asked via voice transmission.","“Did it? I don’t hear it,” Chu Feng replied.","“Haa, it must be because you’re a man. You’re usually very observant, so how can you be so dense about such matters? Either way, it is a change for the better,” Eggy replied.","“That’s good to hear,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","He suddenly narrowed his eyes. The Immemorial Bloodline Tower had started shaking again, but this time, it was not just an intermittent but continuous shaking. He quickly returned to the 99th floor, and the shaking there was much more intense.","“Has it begun?” Instead of panicking, Chu Feng’s smile deepened. “The Huangfu Heavenly Clan moves fast. They are right on time.”","“Are they done yet?” Eggy asked.","“Not yet, but it shouldn’t take long.”","“Are you returning to the 98th floor?”","“No need for that. I can reap the rewards here.”","“Won’t they die of anger?” Eggy asked in excitement. There was not a tinge of fear in her voice because she knew that Chu Feng had a way to escape.","All the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen who entered the Immemorial Bloodline Tower were gathered on the 98th floor. After refining the metal pieces obtained from each level, they brought them to the 98th floor and began piecing them together like a puzzle.","The metal pieces floated in mid-air, emanating terrifying nine-colored lightning that enveloped the 98th floor.","“This thing is highly beneficial to bloodline powers.”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen quivered with excitement. As possessors of the Heavenly Bloodline, they could feel the resonance between their bloodline and the nine-colored lightning emanating from the metal pieces.","Soon, all the metal pieces fused to form a portrait. The portrait began rising into the sky as it expanded until it was finally covering everything above. Nine massive lightning beasts growled in the painting.","The lightning emanated by the nine massive lightning beasts was terrifying. It enveloped not just the 98th floor but the entire tower, including the 99th floor.","“It’s about time to reel in the net,” Chu Feng remarked."]},{"number":6264,"title":"Chapter 6264: Chapter 6262: Chu Feng?!","paragraphs":["Chapter 6262: Chu Feng?!","The portrait dissipated, but the nine massive lightning beasts continued to prowl the sky.","“We succeeded! Congratulations, young master!”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen turned to Huangfu Jiangxing, knowing that the final reward would go to him. He would become the pillar that propped the Huangfu Heavenly Clan to further heights.","“It’s all thanks to Chu Feng, or else we wouldn’t have found this,” the yellow-bearded elder remarked. He was glad that Chu Feng had deciphered the nine-colored lightning sphere, or else they would have never gotten this far.","“So what if he discovered the formations? He has no choice but to obediently hand them over to us. There’s no way he could have refined so many formations by himself and pieced them together,” Huangfu Jiangxing scoffed in displeasure.","Sensing the awry atmosphere, the yellow-bearded elder quickly changed the topic, “You’re right. Young master, what do you plan to do next? If I’m not mistaken, the next step is to absorb the nine lightning beasts, but they aren't that easy to deal with.”","Huangfu Jiangxing frowned. “Is it dangerous?”","“It could be. Young master, you shouldn’t make a move yet. Let me and the other clansmen investigate the situation first.”","The yellow-bearded elder ordered the crowd to construct a formation with him.","Nine-colored lightning flowed out of the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen’s bodies and converged into a massive lightning sword, which surged toward the nine lightning beasts in the sky.","The aggression prompted the nine lightning beasts to simultaneously unleash nine-colored lightning on the lightning sword.","So far, the nine-colored lightning that enveloped the Immemorial Bloodline Tower had been harmless. Despite its intimidating appearance, it didn’t cause tangible damage.","The nine-colored lightning unleashed by the nine lightning beasts, however, was capable of mass destruction.","The two nine-colored lightning entities clashed as if to determine who was the real deal.","The world shook.","The victor was determined right away. The lightning sword dissipated, and all the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen who participated in the formation sustained severe injuries, including the yellow-bearded elder.","What was peculiar was that all of them sustained the same degree of burns regardless of their cultivation. This imposed equality further showed how formidable the nine lightning beasts were.","“What’s going on? Did we get the method wrong?”","Huangfu Jiangxing stared at the yellow-bearded elder in horror. Instead of feeling sorry for the latter, the only thought dominating his mind was how he could absorb the nine lightning beasts.","“Young master, it looks like a forceful approach won’t work,” the yellow-bearded elder reported the situation to Huangfu Jiangxing despite his severe injuries.","“What do we do?” Huangfu Jiangxing asked.","“I don’t know.” The yellow-bearded elder shook his head.","The crowd outside the Immemorial Bloodline Tower was astounded too. They thought that everything was within the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s grasp, but who could have thought that the item they had painstakingly pieced together would be so devastating?","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen outside turned to Huangfu Zhantian and asked, “What’s going on, milord?”","“Why are you asking me? It’s my first time seeing this too!” Huangfu Zhantian glared at the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen.","“Huangfu Shangwu, you go. Charge into the nine-colored lightning without attacking it,” Huangfu Jiangxing ordered.","Huangfu Shangwu frowned. “Young master Jiangxing, you should go instead. It would be terrible if I accidentally obtained the final power.”","He was reluctant to obey the orders because he knew how dangerous it was.","“Stop yapping off and do what you’re told!” Huangfu Jiangxing glared at Huangfu Shangwu.","Huangfu Shangwu was a prodigy, but his standing was beneath Huangfu Jiangxing. He had no choice but to obey the latter’s order and charge straight toward the nine lightning beasts.","Before he could reach the nine lightning beasts, a bolt of lightning fell on him, causing him to plummet to the ground. He was still alive, but he suffered the same burns as the other Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen.","Neither attacking nor approaching the nine lightning beasts worked. This put the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen at a loss.","“We must have been duped by that Chu Feng bastard. This isn’t the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s power at all!” Huangfu Jiangxing exclaimed.","Suddenly, the nine lightning beasts howled, causing the lightning surging through the Immemorial Bloodline Tower to flare up. The previously harmless nine-colored lightning became destructive, and it ripped through the tower’s space.","The hundred floors of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower collapsed into a single floor.","This abrupt twist surprised even the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen in the tower.","“What’s wrong? Can’t subjugate this power?” a voice echoed above the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen.","A person was floating in the sky. He was none other than Chu Feng.","“Men, take him down!” Huangfu Jiangxing ordered.","Many Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen charged into the sky, but they opted to take a huge detour to avoid the nine lightning beasts.","Bzzt!","Yet, the nine lightning beasts still unleashed their lightning on them, causing them to plummet to the ground. Despite the hundred floors collapsing into a giant space, the nine-colored lightning continued to crackle menacingly throughout the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen dared not make a reckless move anymore.","“Huangfu Jiangxing, why aren’t you conquering the nine lightning beasts? Are you not interested in the power that enhances your bloodline?” Chu Feng asked.","“This isn’t the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s power. You deceived us into squandering our energy. What are you scheming?” Huangfu Jiangxing questioned.","“This isn’t the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s power? Hahaha...” Chu Feng burst into laughter. “Fine, I’ll show you whether it’s the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s power or not.”","Chu Feng descended from the sky, heading toward the nine lightning beasts beneath him.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen scoffed in disdain.","“That ignorant fool,” Huangfu Jiangxing sneered.","So many of their clansmen had already been injured by the nine lightning beasts. He thought that Chu Feng was courting his doom by approaching the nine lightning beasts at this juncture.","However, his smile soon eroded.","Not only did the nine lightning beasts not attack Chu Feng, but they even began unraveling into pure lightning so that they could surge into Chu Feng’s body. Under the influx of lightning, Chu Feng’s face began to transform.","Many Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were stunned, for Chu Feng’s face was one that they had seen before. Huangfu Shangwu and Huangfu Zhantian had the most interesting looks on their faces.","“Chu Feng?!”"]},{"number":6265,"title":"Chapter 6265: Chapter 6263: How Am I To Know?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6263: How Am I To Know?","Absorbing the lightning didn't harm Chu Feng, but it removed his disguise, forcing him to revert to his original appearance.","That shocked the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","“You are Chu Feng... You are the real Chu Feng?!” Huangfu Shangwu, despite his injuries, exclaimed at Chu Feng.","He had crossed blows with Chu Feng in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith. There was no way he could forget the latter’s face.","“What do you mean I am the real Chu Feng? I never said I was the fake Chu Feng,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","He didn’t look to be in pain despite the lightning seeping into his body. He stared at Huangfu Shangwu with a calm demeanor. Not only that, but he was so calm that it made Huangfu Shangwu shudder as inexplicable fear crept into his heart.","“What’s going on? You know him?” Huangfu Jiangxing asked.","“Young master Jiangxing, he is Chu Feng, the Nine Heavens’ Zenith’s Chu Feng, the most talented prodigy of the present-era cultivators,” Huangfu Shangwu explained.","Huangfu Jiangxing was no fool. He had figured out as much, but he wanted confirmation. That confirmation further fanned his rage. He had been wanting to confront Chu Feng ever since he heard about the latter, but he didn’t expect to be outdone by Chu Feng on his turf.","The outsiders also snapped out of their daze, and a huge commotion broke out. They had heard about Chu Feng, but most didn’t know what he looked like.","Those who had initially joined Chu Feng’s team but were eliminated sensed their Cosmos Sack being unsealed, so they took it out and inspected its contents. The treasures inside surpassed their wildest imagination.","“We misunderstood Chu Feng!”","They finally understood Chu Feng’s rationale for eliminating them. Those who had entered the tower with Chu Feng were all in trouble. Those people were nowhere to be seen at the moment, but there was no doubt that the Huangfu Heavenly Clan would be going after them.","Being eliminated saved them instead.","The one who looked the most conflicted was Huangfu Zhantian.","“I see. Chu Feng was the one who awakened the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. No wonder, no wonder,” he remarked publicly.","His words were so authoritative that many took them as the truth. However, the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen gathered outside the tower looked as if someone had stuffed feces down their throats.","They had to agree with Huangfu Zhantian’s words, having heard that Chu Feng possessed a formidable bloodline power. On top of that, Chu Feng was able to absorb the energy inside the Immemorial Bloodline Tower when the others weren’t able to do anything about it.","It made perfect sense that the tower was awakened by Chu Feng.","But how could those words be spoken aloud? Wasn’t it putting their clan down? It would tarnish their Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s image!","Had anyone else said those words, their heads would have rolled! But no one dared to stage a protest because those words had come from Huangfu Zhantian’s mouth. No one dared to berate him.","Little did they know Huangfu Zhantian had done it on purpose. He was there at the Nine Heavens’ Zenith too.","Huangfu Shangwu had filled him in on the details as soon as he left the Nine Heavens’ Zenith. While Huangfu Shangwu didn’t get into the final trial, it didn’t take a genius to figure out that Chu Feng and the others must have been behind the deaths of Huangfu Shengyu and the others.","Huangfu Zhantian knew just how much the clan chief doted on Huangfu Shengyu, and that made him determined not to spare Chu Feng.","But he met Song Changsheng.","Song Changsheng warned him not to touch Chu Feng, or else the Huangfu Heavenly Clan would be destroyed. He crossed blows with Song Changsheng and knew that the latter was far stronger than him. Naturally, he knew that Song Changsheng’s warning was not just a threat.","For that reason, Huangfu Zhantian told Huangfu Shangwu not to reveal his conjecture that Huangfu Shengyu had been killed by Chu Feng, for Chu Feng was backed by entities they couldn’t afford to mess with.","So, Huangfu Shangwu feigned ignorance when he returned to the Huangfu Heavenly Clan. If not for that, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan would have already put a kill order on Chu Feng.","Huangfu Zhantian hadn’t expected Chu Feng to come all the way here and conquer the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. He thought of this as a misfortune not for Chu Feng but for them. From the bottom of his heart, he dared not to touch Chu Feng.","That was why he intentionally said those words to lead the crowd into thinking that Chu Feng had obtained the power with his strength instead of snatching it from them. This would justify them not going after Chu Feng.","However, the only ones in the Huangfu Heavenly Clan who dared not touch Chu Feng were Huangfu Zhantian and Huangfu Shangwu; the others harbored no such reservations. Almost all of their clansmen had made up their minds to kill Chu Feng, especially Huangfu Jiangxing.","“Chu Feng, how dare you barge into our territory?” Huangfu Jiangxing glared at Chu Feng with eyes that looked like they could breathe fire.","The Immemorial Bloodline Tower was his opportunity to leave his name in history, but Chu Feng ruined it all. He turned into a clown.","“Didn’t you activate this tower so that someone can help you awaken the power inside the tower? I helped you every step along the way, but it is a pity that you don’t have the means to conquer the power. All of us will die if we fail to conquer this power. I don’t want to die, so I can only do it on your behalf,” Chu Feng replied righteously.","“We’ll die if we can’t absorb the power?”","This sent not just the outsiders but the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen into a panic. That power was indeed terrifying; it didn’t look like Chu Feng was just fearmongering.","Even the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen thought that Chu Feng’s words were credible, let alone the outsiders. No one said it out loud, but most people were starting to think that Chu Feng didn’t come here to steal any treasure. Instead, he was here to rescue the Huangfu Heavenly Clan and the others trapped inside the tower.","“Chu Feng, is that true? Will they all die if you don’t conquer the power?” Eggy asked.","“Of course it’s a lie. I’m just leading them on. Yes, I am the only one who can absorb this power, but this power wouldn’t have killed them even if I didn’t subjugate it,” Chu Feng replied.","“You sure are good at spinning lies,” Eggy replied.","Many people believed Chu Feng’s lie, including Huangfu Jiangxing. However, the latter refused to accept this outcome.","“Stop talking nonsense. This item was born in the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, and it was refined by our Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen. It is rightfully ours! What rights do you have to claim it?” Huangfu Jiangxing questioned.","He didn’t want to let Chu Feng take all the credit.","“What rights do I have?” Chu Feng sneered. “Very well, why don’t you come here to claim the power? Go ahead and stop this power from killing everyone in the tower.”","Huangfu Jiangxing froze. Needless to say, he dared not to do that. Otherwise, he would have already made a move.","“Go ahead and do it. Why aren’t you coming over? It’s right here, waiting for you to absorb it,” Chu Feng dropped taunt after taunt, his tone becoming heavier with each passing sentence.","“Y-y-you must have used some means to prevent us from absorbing it!” Huangfu Jiangxing retorted.","Chu Feng laughed. He only had four words in response, “A useless dog barking.”","He turned away from Huangfu Jiangxing and focused his attention on absorbing the nine-colored lightning. Those words made his face turn livid.","He was indeed a useless dog barking. Reality was not going to change just because of his words. The only way for him to prove himself was to steal the power from Chu Feng. But he could not and dared not do so. He didn’t even dare to attack Chu Feng, fearing that he would face the nine-colored lightning’s backlash if he did so.","It was one thing if the lightning merely injured him like Huangfu Shangwu and the others, but what if something went wrong and the lightning killed him instead? Even the possibility of that was enough to stoke his fear of death.","The crowd was no fool. It was not just the outsiders who could see through Huangfu Jiangxing’s cowardice; even the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen felt some disdain toward their young master.","They believed Chu Feng’s words that they would die if the power was not absorbed. It was one thing for their young master to be unable to save them, but he was even getting in Chu Feng’s way of saving them.","Just then, the nine-colored lightning in the sky became blinding, only for the sky to suddenly turn quiet right away. All the nine-colored lightning surged into Chu Feng’s body.","All of a sudden, Chu Feng vanished into thin air, leaving everyone at a loss.","Huangfu Zhantian glanced toward the northwest direction of the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. He sensed Chu Feng’s aura appearing there.","“Milord, Chu Feng has escaped! Where should we chase after him?”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elders turned to Huangfu Zhantian for further instructions. They knew about Huangfu Zhantian’s incredible capabilities. Even if they had no idea how Chu Feng escaped, they wouldn’t put it beyond Huangfu Zhantian to know where Chu Feng was.","But Huangfu Zhantian glared at them with furious eyes. “Why are you asking me? How would I know?”"]},{"number":6266,"title":"Chapter 6266: Chapter 6264: Traveling Toward the Tiger Mountain","paragraphs":["Chapter 6264: Traveling Toward Danger","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen turned their eyes to Jie Shanxian. She was Chu Feng’s comrade; they could salvage their reputation if they could at least capture her.","Boom!","A powerful surge of spirit power suddenly ravaged the surroundings. The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen who had positioned themselves to encircle Jie Shanxian were swept away like tree leaves.","Jie Shanxian took this opportunity to rise into the sky and head southeast.","Chu Feng had sent her a location through voice transmission, but knowing that the Huangfu Heavenly Clan wouldn’t let her leave easily, she chose to escape in a different direction.","Much to her surprise, there was one person she couldn’t shake off—Huangfu Zhantian.","Huangfu Zhantian had unleashed his Lightning Mark to raise his cultivation level to rank two Heavenly God, but even a rank two Heavenly God level cultivator shouldn’t have been able to match Jie Shanxian’s speed.","Jie Shanxian realized that he was a tricky opponent.","“Hurry up and leave. Don’t come back. I’m begging you,” Huangfu Zhantian suddenly sent a pleading voice transmission to Jie Shanxian.","Jie Shanxian was baffled, especially when Huangfu Zhantian stopped pursuing her after sending the voice transmission.","“What is he up to?”","Jie Shanxian was perplexed. Maintaining her vigilance, she took out her compass to confirm that no one was in her vicinity before turning around to look for Chu Feng.","Wang Qiang was with Chu Feng; the latter had told him the meeting location. All three had disguised themselves, but they quickly confirmed one another’s identities.","“Chu Feng, do you know the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Huangfu Zhantian?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“Is Huangfu Zhantian the rank one Heavenly God level cultivator? I don’t know him,” Chu Feng replied.","“You don’t know him?” Jie Shanxian thought Huangfu Zhantian had stopped pursuing her because he knew Chu Feng, but if that wasn’t the case, she would have no idea what Huangfu Zhantian’s motive was.","Noticing her peculiar reaction, Chu Feng and Wang Qiang asked her what happened.","Jie Shanxian told them about the earlier situation, but neither Chu Feng nor Wang Qiang could make sense of Huangfu Zhantian’s peculiar action.","“Forget it, there’s no need to fuss over what he’s scheming. Chu Feng, I need to tell you something.” Jie Shanxian told Chu Feng about the Seven Realms Immortal Sect seeking her help.","“Elder, do you intend to go?” Chu Feng asked.","“I need you to come with me,” Jie Shanxian replied.","“You must be o-o-out of your mind! Brother Chu Feng has just r-r-revealed his identity! The Seven Realms Immortal Sect is bound to c-c-covet his Ruler’s Bloodline!” Wang Qiang stared at Jie Shanxian with widened eyes as if she was a fool.","“I would have killed you for speaking to me like that if it weren’t for Chu Feng.” Jie Shanxian glared coldly at Wang Qiang.","But Wang Qiang was undeterred. He sneered, “I would have r-r-reduced you to ashes if it weren’t for my Brother Chu Feng, old granny!”","Chu Feng hurriedly dragged Wang Qiang behind him. He had a feeling that even if Jie Shanxian could tolerate the threat, it was unlikely she would take being called an old granny well. That was a sore spot for older women.","As expected, Jie Shanxian glared at Wang Qiang with grudging eyes. She was tempted to rip his mouth apart, but she held back and instead turned to Chu Feng and said, “Chu Feng, I want you to come with me because I need your bloodline. I’ll ensure your safety.”","“Don’t go, b-b-brother! Didn’t you say she’s from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion? She’s u-u-unreliable? Who knows? She might be in c-c-cahoot with the Seven Realms Immortal Sect! Even their names sound similar!” Wang Qiang warned Chu Feng via voice transmission.","“Brother, you should return to the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion first,” Chu Feng told Wang Qiang via voice transmission.","“Brother, do you r-r-really intend to go?” Wang Qiang was taken aback.","“Rest assured, Chu Feng. I, Jie Shanxian, will guarantee your safe departure if they dare make a move against you,” Jie Shanxian told Chu Feng via voice transmission.","“Elder, I’ll go with you,” Chu Feng told Jie Shanxian.","At the same time, he secretly told Wang Qiang his reason for going.","He had come here to repay Jie Shanxian’s favor for saving him at the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, and he was aware of the risks when he accepted the request then. It wouldn’t make sense for him to back out now.","He thought that Jie Shanxian was trustworthy, and she had promised to keep him safe. Furthermore, he wanted to get on good terms with Jie Shanxian for his mother. Someone of Jie Shanxian’s stature must know about the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s secrets.","“F-f-fine! We’ll brave danger together. I-I-I’m going too!” Wang Qiang declared.","Chu Feng didn’t think he could dissuade Wang Qiang, so he turned to Jie Shanxian.","“He can go too if he wants to, but tell him to watch his mouth. I won’t hold back the next time,” Jie Shanxian snorted.","Wang Qiang shamelessly grinned. “Elder, I don’t have a g-g-good head, so I sometimes say things without thinking. Please be m-m-magnanimous and don’t hold a grudge against me.”","Jie Shanxian was rendered speechless.","She brought Chu Feng and Wang Qiang toward the Seven Realms Immortal Sect.","“Chu Feng, does the power you obtained from the Immemorial Bloodline Tower help you advance your cultivation?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“I don’t know yet. I’ll have to refine it with my bloodline power first,” Chu Feng replied.","“That’s more troublesome than I thought. Take this. It should be helpful to you.”","Jie Shanxian passed Chu Feng a pill infused with seven-colored lightning. This pill would aid Chu Feng in the recovery of his bloodline power.","“Thank you, elder. You treat me pretty well,” Chu Feng replied with a grin.","He swallowed the pill right away. Despite having exploited the Huangfu Heavenly Clan in the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, he still depleted some of his bloodline power. Refining the power he had absorbed required a fair bit of his bloodline power, so Jie Shanxian’s pill was a godsend.","“You don’t need to thank me. You have treated me pretty well too.” Jie Shanxian looked at Chu Feng with commending eyes.","To visit the Seven Realms Immortal Sect after having his identity exposed was as good as climbing a treacherous mountain despite knowing a dangerous tiger dwelled there. Not everyone dared to do something like that."]},{"number":6267,"title":"Chapter 6267: Chapter 6265: Xian Jing and Xian Shi","paragraphs":["Chapter 6265: Xian Jing and Xian Shi","The Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster and elders were waiting for Chu Feng and Jie Shanxian at the entrance. They were accompanied by a group of young world spiritists.","“Father, will Chu Feng dare come after revealing his identity?” a fair-skinned man standing next to the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster asked.","He looked beautiful despite being a man, but he had a mean-spirited face.","“I don’t know. I hope they’ll come,” the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster replied unconfidently.","Jie Shanxian had told them to head back and wait for her. The earlier situation was too complicated for them to follow Jie Shanxian, so they could only make use of the chaos to slip away.","He was regretting his decision now. He was worried that Jie Shanxian wouldn’t dare to come.","“I don’t think we should wait any longer,” the fair-skinned man said.","“Little brother, what makes you say that?” a beautiful woman with a pair of blue eyes asked the fair-skinned man.","The beautiful woman and the fair-skinned man bore a striking resemblance to each other, hinting that they were both the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster’s offspring.","“If the rumors are true, and he possesses the Genesis Bloodline and the Ruler’s Bloodline, he would surely move prudently. He knows next to nothing about us, so how can he know whether we covet his possessions or not? Anyone else in his position wouldn’t dare to come unless they know us well enough or have a powerhouse’s backing,” the fair-skinned man replied.","Many nodded in agreement.","Even the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster let out a sigh. He also understood as much, but he still hoped that Chu Feng and Jie Shanxian would come.","All of a sudden, the Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers’ faces lit up in delight. They couldn’t believe their eyes.","Chu Feng, Jie Shanxian, and Wang Qiang had appeared in their line of sight!","Chu Feng and Jie Shanxian had reverted to their original appearances, but Wang Qiang maintained his disguise.","The Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster and his sectmembers stepped forward to welcome them. It was their first time seeing Jie Shanxian’s true appearance, but they could tell right away that she was the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","“I’m grateful for your trust in our sect,” the sectmaster said.","“You need not thank me. Just don’t betray our trust,” Jie Shanxian replied.","“Of course. This way please.”","Chu Feng and the others were brought into the Seven Realms Immortal Sect.","The Seven Realms Immortal Sect lived up to its reputation as a world spiritist power. Everything within was conjured by formations, with plants and buildings emitting lights of different intensities. Colorful lights filled their eyes as if they had stepped into a wonderland.","“Do these f-f-fossils think that this is beautiful? It’s just l-l-light pollution!” Wang Qiang complained to Chu Feng via voice transmission.","“They are from the Ancient Era. It can’t be helped that our sense of aesthetics differs,” Chu Feng replied discreetly. He agreed with Wang Qiang’s evaluation.","A natural item emitting light looked divine, but having artificially constructed items emit light too felt too intentional.","Chu Feng’s group was first brought to a palace to rest.","The Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster left with some elders under the pretext that he had to make some preparations, though he left some elders and juniors behind to host them.","“Brother, these people don’t seem r-r-reliable. They are looking at you with r-r-ravenous eyes like a wolf preying on a l-l-little rabbit,” Wang Qiang said via voice transmission, though it was relayed to Jie Shanxian too this time.","He was indirectly grumbling at Jie Shanxian for bringing them here and demanding her to take responsibility for their safety.","“Don’t stray away from my line of sight. I can guarantee your safety no matter what they are up to,” Jie Shanxian replied via voice transmission.","“Young master Chu Feng, allow me to introduce ourselves. I am the clan chief’s daughter, Xian Jing, and this is my younger brother, Xian Shi,” the beautiful woman approached Chu Feng and said. [1]","“Pu...” Wang Qiang burst into laughter. “A-a-are you two natural oddities?!”","“Young master, what makes you say so?” Xian Jing was confused.","“Your names sound like cultivation resources!” Wang Qiang chortled.","Xian Jing frowned. Xian Shi even began emanating killing intent.","Jie Shanxian turned her eyes to Xian Shi, and a terrifying chill enveloped the palace, overshadowing even Xian Shi’s killing intent.","The elders tensed up upon sensing something amiss with the situation. Xian Jing patted Xian Shi’s back, and the latter retracted his killing intent.","In response, Jie Shanxian retracted her aura.","To defuse the situation, Xian Jing smiled at Wang Qiang and said, “Young master, you sure know how to pull our legs. We got our names from our father. He hopes for me to be as brilliant as crystals and my brother to be as resilient as stones.”","“I see. Those are g-g-good names,” Wang Qiang replied with a smile.","He didn’t care about the origin of their names; he was just happy that Jie Shanxian had stood up for him.","“B-b-bravo, elder,” Wang Qiang sent a voice transmission to Jie Shanxian.","Jie Shanxian didn’t reply, but Wang Qiang’s smile remained unabated. He was at fault for making fun of the other party’s name on their first meeting, but Jie Shanxian didn’t berate him and even stood up for him when the other party threatened him.","This convinced Wang Qiang that Jie Shanxian was a trustworthy person.","“Brother Chu Feng, I have long heard about you. I heard you possess the Ruler’s Bloodline and are the strongest world spiritist in the present era,” the fair-skinned Xian Shi remarked.","“Those are just rumors,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“You’re humble, but humility often stems from a lack of confidence. It looks like you don’t think that you’re worthy of your title as the strongest junior world spiritist.”","The terrifying chill enveloped the palace once again as soon as Xian Shi said those words, causing the elders to tense up.","“Has your father not taught you any manners?” Jie Shanxian coldly spat.","“Forgive me for my discourtesy, elder, but I’m just cracking a joke. I didn’t say a word either when that stutterer cracked a joke with me. Wouldn’t it be narrow-minded to crack jokes about others but not allow the other way around?” Xian Shi asked.","The displeasure in Jie Shanxian’s eyes flared.","“It’s fine, elder.” Chu Feng sent a voice transmission to Jie Shanxian, and the latter finally retracted her aura.","“Chu Feng, here’s a welcome gift,” Xian Shi said as he took out a purple stone around the size of a chicken egg.","This stone was a cultivation resource. It had many bumps and dents as if it was formed by stacking sand, and it emanated powerful spirit power.","“Brother Chu Feng, you can take it with you if you can refine it. Otherwise, I can only say that you’re unfated with it,” Xian Shi said.","“W-w-what do you mean by that? You first said that it’s a w-w-welcome gift, but now you’re imposing a c-c-criterion on it,” Wang Qiang said in displeasure.","“That’s our rule here,” Xian Shi replied before turning his attention back to Chu Feng. “Brother Chu Feng, are you interested in giving it a try?”","Without waiting for an answer, he added, “I hope you aren’t intimidated.”","1. Xian Jing is ‘Immortal Crystal’ whereas Xian Shi is ‘Immortal Stone’. ☜"]},{"number":6268,"title":"Chapter 6268: Chapter 6266: Refinement","paragraphs":["Chapter 6266: Refinement","“What a joke! Why wouldn’t my b-b-brother dare do it? Did you l-l-lace it with poison?” Wang Qiang scoffed in disdain.","Chu Feng grabbed the purple stone and examined it. “It won’t be easy to refine this purple stone. Failure is one thing, but there’s a risk of a major rebound too.”","“Not bad. I guess you aren’t just words, but world spiritists should speak with their strength. All you have is a pair of good eyes if you dare not refine it,” Xian Shi scoffed.","“I’ll give it a try.” Chu Feng clenched his fingers around the purple stone and channeled his spirit power into it.","The Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers stared at Chu Feng with nervous eyes, but they weren’t worried about Chu Feng’s safety but that he might succeed.","The purple stone emitted an explosive surge of purple aura and assaulted Chu Feng like a venomous serpent, but Chu Feng remained unfazed. Xian Shi began to fidget nervously.","“It’s not working.” Chu Feng shook his head.","Xian Shi breathed a sigh of relief as he took the purple stone back from Chu Feng. “You need not feel self-reproach. This purple stone is not easy to refine.”","His tone was mocking despite his consoling words.","Chu Feng paid no heed to his mocking tone and smiled. “It’s harder than I thought.”","Xian Shi’s smile further brightened.","Chu Feng sent a voice transmission to Jie Shanxian, “Elder, these people are scheming something. Should we find a chance to slip away, or do we wait for them to reveal their true colors?”","“The Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster promised me 30% of the Purpledream Ascension refining it into pills. I can’t leave empty-handed now that I’m here. Chu Feng, you trust me, right? There’s no way the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is weaker than them. Since I said I can guarantee your safety, you can be certain that I’ll hold my promise.”","She proceeded to ask, “That item appears to be related to the Purpledream Ascension. I don’t know how they made it, but it looks like only juniors can refine it. Are you truly unable to do so?”","“I can refine it, but I noticed that they don’t truly want me to succeed. This appears to be some kind of test, and it looks to be related to the Purpledream Ascensions. I don’t think that I should let them get their way,” Chu Feng replied.","“You’re a sly one, rascal.” Jie Shanxian chuckled.","“It’s better to be safe than sorry.”","“That’s much better than your stuttering friend.”","“Ah... My friend is usually quite sharp. He’s just acting like that because he has your backing,” Chu Feng explained.","“Is that so?” Jie Shanxian was skeptical.","“Of course it’s true!” Chu Feng nodded.","Soon, the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster rushed back with his sect elders.","“Master, we’re done with our preparations. When is convenient for you?” the sectmaster courteously asked Jie Shanxian.","“Let’s head over now,” Jie Shanxian replied as she headed out.","Chu Feng and Wang Qiang followed her.","The sectmaster hurriedly spoke up, “Master, the Purpledream Ascensions are highly poisonous. Why don’t we let these two young friends rest here?”","“It’s fine. They can handle it.”","Since Jie Shanxian had already said so, the sectmaster didn’t say anything more. He rose into the air and led Chu Feng and the others deeper into the Seven Realms Immortal Sect.","“Little brother, what are your thoughts about Chu Feng?” Xian Jing asked.","“He has some skills to withstand the Purpledream Stone’s rebound, but he lacks guts, so I doubt he poses a threat. Rather, we should be more wary about the stutterer,” Xian Shi replied.","“He lacks guts? He just caused a huge commotion at the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s side. Someone who lacks guts wouldn’t be capable of that,” Xian Jing pointed out.","“You don’t understand, big sister. Dogs fear wolves, and wolves fear tigers. There is a hierarchy in the world. Chu Feng isn’t just a cultivator but a world spiritist too. He must have witnessed our sect’s splendor and is intimidated. Such fear comes right from his bloodline, his soul!” Xian Shi said with a gleeful smile as he glanced at Chu Feng.","Chu Feng noticed his glance and smiled at him.","That made Xian Shi even more gleeful, and he secretly told his big sister, “Look at how humble he is! That’s the prowess of our Seven Realms Immortal Sect!”","“That... seems to be the case.” Xian Jing nodded.","Chu Feng and the others passed through the humongous barrier that extended from the ground into the sky and found themselves faced with a large field of purple flowers.","These were all Purpledream Ascensions! Not only were they of much higher quality than those outside the Seven Realms Immortal Sect, but they also looked far more ancient and dangerous. This was a top-quality cultivation resource!","“Do you need to refine all of these?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“Yes, we have to refine everything, but there’s no need to push it. You may refine however much you deem fit. You may also take your time if you aren’t in a rush,” the sectmaster said.","“This is more than I thought. What about the proportion we have agreed on?”","“We’ll go by our agreement. 30% of the Purpledream Ascensions refined into pills will be yours.”","“Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster, I expect you to honor your promise.”","“Rest assured, master. We, the Seven Realms Immortal Sect, pride ourselves on our credibility.”","The Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers retreated from the flower field, and the sectmaster constructed a barrier around the field. These Purpledream Ascensions’ lethality had reached a level where even they had to tread carefully.","Jie Shanxian didn’t make a move right away. Instead, she constructed a formation that enveloped herself, Chu Feng, and Wang Qiang. She spent some time on it. On the surface, the barrier was intended to protect Chu Feng and Wang Qiang, but it served another purpose.","“Let’s begin, Chu Feng.”","Jie Shanxian activated the formation, and the formation instantly enveloped a huge amount of Purpledream Ascensions. The Purpledream Ascensions, upon sensing the refinement energy, morphed into auras and surged toward her.","“Isn’t this refinement method too crude? Does she not know about the Purpledream Ascension’s lethality?” Xian Shi sighed.","The purple auras surging toward Jie Shanxian were extremely toxic, especially when there was such a massive amount of them. Not even his father would have been able to withstand it.","But soon, he found himself at a loss for words.","He noticed that Jie Shanxian, Chu Feng, and Wang Qiang were unharmed despite the onslaught of the purple auras. Instead, the purple auras manifested into three pills in front of her.","These pills were forged by refining and condensing the Purpledream Ascensions.","“That’s too fast!” The Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s elders were shocked.","Even though Jie Shanxian was only halfway done with the refinement, they were making incredibly fast progress.","“We would have been the sect’s sinners if we had missed her!” the woman and the elder who despised Jie Shanxian earlier at the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s entrance murmured their regrets.","The Purpledream Ascensions here were far harder to refine as compared to the lower-quality products outside. They thought that Jie Shanxian would require a lot of time even if she could refine these Purpledream Ascensions.","Yet, Jie Shanxian was refining these Purpledreams Ascensions faster than she did with the lower-quality products outside. This showed that she had held back earlier.","It was fortunate they didn’t miss Jie Shanxian, or else it would have been a massive loss to the Seven Realms Immortal Sect.","Just then, the sectmaster spoke up, “Her secret art is formidable, but the crux behind their fast refinement speed lies with Chu Feng.”","While the others were focused on Jie Shanxian, the sectmaster’s eyes were on Chu Feng."]},{"number":6269,"title":"Chapter 6269: Chapter 6267: An Unsurprising Fallout","paragraphs":["Chapter 6267: An Unsurprising Fallout","“Chu Feng?”","The crowd looked at the sectmaster in astonishment, especially Xian Shi.","“He is supporting that master with his bloodline power,” the sectmaster replied.","“Lord Father, why can’t I tell?” Xian Shi asked.","“It’s because of that formation. It hinders detection,” the sectmaster replied.","“Can bloodline power make such a huge difference?” Xian Shi asked.","“It makes a difference, but it usually won’t be to such an extent. I can only say that the Ruler’s Bloodline lives up to its reputation.” The sectmaster stared at Chu Feng with contemplative eyes.","Meanwhile, Jie Shanxian was busy refining the Purpledream Ascensions.","The Purpledream Ascensions here, unlike those outside, contained two surges of energy.","The first surge of energy was identical to what she had refined outside, just that it was of a higher quality. With Chu Feng’s help, she easily refined and forged three pills out of it.","The other energy was more violent and harnessed spirit power. It was the purple aura that was currently attacking them, and it would continue doing so unless they neutralized it. This energy was trickier to deal with, such that Jie Shanxian didn’t even know if it could be forged into a pill.","She succeeded in refining the energy, but it formed a purple stone instead of a pill. This purple stone was larger than the stone Xian Shi gave Chu Feng before, but it was identical otherwise.","“I see!”","Jie Shanxian realized something and sent a voice transmission to Chu Feng, “The energy contained in the purple stone can only be absorbed by juniors, so it’s less valuable than the pills, but the energy it contains is pure. I can transfer the refined energy to you without them noticing, but that only works if you can assimilate it, or you’ll suffer a terrible backlash. They must have tested you to ensure that we can’t steal this energy.”","Chu Feng sighed. “I knew their earlier test had something to do with the Purpledream Ascension. So it was regarding this.”","“Chu Feng, I’ll siphon away some of the energy for you since you’re able to assimilate it. They won’t notice a thing anyway,” Jie Shanxian replied.","Jie Shanxian continued refining the Purpledream Ascensions but while forging the purple stones, she secretly siphoned away some energy to transfer them to Chu Feng, and Chu Feng didn’t hesitate to assimilate it.","“How is the energy?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“It’s effective in growing my spirit power, but there’s too little of it. Otherwise, I should be able to make a breakthrough if I can assimilate all the refined purple stones here.” Chu Feng sighed.","“It might be possible,” Jie Shanxian replied discreetly.","“What makes you say so?” Chu Feng asked.","“I doubt they are going to honor their promise. I can see hostility in their eyes. If they turn against us, we’re going to monopolize everything here,” Jie Shanxian pointed out.","“That makes me hope that they will renege on their promise.” Chu Feng laughed.","World spiritist resources were much rarer than cultivation resources.","“Elder, while the pills are easy to assimilate, the purple stones can only be used by juniors. Given the limitations of their talent, I reckon that only a small handful of them can assimilate it, and even so, it would take a great deal of preparation. The chances are that they have a huge stockpile of it in their inventory. Should we put on a show to make them bring out their purple stones?”","Chu Feng proceeded to share his plan with Jie Shanxian.","In gist, the two of them would feign exhaustion and take a break. Jie Shanxian would take this chance to request for purple stones, saying that it would help her better refine the Purpledream Ascensions. The more purple stones there were, the better the effect.","Jie Shanxian might have a straightforward personality, but her acting was on point.","To hasten their refinement of the Purpledream Ascensions, the Seven Realms Immortal Sect took out all their stashed purple stones and handed it to her. There were more than a hundred of them in total.","Based on Chu Feng’s estimation, they could only forge dozens of purple stones at most even if they refined all the Purpledream Ascensions here.","This showed that the Seven Realms Immortal Sect was capable of refining the Purpledream Ascensions, just that they were nowhere as efficient as Jie Shanxian. This also meant that it would have taken them a long time to stockpile so many purple stones.","After duping the Seven Realms Immortal Sect of their purple stones, Chu Feng and Jie Shanxian resumed the refinement process.","In the end, it only took them two hours in total to refine the massive field of Purpledream Ascensions. All in all, they forged 180 pills and 59 purple stones. If Chu Feng hadn’t secretly assimilated some of the purple stones, they could have refined at least 61 purple stones.","Pah pah pah!","An applause could be heard. It was from the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster.","“Master, I am in awe of your means. To be frank with you, it would have taken me a hundred years at minimum to refine all these Purpledream Ascensions. This can only mean that you’re fated with our sect. I can't bear to see you leave,” the sectmaster said.","“We can continue refining if there are more Purpledream Ascensions,” Jie Shanxian replied.","“We only have this many mature Purpledream Ascensions,” the sectmaster said.","“It’s fine. I can return when more Purpledream Ascensions have matured.”","“I’m worried that you won’t return anymore. Why don’t you and young friend Chu Feng stay in our Seven Realms Immortal Sect for good?” the sectmaster said.","A golden light suddenly pulsated in the sky. This was the sealing formation constructed by the sectmaster together with his sect elders.","“Damn it. I-I-I knew they were up to something!” Wang Qiang cursed.","Chu Feng quietly glanced at Jie Shanxian. They had already predicted that this would happen, so all that was left to do was for Jie Shanxian to reveal her hand.","“Looks like you’re planning to double-cross us?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“We don’t want to renege on our words, but your secret art is too valuable for our Seven Realms Immortal Sect to miss out on. Furthermore, both the Ruler’s Bloodline and the Genesis Bloodline are legends. They are the dream of all world spiritists.","“If you want to blame anyone, blame yourselves. You should know how valuable the Purpledream Ascensions are, but you believed me when I told you I’d give you 30%. You are blinded by your greed,” the sectmaster said, showing no remorse for his betrayal.","Their brazen attitudes suggested that this was not the first time the Seven Realms Immortal Sect had done something like this.","“A mere rank two Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist thinks he can stop me?” Jie Shanxian sneered.","Spirit power gushed forth from Jie Shanxian’s body like a sharp sword, piercing through the sealing formation constructed by the sectmaster and his elders. The sectmaster and the elders’ faces warped in pain as they spurted blood.","“You possess heaven-defying battle power?” The sectmaster was taken aback.","He was certain that Jie Shanxian was only a rank one Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, but somehow she was able to easily breach his formation. She had to possess heaven-defying battle power to achieve that.","It was commonplace for cultivators to possess heaven-defying battle power, but the same couldn’t be said about world spiritists. Only the most talented world spiritist prodigies would possess heaven-defying battle power.","“You were the ones who first double-crossed me. Don’t blame me for being heartless.”","Jie Shanxian pointed her finger at the sectmaster, and countless spirit formation swords appeared out of thin air and flew forth like a torrential storm.","Yet, these swords suddenly shattered before they could reach the sectmaster.","An ancient voice echoed, “How dare you cause trouble in our Seven Realms Immortal Sect? You must think that we’re a minor sect!”","There was another brilliant flash of light in the sky, and an aura surpassing that of the sectmaster suffused the surroundings. A white-haired, wrinkled old man could be vaguely seen floating in mid-air amid the light.","He eyed Chu Feng and Jie Shanxian as if they were prey."]},{"number":6270,"title":"Chapter 6270: Chapter 6268: Rank Three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist","paragraphs":["Chapter 6268: Rank Three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist","“Father!”","“Grandfather!”","“Grand elder!”","The Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers exclaimed.","This old man was the incumbent sectmaster’s father and the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s grand elder. He was the strongest person in the sect.","Chu Feng and the others weren’t interested in who he was, but his cultivation made them frown. He was a rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, making him a threat.","Chu Feng glanced at Jie Shanxian and calmed down. She should have sensed his cultivation too, but she remained unfazed. This meant that she was confident to deal with him.","“Chu Feng, can you assimilate these? Go ahead if you can do it.” Jie Shanxian tossed the purple stones to Chu Feng.","“All right.” Chu Feng formed a hand seal, enveloping all the purple stones with his aura.","The Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers were initially horrified, knowing how valuable the purple stones were, but they thought that Chu Feng was out of his mind when they saw how he was assimilating them.","“He must be seeking death!” Xian Shi sneered.","But his face soon warped in shock.","He noticed how Chu Feng’s expression didn’t falter no matter how the purple stones’ violent energy rampaged as if he could neutralize the backlash! More importantly, Chu Feng was swiftly assimilating the purple stones’ energy.","It turned out that Chu Feng could easily assimilate the purple stones!","Boom!","The grand elder released an oppressive might to crush Chu Feng. There was no way he could let him assimilate all these purple stones under his watch.","However, Jie Shanxian released a golden surge of energy to block the oppressive might before it could reach Chu Feng.","“To think you’d have such a valuable treasure. You must be from a distinguished background.” The grand elder could tell that the golden surge of energy didn’t come from Jie Shanxian herself but from a treasure.","“I hope your Seven Realms Immortal Sect has someone above rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, Otherwise, you can only watch in futility as Chu Feng devours these cultivation resources,” Jie Shanxian sneered at the grand elder.","“All sectmembers, construct a formation with me!” the grand elder ordered.","All Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers, regardless of their age and whether they were injured or not, began forming hand seals. A formation began to form in mid-air, and the powerful force building up caused the surrounding space to shatter.","But the golden energy protecting Chu Feng and Wang Qiang didn’t falter.","Not even the grand elder could remain calm, let alone the other Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers. Chu Feng was assimilating the purple stones so fast that it wouldn’t take him long to devour all of them.","But these purple stones were important cultivation resources they had prepared for their juniors!","“How is he doing it that easily?” Xian Jing couldn’t believe her eyes.","As a world spiritist prodigy herself, she knew how terrifying those purple stones were.","“That bastard was faking it earlier!” Xian Shi’s face was livid with anger.","All this while, he thought that Chu Feng was someone he could shove around. Only now did he realize that he had been completely fooled! Chu Feng was even more sly than that stutterer!","But there was nothing he could do now. He could only watch as Chu Feng assimilated all the purple stones.","It didn’t even take Chu Feng long to assimilate all the purple stones.","“How do you feel, b-b-brother?” Wang Qiang asked with widened eyes.","As a world spiritist, he too could feel how formidable the purple stones were. He was curious how far Chu Feng had advanced after assimilating the energy inside the purple stones.","Chu Feng released his spirit power, revealing his might as a rank three True Dragon World Spiritist. He had managed to achieve two consecutive breakthroughs!","Due to his Ruler’s Bloodline, he was capable of rivaling opponents four ranks stronger than him, which meant that he could now stand toe to toe with rank seven True God level cultivators!","“You assimilated those purple stones so quickly. Are you fine?” Jie Shanxian asked with worry.","Even eating food too quickly could result in choking, let alone such violent energy that could induce a backlash in one. She was worried that Chu Feng had assimilated the energy too fast that it introduced instabilities within him.","“I’m fine. These purple stones aren’t that difficult to assimilate,” Chu Feng replied.","“A-a-are they? But t-t-those Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers unable to assimilate them, or else they wouldn’t have s-s-stockpiled that many,” Wang Qiang replied.","“They might just be incompetent,” Chu Feng replied as he glanced at Xian Shi.","“You shameless knave! You pretended to be unable to assimilate it!” Xian Shi hissed through gritted teeth.","“Yes, it was an act. I’m glad you were foolish, or else you would have made sure to stop me from coming here,” Chu Feng replied with an innocent smile.","Xian Shi was so angry that he nearly bit through his teeth.","The other Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers were infuriated too. They thought Chu Feng and Jie Shanxian were meat on their chopping board, but they turned out to be tough bones to chew instead!","“Hahahaha!” The grand elder let out a chilling laugh. He turned his eyes to Chu Feng and said, “Those Purpledream Stones are valuable, but they aren’t worth a mention compared to your Ruler’s Bloodline. Chu Feng, you might have one-upped us, but are you certain you can escape from here?”","The grand elder took out a black handkerchief that harnessed the Ancient Era’s aura. It had golden runes shimmering on its surface.","“Father!” The sectmaster was taken aback.","Knowing how valuable the treasure was, he didn’t want his father to squander it on Chu Feng.","The grand elder tossed the handkerchief into the air, and the handkerchief morphed into a massive black net that fell upon Chu Feng. When the black net touched Jie Shanxian’s golden energy, the golden runes suddenly began revolving.","Sparks flew.","The black net began to devour the golden energy that had withstood even the formation constructed with the full prowess of the Seven Realms Immortal Sect.","However, that only made the Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers’ faces even more grim.","Not only was the black net unable to breach the golden energy right away, it was also being worn thin while devouring the golden energy. Jie Shanxian’s treasure was far stronger than they had expected.","“Let’s see whose treasure is stronger. A battle of attrition? You forgot that you’re in our Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s turf! I’ll fight you to the end!” the grand elder sneered.","The grand elder wasn’t counting on the black net to breach Jie Shanxian’s golden energy. Rather, his goal was to trap Jie Shanxian and Chu Feng here with the black net.","Unfortunately, the black net contained a powerful sealing energy that even rank four Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists could do nothing about."]},{"number":6271,"title":"Chapter 6271: Chapter 6269: Conditions For a Partnership","paragraphs":["Chapter 6269: Conditions For a Partnership","Jie Shanxian calmly flicked her wrist and took out a bamboo tube. It looked ordinary and was only thirty centimeters long, but it emanated the Ancient Era’s aura.","It was a treasure!","“Chu Feng, treat it as if this has never happened. Go and do what you must.”","She pointed the bamboo tube upward, and a brilliant surge of spirit power shot out from it, piercing through the black net to form a teleportation passageway.","The Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers tensed up at the sight of the formation passageway.","Knowing that this was Jie Shanxian and Chu Feng’s escape route, they quickly constructed formations to sever the passageway, but nothing worked. They resorted to their treasures too, but not even the saber emanating the Ancient Era’s aura falling from the sky could sever the passageway.","This put them in a spot.","They had underestimated Jie Shanxian’s treasures. It frustrated them to see the prey they had caught in their net escaping just like that, and it didn’t help that this prey had just devoured the cultivation resources they had prepared for their juniors.","“Elder...” Chu Feng looked at Jie Shanxian with conflicted eyes.","He realized that a restriction was imposed on the formation passageway—only juniors could enter it.","Jie Shanxian looked at Chu Feng with a gleeful smile. “I told you that I’d guarantee your safety. How about it? I’m a person of my word, right?”","Before Chu Feng could answer, she conjured two huge spirit power hands to grab Chu Feng and Wang Qiang and toss them into the formation passageway.","“Chase them! The formation passageway has to stop somewhere!” the grand elder ordered.","The sect elders quickly followed the formation passageway to chase after Chu Feng.","However, the formation passageway disappeared shortly after Chu Feng and Wang Qiang entered it, and the passageway was not a straight path. It was impossible to find the exit just by heading straight.","Thus, the sect elders had no choice but to return.","“You useless things!” the grand elder berated the elders, though he didn’t punish them.","Such escape treasures were meticulously designed to stop pursuers. The outcome would likely be the same even if he was the one who gave chase. He was merely berating the elders to vent his frustration.","In the end, he turned his gaze back onto Jie Shanxian, the cause of his anger. “It looks like you have depleted your means. Let me see how long you can hide in there!”","Jie Shanxian scoffed. She sat down and took out all the pills she had refined from the Purpledream Ascensions to assimilate them.","...","The teleportation passageway was merely concealed; it didn’t truly vanish. The fact that Chu Feng and Wang Qiang appeared somewhere else in this realm was the biggest proof of that.","“B-b-brother, what do we do next?” Wang Qiang asked grimly.","Their best course of action was to leave this place as soon as possible.","However, they knew that Jie Shanxian had sent the two of them out, likely because she had no way of escaping from that situation. In other words, she was in danger.","Despite Wang Qiang’s foul mouth, he was a loyal friend. He couldn’t have become Chu Feng’s close friend if not for that. He, too, was worried about Jie Shanxian.","“Brother, you wouldn’t leave even if I advised you so, right?” Chu Feng asked.","“I’ll f-f-follow you. If you go, we’ll go t-t-together.” Wang Qiang grabbed Chu Feng’s sleeves as if afraid that the latter would shake him off with his means.","“I’ll be frank. Elder Jie has saved us; I can’t leave her to the lurch. Our strength is nowhere enough to deal with the Seven Realms Immortal Sect, so I’m thinking of seeking reinforcement,” Chu Feng said.","“S-s-seeking reinforcement? Are we heading to the T-T-Totem Galaxy?” Wang Qiang asked.","They had chatted quite a bit since their reunion.","From Chu Feng, he learned that the Immortal Sea Fish Clan was also currently in the Totem Galaxy. The Totem Dragon Clan might not be a match for the Seven Realms Immortal Sect, but the Immortal Sea Fish Clan could still put up a fight.","“It’s too far. We won’t make it in time,” Chu Feng replied.","“But w-w-who else can we ask?” Wang Qiang was confused.","“The Huangfu Heavenly Clan.”","“The hell!” Wang Qiang widened his eyes in shock. “Brother, are you o-o-out of your mind?!”","That was Wang Qiang’s first thought, but he knew that Chu Feng was not the type to make ridiculous suggestions. He thought about it before asking, “Are you intending to negotiate with them using the energy you obtained from the Immemorial Bloodline Tower?”","“That’s right,” Chu Feng replied.","“What if that doesn’t work?”","“It will work.” Chu Feng was confident in the attractiveness of his bait.","“All right, l-l-let’s go,” Wang Qiang said.","The two of them got into action.","The Immemorial Bloodline Tower had collapsed, so the Huangfu Heavenly Clan returned to their headquarters.","Chu Feng approached the Huangfu Heavenly Clan without disguising his appearance. Their guards could hardly believe their eyes when they saw him. They couldn’t understand where he had found the guts to march up into their base.","Regardless of Chu Feng’s intention, the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen rushed out and encircled him. Soon, the encirclement opened up, and Huangfu Zhantian walked up to Chu Feng.","“What are you doing here?” Huangfu Zhantian asked.","Chu Feng and Wang Qiang were dumbstruck.","To their disbelief, Huangfu Zhantian sounded unhappy even though they had practically offered themselves up to the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","“Elder, can you call the shots in the Huangfu Heavenly Clan?” Chu Feng asked politely.","He had no idea what was going on with Huangfu Zhantian, but it was a good thing that the latter wasn’t hostile toward them.","“What do you want?” Huangfu Zhantian asked.","“I’ll tell you if you can call the shots. Otherwise, please call someone else who can make decisions in the Huangfu Heavenly Clan. I have a request to make,” Chu Feng said.","A deep, resonant voice echoed from afar. “I can call the shots. Speak your mind.”","The encirclement opened up once more. A large group of Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen reminiscent of celestial troops descended from the sky toward them. The group included not just Huangfu Jiangxing and Huangfu Jiangyue, but Huangfu Shangwu as well.","Chu Feng could tell at a glance that this group was extraordinary. He turned his eyes to the person standing at the forefront of the group.","It was a gray-haired, middle-aged man.","“Father, that’s the brazen scoundrel who stole our treasure in the Immemorial Bloodline Tower! He must be responsible for Shengyu’s disappearance! Hand him to me! I’ll make him confess to everything!” Huangfu Jiangxing exclaimed.","The gray-haired, middle-aged man was the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief.","The clan chief paid no heed to Huangfu Jiangxing; his eyes remained focused on Chu Feng.","“Why have you come?” the clan chief asked.","“I came to request a partnership,” Chu Feng replied.","“A partnership?”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen couldn’t believe their ears. They wondered if Chu Feng was off his rockers. Who, in their right mind, would request a partnership with someone whom they had stolen from and utterly humiliated?","However, the clan chief asked, “What kind of partnership are you looking for?”","“I want you to rescue someone from the Seven Realms Immortal Sect,” Chu Feng replied.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were flabbergasted.","“You are on bad terms with the Seven Realms Immortal Sect?” the clan chief asked.","“You can say so,” Chu Feng replied.","“Who are we rescuing? The Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist who accompanied you here?”","“That’s right.”","Chu Feng proceeded to share his conflict with the Seven Realms Immortal Sect.","“Hahaha...” Huangfu Jiangxing burst into laughter. “So that’s how you slipped away! The Seven Realms Immortal Sect helped you! You must have thought that they are your backing, but they are after your life! Chu Feng, fear must have made you dumb. Have you forgotten about your conflict with our Huangfu Heavenly Clan? What makes you think that we’ll help you?”","The other Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen also burst into laughter. They didn’t think that anyone sane could have done this.","The clan chief suddenly glanced at his clansmen, and the mocking laughter vanished.","“I understand your agenda here. Give me a reason to help you,” the clan chief said.","“I have no reason,” Chu Feng replied.","The clan chief was taken aback.","Huangfu Jiangxing took this chance to interject, “Father, that fellow is here to make a fool out of us. Let’s not waste our time with words and capture him! I’ll teach him a lesson!”","Chu Feng added, “But I have a hostage.”","He opened his palm and released a surge of spirit power. A figure appeared out of thin air.","All the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen, as well as Wang Qiang, froze in place.","“T-t-t-t-the heck! Huangfu Shengyu?!”"]},{"number":6272,"title":"Chapter 6272: Chapter 6270: I Agree","paragraphs":["Chapter 6270: I Agree","All eyes were locked on the person whom Chu Feng conjured out of thin air. The crowd couldn’t believe what they were seeing, for the other party was indeed Huangfu Shengyu!","“B-b-brother, what’s going on? You didn’t kill him?” Wang Qiang asked via voice transmission.","Back in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith, Chu Feng fought with Huangfu Shengyu, but only Chu Feng was left standing in the end. This led everyone to think that he had killed Huangfu Shengyu.","“I didn’t know how powerful the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was, so I kept a hand and merely stowed Huangfu Shengyu away in a spatial formation. I thought that I could use him as leverage against the Huangfu Heavenly Clan. I didn’t expect him to come in handy now,” Chu Feng replied via voice transmission.","“The hell! No wonder you were s-s-so fearless!” Wang Qiang widened his eyes in realization.","He finally understood why Chu Feng had remained calm despite having made a fool of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan in the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. By then, Chu Feng had already realized how important Huangfu Shengyu was to the Huangfu Heavenly Clan, and that he could use the latter as a hostage against them.","All Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen turned to their clan chief.","“Lord Clan Chief, is that truly young master Shengyu?” a clansman asked.","They couldn’t tell if Chu Feng had conjured a fake Huangfu Shengyu to fool them. They reckoned that the clan chief should know better, given that Huangfu Shengyu was his son.","“Yes, it’s Shengyu,” the clan chief replied hoarsely.","Huangfu Shengyu’s life token had shattered, but his corpse was nowhere to be found. So, the clan chief harbored a sliver of hope that Huangfu Shengyu was alive, though he also mentally prepared himself for the latter’s death.","Despite his best attempt to remain calm, the clan chief couldn’t conceal his relief and delight when Huangfu Shengyu appeared alive in front of him.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were overjoyed to hear that.","Huangfu Shengyu possessed the Saint-tier Heavenly Lightning Bloodline. Many viewed him to be their clan’s hope, and they lamented his death. His return was, needless to say, good news.","However, two people had awkward looks on their faces—Huangfu Jiangxing and Huangfu Jiangyue. They had thought Huangfu Jiangxing would become the next clan chief after Huangfu Shengyu’s demise, but their plans were dashed now that Huangfu Shengyu had returned alive.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan was going to be Huangfu Shengyu’s.","This made Huangfu Jiangxing look at Chu Feng with further hatred. It was one thing for the latter to steal his energy in the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, but him bringing Huangfu Shengyu back to the clan had truly put him in a dire position.","“So you were the one who hurt Shengyu! Men, capture him!” Huangfu Jiangxing roared.","But much to his astonishment, not a single person heeded his command. The clan chief’s contemptuous gaze made his face turn even paler—the clan chief was telling him that he had no place to be issuing commands here.","Intense killing intent enveloped Chu Feng, causing both Chu Feng and Wang Qiang’s robes to flutter wildly.","“I advise you to stay calm, Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief. My life is bound to your son’s.”","He opened up his finger and showed that each of his fingers was tied to an almost indiscernible formation thread. These formation threads were linked to Huangfu Shengyu’s dantian.","“Father, he’s telling the truth.” Huangfu Shengyu raised his head to look at his father.","“Shengyu, what happened?” the clan chief asked Huangfu Shengyu. He was more inclined to believe his son than Chu Feng.","“I was useless. I brought shame to the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.”","Huangfu Shengyu’s face was filled with shame, but he still told the clan chief about everything that had happened in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith.","“Chu Feng, even if you have spared my son, Shengyu, you have still taken the lives of our other clansmen. Do you expect us to turn a blind eye to that?” the clan chief questioned.","“Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, you are a cultivator too, so I shan’t waste my breath preaching the law of the jungle. Your son is here; why don’t you ask him who started it? Your son should be glad he has your backing. I only spared his life because I don’t want things to reach an irreconcilable stage, or else he deserves death for what he has done,” Chu Feng sneered.","“Audacious! You hurt our young master and killed our clan’s prodigies! Such a crime is enough for us to sentence your clan to death! How dare you continue uttering nonsense here?”","Thunderous voices echoed from the surroundings. The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s domineering attitudes could be fully felt.","Wang Qiang tried to speak up for Chu Feng, but his words drowned in the sea of voices around them. No one could hear his words. All that could be heard was the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s criticisms of Chu Feng.","Chu Feng didn’t say a word. He merely did an action, and everything fell silent.","He whipped out a dagger.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen thought that Chu Feng was going to harm Huangfu Shengyu, so they quickly shut their mouths out of fear. But what Chu Feng did next shocked them.","Chu Feng plunged the dagger into his own chest.","AH!","A wail of agony ensued, but it was not from Chu Feng but Huangfu Shengyu.","Huangfu Shengyu clutched his chest. To the crowd’s shock, a wound identical to Chu Feng’s had appeared on his chest and was bleeding profusely.","It dawned on the crowd that Chu Feng had linked his life to Huangfu Shengyu. Any injury sustained by Chu Feng would be inflicted on Huangfu Shengyu too.","Chu Feng was threatening them now with his action. If the Huangfu Heavenly Clan dared to lay their hands on him, Huangfu Shengyu would go down with him.","Pu!","Fresh blood spurted as Chu Feng pulled out his dagger. He looked as if he was going to stab himself once more.","“Stop! Stop right now!” the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen exclaimed, frightened that Chu Feng would continue to self-harm.","They couldn’t care less about Chu Feng, but their young master was already in poor condition. He couldn’t take such torture!","Chu Feng held his dagger up as he looked at the clan chief. “I’m not here to debate right and wrong with you. I’m here to negotiate with you. There are only two options. You can either work with me to take down the Seven Realms Immortal Sect, and I’ll fuse the energy I obtained from the Immemorial Bloodline Tower into Huangfu Shengyu and return him safely to you. Or else...”","Chu Feng was about to reveal the second option when the clan chief interjected, “I’ll accept your partnership.”"]},{"number":6273,"title":"Chapter 6273: Chapter 6271: Leaving Goodwill","paragraphs":["Chapter 6271: Leaving Goodwill","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief knew that Chu Feng’s other option couldn’t be anything good. Chu Feng was going to blackmail him using Huangfu Shengyu’s life, and that was not a risk he was willing to take.","That was also why he did not attempt to suppress Chu Feng or save Huangfu Shengyu despite his overwhelming strength as a Heavenly God level cultivator.","Huangfu Shengyu was too important to them.","Besides, Chu Feng’s offer was highly tempting.","If Huangfu Shengyu could obtain the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s energy, he could lead the Huangfu Heavenly Clan to greater heights than it did in the Ancient Era. The possibilities were unimaginable!","“Brother, t-t-this isn’t worth it, no?” Wang Qiang asked.","That energy was of great use to Chu Feng too. How could he give it to someone else so easily?","“Brother, I’ve examined the energy and noticed that my bloodline is averse to it. It might instead weaken my bloodline power if I forcefully fuse it with my bloodline. Since I can’t use it, I might as well sell the Huangfu Heavenly Clan a favor,” Chu Feng said.","“Ah!” Wang Qiang widened his eyes. “That sounds fine.”","Meanwhile, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan looked overjoyed. The deaths of their prodigies at the Nine Heavens’ Zenith was a massive grudge, but supposing what Chu Feng said was true, they would be at fault too. If they put aside everything, they didn’t have the moral high ground.","Besides, Chu Feng’s offer opened new horizons for them. No matter how big the grudge between them was, it could be overlooked given that. This was a profitable deal for them.","Only one person didn’t share those thoughts—Huangfu Jiangxing.","His world had collapsed when he heard Chu Feng’s words. He turned to the clan chief and exclaimed, “Lord Father, we mustn’t! This scoundrel has not only killed our clansmen but captured Shengyu too. He wouldn’t have let Shengyu out if he didn’t need our help. His words can’t be trusted! Lord Father, you...”","Pah!","Huangfu Jiangxing saw stars. There was a burning sensation on his cheek.","The clan chief had slapped him.","“When have you started calling the shots in the Huangfu Heavenly Clan? I’m still not dead yet! Even if I’m dead, this position will never be yours!” the clan chief sneered.","Huangfu Jiangxing was stunned. Those words effectively spelled the end of his future.","Huangfu Jiangyue quickly kneeled before the clan chief and said, “Lord Father, Jiangxing has only said those words because he’s concerned about little brother Shengyu! He bears no other intention!”","But the clan chief paid her no heed. He turned to the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s elders and said, “Relay my orders. Gather our elites to attack the Seven Realms Immortal Sect.”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan began gathering its army.","Meanwhile, Huangfu Shengyu looked at Chu Feng with fearful eyes.","He had been trapped in Chu Feng’s spatial formation all this while. Terrifying energies would occasionally seep into the spatial formation and shake him up. There were at least two times when the energy nearly claimed his life.","He thought that Chu Feng was torturing him and begged for mercy, but the latter replied that he was undergoing a trial and was enduring the energy too, and that he didn’t mean to torture him.","Huangfu Shengyu didn’t know if those words were true.","If Chu Feng was lying, it would mean that he was able to control those terrifying energies, suggesting that he had someone incredible backing him.","If Chu Feng was telling the truth, it would mean that Chu Feng was an incredible prodigy capable of overcoming those terrifying energies.","When Chu Feng released him, he received many voice transmissions from the Huangfu Heavenly Clan, and from that, he learned that Chu Feng had awakened the Immemorial Bloodline Tower. That further reinforced his impression of Chu Feng.","He had been arrogant from a young age due to his supreme bloodline, but now, he had no choice but to concede defeat. His opponent was simply too powerful. He no longer wanted to become Chu Feng’s enemy anymore.","“Chu Feng, do you mean it when you say that you’ll give me the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s energy?” Huangfu Shengyu asked.","“I have always kept my promises,” Chu Feng replied.","“Then I’ll guarantee your safe departure,” Huangfu Shengyu said.","“I trust that you can do so.” Chu Feng smiled.","Huangfu Shengyu didn’t respond to Chu Feng’s smile. His pride didn’t allow him to express goodwill to Chu Feng, but the stone weighing on his heart had finally shattered. He was also wishing to resolve his conflict with Chu Feng.","Soon, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was done gathering its army. They boarded a floating warship and began making their way toward the Seven Realms Immortal Sect.","Chu Feng, Wang Qiang, Huangfu Shengyu, the clan chief, and the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s top echelons boarded the same warship. As for Huangfu Jiangxing and Huangfu Jiangyue, they were told to stay behind at the clan.","Huangfu Jiangxing’s face had paled in despair.","“You should keep a low profile in the future. No one can protect you anymore,” Huangfu Jiangyue said before taking her leave.","She was worried about her little brother too, but she needed to self-preserve too.","The power balance in the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was going to shift with Huangfu Shengyu’s return. The two of them were going to suffer when Huangfu Shengyu heard about what they did during his absence.","On the warship, the clan chief secretly conversed with Huangfu Shengyu to check if Chu Feng had tortured him. His son’s complexion didn’t look too good, after all.","Huangfu Shengyu’s answer convinced him that Chu Feng was no ordinary person. He also recalled what Huangfu Zhantian had previously reported to him, and that made him let go of all ideas of turning Chu Feng into an enemy.","The clan chief turned to Chu Feng and said, “Chu Feng, our Huangfu Heavenly Clan can let bygones be bygones, not just because of the conditions you have raised but because we want to express goodwill to a prodigy like you too. However, you shouldn’t dream of blackmailing our Huangfu Heavenly Clan just because you have Shengyu in your hands.","“I hope that you’ll fulfill your promise and let Shengyu go once this matter is over. If you break your promise, I’ll claim your life even if it means sacrificing Shengyu. Your friends will not get off scot-free either.”","“Rest assured, Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief. Since you know about my friends, I’m sure you have heard about my reputation too. I think I have proven myself to be trustworthy, or else I wouldn’t have so many loyal friends, right? As long as you help me rescue my elder, I guarantee that Huangfu Shengyu’s bloodline will be strengthened,” Chu Feng said.","Huangfu Zhantian also added with a smile, “Clan chief, young friend Chu Feng does have a good reputation.”","“Know a person but not his heart. I don’t trust rumors, but if you can hold your end of the bargain, our Huangfu Heavenly Clan would be willing to have you as a friend,” the clan chief said.","“Clan chief, should we first attempt diplomacy or should we make a move straight away?” an elder asked.","“We should be thorough since we have already decided to make a move. Relay my orders! The goal of our operation is not just to rescue the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist but also to thoroughly destroy the Seven Realms Immortal Sect so that they can never pose a threat to us in the future,” the clan chief declared.","Chu Feng and Wang Qiang exchanged looks.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief was a vicious man."]},{"number":6274,"title":"Chapter 6274: Chapter 6272: The Heavenly Clan Invades; Cultivators vs. World Spiritists","paragraphs":["Chapter 6272: The Heavenly Clan Invades; Cultivators vs. World Spiritists","Meanwhile, Jie Shanxian was still meditating on the spot in the Seven Realms Immortal Sect, assimilating those pills. She looked unfazed, but her mind was so shaken that her speed of assimilation became exceedingly slow.","She was bothered by the ten ten-thousand-meter-tall golden bells floating in the vicinity of the energy protecting her. The bells were linked by a red thread where many smaller bells hung.","This was a formation, and it was channeled by the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s sectmaster and grand elder.","The giant bells and smaller bells were swaying simultaneously, but the Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers couldn’t hear a thing because the sound was completely concentrated toward Jie Shanxian’s ears.","“Why does it feel like she’s not affected? Is our grand elder’s treasure unable to interrupt her too?”","The Seven Realm Immortal Sect’s elders were distressed. The bells were their Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s treasures, and channeling them greatly depleted their energy.","“She’s just feigning composure. There’s no way she’s unfazed. She’s bound to go berserk if she continues to cultivate forcefully. Trying to assimilate our cultivation resources under our eyelids? Dream on!” the sectmaster sneered.","The other elders breathed a sigh of relief, but they felt bitter too.","If not for the elaborate preparations required to set up this treasure, they wouldn’t have had to watch helplessly as Chu Feng assimilated those Purpledream Stones and escaped. But again, the issue was that Chu Feng assimilated those Purpledream Stones so quickly that they didn’t have time to take any countermeasures.","“Grand elder!”","“Sectmaster!”","Several other sect elders flew over with horrified faces.","“What’s wrong?” The sectmaster could tell from their complexion that something troublesome had just happened.","“The Huangfu Heavenly Clan insists that we rescued Chu Feng, and their clan chief has led his army here to demand him. They say that they will attack our Seven Realms Immortal Sect if we don’t have Chu Feng over to them.”","The Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers’ faces darkened.","They had a grasp of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s strength. This was going to be tricky.","The only thing that confused them was why the Huangfu Heavenly Clan would insist that they were the ones who saved Chu Feng. Even though Chu Feng and Jie Shanxian did come here, they had escaped and traveled here without their help.","The world began to tremor, and the source of the tremor appeared to be the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s entrance.","The sectmaster took out a compass, which should have contained a complete protective formation, but there was now a crack on it at where their entrance was. The culprit behind that could only be the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","“The Huangfu Heavenly Clan truly dares to attack our Seven Realms Immortal Sect?”","The others also noticed the compass, and they felt a mix of fear and anger.","The Seven Realms Immortal Sect had always been on good terms with the Huangfu Heavenly Clan, yet the latter was attacking them on mere suspicion. Clearly, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was looking down on their Seven Realms Immortal Sect.","“Relay my orders! All sectmembers, except for the juniors, are to follow me to confront the Huangfu Heavenly Clan!” the sectmaster ordered in a fit of rage.","Just as he was about to make a move, an old palm grabbed his shoulder, and the grand elder said, “Stay here and continue channeling the formation. Don’t let her escape amid the chaos.”","With the formations in place, he didn’t think that Jie Shanxian could turn the tables on them anymore; all they had to do was continue guarding her. The bigger threat was the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","The sectmaster couldn’t deal with the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief.","Knowing the severity of this issue, the sectmaster said, “Father, you must be careful.”","The grand elder laughed. “The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief is a rank three Heavenly God level cultivator, and Huangfu Zhantian is a force to be reckoned with too. I wouldn’t have the confidence to attack the Huangfu Heavenly Clan. But since they dared to attack our Seven Realms Immortal Sect, we shall be the ones to call the shots in this realm from this day forth!”","The grand elder led the sectmembers to confront the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","When he arrived at their entrance, he was met with powerful lightning bolts that relentlessly zapped their gates. It was the doing of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","It was a lightning formation centered around the warship helmed by the clan chief and Huangfu Heavenly Clan and supported by the rest of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s army. Its attacks were so powerful that the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s gates were on the verge of collapsing.","“Hold it right there!” the grand elder’s voice boomed across the thunderous lightning.","At the same time, the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s gates turned transparent, allowing the Huangfu Heavenly Clan to see the grand elder and the others inside.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief had met the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s grand elder before, and he knew that this old man was the true decision-maker in the Seven Realms Immortal Sect.","He raised his hand, and the nine-colored lightning halted its bombardment.","This allowed the Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers to get a better glimpse of the situation outside.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen stood in a formation reminiscent of a towering wall of humans, and each was holding a lightning compass. The earlier lightning bombardment was unleashed through those compasses.","At the center of the army was the clan chief’s warship.","“Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, are you waging war on our Seven Realms Immortal Sect now?” the grand elder asked with a face quivering with anger.","“Chu Feng humiliated our Huangfu Heavenly Clan, yet you secretly rescued him. Aren’t you the ones who waged war on us first?” the clan chief questioned wrathfully.","“Nonsense! How can you assert something without evidence? You’re maligning us!” the grand elder roared.","“Who else in this realm, other than your Seven Realms Immortal Sect, has the means to rescue Chu Feng? There are no Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists in this realm outside your sect!” the clan chief questioned.","The Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers frowned, for the clan chief’s words made sense. However, they knew better than anyone that they didn’t rescue Chu Feng.","“I stand by my words. You need to show us the evidence. If all you have is your speculation, I can only say that you’re too naive as a clan chief,” the grand elder sneered.","“I’m not going to waste my breath arguing. Hand Chu Feng over, or our Huangfu Heavenly Clan is going to decimate your Seven Realms Immortal Sect,” the clan chief ordered","“Obstinate! I told you Chu Feng isn’t here. What do I have to do to make you believe me? Do you want to search our sect?” the grand elder huffed.","“That will do too,” the clan chief replied.","“Very well. We shall prove our innocence. Open the gates!” the grand elder declared.","The other Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s elders were horrified.","“Grand elder, we mustn’t!”","But the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s grand elder had already made up his mind. He opened the gates with a wave of his sleeves.","“That’s more like it,” the clan chief replied with a smile before marching in with his army.","The Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers slowly retreated with wary gazes.","The clan chief cast a glance backward, and all the Huangfy Heavenly Clansmen suddenly raised the compass in their hands, and bolts of lightning hurtled toward the Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers.","A charred smell suffused the surroundings.","Despite not having let their guard down, many Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers were blasted into bits due to their lacking strength. Those who survived were enveloped in a purple barrier channeled through a purple token they held in their hands.","They quickly formed hand seals that caused the surrounding energy to flow into the token, making it glow even more brilliantly than before.","Weng!","The purple tokens emanated purple lights that connected all the purple token holders. From the purple lights, a formation enveloped in runes manifested, forming a massive net that covered the sky, trapping the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen within.","“This isn’t good.” The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were appalled.","The Seven Realms Immortal Sect had intentionally let them in. This was their home turf, which meant that they could tap into the formations here to deal with invaders. This was evident from the sealing formation they had used to trap them here.","The Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s grand elder and elders smirked in glee.","“Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, do you think I’m a fool who would let you in just so you can go on a massacre? You fell for my trap!”","The grand elder raised his arm and roared, “Spare no one!”","Purple lights rained down torrentially upon the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen fought back too. They channeled their lightning formation to fight back, but it didn’t take long for some to reach their limits and be skewered by the raining purple lights.","Even though the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was still holding its ground for the time being, it was apparent that the lightning formation was no match for the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s purple light formation.","“What a joke! A bunch of cultivators competing with us world spiritists in formations?”","The grand elder was channeling the purple light formation too, and he couldn’t help but smirk when he saw the strained look on the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief’s face. He knew that victory was in his grasp.","Chu Feng’s escape was lamentable, but there was much to gain if they could decimate the Huangfu Heavenly Clan and loot their treasures. This was a blessing in disguise.","“I don’t think so!” a voice suddenly boomed.","The grand elder was stunned by the voice. Why does it sound so familiar?","He looked over, only to freeze in bewilderment. He saw Chu Feng emerging from the clan chief's warship with two nine-colored compasses in his hands. He placed the compasses together and channeled his lightning power into the formation core.","That greatly strengthened the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s lightning formation.","“Chu Feng, w-why are you there?” the grand elder blurted out.","He was too shocked to pay any heed to the changes in the lightning formation.","Before Chu Feng could answer, Wang Qiang said, “F-f-fool! My brother was the one who m-m-mobilized the Huangfu Heavenly Clan against you!”","The grand elder was initially confused, but when he noticed the clan chief’s triumphant smirk, his face turned so livid that it looked like he could gobble someone whole. He turned to the clan chief and screamed, “I’ll bloody rip you a new one, Huangfu Heavenly Clan!”"]},{"number":6275,"title":"Chapter 6275: Chapter 6273: The Immortal Sect’s Final Formation","paragraphs":["Chapter 6273: The Immortal Sect’s Final Formation","Along with the furious roar, the purple light pillars grew even brighter.","From Chu Feng’s angle, the purple light pillars looked like an inescapable net, and they looked stronger than before, harnessing enough power to crush the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","Those from the Seven Realms Immortal Sect had no idea why the Huangfu Heavenly Clan had chosen to side with Chu Feng, but there was no way they could tolerate their deed. Their anger allowed them to draw forth far greater power than usual, causing their formation to be stronger.","Yet, they were still unable to reclaim their previous advantage. On the contrary, their situation only worsened.","And this was all because of one person—Chu Feng!","Not only was his compass different, but the lightning he released was also different from the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen. The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were releasing lightning of different colors, but most were only releasing a single colored lightning.","Even the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief and Huangfu Zhantian, the two strongest individuals of the Huangfu Heavenly Clan, were only releasing six-colored lightning.","But Chu Feng was unleashing the complete nine-colored lightning.","He might only be a junior, but with so many experts channeling the formation, the key determining factor to its strength was no longer about one’s cultivation but one’s bloodline power. Chu Feng’s bloodline was clearly stronger than the others.","“What’s wrong? Isn’t the Seven Realms Immortal Sect a world spiritist sect? Why are your formations weaker than that of a cultivator clan?” Chu Feng scoffed. His voice echoed through the crackling lightning and the buzzing purple light formation, allowing everyone to hear him loud and clear.","“You cultivators aren’t the only ones who can construct formations with your bloodlines!” the grand elder sneered. “Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers, with your bloodline as the foundation and your blood as fuel, we shall borrow our ancestors’ strength to vanquish the invading ants!”","Determination seeped into the eyes of the Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers. They changed their hand seal, and their bodies began emanating blood-red auras that gave off a terrible stench. These auras were manifested from their blood.","They had ignited their bloodlines.","Under the desperate channeling of the Seven Realms Immortal Sectmembers, the purple formation howled like a vengeful ghost. The runes wiggling in their formation transformed into savage blood skeletons, causing their formation to be greatly strengthened.","“What a vile formation, the Seven Realms Immortal Sect. How can they be worthy of the word ‘immortal’? They are obviously a demonic cult!” Chu Feng sneered.","Any rational person could tell that the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s formation was built upon the blood and flesh of countless victims. Each of those runes represented a life.","“Nonsense. Only a brat like you can utter such words. This world is not divided by good and evil; it’s only divided by the strong and the weak. I shall defeat you today and turn you into our sect’s skeleton spirit. Our Seven Realms Immortal Sect will remain as ever, respected by the masses,” the grand elder sneered.","“Hmph! Even if it’s just for today, I won’t allow evil to triumph over good!” Chu Feng spat.","Nine roars echoed from Chu Feng’s body, causing the surrounding space, which had been reinforced by formations, to crack. The nine-colored lightning Chu Feng emanated morphed into nine lightning beasts.","The nine lightning beasts suffused the formation core, causing the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s lightning formation to transform as well. The lightning emanating from all the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen’s compasses turned into nine-colored lightning, greatly boosting the formation.","The purple light pillars shattered like fragile glass.","“Activate our protective formation!”","The grand elder quickly changed his hand seal, and the formation changed. The remaining purple light quickly congregated to form a purple barrier to block the onslaught of lightning.","However, the lightning formation was so powerful that it didn’t take long for the purple barrier to begin cracking. It was evident that the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s formation wouldn’t last for long.","“Incredible!”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, Huangfu Zhantian, Huangfu Shengyu, and the others looked at Chu Feng. This was not their first time employing this lightning formation, so they had a grasp of how powerful it was.","It was Chu Feng who made their lightning formation much stronger than before. In particular, sectmembers beneath Heavenly God level could sense the drastic difference in the lightning formation from the compasses in their hands. They had never felt so indomitable before.","“Chu Feng!!!” the grand elder roared in frenzy.","His eyes were bloodshot, and veins were popping from his face. He glared at Chu Feng with terrifying eyes reminiscent of a demon. The blood aura he emanated was much stronger than before.","The ground began to crack, and lava churned beneath his feet. A furious heatwave rushed into the sky.","“This isn’t good!”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen sensed that something was amiss.","The heat wave didn’t pose a threat to them, but they could sense tremendous spirit power rising from the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s ground, and it enveloped the vast entirety of their sect. The Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s ancestors must have left behind an even stronger formation for their descendants in times of crisis!","“Chu Feng!!! Our Seven Realms Immortal Sect will return the favor to you a thousand times over!!! Everyone related to you will die because of you!” the grand elder roared as his flesh began to disintegrate.","The spirit power enveloping the Seven Realms Immortal Sect suddenly materialized, only to disappear in the next second. Everyone from the Seven Realms Immortal Sect also vanished into thin air.","“What happened?” The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were bewildered.","“It’s a teleportation formation. The formation left by their ancestors is a teleportation formation. They escaped,” Chu Feng said.","There was a brief silence as the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen struggled to come to terms with the situation. They turned to look at their clan chief.","“Yes, they have escaped,” the clan chief confirmed the matter with a smile.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen burst into laughter. They didn’t expect the Seven Realms Immortal Sect to use such a powerful formation just to escape, though it made perfect sense on second thought.","They wouldn’t have been so angry if they had such a powerful hand.","Chu Feng made his way into the Seven Realms Immortal Sect.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen quickly followed him, for Chu Feng brought with him not only Wang Qiang but Huangfu Shengyu as well."]},{"number":6276,"title":"Chapter 6276: Chapter 6274: Look of Respect","paragraphs":["Chapter 6274: Look of Respect","Chu Feng and the others rushed to where Jie Shanxian was trapped. There was not a single Seven Realms Immortal Sectmember to be seen en route, and the previously glowing buildings also lost their luster.","The Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s formation must have transported all their sectmembers and treasures away.","Fortunately, they found Jie Shanxian where she was previously trapped.","Upon sensing Chu Feng’s arrival, Jie Shanxian stowed away the pills she had yet to assimilate and the golden energy she had used to fend against the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s attacks earlier.","“Elder, are you fine?”","Chu Feng, Wang Qiang, and Huangfu Shengyu descended before Jie Shanxian. Wang Qiang was following Chu Feng out of his own volition, whereas Huangfu Shengyu had no choice but to remain within a certain radius of Chu Feng.","“Do I look like I’m not fine? I’m merely annoyed by their damned bells,” Jie Shanxian replied with a smile.","“Bells?”","“Those are treasures they used to disturb me. The earlier teleportation formation transported their sectmaster away with those treasures,” Jie Shanxian explained as she eyed the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s army. “How did you get them here? Is it because of him?”","Jie Shanxian eyed Huangfu Shengyu.","She was keen enough to guess what was going on from circumstantial evidence, especially given the life binding formation between Chu Feng and Huangfu Shengyu.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen scattered to scour the grounds for treasures, leaving just the clan chief and their elites behind. They had planned to destroy the Seven Realms Immortal Sect in a single sweep as they weren’t a force to be underestimated.","For instance, their lightning formation wouldn’t have been able to best the Seven Realms Immortal Sect’s purple formation if not for Chu Feng’s powerful bloodline. But Chu Feng wouldn’t stay in the Huangfu Heavenly Clan forever, and it was only a matter of time before the Seven Realms Immortal Sect returned to exact vengeance.","It would be best if they could find some treasures to make up for it, or else they would have been making a huge loss.","“Chu Feng, our Huangfu Heavenly Clan has accomplished your request. Now that you have rescued the person you want to, it’s time for you to hold the end of your bargain,” the clan chief declared loudly.","Jie Shanxian was taken aback. She turned to Chu Feng and asked, “You got them here to save me?”","“You saved us, elder. It’s only natural for us to find a way to save you too,” Chu Feng replied.","Wang Qiang added, “D-d-don’t be too surprised, elder. My brother is just t-t-that loyal. To be honest, I wouldn’t have the c-c-courage to seek the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s help if I were him. Just the killing intent they emanated when they encircled us nearly made me p-p-pee my pants. They only accepted my b-b-brother’s request because he promised to give away the energy he obtained from the Immemorial Bloodline Tower.”","With just a few short words, Wang Qiang revealed the sheer danger of what they had just done and the price Chu Feng had to pay for this exchange.","Jie Shanxian’s face turned increasingly livid, and she glared at Chu Feng with angry eyes. “What’s wrong with you? I went through so much to rescue you, yet you ran back here and even gave away the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s energy. Isn’t that a waste?”","She felt sorry for Chu Feng.","“You saved me, elder. How can I leave you in the lurch? I’m not that kind of person,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“It’s not about being loyal. I sent you out and stayed behind because I have the power to protect myself. Have you handed that energy over yet?” Jie Shanxian asked.","Wang Qiang quickly replied on Chu Feng’s behalf, “N-n-not yet.”","“Then we shan’t give it to them,” Jie Shanxian said.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen’s eyes turned cold. The compasses they had just stowed away reappeared in their hands.","“Elder, we can’t lose our integrity. I will not shirk off the promises I have made. Give me a moment, elder.”","Chu Feng rose into the air with Huangfu Shengyu and returned to the clan chief’s warship.","“I trust the Huangfu Heavenly Clan will hold its promise too, right?” Chu Feng asked.","“Of course,” the clan chief replied.","“Very well.”","Chu Feng first formed a hand seal that caused light to emanate from his palm. Without any hesitation, he brought it down on the threads between him and Huangfu Shengyu.","Spirit power receded from the two of them. The life binding formation had been dispelled.","Next, Chu Feng placed his palm on Huangfu Shengyu’s dantian.","This made many Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen nervous, but the clan chief and Huangfu Zhantian remained calm. In their eyes, Chu Feng’s movements were extremely slow. Now that Huangfu Shengyu had been freed from the life binding formation, they were no longer worried about Chu Feng attempting anything.","“You... Are you truly giving it to me?” Huangfu Shengyu stared at Chu Feng.","He could feel a formidable energy flowing from Chu Feng’s palm into his dantian. The energy was wild and domineering like a beast, but its sheer power excited him.","The rumors about this energy were true. He could feel it qualitatively enhancing his bloodline power.","“You should try assimilating it by yourself first, but tell me if you reach your limit. I’ll help you,” Chu Feng said.","“Heh...” Huangfu Shengyu chuckled. “I can easily assimilate the energy by myself, so you don’t have to be worried about that. All you have to do is to pump all that energy into my dantian.”","Huangfu Shengyu formed a hand seal and projected his consciousness into his dantian.","Chu Feng pumped all the energy he had received from the Immemorial Bloodline Tower into Huangfu Shengyu’s body in a single breath.","Huangfu Shengyu’s eyes shot open, and he exclaimed through gritted teeth, “Save me, Chu Feng!”","That shocked the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen. Cracks appeared on Huangfu Shengyu’s skin, and nine-colored lightning leaked out. It looked like he was on the verge of exploding.","Worst of all, the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s nine-colored lightning was opposing Huangfu Shengyu’s nine-colored lightning. Eighteen lightning beasts were brawling with one another, threatening to destroy the realm inside his dantian.","“Relax, you won’t die,” Chu Feng calmly replied.","He placed his palm firmly on Huangfu Shengyu’s dantian, and the latter felt an aura that caused his bloodline to turn cold. The aura swiftly flowed from Chu Feng’s palm into his dantian realm.","In an instant, it calmed not only his bloodline but the rampaging energy as well. The two forces began to fuse as if having received someone’s order.","Whose order could it be?","Huangfu Shengyu looked at Chu Feng with unprecedented respect."]},{"number":6277,"title":"Chapter 6277: Chapter 6275: Immemorial Lightning Pillar","paragraphs":["Chapter 6275: Immemorial Lightning Pillar","Huangfu Shengyu suddenly felt something. He quickly sat down and closed his eyes.","Boom!","A rumbling could be heard in the sky. Dark clouds covered the sky, and nine-colored lightning lit up the world. It was a phenomenon!","“Shengyu is going to make a breakthrough!” The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were overjoyed.","Huangfu Shengyu successfully made consecutive breakthroughs, and his cultivation eventually stabilized at rank two True God level. This delighted the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen.","Huangfu Shengyu’s cultivation was already lagging behind his peers, and the Huangfu Heavenly Clan was planning to help him catch up with them. It was great that he advanced to rank two True God level just like that.","If the Huangfu Heavenly Clan devoted all their resources to him, he might just be able to reach rank three True God level very soon.","Wang Qiang, however, was a little displeased.","“The hell! T-t-that energy is so strong! We shouldn’t h-h-have given it to him!” Wang Qiang said with a sigh via voice transmission.","“He only advanced his cultivation by so much because that energy is useful to him. If I had assimilated it instead, not only would I be unable to make a breakthrough, but it might even hinder my cultivation in the future,” Chu Feng replied.","“There are o-o-other people in your Chu Clan. You can g-g-give it to them,” Wang Qiang said.","“I doubt I have any peers in the Chu Clan who can withstand that energy, not to mention that I don’t know where they are. It’d be more worthwhile to sell the Huangfu Heavenly Clan a favor. With the world of cultivation in chaos, having more friends is better than having more enemies,” Chu Feng replied.","“T-t-then I can only say that it’s good we gave the energy to them,” Wang Qiang replied with a smile.","Huangfu Shengyu walked up to Chu Feng and clasped his fist. “Thank you, Chu Feng.”","“You need not thank me. It’s a partnership. It’s only right for me to help you when you have helped me,” Chu Feng replied.","He then turned to the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, knowing that the latter was the one who called the shots here.","“It was a pleasure working with you,” the clan chief replied with a smile.","That indicated that he wouldn’t make things difficult for Chu Feng anymore.","“It was a pleasure working with you as well,” Chu Feng replied.","“Chu Feng, have you tested your Heavenly Bloodline?” the clan chief asked.","“Not yet.” Chu Feng shook his head.","“Our Huangfu Heavenly Clan has a treasure from the Immemorial Era to test a person’s Heavenly Bloodline. Why don’t you give it a try if you’re interested? Of course, it’s all up to you,” the clan chief said.","“I’d like to test my bloodline if it’s not too much trouble,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","He had already revealed the prowess of his Heavenly Lightning Bloodline through the Immemorial Bloodline Tower, the earlier lightning formation, and at the Nine Heavens’ Zenith. There was no question that his bloodline was superior to Huangfu Shengyu’s Saint-tier.","But Chu Feng didn’t know exactly how strong his bloodline was. It would be great if he could know what tier it was at.","Shoosh!","The clan chief whipped out a metal rod with a flick of his sleeves. The rod was completely black and had a black sphere sitting on its tip. Other than that, it looked completely ordinary.","Nevertheless, Chu Feng could sense that the rod was anything but simple. It emanated an ancient aura that hinted that it was from the Immemorial Era.","The clan chief waved his arm, and the black rod grew to tens of thousands of meters long before landing heavily on the ground. It was now a massive pillar that surged into the sky.","The black pillar comprised five sections, demarcated by ancient characters. The ancient characters, from the lowest section to the highest, wrote ‘Lower’, ‘Middle’, ‘Upper’, ‘Heaven’, and ‘Saint’.","“Father, is this the item to test bloodline?” Huangfu Shengyu asked the clan chief.","Even the elders present were intrigued. This was their first time seeing this item.","“Clan chief, you’re going all out to test Chu Feng’s bloodline. To think you’d bring out the Immemorial Lightning Pillar.” Huangfu Zhantian’s interest was piqued.","He proceeded to explain the history of the item.","There was a formidable person in the Ancient Era whose bloodline suppressed all Heavenly Bloodlines and other bloodlines too. His bloodline was so powerful that it shook everyone in the Ancient Era.","There were rumors that he didn’t possess the Heavenly Bloodline but something else altogether.","No treasure could accurately test his bloodline power as there were no means capable of grasping his true potential.","However, someone still managed to test his true bloodline through an Immemorial Era’s treasure. It turned out that the person possessed the Heavenly Bloodline too, just that his bloodline tier surpassed all else—Saint King-tier!","He became renowned throughout the world and eventually became one of the strongest powerhouses of the Ancient Era.","The item that tested his bloodline was a humongous tower. That tower was a treasure from the Sacred Heavenly Temple, and it was known to be capable of testing all bloodlines.","However, there was also another item capable of testing one’s bloodline up to Saint King-tier. That item was prepared specifically for those who possessed the Heavenly Lightning Bloodline. Due to its shape, it became known as the Immemorial Lightning Pillar.","And that was the item that the clan chief had brought out.","While the pillar could test for Saint King-tier bloodlines, it had a fatal flaw. Once the treasure was activated, it would swiftly deplete itself and collapse. In other words, it could only be used once.","That was also why Huangfu Zhantian said that the clan chief was going all out."]},{"number":6278,"title":"Chapter 6278: Chapter 6276: Chu Feng’s Bloodline Tier?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6276: Chu Feng’s Bloodline Tier?","“Shengyu, I didn’t tell you the truth because I wanted to build up your confidence. Heavenly Bloodlines aren’t just divided into Lower-tier, Middle-tier, Upper-tier, General-tier, and Saint-tier. Those who have Lower-tier, Middle-tier, and Upper-tier bloodlines aren’t true prodigies, so I shan’t touch too much on them. The minimum level required to be a prodigy is Heaven-tier.","“Heaven-tier is divided into Heaven Lower-tier, Heaven Middle-tier, Heaven Upper-tier, and Heaven General-tier. Huangfu Fanni is at Heaven Middle-tier. Despite his name carrying the character ‘Fan (Middle)’, his bloodline is only slightly weaker than yours. In truth, he’s also considered a true prodigy,” the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief said.","Huangfu Shengyu interjected, “So, Huangfu Shangwu, Huangfu Shangyang, and the others are actually at Heaven Upper-tier.”","“Indeed.” The clan chief nodded.","Huangfu Shengyu widened his eyes in horror as he realized what his father was getting at. His breathing hastened, his complexion turned awful, and his hands began trembling.","He was panicking!","The clan chief had expected such a response when he chose to reveal the information, so he didn’t bother consoling Huangfu Shengyu.","Since it was already established that Chu Feng’s bloodline was stronger than Huangfu Shengyu’s, it was about time to let the latter know that his bloodline was not the strongest of all.","“You’re saying that the Heavenly Lightning Bloodline Saint-tier can be further divided into different tiers?” Huangfu Shengyu sought clarification from his father.","That was the conclusion he had come to. He realized that even though his bloodline was indeed at Saint-tier, unlike what he had believed thus far, it was not at the strongest tier.","“Yes, the Heavenly Lightning Bloodline’s Saint-tier can be further divided into Saint Lower-tier, Saint Middle-tier, Saint Upper-tier, and Saint King-tier. Saint King-tier is the highest tier for the Heavenly Lightning Bloodline,” the clan chief replied.","“What’s my tier?” Huangfu Shengyu asked.","“The Immemorial Lightning Pillar is here. Why don’t you give it a try?” the clan chief said.","Huangfu Shengyu made his way toward the Immemorial Lightning Pillar. He had been through many talent evaluations from a young age, and the evaluation methods didn’t differ vastly from one another. It was his first time seeing the Immemorial Lightning Pillar, but he could guess how it was meant to be used.","He walked up to the Immemorial Lightning Pillar, placed his palm on it, and fused his bloodline into it.","Tzzzzzz!","Nine-colored lightning flowed from his palm to coil around the Immemorial Lightning Pillar and began swiftly ascending.","Wherever the lightning passed, the pillar’s black exterior would be replaced by a nine-colored light. This sight piqued the interest of not just the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen but Jie Shanxian too.","Huangfu Shengyu’s bloodline was formidable. It gushed right through the Lower-tier, Middle-tier, and Upper-tier section, not slowing the least even as it ascended through the Heaven-tier. It was racing straight toward the Saint-tier section!","But upon reaching Saint-tier, the ascension rapidly slowed down. A character appeared on the sphere located at the tip of the Immemorial Lightning Pillar—’Lower’!","Huangfu Shengyu frowned. Does this mean that I’m only at Saint Lower-tier?","To his relief, the nine-colored lightning was still ascending, albeit at a slower pace.","Some time later, the ‘Lower’ character disappeared and was replaced with ‘Ordinary’, but it was also then that Huangfu Shengyu’s nine-colored lightning stopped moving.","“So I’m only at Saint Middle-tier!” Huangfu Shengyu felt conflicted.","He was not satisfied with this outcome, but it was still acceptable to him.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, however, smiled in delight. He knew that Huangfu Shengyu’s bloodline was previously at Saint Lower-tier, which meant that the energy from the Immemorial Bloodline Tower must have raised his bloodline to a greater height.","This was wonderful news for the Huangfu Heavenly Clan! Their partnership with Chu Feng had been worthwhile!","“Chu Feng, this Immemorial Lightning Pillar will not remain activated for long. Why don’t you give it a try while it’s still functioning?” the clan chief said.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen turned to Chu Feng. They were curious to know how strong his bloodline was. Would he be stronger than Huangfu Shengyu but remain at the same Saint Middle-tier, or would he be a step closer to the legendary level, Saint Upper-tier?","“Father, the only bloodlines above me are Saint Upper-tier and the legendary Saint King-tier, right?” Huangfu Shengyu asked.","“That’s right,” the clan chief replied.","Huangfu Shengyu looked at Chu Feng with encouraging eyes. “Don’t feel burdened, Chu Feng. Your bloodline is stronger than mine. There’s a good chance you’re at Saint Upper-tier. The worst-case scenario is that you’re at Saint Middle-tier, just like me.”","“Burdened?” Chu Feng chuckled. “I don’t feel that at all.”","He walked up to the Immemorial Lightning Pillar and placed his palm on it.","Gwar!","The earth tremored. Nine massive lightning beasts gushed out from Chu Feng’s palm and swiftly ascended the black pillar.","Huangfu Shengyu’s nine-colored lightning ascended fast, but Chu Feng’s nine lightning beasts were at least fifty times faster! Had those present been any weaker, they wouldn’t even be able to follow their movements.","But it was also for that very reason that they quickly realized something was amiss.","Cracks appeared on the Immemorial Lightning Pillar where the nine lightning beasts passed. The pillar looked to be approaching its limit.","But the crowd was more curious about Chu Feng’s bloodline tier to pay much heed to that.","The nine lightning beasts reached the Saint region in less than the blink of an eye, but their movement speed didn’t slow. On the contrary, they moved even faster. In the end, they gushed out of the Immemorial Lightning Pillar and ascended into the sky.","Half of their bodies remained coiled around the Immemorial Lightning Pillar, while the other half covered the sky. They turned around and gazed down on the pillar with disdain in their eyes.","Grar!","The nine lightning beasts howled simultaneously, causing the black pillar to shatter and disintegrate with the lightning.","“What’s going on? Did we run out of time on the Immemorial Lightning Pillar?” the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen asked.","“Perhaps so,” the clan chief replied.","Despite his response, the clan chief was so shaken up that he could hardly maintain his composure. He knew that the Immemorial Lightning Pillar hadn’t run out of time; it was simply unable to withstand Chu Feng’s bloodline.","But according to the records, the Immemorial Lightning Pillar was capable of testing Saint King-tier! So how could it be unable to withstand Chu Feng’s bloodline?","It was one thing if the records were wrong, but if the records were on point, the implications were terrifying. It would mean that Chu Feng’s bloodline surpassed what was believed to be the peak of the Heavenly Lightning Bloodline, above Saint King-tier!"]},{"number":6279,"title":"Chapter 6279: Chapter 6277: The Silent Clan Chief Planning to Clear the Hurdles?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6277: The Silent Clan Chief Planning to Clear the Hurdles?","Most Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen claimed that the Immemorial Lightning Pillar shattered because its time was up, but it was to preserve their dignity. Be it the ones saying those words or the ones listening to them, they were feeling stifled inside.","“W-w-what do you mean run out of time? The pillar reached its limit! Looks like Saint King-tier isn’t the s-s-strongest tier since my brother surpasses that.” Wang Qiang’s words eroded the pride of the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen.","Since Chu Feng had accepted the test to flaunt his bloodline, he didn’t mind driving in just how ridiculously strong Chu Feng’s bloodline was.","The Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen were put in an awkward position.","Wang Qiang’s words made sense. Chu Feng’s bloodline power had surged out of the pillar before it shattered into pieces. This was an irrefutable fact, but it was much too shocking.","Even someone who possessed the Saint King-tier bloodline could dominate in the Ancient Era. They couldn’t imagine the heights that someone who surpassed Saint King-tier could reach.","“We ran out of time, though we can’t eliminate other possibilities. Either way, Chu Feng’s bloodline has surpassed Saint Middle-tier, reaching Saint Upper-tier or perhaps the legendary Saint King-tier.”","The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief looked at Chu Feng with approving eyes.","“Can’t eliminate other possibilities? My brother i-i-is at Saint King-tier at the minimum!” Wang Qiang exclaimed.","The clan chief didn’t bother replying. Wang Qiang’s lack of tact was grinding on his nerves. If Wang Qiang hadn’t been Chu Feng’s friend, he would have long killed Wang Qiang with a single palm strike.","“Elder, is Saint King-tier the strongest bloodline recorded in the Ancient Era?” Chu Feng asked.","He also wanted to understand just how powerful his bloodline was.","“That’s right,” the clan chief replied.","“Chu Feng, the Ancient Era’s records are not necessarily accurate. Before you, the strongest bloodline in the Nine Provinces Continent was Emperor-tier bloodline. They have never heard about the Heavenly Bloodline. In my opinion, your bloodline is definitely above Saint King-tier,” Eggy said.","She sat inside Chu Feng’s World Spirit Space with her hands on her snowy-white thighs. She had seen everything that had just happened, and she was more excited than anyone else. Her excitement was palpable from her face.","“My thoughts exactly, but what could be above Saint King-tier? Elder, do you know?”","Chu Feng was directing the latter question to not just the Divine Deer but the red lightning beast as well. He thought that they might know more than the Huangfu Heavenly Clan.","The red lightning beast kept his silence, but the Divine Deer answered, “He’s right. The strongest recorded Heavenly Bloodline in the Ancient Era’s record is Saint King-tier, but that doesn’t mean that it is the ceiling for Heavenly Bloodlines. There could have been stronger ones in the Immemorial Era.”","The Divine Deer’s answer coincided with Eggy’s conjecture.","Chu Feng exchanged pleasantries with the Huangfu Heavenly Clan before he took out a high-quality God Armament and passed it to Huangfu Shengyu.","“What’s this?” Huangfu Shengyu was confused.","“I lost your previous God Armament, so I’m compensating you with this one. Accept it, and we’ll let bygones be bygones,” Chu Feng said.","Huangfu Shengyu understood what Chu Feng was getting at, so he replied, “I’ve already let it go. You don’t have to compensate me anything. Don’t worry, I mean what I say. I won’t go after your friends in the Nine Heavens’ Zenith either. However, Chu Feng, you should remember that I’m only doing this on your account.”","“I understand.” Chu Feng smiled.","No man was infallible. Huangfu Shengyu had been revered as the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s most talented prodigy for the longest time, so it was unsurprising that he grew up arrogant.","What was more important was his sincerity about turning over a new leaf and not seeking vengeance over what happened then. If he was not sincere about his words, Chu Feng would not spare him the next time.","Meanwhile, the Huangfu Heavenly Clansmen thoroughly combed the Seven Realms Immortal Sect, but there was not a single person to be found.","“The Seven Realms Immortal Sect is a cunning one. Not only did they escape, but they also took all their treasures with them. This means that their foundation is still intact. We will have to be wary of them in the future. Still, it’s worth it given what Shengyu received, and our Huangfu Heavenly Clan doesn’t fear them either.","“Rather, Chu Feng, you will have to tread carefully. The Seven Realms Immortal Sect is extremely vindictive. They might go after you like mad dogs. I wouldn’t exclude the possibility of them striking an alliance with the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to deal with you,” the clan chief said.","“I’ll be careful. Thank you for your help.”","Chu Feng clasped his fist at the Huangfu Heavenly Clan, focusing on Huangfu Shengyu, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief, and Huangfu Zhantian. He didn’t talk much with Huangfu Zhantian, but he had a peculiar feeling that the latter was on his side even though he didn’t know why.","Regardless, he had a better impression of Huangfu Zhantian compared to the others.","With that, they parted ways.","The only ones left on the warship were the clan chief, Huangfu Shengyu, and Huangfu Zhantian.","The clan chief took the center seat, whereas Huangfu Shengyu and Huangfu Zhantian settled down beside him. The latter two kept sneaking glances at the clan chief, who looked livid. After Chu Feng had taken his leave, the clan chief dismissed everyone except for Huangfu Zhantian and Huangfu Shengyu. Since then, he had been silent.","His reaction was normal.","Huangfu Shengyu’s bloodline advancing to Saint Middle-tier should have been news worth celebrating, but Chu Feng’s trial result was like a fish bone stuck in their throats, leaving them uncomfortable.","They had thought that Huangfu Shengyu, with his bloodline power, had a chance to become the strongest person in the world. The Huangfu Heavenly Clan had high hopes for him.","Yet, someone stronger than him suddenly appeared out of nowhere, dashing their hopes for good. They were aiming to be number one, only to realize that the best they could do was to be number two. Anyone in their position was bound to feel uncomfortable.","Huangfu Zhantian felt uneasy.","The natural thing to do when faced with a hurdle was to remove it, especially if this hurdle stood in the way of their clan’s glory and future.","He was worried that the clan chief harbored such thoughts about Chu Feng."]},{"number":6280,"title":"Chapter 6280: Chapter 6278: Shocking News","paragraphs":["Chapter 6278: Shocking News","“Clan chief, that stutterer is right. Chu Feng’s talent is unfathomable. His bloodline is at least at Saint King-tier, and there’s a good chance it might have surpassed that. No wonder he has such a powerful person backing him!” Huangfu Zhantian intentionally mentioned Chu Feng’s backing.","When Chu Feng stole the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s energy, Huangfu Zhantian informed the clan chief about his encounter with Song Changsheng to discourage the clan chief from messing with Chu Feng.","That was why the clan chief remained calm when Chu Feng went to the Huangfu Heavenly Clan to negotiate. The clan chief had his reservations.","Even so, Huangfu Zhantian was still worried that the clan chief would change his mind, especially given the history between Chu Feng and Huangfu Shengyu.","The clan chief had doted on Huangfu Shengyu from a young age, which gave rise to the latter’s arrogant personality. Huangfu Shengyu had suffered a huge setback to Chu Feng back then. Would the clan chief let things slip when Huangfu Shengyu had suffered a huge setback to Chu Feng?","If Huangfu Shengyu harbored a grudge against Chu Feng, the odds were that the clan chief would get even with Chu Feng on his behalf.","Huangfu Zhantian was worried that they would renege on their promise.","“Father!”","Right after Huangfu Zhantian said those words, Huangfu Shengyu shot to his feet and exclaimed, “I was the one at fault at the Nine Heavens’ Zenith. Even for the Immemorial Bloodline Tower’s energy, I wouldn’t have been able to assimilate it without Chu Feng’s help, let alone awaken it. I am in awe of Chu Feng’s talent.”","Huangfu Zhantian was stunned.","Huh? Did this lad get possessed? Why is he so different from usual? Not only is he not complaining to his father, but he’s even advising his father not to get back at Chu Feng?","“You two. Look at my face.” The clan chief pointed at his face.","Those two stared at the clan chief’s face, but they didn’t see anything.","“Do I look like a fool to you?” the clan chief asked.","“Huh?” Those two were stunned.","“Do you think I need your convincing?” The Huangfu Heavenly Clan’s Clan Chief stood up, rolled his eyes at those two, before continuing, “Putting aside Chu Feng’s backing, I’d be a fool to turn someone of his capability and potential into an enemy. If not for him, Shengyu wouldn’t have been able to assimilate that energy, raise his bloodline, and advance his cultivation. Who knows? He might be able to help Shengyu even more in the future.","“And as you have mentioned, Chu Feng has formidable backing. The man you have encountered that day is one thing, but there’s something amiss about the Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist we rescued as well. She... doesn’t seem afraid at all, as if everything was still under control. There’s no reason for us, the Huangfu Heavenly Clan, not to befriend Chu Feng!”","Confused, Huangfu Zhantian asked, “Then why were you brooding just now?”","“I was lamenting! I shouldn’t have let Chu Feng leave like that. I should have given him some benefits as a gesture of goodwill on our part. We have been the rulers in this isolated world for so long that we have become too awkward and prideful. This might just become the biggest obstacle in our path. Haa!” the clan chief said as he slapped his own thigh.","The other two could tell that their clan chief was regretting not taking a more proactive stance.","...","Meanwhile, Chu Feng’s group had departed from the formation realm and returned to the real world.","Jie Shanxian, Chu Feng, and Wang Qiang exchanged looks.","“In the end, I still owe you a favor,” Jie Shanxian remarked with a smile.","“You’re being too polite, elder. You don’t owe me anything. Truth be told, you would have been safe even if I didn’t bring the Huangfu Heavenly Clan over, right?” Chu Feng asked.","“That’s hard to say.” It was hard to decipher Jie Shanxian’s smile. Her expression suddenly became serious as she said, “I’ll investigate the matter concerning your mother. If Jie Tianran truly exploited his authority, I’ll seek justice on your behalf. Till then.”","Jie Tianran suddenly vanished after saying her piece.","“She’s leaving j-j-just like that?” Wang Qiang looked around as if searching for Jie Shanxian.","Chu Feng was not surprised by her abrupt departure.","After confirming Jie Shanxian was gone, Wang Qiang turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Brother, where are y-y-you going next?”","“I’ll visit Zi Ling before making a trip to the Totem Galaxy. What about you?”","“I have already left the Divine Body Heavenly Mansion in name. I’ll go with you.”","“Sure,” Chu Feng accepted his offer with a smile. It would be less lonely to have Wang Qiang as a companion.","The two of them quickly made their way to the Martial Cultivator Commerce Guild’s guild leader’s hidden base.","Unfortunately, Zi Ling was still in her closed-door cultivation. Chu Feng could sense that she was in good condition, so he knew there was nothing to be worried about.","In the first place, closed-door cultivation could easily take years, decades, or even centuries. Chu Feng and Wang Qiang were the weird ones for thinking that Zi Ling was taking a long time in her closed-door cultivation.","Knowing that he couldn’t help Zi Ling here, Chu Feng decided to greet the guild leader before making his way to the Totem Galaxy with Wang Qiang.","“Chu Feng!”","Just as Chu Feng was about to make his way to the guild leader, the guild leader suddenly appeared before him. She was holding onto a stone—it was a Skygazing Divine Stone, which allowed one to peer into the distant galaxy.","“God’s Era,” the guild leader said as she handed the Skygazing Divine Stone to Chu Feng.","Chu Feng took the stone to look at God’s Era. The humongous incense stick there had burned out, and the massive mirror face had vanished. A new gate appeared in the heart of God’s Era’s avatar.","The gate was so massive that it encompassed several realms. It was tightly shut.","Wang Qiang also used the Skygazing Divine Stone to observe the changes in God’s Era.","“I-i-is it over? But it doesn’t look l-l-like anyone has obtained God’s Era’s power yet. Otherwise, God’s Era s-s-should have disappeared instead of conjuring a new gate. What do you t-t-think, brother?” Wang Qiang asked.","“I don’t think anyone has obtained God’s Era’s true power yet, but they must have received some benefits, perhaps an advantage in subsequent God’s Era’s opening. Otherwise, there wouldn’t have been such a huge commotion,” Chu Feng said.","“It’s good a-a-as long as its true power is still there. Otherwise, your foolish g-g-grandfather will stir unrest in the world of cultivation,” Wang Qiang said.","“It’s not like things are calm in his absence. It’s not necessarily a bad thing for us if he joins the war between the present-era cultivators and the Ancient Era’s powers,” Chu Feng said.","“That’s t-t-true. Let them fight it out. It’ll be best if they destroy each other,” Wang Qiang smiled.","Chu Feng and Wang Qiang bade farewell to the guild leader before making their way to the Totem Galaxy to meet Little Fishy and the others.","At the Totem Dragon Clan, Chu Feng met the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief, the Immortal Sea Fish Clan’s Clan Chief, Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, Long Chengyu, and the others. However, he also learned a shocking piece of news on top of that."]},{"number":6281,"title":"Chapter 6281: Chapter 6279: Something Happened to the Ancestral Dragon’s Remnant?","paragraphs":["Chapter 6279: Something Happened to the Ancestral Dragon’s Remnant?","Chu Feng and Wang Qiang reached the Totem Dragon Clan’s main camp.","Most of Chu Feng’s comrades were around, though the Dragon Breath Clan was away dealing with matters.","However, Long Chengyu and Long Muxi weren’t doing well. They suddenly felt unwell at the same time last night, and their bodies began burning up. It eventually reached a point where the two of them fell unconscious.","Even Daoist First Dragon and Daoist Second Dragon were unable to diagnose their conditions. The more they examined them, the more they felt like Long Chengyu and Long Muxi were being possessed by some kind of power.","Chu Feng looked at Long Muxi and Long Chengyu, who were resting on a cold stone, but was unable to discern anything with his eyes. So, he decided to step forward to inspect their bodies.","Much to his astonishment, their body temperatures were so high that Chu Feng, despite his cultivation, couldn’t touch them.","Something was wrong!","Even if Chu Feng couldn’t touch them, Long Muxi and Long Chengyu should have been reduced to ashes by now! Perplexed, he decided to still reach out to grab Long Chengyu’s wrist to see just how he was.","Daoist First Dragon hurriedly grabbed Chu Feng’s wrist to stop him. “Young friend Chu Feng, even I was scalded.”","He flipped over his other palm—there were burn marks on it, and it was showing no signs of healing even though medicine had been applied.","“Big brother, there’s something amiss about the heat they are emanating. We should observe from afar for the time being,” Little Fishy said concernedly.","Chu Feng retracted his hand. If even someone as powerful as Daoist First Dragon was burned, it would indeed be inadvisable for him to touch Long Chengyu and Long Muxi. The only problem was that he couldn’t see through that bizarre fever even with his Heaven’s Eyes.","“Young friend Chu Feng, are you unable to diagnose their condition too?” the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief asked nervously.","Daoist First Dragon and Daoist Second Dragon had already given up.","Chu Feng’s arrival brought the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief a ray of hope, but he was unsure whether Chu Feng was able to resolve this issue or not, especially after seeing the latter’s expression.","Chu Feng shook his head. The clan chief’s heart skipped a beat.","“Elder Clan Chief, you don’t have to be too worried. Their vitals are stable despite the bizarre fever. I’d like to ask if they have been to anywhere or came into contact with anything in recent days?” Chu Feng asked in hopes of getting some clues.","“They have been cultivating in their respective chambers, and they haven’t come into contact with anything filthy,” the clan chief replied.","“Lord Clan Chief!” a Totem Dragon Clan’s elder exclaimed from afar as he rushed over.","Knowing something huge must have happened, the clan chief and the others rushed out.","It turned out that a huge fire had broken out in the Totem Dragon Clan’s ancestral dragon forbidden land.","The clan chief anxiously led his men to the ancestral dragon’s remnant. The remnant was extremely important to their clan. If not for it, the Totem Dragon Clan would have never enjoyed its current level of glory and honor.","Many Totem Dragon Clansmen viewed the ancestral dragon’s remnant as their ancestor, and they were willing to sacrifice their lives to protect the ancestral dragon.","“We’ll go too.” Chu Feng constructed a formation realm with a wave of his sleeves and stowed into it Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, and the cold stone they were resting on.","Then, he turned to Daoist First Dragon and Daoist Second Dragon.","“Young friend Chu Feng, do you think that young friends Long Chengyu and Long Muxi’s conditions are related to the situation in the ancestral dragon’s forbidden land?”","Daoist First Dragon saw through Chu Feng’s thoughts.","“Their fevers are coming from within. I suspect it stems from their bloodlines. It’s too much of a coincidence for fire to break out at the ancestral dragon’s remnant at a time like this,” Chu Feng replied.","“Indeed.”","The crowd nodded in agreement, thinking that Chu Feng’s words made sense.","“Big brother, I’ll go too.”","“I-I-I’m coming along as well!”","Little Fishy, Xianhai Shaoyu, Wang Qiang, and the others expressed their desire to tag along. Chu Feng had no reason to stop them.","Thus, they quickly caught up with the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief and accompanied them to the realm where the ancestral dragon’s remnant was located.","“Young friend Chu Feng, do you mean that this matter might have something to do with Lord Ancestral Dragon? If so, it might not necessarily be a bad thing.” The Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief breathed a sigh of relief.","He treasured the ancestral dragon’s remnant so much that he felt immense worry the moment he heard that something had happened to it, prompting him to toss everything to the back of his mind, including his children’s safety.","But Chu Feng’s words suggested that this matter could be a fortuitous encounter for Long Chengyu and Long Muxi.","“It’s only a conjecture on my part. We’ll only know for sure once we see the ancestral dragon’s remnant,” Chu Feng replied.","“Your words sound plausible. I’d be relieved if that’s the case,” the clan chief replied with a sigh.","The Totem Totem Dragon Clan’s experts also no longer looked as worried as before. They would have been skeptical had it been anyone else raising that suggestion, but they had great trust in Chu Feng.","This trust was built up from the astute judgment Chu Feng had displayed time and time again.","With the Totem Dragon Clan’s special means, it didn’t take them long to arrive at the realm where the ancestral dragon’s remnant was located. Immense heat could be felt as soon as they stepped into the ancestral dragon’s forbidden land.","Infernos raged where the ancestral dragon lay, forming a wall of flames that extended from the earth to the sky. The immense heat was coming from none other than the flames.","Shockingly, the heat level was similar to what Long Chengyu and Long Muxi were emanating.","“Could this be truly related to Lord Ancestral Dragon?”","This further lent credence to Chu Feng’s conjecture.","Unfortunately, the raging flames obstructed the crowd’s vision, preventing them from gathering more information about the situation. On top of that, the flames encircled the ancestral dragon’s remnant. This made the Totem Dragon Clansmen worry once more.","“Lord Ancestral Dragon, is that you? Are you still alive? Please let us know if we have done anything to anger you.”","Left with no choice, the Totem Dragon Clan’s Clan Chief led his clansmen forward and kneeled toward the ancestral dragon’s remnant.","The flames transformed, vaguely revealing a massive circular imprint.","The crowd turned their eyes over to take a better look at the imprint, only to hurriedly retract their gazes right after.","“H-h-huh? Is the ancestral dragon trying to kill us?!” Wang Qiang exclaimed in horror.","Even Little Fishy had a tinge of fear in her eyes.","The Totem Dragon Clansmen hurriedly lowered their eyes and kowtowed nonstop. Despite having yet to make sense of the situation, they apologized profusely under the assumption that they had done something that angered the ancestral dragon.","The problem lay with the imprint.","Anyone who looked at the imprint would feel immense heat surging into their bodies, as if the terrifying flames had been ignited in their souls. If they continued to examine the imprint, the flames would burn their souls until they were reduced to ashes.","Wu!","Long Chengyu and Long Muxi suddenly moaned in pain as faint lights radiated from their skin. As these lights grew brighter, they began to resemble scales plastered on their bodies.","This should have been a divine sign, but Long Muxi and Long Chengyu’s twisted faces showed that they were being put through immense pain. This further lent credence to the conjecture that their conditions were caused by the ancestral dragon’s remnant.","“Eggy, don’t look at what I’m seeing,” Chu Feng said before focusing his eyes on the circular imprint amidst the flames.","Whether the imprint was a trial or not, it was their only way out of this impasse. The only way to get to the bottom of this situation was to decipher the imprint.","The more Chu Feng stared at the imprint, the clearer the imprint became. He felt like his soul was going to burst into flames and that death was swooping down on him.","However, he didn’t waver in the least. He continued staring at the imprint as if determined to peer through its secrets even at the expense of his life.","Everything suddenly fell silent.","The burning heat inside and outside of him disappeared. Even the surrounding voices had vanished without a trace. Chu Feng felt like he had entered a quiet realm.","Until a voice echoed in his ear, “Do you not fear death?”"]},{"number":6282,"title":"Chapter 6282: Chapter 6280: Number One Beauty of the Ancient Era","paragraphs":["Chapter 6280: Number One Beauty of the Ancient Era","As the voice echoed, the scenery around Chu Feng changed.","He returned to the ancestral dragon’s forbidden land, but everything was frozen in place, be it Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, and the others. Even the flames had stalled to a complete halt.","The only ones who could move in this frozen world were Chu Feng and the voice’s owner.","It was a feminine voice. A hole was ripped open in the raging flames, and a beautiful woman emerged with graceful footsteps.","It was a gorgeous woman. She had curled, fiery-red hair that cascaded like flames. Her red eyes were big, similar to Little Fishy’s, but Little Fishy’s eyes twinkled with purity and innocence while hers were filled with seduction. Her lips were thick and sexy.","The clothes on her were daring too. She wore a fiery-red world spiritist cloak, but her skirt split open beneath her waistline, vaguely revealing curvaceous, fair thighs. Her shoulders were also fully exposed.","She naturally commanded attention wherever she went.","However, Chu Feng’s eyes were more focused on her head. There was a pair of dragon horns extending from her forehead!","“You are...” Chu Feng could fathom a guess, but he still had to seek clarification. “Are you Lord Ancestral Dragon?”","“Waaa! Lord Ancestral Dragon? That ancestral dragon’s remnant, that massive sack of bones, is such a beautiful big sister?” Eggy rested her chin on her arm as she admired the beautiful woman’s visage.","Beautiful women were pleasing to the eye even for fellow women, but Eggy’s beauty standards were extremely high. Putting all things aside, Little Fishy and Eggy were incredible beauties that others would struggle to tear their eyes away from.","But this red-haired woman’s beauty was on the same level as Eggy and Little Fishy. Her curvaceous figure and seductive features gave her beauty a unique twist that allowed her to charm not just men but also fellow women.","“Brat, there’s something unusual about you. Do you truly not fear death?”","She walked extremely close to Chu Feng before abruptly placing her hand on his heart.","“Ah, you must be very experienced. I’m standing so close to you, but you aren’t blushing, and your heart isn’t beating fast either.”","She turned her eyes to Little Fishy. “She’s indeed a beautiful one, but there seems to be an even more beautiful one in you?”","Chu Feng’s heartbeat hastened. Goosebumps rose all over his body.","The red-haired woman in front of him suddenly vanished, only to reappear in his World Spirit Space. Just how strong must she be to achieve such an incredible feat?","“You... can get in here?” Eggy’s eyes widened in disbelief when she saw the woman inside Chu Feng’s World Spirit Space.","“You’re indeed ravishing. You would have taken my title as the Ancient Era’s number one beauty if you had existed in that era,” the red-haired woman said.","“Are you truly Lord Ancestral Dragon?” Eggy asked.","The red-haired woman smiled without answering the question. She turned her eyes to the Asura Sword, and her eyes suddenly turned grim. “This sword... seems very unusual.”","Before she could do a thing, the Asura Sword suddenly roared, “Scram!”","The red-haired woman was stunned. A formidable force gushed toward her, jolting her out of Chu Feng’s World Spirit Space. Even after emerging from Chu Feng’s World Spirit Space, she had to retreat several steps before she regained her balance.","“The hell...” The woman looked at Chu Feng with shocked eyes, but she looked more excited than intimidated. “You’re more extraordinary than I thought.”","“Elder, are you truly Lord Ancestral Dragon?” Chu Feng asked once more.","He was now more convinced that the red-haired woman was the ancestral dragon on the sole basis of her overwhelming strength. She was both a powerful cultivator and a formidable world spiritist.","“Don’t call me elder. It sounds so uptight,” the red-haired woman replied with a radiant, light-hearted smile.","“My apologies if I was discourteous, milord,” Chu Feng replied with a bow.","“What’s going on? Why are you becoming more uptight when I’m telling you to stop being so uptight?” The red-haired woman frowned in displeasure.","“This...” Chu Feng was confused as to what she wanted.","“Call her big sister!” Eggy exclaimed.","“Big sister?” Chu Feng uttered those words aloud despite thinking they were inappropriate.","Much to his astonishment, the red-haired woman smiled in delight and clapped her hands. “That’s more like it!”","She flitted over to Chu Feng’s side like a specter and casually wrapped her hand around his shoulders. Her figure was so excellent that Chu Feng could feel her softness pressing against him.","“You’re Chu Feng, right? You shall be my little brother from this day on.”","“Ah...” Chu Feng was at a loss for words.","His heartbeat hastened not because of the red-haired woman’s beauty but because of her antics.","What’s going on? Isn’t the ancestral dragon’s remnant dead? Is it still alive? But even if it’s still alive, I didn’t expect it to behave in such a way.","He had once wondered how the ancestral dragon was when it was still alive, and he envisioned it as a brawny and dignified old man. But the red-haired woman was nothing like that!","The red-haired woman eyed the kneeling Totem Dragon Clansmen and asked, “Don’t be nervous, little brother. Let me ask you a question. Do you think that the Totem Dragon Clan deserves death?”","Chu Feng’s heart shuddered.","He didn’t know much about the ancestral dragon’s remnant, but he had heard that it was the reason the Totem Dragon Clan was able to reach its current height. For that reason, the Totem Dragon Clan maintained a respectful attitude to the ancestral dragon’s remnant, and they would even put their lives on the line to protect it.","But thinking about it from another perspective, if the founder of the Totem Dragon Clan rose to greatness through the ancestral dragon, it would mean that he had exploited the treasures left by the ancestral dragon’s remnant.","“Elder... The Totem Dragon Clan didn’t mean to disrespect you. They didn’t know you were alive when they first discovered you. They, as the Dragon Clan’s descendants, might have done something to you to advance their cultivation, but they have always respected you.","“They remember the grace you have shown them, and they understand that they would have never risen to their current height if not for you. They see you as their ancestor and are willing to lay down their lives for you.","“They should have seen how they fought for you when the Heavenly Dome Immortal Sect’s sectmaster sought to desecrate your body,” Chu Feng anxiously spoke up for the Totem Dragon Clan, fearing that the red-haired woman would do something to them.","However, the red-haired woman retracted the hand she had wrapped around Chu Feng’s shoulder, backed off, and stared at him with a frown.","Chu Feng was flustered, knowing how powerful the red-haired woman was.","The Asura Sword might have expelled her from his World Spirit Space, but it was never one to care about his survival. No one could stop her if she decided to go on a massacre here.","“Are you certain?” the red-haired woman asked.","“There might be some inaccuracies in my words, but...”","Chu Feng tried to explain, but the red-haired woman angrily interjected, “I’m talking about the way you address me. Weren’t you calling me ‘big sister’ a moment ago? Why did you suddenly revert to ‘elder’?”","“...” Chu Feng was at a loss for words.","Her focus is completely off!"]},{"number":6283,"title":"Chapter 6283: Chapter 6281: The Dragon Clan’s Demoness, Long Zhuoyan","paragraphs":["Chapter 6281: The Dragon Clan’s Demoness, Long Zhuoyan","“Big sister, are you really...”","Chu Feng was dying to know the answer. He had his conjecture, but he needed confirmation to know for sure.","“Come with me.”","The red-haired woman grabbed Chu Feng’s arm and leaped into the flames.","Passing through the flames, Chu Feng saw that the humongous ancestral dragon’s remnant lying on the ground like a boundless mountain range had vanished.","The red-haired woman brought Chu Feng deep underground. By the time she came to a halt, Chu Feng was utterly confused.","Like most realms, lava gushed in the deepest underground regions of this realm. Such lava could no longer harm cultivators of Chu Feng’s caliber, but it was also precisely due to how normal the lava was that he was confused.","Why did the red-haired woman bring me here?","The red-haired woman noticed Chu Feng’s confusion and smiled. She pointed at the lava below, and a mini crystal palace emerged from within.","Chu Feng was stunned.","The mini crystal palace was transparent, allowing one to see its layout. It was a treasure harnessing incredible recovery energy, but much of its energy had been depleted. Even so, it was still a formidable force by Chu Feng’s standard. It must have been an incredible treasure in its complete form.","But what shocked Chu Feng more was not the crystal palace itself but the fact that it had been there all along. To think he didn’t notice the crystal palace despite it being so close to him!","The red-haired woman’s world spiritist techniques must be at a level far beyond his reach.","“I was severely injured back then, so I had to forsake my shell and seek refuge here as I healed up. It’s only recently that I regained my freedom. Yes, I am the Lord Ancestral Dragon that they speak about. Little brother, let me ask you a question,” the red-haired woman asked.","“Feel free to ask anything, big sister,” Chu Feng replied.","“If someone looted your shell without your permission for their cultivation, only to proclaim you as their ancestor afterward and hypocritically worship you, would you forgive them or kill them?” The red-haired woman looked at Chu Feng with a smile.","Chu Feng fell silent. That was a difficult question to answer.","That was the red-haired woman’s own experience. He was not qualified to tell the red-haired woman what she should do.","But Chu Feng couldn’t stay silent here.","“Big sister, I can tell that the Totem Dragon Clan’s deeds have enraged you. Regardless of their reasons, they are at fault for looting your shell without your permission. The looting was done by their ancestors, but I think it’s fair for you to vent your anger on their descendants since they have benefited from your shell as well.","“However, I have friends in the Totem Dragon Clan, so I can only make an unreasonable request of you. Big sister, please spare the Totem Dragon Clan on my account. Please give them a chance to make up for their mistakes.”","Chu Feng bowed deeply after saying those words.","He knew the red-haired woman had both the reason and ability to vanquish the Totem Dragon Clan, and he had no right to ask her to give up on her vengeance. But he was on close terms with the Totem Dragon Clan and couldn’t turn a blind eye to their plight. He could only muster his courage to speak up on their behalf.","“Give them a chance to make up for their mistakes? How can those trash make up to me?”","Chu Feng’s heart sank upon hearing those words, but the red-haired woman looked at Chu Feng and soon added, “Little brother, I can spare their lives on your account, but even family members keep scores with one another. You’ll have to return the favor on their behalf.”","“How can I return the favor?” Chu Feng asked.","“I haven’t thought about it yet, but you’re different from them. With your talent, you’ll have plenty of ways to return my favor once your abilities mature,” the red-haired woman said.","“Rest assured, big sister. It’s my honor to be your little brother, and I am thankful that you’re willing to spare the Totem Dragon Clan on my account. If you need me for anything, as long as it’s within my means, I’ll do my best to aid you,” Chu Feng gave his promise.","But the red-haired woman continued staring at him with a smile that unnerved him. What she said next were words that he didn’t want to hear the most.","“Little brother, you must know that words are cheap. People can easily say whatever they want, but whether they will follow through with it is a different matter. For instance, there are plenty in the world who always say that they will work hard, but how many of them have truly followed it through?” the red-haired woman asked.","“I concur, big sister.”","Diligence was a talent too, and not everyone had the diligence to see through their words. In that case, their promises were bound to be empty.","“That’s why I look at actions instead of words. Little brother, you should show some sincerity if you truly mean what you say. Men should speak less and do more.”","The red-haired woman opened up her palm, revealing a sixteen-centimeter-long red dragon coiled in her hand. The red dragon raised its head to look at Chu Feng. For some reason, its blood-red eyes sent shudders down his spine.","This red dragon was a bizarre entity. It appeared to be a living creature, yet it was filled to the brim with medicinal energy as if it was forged from a pill.","“This is bad!” the Divine Deer suddenly exclaimed.","“Elder, do you recognize that red dragon?” Chu Feng hurriedly asked.","“I wasn’t sure before, but there’s no doubt about it now that she has taken that out. Chu Feng, she’s not someone you should have gotten involved with. That person could be the demoness of the Ancient Era’s Dragon Clan, Long Zhuoyan.","“I have only heard about her; I have never met her before. Long Zhuoyan possesses the most orthodox Dragon Clan’s bloodline, but she is exceptionally fond of world spiritist techniques, and she is highly talented in that field too. She was one of the top world spiritists in the Ancient Era.","“Few people have met her, but those who have always complimented her beauty. She does enjoy the title of the Ancient Era’s number one beauty.","“I also heard that Long Zhuoyan has a quirk. She’s fond of acknowledging little brothers and little sisters, but that’s not a good thing for them. She’s picking people with potential to use, and she would coerce them to swallow a dragon-shaped gu poison to ensure they remain under her control. The gu poison is extremely potent, such that many fail to withstand it and die on the spot,” the Divine Deer said.","That gave Chu Feng a good grasp of the red-haired woman.","Long Zhuoyan’s name sounded like a young lady, but her deeds were more aligned with that of a demoness.","But Chu Feng had no choice but to play along with her, or else she could obliterate the Totem Dragon Clan with a wave of her hand. So, he turned to the Divine Deer and asked, “Elder, is there any benefit to that gu poison?”","“...I don’t know. Chu Feng, are you planning to swallow that?” the Divine Deer asked.","“I have no other choice,” Chu Feng replied.","“You have a choice. I have recovered my energy. I can take you away, but...”","“But what?” Chu Feng asked.","“I don’t know if my ability is enough to escape from someone of her caliber. I can only pray that she hasn’t fully recovered yet. If we fail, our only fate is death. It would be a gamble.”","The Divine Deer’s words further drove in just how powerful Long Zhuoyan was. To think not even the Divine Deer was confident of escaping from her!"]},{"number":6284,"title":"Chapter 6284: Chapter 6282: Do Something For Me First","paragraphs":["Chapter 6282: Do Something For Me First","“Chu Feng, you decide,” the Divine Deer said.","“All right.”","Chu Feng looked at Long Zhuoyan’s gu. His decision would be to consume the gu, and the reason for that was simple. If that red-haired woman was indeed Long Zhuoyan, she would be a powerhouse whom neither he nor the Totem Dragon Clan could offend.","They could escape from her once, but could they do so for a second time?","Rather than offending her, he would rather take a risk and try to befriend her.","“Why are you standing in a daze, little brother? Are you afraid?” Long Zhuoyan smiled at Chu Feng.","“Big sister, that thing you have in your hand looks intimidating,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","“Intimidating? Indeed, it should intimidate you. This thing is a gu—if you eat it, you’ll have to keep your promise to me and fulfill whatever request I make to you in the future. If you refuse, the gu will take your life. This gu is highly poisonous, so those who aren’t tough enough may die on the spot. I’d force anyone who makes a promise to me to swallow this gu,” the red-haired woman frankly revealed the effects of the gu.","She continued looking at Chu Feng with a persistent smile, but her smile made Chu Feng’s blood turn cold.","She’s definitely an old demoness.","But Chu Feng was already prepared for this. Just as he was about to express his willingness to swallow the gu, the red-haired woman suddenly flicked her wrist and stowed away the gu.","“But this is for outsiders. Little brother, you won’t have to swallow this.”","Long Zhuoyan looked at Chu Feng with a mischievous smile. In particular, her smile deepened when she saw how confused he was. She was teasing him.","Chu Feng welcomed her teasing if it meant lessening his suffering.","“Big sister, what about the Totem Dragon Clan?” Chu Feng asked. That was the matter he was the most concerned about.","“I shall drop the matter. I’ll be counting on you to do me a huge favor in the future. However, there’s something else I need your help for now. I trust that you won’t turn me down, right?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","“Isn’t that too much? She’s asking you to do her a favor now, and you’ll still owe her a favor after that?” Eggy grumbled in displeasure.","As beautiful as the red-haired woman was, Eggy’s impression of her plummeted after she took out that terrifying gu. It also didn’t help that the red-haired woman was being greedy right now.","“Eggy, she’s no ordinary person. It’ll be highly advantageous to us if we can win her goodwill by doing her a favor.” Chu Feng quickly told her about what he had heard from the Divine Deer.","“Are you serious? She’s a top world spiritist from the Ancient Era?” Eggy reassessed the beautiful red-haired woman before her.","Seeing that Chu Feng had gone quiet, Long Zhuoyan’s smile faded. “Am I putting you in a spot, little brother?”","“Of course not. Big sister, feel free to ask anything of me,” Chu Feng hurriedly replied.","“You should have realized by now that your predecessors have imposed restrictions on their remnants to prevent powerhouses from monopolizing all the resources they have left behind. That’s why most remnants can only be accessed by juniors. This is a good thing for you juniors. As long as you’re talented, you can acquire resources without any background. However, this makes things difficult for older folks like us.","“You see, there is something I covet but am unable to acquire. Even though I have been staying here, I still keep tabs on the world of cultivation’s happenings. You are the strongest junior in the world of cultivation, and your friends are also outstanding among your peers. I require six juniors for this matter. Pick five of your peers, and we can set off right away,” Long Zhuoyan said.","“Me, Wang Qiang, Xianhai Yu’er, Xianhai Shaoyu, Long Chengyu, and Long Muxi. They should suffice,” Chu Feng replied.","“Those few outside? You aren’t going to choose anyone else?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","“They should be strong enough. May I know where we are heading and if that place will be dangerous?” Chu Feng asked.","“Whether it will be dangerous or not depends on how strong you are, but some words of advice: don’t be arrogant. Your generation of juniors is indeed formidable; very few juniors in our era were as strong as you. This matter shouldn’t be dangerous to you, but I can’t guarantee that.","“Go and ask if they are willing to come along. If they refuse, I’ll beat them up, and you can pose the question to them again,” Long Zhuoyan said.","Chu Feng hurriedly interjected, “There’s no need for that. We have been through thick and thin. They will not refuse my request. But how should I present this matter to them?”","He needed a pretext to ask the others to go on an expedition with him. He was asking Long Zhuoyan whether he should fabricate a reason or tell them the truth. If it was the latter, it would be best for Long Zhuoyan to do it.","“It’s not as if I’m a hideous creature. Tell them the truth. Tell them I am coercing you to come with me, or else I’ll kill all of you,” Long Zhuoyan replied with a sinister smile.","“All right,” Chu Feng replied.","“Let’s go.”","Their surroundings suddenly morphed. In the blink of an eye, Chu Feng returned to where he was standing before. The flames continued crackling once more, and the frozen people reverted to normal.","However, they looked confused.","“What happened earlier?” Little Fishy murmured.","Only the space around them had been frozen; time was still flowing normally for them. Even though they hadn’t been frozen for a long time, the time skip still left them feeling incongruous.","Chu Feng was about to explain the situation when Long Zhuoyan’s voice boomed from the flames. Unlike how she had talked to Chu Feng earlier, her voice was much more forceful, putting on the airs of an expert.","“Totem Dragon Clan, you looted my body and used it as resources for your cultivation while I was in hibernation. Do you think your sins will be absolved just because you call me your old ancestor?”","Those words shocked everyone. The Totem Dragon Clan was gripped by fear like never before. They couldn’t deny their ancestral dragon’s accusation. Even though they weren’t the ones who looted the body, it was true that their clan was responsible for it.","Before they could say a word, Long Zhuoyan continued, “But I’ll give you a second chance on Chu Feng’s account. Remember this: I’m only sparing you because of Chu Feng. He owes me a favor because of you, and I’ll demand it from him in the future. With this, our ties are severed. Don’t disgust me by calling me Lord Ancestral Dragon anymore. Look for Chu Feng if you want to repay the favor.”","The Totem Dragon Clan was nervous. It was not because of the disappearance of their ancestral dragon’s remnant but because their ancestral dragon was alive and harbored a deep grudge against them.","“Wu...”","Long Chengyu and Long Muxi suddenly moaned. The crowd looked over and realized that their bodies, which were emanating immense heat earlier, had cooled down, and their eyes fluttered open.","“Chengyu, Muxi, how are you feeling?” The Totem Dragon Clansmen, Chu Feng, and the others rushed forward to check on them.","Long Chengyu and Long Muxi sat up at the same time and turned to Chu Feng. Even though their bodies were incapacitated earlier, they retained consciousness, so they knew about everything that had happened.","“I’m fine, father. It might even be a blessing in disguise. My bloodline became stronger,” Long Chengyu said.","The Totem Dragon Clansmen looked conflicted. Why would his bloodline suddenly strengthen? It must be Lord Ancestral Dragon’s doing.","“If I’m not mistaken, it should also be the same for you, big sister.” Long Chengyu looked at Long Muxi.","“Mm.” Long Muxi nodded. She turned to Chu Feng and sighed. “It looks like we won’t be able to repay the debt we owe to you in this lifetime.”","The Totem Dragon Clansmen looked at Chu Feng with eyes filled with gratitude. Some of them even teared up. They understood that Chu Feng had just saved them from another crisis.","They were about to voice their gratitude when Chu Feng hurriedly raised his hand and said, “There’s no need for us to be so courteous, given our relationship. I’m only doing what I should. Also, there’s something else we need to do now.”","Chu Feng turned his gaze to Xianhai Shaoyu and Little Fishy."]},{"number":6285,"title":"Chapter 6285: Chapter 6283: Journey","paragraphs":["Chapter 6283: Journey","Chu Feng told the crowd about what had happened earlier.","“What else is there to t-t-talk about? Let’s go!” Wang Qiang exclaimed.","“It’s no problem for me and my little sister, right?” Xianhai Shaoyu glanced at Little Fishy as he asked.","“Of course! Big brother’s business is my business,” Little Fishy replied with a radiant smile. Rather than feeling conflicted, she looked forward to spending more time with Chu Feng.","“Thank you.” Long Chengyu and Long Muxi bowed to Chu Feng and the others.","The Totem Dragon Clansmen bowed deeply to Chu Feng and the others, too. They knew that Chu Feng and the others could have stayed out of this matter, and they had only gotten involved to save them.","“But w-w-where are we going?” Wang Qiang asked.","As soon as he said those words, his surroundings suddenly warped.","Chu Feng and the others vanished into thin air.","The Totem Dragon Clansmen weren't surprised, knowing that their Lord Ancestral Dragon must have been behind this. However, they felt conflicted. Even though they had suspected that Long Chengyu and Long Muxi’s conditions were related to the ancestral dragon, they hadn’t expected the ancestral dragon to be truly alive.","Everything had happened so fast that they needed some time to digest the situation. However, their greatest concern was still the safety of Chu Feng and the others.","It was likely for a request from the ancestral dragon to be anything but simple.","...","A powerful force dragged Wang Qiang away from the ground. By the time he regained his balance, he was already traveling amid the clouds at an unbelievable speed.","Chu Feng, Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu were with him, but there was also an unfamiliar figure. It was a red-haired woman.","The red-haired woman had concealed her face behind a veil, possibly because she didn’t want Wang Qiang and the others to see her face. Nevertheless, her curvaceous figure was still open for all to see.","“T-t-the heck! Where did this beauty c-c-come from!” Wang Qiang exclaimed in excitement. He turned to Long Chengyu and Long Muxi. “Is she your Lord Ancestral Dragon?”","Long Chengyu and Long Muxi turned to Chu Feng. They had never met their ancestral dragon before.","“Stop calling me Lord Ancestral Dragon. I have no ties with the Totem Dragon Clan. If you want, you can call me Lord Long,” the red-haired woman said.","“Paying respect to Lord Long.” Long Chengyu, Long Muxi, Xianhai Shaoyu, Little Fishy, and Chu Feng simultaneously bowed to her.","“Little brother, why are you calling me lord? Call me big sister,” the red-haired woman told Chu Feng with a smile.","“Big sister?” Wang Qiang’s mouth fell agape as his gaze alternated between Chu Feng and the red-haired woman.","Long Chengyu and Long Muxi also stared at Chu Feng in shock.","That was their Lord Ancestral Dragon, a figure whom they revered! How did their good friend become her younger brother?","“It just happened,” Chu Feng replied with an awkward smile. Those present are my brothers, but Long Zhuoyan suddenly acknowledged me as her little brother. This messes up the relationship.","Wang Qiang turned to the red-haired woman with yearning eyes. “Lord Long, I-I-I am brothers with Chu Feng. If he calls your big sister, s-s-shouldn’t I...”","“Don’t bother. I acknowledge little brothers not just based on their strength but their appearances too,” the red-haired woman pointed out.","“Appearances? Am I not dashing enough?” Wang Qiang confidently pointed at his own face.","“Do I look blind to you?” the red-haired woman scoffed.","Wang Qiang directed pleading eyes at Long Chengyu, Little Fishy, and the others in hopes that they could put in a good word for him, but they averted their eyes, not wanting to get involved.","“Cough cough!” Wang Qiang awkwardly coughed before looking back at the red-haired woman with a smile. “Big sister, my appearance is more of the type that slowly grows on you.”","“I don’t have the patience for that,” the red-haired woman curtly cut him off. She walked up to Little Fishy and propped up the latter’s chin. “You, however, look rather pleasing. Are you willing to be my little sister?”","“Yes, I’m willing.”","Little Fishy’s immediate answer caught the red-haired woman by surprise.","Chu Feng’s heart lurched. What if that red-haired woman coerces Little Fishy to swallow that gu?","“Good. I have another little sister now.” The red-haired woman patted Little Fishy’s head with a smile.","“Great! I have another beautiful big sister!” Little Fishy replied with a beaming smile. She was so adorable that it was hard not to be fond of her.","While others were looking elsewhere, she glanced at Chu Feng. She had quickly accepted the offer because she thought it wouldn’t be bad to have the same big sister as Chu Feng.","The red-haired woman didn’t extend the offer to anyone else after Little Fishy. This made the others feel a little awkward. They were all prodigies here, but the red-haired woman’s actions made it clear that Chu Feng and Little Fishy were the only ones who caught her eye.","It was one thing for Long Chengyu and Long Muxi to be overlooked, but even Xianhai Shaoyu was ignored.","Xianhai Shaoyu didn’t seem bothered by this matter. He was even smiling brightly as he was happy for Little Fishy.","“I bet she is g-g-gorgeous. Brother, how are y-y-you so lucky?” Wang Qiang sent an envious voice transmission to Chu Feng.","“What nonsense are you spouting? That’s an elder from the Ancient Era,” Chu Feng replied via voice transmission too.","“Age is n-n-nothing compared to appearance! Look at her f-f-figure! Wew!” Wang Qiang gulped his saliva halfway through his voice transmission.","“What are you thinking?” Chu Feng was rendered speechless.","Wang Qiang suddenly turned to look at Chu Feng. “You have changed.”","“How have I changed?” Chu Feng was confused.","“You aren’t like a man anymore.”","Chu Feng was about to refute those words when Wang Qiang pushed on, “It’s a m-m-man’s nature to fall in love with fair maidens that crosses his path. You have strayed. Only I, Wang Qiang, remain s-s-steadfast to my core.”","Chu Feng was even more speechless. You’re just a pervert. Don’t make yourself sound so upright and principled.","Suddenly, the red-haired woman asked, “Have any of you never entered a remnant that restricts access to only juniors?”","Chu Feng and the others’ gazes turned serious. They were finally going to talk business.","“Big sister, we have all been to such remnants before,” Chu Feng replied.","“Good. The place we’re heading to has six trials, and only one person can challenge each trial. What I need you to do is to clear all the trials. You are free to keep whatever benefits you obtain from the remnant; I don’t need them,” the red-haired woman said.","Her words left Chu Feng and the others excited but confused. They were excited to be able to keep the rewards, but they were confused because they thought the red-haired woman wanted them to breach the remnant to claim the rewards for herself.","Could there be other rewards after the remnant was breached?","But Chu Feng and the others didn’t probe into it. They were here to help the red-haired woman anyway, so they just had to do as they were told.","The cloud transporting them soon entered a teleportation passageway. They moved so quickly that not even Chu Feng had any clue where they were heading to.","After filling them in on the situation, the red-haired woman sat down and cultivated.","Seeing that, Chu Feng and the others sat down and cultivated as well instead of engaging in idle chatter. Even Wang Qiang followed suit.","Chu Feng wasn’t exactly cultivating. He was tempering the black metal fused inside his body. He wanted to finish forging his Bloodline Soul Puppet as soon as possible."]},{"number":6286,"title":"Chapter 6286: Chapter 6284: The Aura of Chu Feng’s Father","paragraphs":["Chapter 6284: The Aura of Chu Feng’s Father","Some time later, Chu Feng opened his eyes.","They were still in the teleportation passageway, but Chu Feng sensed spirit power pulsations. The red-haired woman was secretly releasing powerful surges of spirit power to oppose some kind of power outside.","Soon, Little Fishy opened her eyes and curiously assessed her surroundings too. She couldn’t sense the spirit power, but she sensed that something was amiss even though she couldn’t put her finger on what it was.","Thus, she smiled at Chu Feng and whispered, “Big brother, are we going through somewhere special?”","“Seems like it,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","Little Fishy was always this radiant. Chu Feng felt his mood lifting just by looking at her.","The red-haired woman turned to Chu Feng and Little Fishy. “You can sense it?”","Those words prompted the others to open their eyes too.","“Elder, are you breaching a formation?” Chu Feng asked.","“Yes, I have breached it. The rest is up to you.”","The red-haired woman waved her sleeves, and the teleportation passageway abruptly shattered. Chu Feng and the others flew out of the teleportation passageway atop the cloud.","A massive realm appeared before their eyes. They couldn’t tell if this realm was real or a formation; they didn’t even know where they were.","But that didn’t matter now.","A palace could be spotted in front of them. Beneath them was a huge mountain range, with each mountain spanning at least a million meters from one end to the other. In comparison, the palace was of normal size, making it inconspicuous amid the mountain range.","Yet, Chu Feng and the others’ attention was still drawn to it right away.","The palace was constructed out of blue stone, and its shape was unassuming too. Yet, it commanded an inviolable air. On top of that, it also emanated an extremely old aura that hinted that it was from the Immemorial Era.","This was likely the place that the red-haired woman wanted them to enter.","“This palace is n-n-not simple,” Wang Qiang blurted out in excitement.","Such places usually signified great fortuitous encounters.","“Elder, is there anything we need to take note of?” Chu Feng looked at the red-haired woman.","“Not at all. Just do your best. You can go now,” the red-haired woman replied.","A surge of energy suddenly enveloped Chu Feng and the others. By the time they realized what was happening, they were already standing at the palace’s entrance.","Sensing their presence, the palace’s heavy stone doors slowly creaked open. A long passageway awaited them inside.","“I knew there was s-s-something more inside! It can’t be as s-s-small as it looks on the outside,” Wang Qiang exclaimed.","While everyone was observing the palace, Chu Feng suddenly turned around and warily scanned his surroundings.","“What’s wrong?” Xianhai Shaoyu asked.","“Elder.” Chu Feng turned to the red-haired woman in the sky and asked via voice transmission, “Are there other people in here?”","He sensed someone observing them for a moment there, but the gaze only lasted for a brief moment. The only thing Chu Feng was certain of was that the gaze wasn’t from the red-haired woman.","“Do what you have to. I’ll ensure your safety,” the red-haired woman said confidently.","Little Fishy and the others felt stifled. They knew that Chu Feng must have communicated with the red-haired woman, but they chose not to probe since Chu Feng must have his reason for not speaking aloud.","Little Fishy turned to Chu Feng and asked, “Big brother, should we enter?”","The others also looked at Chu Feng. They viewed him as their leader.","“Let’s go,” Chu Feng said, and the group entered the palace.","The doors remained open behind them.","The passageway was much deeper than they had expected. Despite their swift advancement, they couldn’t see the end of the passageway even after walking for a while. They were walking in a straight line, yet they could no longer see the stone doors behind them.","This showed just how exaggeratedly long the corridor was.","“Why h-h-haven’t we reached the other end of the passageway yet? Could we have unknowingly s-s-stumbled into a labyrinth?” Wang Qiang glanced at Chu Feng as he asked.","He was inclined to trust Chu Feng’s judgment.","“It doesn’t feel like a labyrinth. This passageway just seems to be exceptionally long. Let’s hurry,” Chu Feng said.","The group sped up, but despite traveling at full speed, it still took them a while before they finally saw the end of the passageway and found themselves faced with a pair of massive doors.","These stone doors were similar to the ones at the entrance; despite their unassuming appearances, it was impossible to see past them.","“W-w-we finally reached the end!” Wang Qiang exclaimed.","“Indeed. Is there a reason the passageway is so long?” Little Fishy was bewildered.","They had been to countless remnants, but this place still felt unusual to them.","“Forget it. Let’s head in and take a look,” Xianhai Shaoyu said as he stepped forward and pushed the stone doors open.","Beyond the stone doors was a circular hall with six doors. At the center of the hall was a pillar covered in protrusions. Each protrusion was inscribed with an ancient talisman.","But what was more eye-catching were the words inscribed on the ground in front of the entrance—’Heed my advice. The items here are not to be claimed. Retreat now.’","The crowd was stunned.","Everything in here gave off the Immemorial Era’s aura except for these words. These words were left very recently, not only in this era but perhaps just a few years ago.","But there was something about the words that further shocked Chu Feng.","“Eggy, these words seem to be from my father,” Chu Feng told Eggy.","“Are you for certain? Do you sense your father’s aura?” Eggy asked.","“It is so faint that I can’t be certain of it, but it resembles my father’s aura,” Chu Feng replied.","“It should be from your father. Your father is the god of tomb-raiding, after all,” Eggy remarked.","“The god of tomb-raiding?” Chu Feng was confused.","“Haven’t you noticed it? Your father’s trail can always be found in the better remnants. I think you’re already quite lucky. If not for the red-haired woman bringing you here, you wouldn’t have known that there’s a remnant here.","“Yet, your father found such a place. Just how incredibly lucky must he have been? I even wonder if he has some fortuitous encounter that gives him the location of most hidden remnants and treasures in the world. No wonder your father is so powerful. He has taken all the good things for himself and left only the crumbs behind for you.”","Eggy’s analysis sounded like nonsense, but Chu Feng thought it made sense.","Chu Feng walked up to touch the words. The lingering aura flowed up his palm and into his body, allowing him to better sense the faint aura.","“It’s indeed my father’s aura,” Chu Feng said.","“Did you sense anything else?” Eggy asked.","“I’m afraid not. He only left these words behind.”","“Could your father have intentionally left his aura here because he thought that you might come here in the future?”","“It doesn’t seem like it. My father would have constructed a formation to provide me with more information if he wanted to stop me from coming here, but that’s not the case here. These words probably serve to warn others who stumble in here. However, I have a guess,” Chu Feng said.","“What is it?” Eggy asked.","“My father might have sensed danger, so he steered clear of everything in here and left only these words infused with his aura behind,” Chu Feng replied."]},{"number":6287,"title":"Chapter 6287: Chapter 6285: The Golden Light Shines; The Wish Gate","paragraphs":["Chapter 6285: The Golden Light Shines; The Wish Gate","“Danger? What danger?” Eggy asked.","Chu Feng first closed the stone doors before turning to Little Fishy and the others. “I sensed someone spying on us when we were outside earlier. It was a discreet gaze, and it was coming from extremely far away. Someone else is in this realm, and that person is extremely powerful.","“The person who left these words behind must have noticed that person too and the dangers lurking here, so he didn’t breach this remnant and instead just left these words behind and left.”","“Is that what you were secretly asking big sister earlier?” Little Fishy asked.","“Yes,” Chu Feng replied.","“No wonder she declared that she would guarantee our safety. She must have sensed something,” Little Fishy said.","“She might even know who that person is,” Xianhai Shaoyu deduced.","“The things in h-h-here must be incredible for someone to be eyeing it. Brother, w-w-what are your thoughts? Advance or retreat?” Wang Qiang asked.","“We’ll advance,” Chu Feng replied.","They had no choice now that they were here. In the first place, the red-haired woman might not even let them off if they didn’t do as they were told.","“Let’s do it then!” Wang Qiang roared.","The others also expressed their willingness to follow Chu Feng.","“But h-h-how should we do it?” Wang Qiang suddenly asked.","Most remnants would have provided them a clue by this point, but there had been absolutely no clue ever since they entered the palace.","Chu Feng placed his hand on a stone door, and a formation whirred to action. He communed with the formation, and soon, the words ‘Chu Feng’ appeared on the door.","“Place your hand on the stone door, and a formation will commune with us,” Chu Feng said.","Wang Qiang and the others dove into action.","Just then, the pillar at the hall’s center began revolving. A ray of light shot out from Chu Feng’s stone door and swiftly traversed through the runes as the pillar spun. The light alternated colors among white, green, blue, purple, and golden.","When the pillar finally stopped, the light settled on white. The white light then shot from the pillar toward the stone door, forming two massive words—Resource Gate.","The crowd was confused.","Another light silhouette descended from the hall’s ceiling and landed next to the pillar. The light silhouette was humanoid, but it was impossible to tell its gender or make out its facial features. Even its voice was ambiguous.","“Clearing the Resource Gate will entitle you to rewards. Unfortunately, this gate contains the poorest resource in this hall,” the light entity said before disappearing.","“Poorest resource? Am I that unlucky?” Chu Feng sighed.","“Brother, t-t-that looks like it.” Wang Qiang nodded.","The stone door suddenly opened, and Chu Feng was dragged into it before he could react.","...","“Looks like the difficulty level and rewards differ for each door,” Long Chengyu remarked.","“That seems to be the case.” Long Muxi nodded too.","“D-d-damn it! My brother has always had good luck. If h-h-he got the worst one... could the other trials be impossible for us to clear?” Wang Qiang felt ominous.","“That’s indeed a problem,” Xianhai Shaoyu concurred.","“Forget i-t-it! We’re already here anyway. Let’s g-g-give it a try! Why don’t we d-d-do it together and see whose luck is the best?” Wang Qiang suggested as he approached a stone door.","“Sure,” Xianhai Shaoyu replied.","The others selected a door each too.","They placed their palms on the stone door at the same time and communed with their respective formations. Soon, their names appeared on their respective stone doors. The pillar began revolving, but this time, there were five rays of light shining on it.","In the end...","Wang Qiang got the Purple Resource Gate.","Little Fishy got the Purple Resource Gate.","Long Chengyu got the Purple Resource Gate.","Long Muxi got the Purple Resource Gate.","Xianhai Shaoyu got the Golden Wish Gate.","The brightness of the light varied as well. The golden light produced by Xianhai Shaoyu’s Golden Wish Gate was so bright that it lit up the entire hall. Anyone could tell that there was something incredible inside with just a glance.","The light entity descended beside the pillar once more to explain the situation with the gates.","The Resource Gates were easy to understand—they were in the same situation as Chu Feng. The only difference was their luck. They had the chance to obtain better cultivation resources, but the difficulty of their challenge was much higher too.","The most formidable one of all was Xianhai Shaoyu’s Wish Gate. If he succeeded, he could have a reasonable wish fulfilled.","“Damn it! My b-b-brother was the only unlucky one!” Wang Qiang lamented for Chu Feng.","“How can this be? How can big brother receive the White Resource Gate?” Little Fishy also felt that this was unfair for Chu Feng.","It was one thing if everyone got the White Resource Gate, but Chu Feng was the only one who got the worst one.","“Elder, is there a second chance?” Little Fishy asked.","The light entity didn’t answer. It appeared to be a formation devoid of intelligence.","It was then that the stone doors in front of Little Fishy and the others opened and sucked them. Only one person was left in the hall—Xianhai Shaoyu. His door didn’t open.","While Xianhai Shaoyu was bewildered, the light entity turned to him and said, “Your luck is harder to say. One can say you have the best luck, but one can also say you have the worst luck. You’ll reap great rewards if you clear the trial; I can even raise your base cultivation by three ranks. However, you also have to undergo the hardest trial.","“I’ll allow you to bring a companion in with you to confront the trial together, but only if your companion is willing.”","Right after the light entity said those words, a voice echoed, “I’m willing.”","Chu Feng was standing in front of the first stone door. His name had vanished from the stone door, a sign that he had cleared his trial.","The light entity didn’t reply. It didn’t even look at Chu Feng before dissipating.","“So fast?” Xianhai Shaoyu turned to Chu Feng.","“It’s a simple trial. Just a few lightning bolts falling from the sky—it barely scratched my itch. However, the rewards are as miserable.” Chu Feng opened his palm up to reveal a martial power bead.","The martial power bead was of decent quality, but it would be of very little use to Chu Feng at his current cultivation level.","“Your luck is terrible this time,” Xianhai Shaoyu remarked.","“Indeed, but it’s at least not a wasted trip with you getting the big prize. How about it? I’ll accompany you,” Chu Feng said.","He happened to overhear the light entity’s words. Being able to raise one cultivation by three ranks was a humongous fortuitous encounter.","Xianhai Shaoyu looked at Chu Feng contemplatively.","“What’s wrong? You can’t trust me?” Chu Feng asked.","“That’s not it.” Xianhai Shaoyu shook his head.","“You’re worried about implicating me into a dangerous situation, but that’s even more reason for you to take me with you. We can at least cover each other if we go in as a pair, right?” Chu Feng said as he approached Xianhai Shaoyu’s golden stone door.","Xianhai Shaoyu still looked hesitant, but in the end, he nodded. “All right.”","The stone door sensed his decision and opened up. A powerful suction force dragged Chu Feng and Xianhai Shaoyu in."]},{"number":6288,"title":"Chapter 6288: Chapter 6286: A Good Helper","paragraphs":["Chapter 6286: A Good Helper","By the time the suction force dissipated and Chu Feng regained his balance, he and Xianhai Shaoyu were around standing in the middle of a barren plain.","The plain looked boundless, and the ground was cracked and devoid of life.","In contrast, the night sky was filled with stars and hope.","Barren and hope; this seemed to be hinting at something.","But Chu Feng was more focused on Xianhai Shaoyu.","“What’s wrong, Brother Shaoyu? Are you feeling nervous?” Chu Feng asked, for he could clearly see Xianhai Shaoyu’s heartbeat.","Their quiet surroundings made Xianhai Shaoyu’s erratic heartbeat even more apparent.","“It’s not nervousness. I’m just excited to be together with Brother Chu Feng.” Xianhai Shaoyu grinned as he grabbed Chu Feng’s shoulder and blinked his eyes seductively.","Any other men in Chu Feng’s place might have gotten the goosebumps, but Chu Feng responded with a smile, knowing that Xianhai Shaoyu had a bizarre sense of humor. However, he couldn’t help but think that there was something amiss with Xianhai Shaoyu’s condition.","Xianhai Shaoyu was fond of joking, but he always dealt with situations confidently and maturely when it came down to it. However, Chu Feng could sense his nervousness and fear.","A white light suddenly descended from the sky. It was also a light entity. It had clearer outlines, though its facial features remained indistinct. This time, they could make out its white hair and white robe.","However, they couldn’t tell if it was the same light entity as they had encountered in the hall.","Shoosh!","With a wave of his sleeves, the light entity elder drew a circle of a million meters in radius around Chu Feng and Xianhai Shaoyu. He then waved his arm, and an immortal grass flew toward Xianhai Shaoyu.","“Hold the immortal grass and commune with it. Use your will to envelop the earth with the immortal grass. You’ll be entitled to a wish if the proliferation of the immortal grass exceeds the area I have drawn out.”","Xianhai Shaoyu took the immortal grass and closed his eyes. After a brief silence, his muscles suddenly tensed up.","Countless immortal grasses emerged from the ground beneath him and swiftly proliferated.","“Xianhai Shaoyu is not too bad,” Eggy remarked.","At the rate Xianhai Shaoyu was going, he should cross the area drawn by the light entity elder with ease.","However, the proliferation of the immortal grass swiftly slowed, and Xianhai Shaoyu gritted his teeth as a sign of strain. Filling the area with immortal grass was easier said than done.","Chu Feng extended his psyche to the immortal grass to see if he could help Xianhai Shaoyu, but before his psyche could reach, the light entity elder said, “You can help him, but if you clear the trial, the wish will go to you instead of him.”","Chu Feng hesitated. He had come here to help Xianhai Shaoyu; the last thing he wanted to do was to steal the latter’s fortuitous encounter.","“Don’t worry, Brother Chu Feng. I can do it,” Xianhai Shaoyu said with a strained face.","He succeeded in the end, but he weakly collapsed as soon as the immortal grass crossed the demarcated area.","Chu Feng rushed over to support him. ”Brother Shaoyu.”","His heart clenched up. Xianhai Shaoyu’s mind was terribly weakened, resulting in his soul’s instability. The immortal grass must have attacked his psyche earlier. His life had been at risk.","To make things worse, his injuries were so severe that Chu Feng could do nothing about them.","Even so, Xianhai Shaoyu flashed a smile at Chu Feng and bragged, “How about that? I told you I can do it, right?”","“You have astounding willpower. A prodigy indeed.”","The light entity elder pointed his finger at Xianhai Shaoyu, and a gentle surge of energy enveloped him. The latter instantly recovered from his earlier weakness.","This made Chu Feng realize that this remnant was more incredible than he had expected, and this light entity elder might not just be a formation manifestation.","“Thank you, elder.” Xianhai Shaoyu quickly bowed to the light entity elder upon sensing his recovery.","“You need not thank me. This was a trial. Since you have cleared it, there’s no need for you to suffer beyond that. Do you wish to advance your cultivation, or do you have other wishes?” the light entity elder asked.","“Elder, I’d like to make another wish,” Xianhai Shaoyu said.","“What is it?”","“I wish to restore my little sister’s bloodline.”","Chu Feng widened his eyes as a thought suddenly surfaced in his mind, but he didn’t probe any deeper and instead waited for the light entity elder’s answer.","“Xianhai Yu’er, right?” the light entity elder asked.","“That’s right.” Xianhai Shaoyu nodded.","The light entity elder fell silent. Despite his indistinct facial features, Chu Feng and Xianhai Shaoyu could sense that he had closed his eyes. He might have gone off to check Xianhai Yu’er’s condition.","A moment later, the light entity elder opened his eyes and said, “It won’t be easy to heal your little sister’s bloodline. How about this? If you give up on the wish, I’ll make an exception and raise your cultivation by four ranks.”","“Elder, I only have this wish. Please help me if it’s within your means.” Xianhai Shaoyu kneeled onto the ground.","“I’ll raise your cultivation by five ranks,” the light entity elder counter offered.","“Elder.” Xianhai Shaoyu kowtowed to him.","“Haa, why are you so obstinate? It’s not that I don’t want to help you, but this won’t be easy. If you insist on this wish, you’ll have to relinquish your current rewards and undergo the trial again, but this time, the trial won’t be as easy as planting immortal grass. If you fail, not only will you not receive any rewards, but you could lose your life too,” the light entity elder said.","“Elder, will you restore my little sister’s bloodline if I clear the trial?” Xianhai Shaoyu asked.","The light entity elder stared at Xianhai Shaoyu for several seconds before finally nodding.","“Elder, please let me take the trial.” Xianhai Shaoyu kowtowed to the light entity elder once more.","“All right.”","The light entity elder waved his sleeves, and the immortal grass vanished. Instead, a quiver filled with ten arrows appeared in front of the light entity elder. At the light entity elder’s gesture, the ten arrows flew out of the quiver and whizzed into the ground.","As they penetrated the ground, the earth shook.","“Pull out all ten arrows and return them to the quiver to clear the trial. Some words of warning: the arrows harness dangerous energy that can claim your life. Let go if you’re unable to withstand the arrow’s energy. Don’t lose your life over your obstinacy,” the light entity elder said.","Without any hesitation, Xianhai Shaoyu reached out to grab an arrow.","Before he could even touch the arrow, Chu Feng suddenly grabbed his wrist and asked, “Brother Shaoyu, what’s wrong with Yu’er’s bloodline?”","“It’s fine. I’ll tell you later,” Xianhai Shaoyu replied with a smile.","He tried to reach for the arrow, but Chu Feng continued to stop him.","“Tell me right now,” Chu Feng insisted.","Faced with Chu Feng’s unwavering gaze, Xianhai Shaoyu understood that Chu Feng would not let him proceed till he revealed the truth.","“In my clan, our bloodline potency is measured in terms of fish immortals. Every clansman has at least a fish immortal in their bloodline. Those with three fish immortals can be categorized as an expert. I have eight fish immortals, whereas Yu’er has nine. That’s why everyone in the clan believes she’ll surpass me in the future from the moment of her birth. And indeed, her talent is above mine.”","Xianhai Shaoyu had a proud smile as he spoke, but his smile soon faded to shame.","“When we were subjugated by the God Clan, Yu’er tried to fight back by using the God Clan’s formation to ignite her bloodline, but she ended up paying a heavy price for it. She depleted a fish immortal in the process.”","Xianhai Shaoyu lowered his head.","Chu Feng suddenly felt the world spinning around him despite standing still. Even Eggy’s expression stiffened up, and she felt like something had pierced her heart.","They understood what had happened.","Back then, in the Immemorial Massacre Sea, Little Fishy had utilized a peculiar power to save Chu Feng. When Chu Feng recovered, he found a fish imprinted on his chest. That led him to think that the power was related to Little Fishy’s bloodline.","But the power had already fused into him, so there was no way for him to return it to Little Fishy. He asked Little Fishy about it afterward, and the latter replied that it was no big deal.","It was now clear to him that Little Fishy had lost the fish immortal while trying to save him. Everything finally made sense now. That would explain how she was able to save him from the verge of death; she had made a huge sacrifice for that.","“Elder, can I complete the trial on his behalf?” Chu Feng asked the light entity elder.","“The wish will be yours if you complete this trial,” the light entity elder replied.","“I wish for the same thing too,” Chu Feng replied.","“You must be truly close, but...”","Boom!","Chu Feng grabbed an arrow and tried to pull it out, but it was easier said than done. In the process of doing so, the surrounding earth cracked, and it felt like the world would crumble.","“Chu Feng!!!” Xianhai Shaoyu was worried.","He sensed terrifying energy flowing from the arrow into Chu Feng’s body. This was far more dangerous than the immortal grass’ attacks.","But Chu Feng remained unfazed. He exerted his strength and pulled out the arrow in one shot. Then, with a wave of his sleeves, he pulled out the remaining nine arrows too.","The earth collapsed inward, and the world crumbled into chaos. Everything had been reduced to the void.","With the ten arrows in hand, every step Chu Feng took left cracks in space. However, he didn’t hesitate in the least as he swiftly advanced toward the quiver, as if fearing that he would fail the trial if he didn’t hurry.","In the end, he successfully placed the ten arrows into the quiver.","As soon as the feat was accomplished, Chu Feng collapsed like a deflated ball.","Xianhai Shaoyu rushed over to catch Chu Feng, but a gentle surge of energy suddenly enveloped Chu Feng. It was the light entity elder’s doing.","The light entity elder turned to Xianhai Shaoyu and said, “You have great luck. There’s no way you could have cleared this trial given your earlier performance, but you picked a good helper.”"]},{"number":6289,"title":"Chapter 6289: Chapter 6287: Restoring Little Fishy’s Bloodline","paragraphs":["Chapter 6287: Restoring Little Fishy’s Bloodline","Xianhai Shaoyu felt ashamed looking at Chu Feng.","The recovery energy that had instantly healed him needed time to work on Chu Feng. This showed that the light entity elder’s words were true and that the difficulty of the trial was much higher than the proliferation of the immortal grass.","He should have been the one to clear the trial, but Chu Feng did it for him.","Fortunately, Chu Feng regained consciousness shortly after, and his weak body began swiftly recovering.","“Brother Chu Feng, how are you faring?” Xianhai Shaoyu asked concernedly.","“I’m fine. Did I succeed?” Chu Feng asked.","Instead of answering, Xianhai Shaoyu raised his head to look at the light entity elder.","“Mm.” The light entity elder nodded.","Chu Feng and Xianhai Shaoyu breathed a sigh of relief.","“Brother Chu Feng, it’s all thanks to you.”","Xianhai Shaoyu looked at Chu Feng with grateful eyes. The impairment of Little Fishy’s bloodline had always been a thorn in his heart, especially when he was helpless when his clan was in trouble. He could only watch as his little sister sacrificed herself to fight for their clan.","He didn’t want to feel such helplessness a second time.","That was why he was nervous when he entered this place. He harbored hopes about this remnant, knowing that it was a formidable place, but he also knew that recovering a bloodline was no easy feat, especially one as strong as his little sister’s.","He couldn’t begin to imagine what kind of power was needed to heal his little sister’s bloodline.","He was not afraid of a failure, but he was afraid that this remnant could not fulfill his wish even if he succeeded.","Fortunately, things ended well. That was why he was so grateful to Chu Feng.","Seeing Xianhai Shaoyu’s grateful and solemn expression, Chu Feng said, “I should be the one to restore Yu’er’s bloodline. Brother Shaoyu, you are unaware of the truth, but Yu’er didn’t lose that fish immortal when fighting against the God Clan. She fused it into my body to save me in the Immemorial Massacre Sea. Her fish immortal is currently in my heart.”","“Ah?” Xianhai Shaoyu was taken aback.","In truth, he had no idea how Little Fishy had lost her fish immortal. He conjectured that she had lost it when fighting against the God Clan.","Only now did he learn the truth, but instead of blaming Chu Feng, he laughed in relief.","“I see.”","Xianhai Shaoyu patted Chu Feng’s shoulder before turning to the light entity elder and saying something that horrified Chu Feng. “Elder, can I cancel that wish?”","“Huh? What nonsense are you spouting! It wasn’t easy for me to clear that trial!” Chu Feng anxiously clasped Xianhai Shaoyu’s mouth.","The light entity elder replied, “Only Chu Feng can decide that. The wish belongs to him since he’s the one who cleared the trial. More importantly, the fish immortal is indeed currently in his heart. I can remove it without hurting him, but I’ll require his agreement.”","Chu Feng replied without hesitation, “I agree.”","Xianhai Shaoyu struggled free of Chu Feng’s grasp and sighed. “How can I be so dumb? I can see now that my little sister is the far smarter one. We should have let you owe her, so that our Immortal Sea Fish Clan can clutch onto you as our backing. You’re bound to share good stuff you obtain with my little sister, and I can benefit off that.”","Xianhai Shaoyu sighed regrettably.","Chu Feng rolled his eyes. He knew that Xianhai Shaoyu was joking, though he didn’t think the joke was funny.","“Elder, will it be troublesome? How long will it take?” Chu Feng asked the light entity elder.","He understood that this was a difficult feat, and his heart wouldn’t rest at ease until Little Fishy regained her fish immortal.","“It is troublesome, but it won’t take too long.”","The light entity elder raised his left hand and released a burst of light that pierced through Chu Feng’s heart. Chu Feng’s heart became transparent, revealing a little fish imprint on his heart.","It was the fish immortal.","The fish imprint morphed into a fish and swam out of Chu Feng’s body to the elder’s palm.","“Brother Chu Feng, how are you feeling? Do you feel any discomfort?” Xianhai Shaoyu nervously asked.","Considering that the fish immortal had fused with Chu Feng, extracting it was bound to inflict some damage to him.","“Do I look unwell to you?” Chu Feng smiled.","“You look fine.” Xianhai Shaoyu chuckled.","Chu Feng turned to the light entity elder.","The latter shifted the fish immortal with his left hand while waving his right hand. A rune appeared each time he waved his right hand, and the runes intersected one another to form a formation.","But Chu Feng couldn’t tell if that formation was constructed out of spirit power or martial power. He couldn’t sense the slightest aura from it, making it hard for him to discern its nature.","At the same time, he was also impressed by the light entity elder’s means. He astonishingly didn’t experience any discomfort when the fish immortal was extracted from his body.","Looks like there’s hope for the restoration of Little Fishy’s bloodline.","...","Little Fishy, Wang Qiang, Long Chengyu, Long Muxi and the others cleared their respective trials and returned to the hall. The last one to return to Long Muxi.","“Is Chu Feng not done yet?” Long Muxi asked.","Chu Feng had entered his trial first, and his trial should have been easier than theirs. He should have returned to the hall earlier than the rest of them.","“Don’t worry. Considering Brother Chu Feng’s means, he might have triggered an even harder trial.” Long Chengyu had unwavering confidence in Chu Feng. Instead, he turned to Long Muxi and asked, “Big sister, did you make a breakthrough?”","“Yes, I have reached rank two True God level,” Long Muxi replied.","“Me too.” Long Chengyu smiled. He was in much higher spirits than before.","The trial had been difficult, but he still succeeded in clearing it. There was no greater joy to a cultivator than advancing their cultivation.","Long Muxi looked at Wang Qiang and Little Fishy.","“W-w-we all made breakthroughs,” Wang Qiang replied.","It should have taken him a bit more time to reach rank three True God level, but when he cleared the trial, the cultivation resources were directly fused into his body, allowing him to make a breakthrough earlier than expected.","It was the same for Little Fishy. She had reached rank three True God level as well.","“Miss Yu’er, why do you look so unhappy?” Long Muxi was confused.","Somehow, Xianhai Yu’er appeared annoyed despite having made a breakthrough.","“She w-w-wanted to reserve a portion of the cultivation resources for Brother Chu Feng, but it was automatically f-f-fused into her body. That’s why she’s u-u-unhappy. Well, it can’t be helped that my brother is too charming l-l-like me.” Wang Qiang thumped his chest and grinned.","Little Fishy glared at him, but she didn’t say a word as she wasn’t in the mood to bicker.","Long Muxi couldn’t smile either. She wanted to reserve all the cultivation resources for Chu Feng as the latter had just saved the Totem Dragon Clan from yet another crisis.","Weng!","A ray of light suddenly shone down on Little Fishy and took her away.","“What’s going on?” Long Chengyu was worried.","“It should be fine. S-s-she must have triggered something,” Wang Qiang was not worried.","Little Fishy was transported to where Chu Feng and Xianhai Shaoyu were, but the light entity elder immediately sealed her off in a formation as soon as she landed on the ground.","She could still see Chu Feng and Xianhai Shaoyu, but she could also see the fish immortal in the light entity elder’s hand. That was her bloodline, after all. It resonated strongly with her.","“Brother, big brother, what’s going on?” Little Fishy anxiously asked.","“Don’t worry, little sister. Brother Chu Feng wished for the restoration of your bloodline. Don’t move around and cooperate,” Xianhai Shaoyu explained.","“What? I don’t need to restore my bloodline! Let me go!” Little Fishy was horrified and began struggling with all her might.","“This matter isn’t up to you. The wish maker has made his wish,” the light entity elder said.","The formation suddenly glowed brightly, and the fish immortal flew up and fused into the formation. Shortly after, the formation dissipated, and Little Fishy regained her freedom.","The first thing she did was rush to Chu Feng’s side. She grabbed his wrist with one hand and placed the other on his chest to examine his condition. Her beautiful face had turned pale out of fright.","She was worried that Chu Feng would be harmed by the removal of the fish immortal. That was why she didn’t want to restore her bloodline even though it was beneficial to her."]},{"number":6290,"title":"Chapter 6290: Chapter 6288: Heavenly Temple Aura","paragraphs":["Chapter 6288: Heavenly Temple Aura","Looking at Little Fishy’s worried pale face up close, Chu Feng felt warmth in his heart.","“Stop looking, Yu’er. I’m fine.”","Little Fishy could tell that Chu Feng was fine, but she found it unbelievable that he was unharmed despite having the fish immortal extracted from his body, which was why she kept examining his body over and over again.","“Big brother, are you really fine?” Little Fishy looked at Chu Feng with skepticism in her eyes. She wondered if he was deceiving her with an illusion, though she was unable to find any gaps in it.","“I’m truly fine. Unlike you, I’m not in the habit of lying to others,” Chu Feng said.","“When have I lied to you?” Little Fishy replied innocently.","“You told me it was no big deal when you fused that fish immortal into my body, but it impaired your bloodline. You should have known that it will affect your future progress,” Chu Feng said.","“I... didn’t want you to worry.” Little Fishy lowered her head.","“I’ll forgive you this time, but you mustn’t do this again. I am more resilient than you think. I’ll survive no matter how difficult the ordeal is. Don’t forget that I have been through plenty while you’re not around.”","Chu Feng didn’t truly blame Little Fishy for what she did. He just hoped that she wouldn’t do something as foolish as this ever again. He earnestly regretted forcing Little Fishy to make such a decision.","Instead of answering his question, Little Fishy asked, “Are you truly fine, big brother? You mustn’t lie to me.”","“I’m fine. I swear to heaven.” Chu Feng even made a vow to convince her.","“That’s good.” Little Fishy revealed a relieved smile.","“What about you? Do you feel any discomfort? How’s the recovery of your bloodline going? You can tell this elder here if you’re facing any issue. He should be able to help you,” Chu Feng said.","“You brat. Are you worried that I won’t see this matter through? Nothing will go wrong now that I have given you my word.” The light entity elder saw through Chu Feng’s intention. He turned to Little Fishy and said, “Lass, go ahead and speak the truth. Does your bloodline feel any different from before you lost your fish immortal?”","“It feels the same. Thank you, elder. Thank you, big brother. And I should thank my brother too.” Little Fishy bowed deeply to the trio one after another. Her sincere attitude made her likeable.","Even the light entity elder revealed a vague smile.","“Elder, who are you? How are you able to recover my bloodline without causing any discomfort?” Little Fishy took this opportunity to ask.","Chu Feng and Xianhai Shaoyu pricked up their ears, curious to know the answer too.","“The four of you have obtained the recognition of the Immemorial Land of Dao Creation, right?” the light entity elder asked instead.","“You’re able to tell?” Chu Feng and the others were taken aback.","But on second thought, it wasn’t that surprising for someone capable of seeing through their bloodlines to tell that they had received the recognition of the Immemorial Land of Dao Creation.","A light suddenly descended from the sky, and Wang Qiang emerged from it.","“Brother, w-w-what’s going on? Who is this?”","Wang Qiang was chatting with Long Muxi when he was suddenly dragged here, so it was no wonder he was confused. On top of that, this light entity looked different from the one he had seen in the hall.","“Don’t utter nonsense. He’s likely to be the master of this remnant. He’s not a formation entity but a true expert,” Chu Feng quickly sent a voice transmission to Wang Qiang.","“Junior Wang Qiang p-p-pays respect to milord!” Wang Qiang bowed to the light entity elder.","“You have been to the Sacred Heavenly Temple?” the light entity elder asked.","“Yes, we have been there,” Chu Feng and the others replied in unison.","“Do you know what kind of place the Sacred Heavenly Temple is?”","“It’s the greatest remnant and the biggest treasure trove in the world of cultivation. A Sacred Temple Bead is required to enter its premises, and one will be granted a corresponding treasure or power. Unfortunately, there aren’t many high-tier Sacred Temple Bead left in the present era,” Xianhai Shaoyu lamented.","He earnestly wanted to visit the Sacred Heavenly Temple to see what was there.","“Mm, you’re on point. A Sacred Temple Bead is required to enter the Sacred Heavenly Temple, but there is another way to access the Sacred Heavenly Temple and obtain its true treasure and power.”","This piqued Chu Feng and the others’ curiosity. This was their first time hearing about this.","“What’s the way to do so?” Wang Qiang blurted out.","“Obtaining the Heavenly Temple Aura,” the light entity elder replied.","“How can the Heavenly Temple Aura be obtained?” Chu Feng asked.","“You can obtain it here.”","“Here?”","“The heck!”","The lower jaws of Chu Feng and the others slackened. Desire brimmed in their eyes.","“Don’t get too excited yet. There are other remnants in the world of cultivation that you can obtain Heavenly Temple Aura from, but the amount you can obtain from each place is limited. The amount you can obtain here is not enough for you to access the Heavenly Sacred Temple,” the light entity elder said.","“Elder, can we obtain the Heavenly Temple Aura here? Do we need to undergo some trial?” Xianhai Shaoyu asked in a mixture of excitement and worry.","Even though the light entity elder had made it clear that they couldn’t obtain enough Heavenly Temple Aura here to enter the Sacred Heavenly Temple, this was still a fortuitous encounter.","But the fact that he had never heard of this method before hinted at its difficulty, and he also knew how difficult the trials in this remnant could get.","“Under normal circumstances, yes, you would have to undergo a trial to obtain the Heavenly Temple Aura, but since you have the Immemorial Land of Dao Creation’s recognition, I shall make an exception here. You can obtain the Heavenly Temple Aura straight away if you wish,” the light entity elder said.","“Will the Heavenly Temple Aura be distributed to the four of us or our entire group?” Chu Feng asked. He hoped Long Chengyu and Long Muxi could obtain the Heavenly Temple Aura too.","“Those two aren’t qualified,” the light entity elder replied.","“C-c-can we let them undergo the trial then?” Wang Qiang asked.","“Let me make it clearer to you since you don’t seem to understand what I mean. Those two aren’t even qualified to know about this matter,” the light entity elder replied."]},{"number":6291,"title":"Chapter 6291: Chapter 6289: Someone I Should Get On Good Terms With","paragraphs":["Chapter 6289: Someone I Should Get On Good Terms With","“I shan’t talk too much about those two, but are the four of you willing to accept the Heavenly Temple Aura?” the light entity elder asked.","“Of course w-w-we are! Is there a reason for us to t-t-turn it down?” Wang Qiang asked.","The light entity elder chuckled softly. “There’s something I ought to warn you. The Heavenly Temple Aura should only be discernible by the Sacred Heavenly Temple once fused into your body, but there are many talented individuals in this world capable of doing what others can’t. Over time, some might have developed means to detect Heavenly Temple Aura and siphon it. That’s why I asked if you’re willing.”","His words were clear—there was a risk to accepting the Heavenly Temple Aura.","“Elder, my brother sensed someone eyeing this place earlier. Could it be someone who covets the Heavenly Temple Aura earlier?” Xianhai Shaoyu asked.","The light entity elder didn’t answer the question. “You only have to tell me whether you’re willing to accept the Heavenly Temple Aura or not.”","“Yes, I’m willing,” Chu Feng replied without hesitation.","Be it wealth or a beautiful face, all good things in this world came with risks. However, the benefits they brought about were irrefutable. On the contrary, forgoing these good things might not necessarily free one from danger.","The strong at least had the power to retaliate. The weak could only resign themselves to fate.","“I’m willing too.”","“Elder, I’m willing to accept the Heavenly Temple Aura.”","“M-m-me too!”","Little Fishy and the others expressed their stances as well.","The light entity elder formed a hand seal, and the surrounding space shook. Four light pillars descended from the sky and glowed into the bodies of Chu Feng and the others.","This process didn’t take too long.","“Can someone really detect the Heavenly Temple Aura?” Wang Qiang asked Chu Feng.","“It would be very difficult,” Chu Feng replied with a smile.","Wang Qiang was asking that question because he couldn’t sense the Heavenly Temple Aura that had flowed into his body, so he was curious to know if Chu Feng could sense it.","Chu Feng could indeed vaguely detect it. It was hidden very deeply in his dantian, such that he wouldn’t have noticed it if he hadn’t known about it.","“All right, you have obtained what you wanted. It’s time for you to leave,” the light entity elder said before waving his sleeves.","Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu disappeared into thin air.","Chu Feng was taken aback as he was not sent away. Only he and the light entity elder were left in this space.","“Elder, is there something you’d like to tell me?” Chu Feng asked.","“The other three have already found their paths after returning from the Immemorial Land of Dao Creation, but you’re still at a loss, right?” the light entity elder asked.","“That’s right.” Chu Feng nodded.","He, Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, and Xianhai Shaoyu had been recognized by the Immemorial Land of Dao Creation. The latter three had already received benefits for that; he was the only one who hadn’t gotten anything out of it.","The Dao Creation Palace inside his body did offer him guidance, but it only pointed to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy. He had tried returning to the Ancestral Martial Galaxy, but he didn’t find anything there.","Right now, the Dao Creation Palace still stood imposingly inside Chu Feng’s dantian, but it felt more like a decorative piece.","“The three of them constructed Dao Creation Pavilions, whereas yours is a Dao Creation Palace. It would be peculiar if your trial is not harder than theirs. No more than ten people have constructed Dao Creation Pavilions in the Ancient Era, but none has succeeded in constructing a Dao Creation Palace.”","“Oh? Is your Dao Creation Palace one-of-a-kind?” Eggy’s eyes lit up in excitement.","It might be useless right now, but it might prove to be an invaluable asset in the future.","“Elder, are you worried that I’ll give up on it?” Chu Feng asked.","“What I want to say is that it’s not that I don’t want to help the Long siblings outside, but this place has its rules. Those two do not reach the qualification required to undergo the trial. The most I can do is to exempt your friends from the trial on your account.”","The light entity elder’s words were very clear. Under normal circumstances, only Chu Feng could be exempted from the trial. The light entity elder extended that benefit to Little Fishy and the others on his account.","“Thank you, elder. May I have the honor of knowing your name?” Chu Feng asked.","“You need not remember me; I am merely a guard here. You should be focusing your efforts on the woman outside instead,” the light entity elder replied with a smile.","He was naturally referring to Long Zhuoyan, the red-haired woman outside.","“Elder, it sounds like you know that big sister of mine,” Chu Feng remarked.","The light entity elder smiled.","A ray of light enveloped Chu Feng and transported him out of the hall to the remnant’s entrance. Wang Qiang, Little Fishy, and the others were already waiting for him at the entrance.","The remnant’s stone doors had closed shut. Chu Feng could tell that it would be impossible for them to open them.","“Brother, did t-t-that guy tell you something?” Wang Qiang asked.","“He said some encouraging words to me,” Chu Feng replied.","Dark clouds suddenly covered the sky, and a violent storm brewed. Two eerie, red suns rose in the far distance. For some reason, not even the dark clouds could block their blinding light.","As the two suns rose into the sky, a terrifying aura enveloped the surroundings.","“This is bad!”","Little Fishy and the others frowned. Long Chengyu and Long Muxi’s faces paled.","They could tell that the two suns were eyes. An absurdly huge entity was staring at them from the distance, and the aura it emanated pushed them into the pits of despair.","Unlike the others, Chu Feng remained calm. He was able to see further with his sharp eyes, allowing him to discern the monstrous beast’s full form.","The monstrous beat was larger than most realms, but this realm was so huge that the monstrous beast could reside in it. It also had a unique appearance—it had a long body resembling a snake, but it had four legs. It also had short horns on its head reminiscent of a dragon.","It was an exceptionally powerful flood dragon.","Chu Feng and the others were completely outclassed here. This was an entity that they didn’t stand a chance against.","The only reason Chu Feng didn’t panic was due to the red-haired woman. He was observing her on top of the flood dragon, and she remained perfectly composed despite the monstrous beast.","Boom!","An explosion broke out, and a massive cloud of dust gushed in and enveloped the land.","The flood dragon unleashed an attack, but it was blocked by another force.","It was the red-haired woman.","Seeing that someone had blocked its attack, the flood dragon halted his attack and instead turned tail to flee. At the same time, its figure slowly became increasingly transparent until it disappeared into thin air.","Gwah!","A pained cry echoed.","The vanished flood dragon reappeared. It was thrashing around with all its might, causing the realm to quake as if it was the end of the world.","“What’s going on?” Long Chengyu and the others were flabbergasted.","“It’s big sister?” Little Fishy exclaimed in astonishment.","Chu Feng realized that he was still underestimating Little Fishy. The latter was able to see what he was seeing.","The red-haired woman had instantly flitted up to the flood dragon and grabbed it, hindering the latter’s escape."]},{"number":6292,"title":"Chapter 6292: Chapter 6290: Immemorial Concealment Flood Dragon vs. True Dragon","paragraphs":["Chapter 6290: Immemorial Concealment Flood Dragon vs. True Dragon","The red-haired woman held a seemingly endless shackle that was coiled around the flood dragon, holding it in place and rendering its struggles futile.","The flood dragon had long noticed the red-haired woman, but it initially didn’t see her as a threat. It was only when the red-haired woman casually blocked its attack that it realized she was more dangerous than it had thought.","That was why its humongous sun-like eyes reflected not ferocity but a pleading gaze.","“May I know who you are? Why are you making a move against me when there’s no grudge between us?” the flood dragon asked.","Its powerful voice shook the world. Even Chu Feng and the others, despite standing a far distance away, felt their eardrums on the verge of being popped.","And that was the flood dragon lowering its tone as a sign of submission.","“No grudge between us? You tried to capture those juniors; among them are my little brother and little sister. Yet, you’re feigning innocence now?” the red-haired woman questioned.","“Milord, the ignorant should not be held guilty, and your little brother and little sister have not been harmed. I’ll compensate you with treasures, so please have mercy on me.”","One of the flood dragon’s scales opened up, and several Cosmos Sacks harnessing the Ancient Era’s aura flew out.","These Cosmos Sacks fell into the red-haired woman’s hands, and she didn’t hesitate to stow them away. This brought a glimmer of hope to the flood dragon’s eyes.","It thought that her acceptance signalled room for reconciliation. The treasures in its Cosmos Sacks were overflowing with sincerity, after all.","But what the red-haired woman said next quelled its hope.","“Immemorial Concealment Flood Dragon. That’s a lineage descending from the Immemorial Era. It boasts the strongest flood dragon bloodline, but the race is fixated on metamorphosizing into dragons.","“There are rumors that a Concealment Flood Dragon in the Immemorial era metamorphosized into a dragon and rose above the true dragons, forcing true dragons to bow in submission to it. That was often thought to be the reason true dragons often capture Immemorial Concealment Flood Dragons before they metamorphosize lest another threat is born.","“However, there’s another rumor that the flesh, blood, and soul of Immemorial Concealment Flood Dragons are incredible tonics for true dragons when they are morphed as flood dragons, prompting the true dragons to capture and rear Immemorial Concealment Flood Dragons as livestock.","“However, the Immemorial Concealment Flood Dragons are named after their ability to conceal themselves thoroughly. Even true dragons can’t find them until they reveal themselves, making it hard for them to capture a Concealment Flood Dragon.","“There was a Concealment Flood Dragon in the Ancient Era who was a step from metamorphosizing into a true dragon, but it was lacking an impetus. It searched far and wide but to no avail. Later, it learned about an alternative way to enter the Heavenly Sacred Temple, a place filled with countless fortuitous encounters. This led it to turn its focus toward acquiring Heavenly Temple Aura.","“Unfortunately, it couldn’t earn the recognition of the Heavenly Sacred Temple, so it turned to plundering the Heavenly Temple Aura from others. It camped outside remnants that bestowed the Heavenly Temple Aura and waited for successful challengers to emerge, so that it could claim the Heavenly Temple Aura for itself,” the red-haired woman looked at the flood dragon as she spoke.","The flood dragon looked horrified. It roared in anger, “Who are you?!”","“I came here not for the Heavenly Temple Aura but for you. The rumors are true; the Immemorial Concealment Flood Dragons are rich tonic for true dragons. I am in a weakened state, so I’ll be devouring your blood, flesh, and soul today to hasten my recovery,” the red-haired woman calmly explained.","There was a tinge of excitement in her voice.","“You are a true dragon!!!” the flood dragon roared.","Aside from the palace related to the Heavenly Sacred Temple, the boundless mountain range split apart, causing everything to collapse inward. Everything turned dark.","Only the palace floated amid the void, unfazed by everything.","“Strong!”","Chu Feng and the others were shocked.","Similar to how metals had different durabilities, spaces could have different degrees of resilience too. The stronger a realm, the more stable its space was. This realm’s space, be it a formation or a natural one, was not one that ordinary people could faze.","But the flood dragon easily shattered the realm’s space with a roar. On top of that, the space showed no signs of mending, possibly because it couldn’t be mended. That was how terrifyingly powerful it was.","Yet, the palace was still unfazed against such a powerful roar.","If not for the barrier the red-haired woman had constructed around them, the earlier roar would have reduced Chu Feng and the others to ashes before they could register what was happening.","Chu Feng and the others looked at the flood dragon with grim eyes.","“Can big sister win?”","Little Fishy grabbed Chu Feng’s sleeves with uncertain eyes.","The flood dragon exploded its scales, shattering the red shackles binding it. Its body grew larger, and its aura intensified to a completely different level. It felt like it could devour even an entire starfield if it wanted to.","It was incomparably powerful, to the point where it plunged Chu Feng and the others into despair.","They would be doomed if the red-haired woman couldn’t defeat this monster.","Shoosh shoosh shoosh!","With a shake of its body, the flood dragon unleashed countless scales that encircled the red-haired woman. The humongous scales stacked up like a mini realm in the sky. Each scale wielded the power to destroy a realm; the destructive potential of so many stacked scales was unimaginable.","“It’s not without a reason that I survived the heyday of the True Dragon Clan,” the flood dragon sneered with anger seething in its voice. It harbored great enmity for the True Dragon Clan.","But soon, it suddenly widened its eyes in fear.","A brilliant red light swiftly shone through the cracks of the stacked scales like a leaking dam and enveloped the stacked scales.","Despite the barrier, Chu Feng and the others could feel the intense heat.","Flames were spreading swiftly, devouring the scales at an unimaginable speed. In the blink of an eye, they had grown to a scale even greater than the flood dragon itself.","The flood dragon turned tail to run, but the flames were proliferating faster than it could escape. Eventually, the humongous flood dragon looked no more than an insignificant mudskipper in the face of the flames.","Even the nearby realms looked no more than the flames’ sparks.","“I know what you’re capable of, but I don’t think you know what I can do.”","A humongous fire dragon emerged from the raging flames. It was so huge that even Chu Feng couldn’t see its full form. It towered in the darkness like a winding celestial river of fire, looking down on everything.","The flood dragon looked no more than a speck of dust in its presence."]},{"number":6293,"title":"Chapter 6293: Chapter 6291: Big Sister is a Demoness","paragraphs":["Chapter 6291: Big Sister is a Demoness","The red-haired woman’s words signaled the end of the battle.","The shattered space returned to normal, and the palace remained on top of a boundless mountain range. The flames that covered one’s entire line of sight vanished. If not for the heat lingering in the air, one would have to doubt whether what had just happened was real.","Chu Feng and the others, despite being the most outstanding juniors in the present era, were dazed by everything they had just witnessed.","“Was that a-a-all real?” Wang Qiang asked.","“Of course it is,” Chu Feng replied.","“I’m asking if o-o-our big sister is truly that powerful,” Wang Qiang asked.","“You still dare to call her that? Aren’t you afraid that big sister might roast you alive?” Little Fishy asked.","“Oops, I-I-I’ll change!” Wang Qiang clasped his mouth. “I envy t-t-the two of you! How did you find such a huge t-t-thigh to clutch onto? That’s probably the biggest thigh in t-t-this world!”","“I don’t know if it’s the biggest one, but it’s definitely something for sure. That’s a true dragon from the legends!” Xianhai Shaoyu exclaimed.","While Chu Feng and the others were chatting away, Long Chengyu and Long Muxi struggled to return to their senses. True dragons had been inviolable existences to them for the longest time, and the true dragon they had just witnessed was the one they had worshiped as their ancestral dragon.","But in truth, it was not their ancestor. Their ancestors had merely borrowed her flesh and blood to attain power.","They were sinners.","She could have destroyed their clan in a heartbeat, but fortunately, Chu Feng intervened and saved their lives.","Wang Qiang secretly asked Chu Feng, “Brother, it looks like they k-k-know that we have obtained the Heavenly Temple Aura. If your b-b-big sister covets the Heavenly Temple Aura too, we’ll be doomed.”","That was also what Chu Feng was worried about.","But there was nothing they could do about it. They didn’t stand a sliver of hope against the red-haired woman in a fight. Thus, Chu Feng could only say, “It’s up to fate.”","A gentle force lifted Chu Feng above the clouds, where he found himself face to face with the red-haired woman. She had sealed off the surroundings, such that Wang Qiang and the others couldn’t see what was happening on their side.","She lifted her disguise, revealing her beautiful, dreamy face. She felt more like a succubus despite being a true dragon.","“As expected of my little brother. You should have obtained the Heavenly Temple Aura, right?” the red-haired woman asked.","She was in a visibly good mood as she smiled at Chu Feng, but the latter dared not lower his guard. He couldn’t tell if she wasn’t certain that they had obtained the Heavenly Temple Aura or that she wanted to see if Chu Feng would lie to her.","“We obtained it.” Chu Feng decided to go with the truth.","“Amazing.” The red-haired woman patted Chu Feng’s head as if coaxing a child. “I was able to capture this Immemorial Concealment Flood Dragon thanks to you. I’ll fulfill one of your wishes in return, so tell me what you want. There’s no need to hold back. I’ll satisfy you as long as it’s within my means, including...”","She pulled down her robe, revealing her fair shoulders... and she didn’t just stop there. Her robe continued flowing down her arm, revealing more and more skin.","“We can’t, big sister. We’re siblings!” Chu Feng hurriedly pulled the red-haired woman’s clothes back up.","“What are you doing? I want to apply medicine on my wounds.”","The red-haired woman initially looked at Chu Feng in confusion, but she quickly understood his misunderstanding upon noticing his reddened face.","“My good little brother, did you think that I, your big sister, covet your body?”","The red-haired woman revealed a mischievous smile as she leaned closer to Chu Feng.","“You look decent now that I’m looking close up. If that’s what you want...”","Her mellow words and alluring face made Chu Feng’s heartbeat hasten. She burst into hearty laughter.","“Little brother, I’m teasing you. I don’t easily offer myself to anyone. Come, help me apply this medicine,” the red-haired woman said.","She passed an ointment to Chu Feng. This ointment had the texture of a silk handkerchief, and it emanated a faint floral fragrance.","She turned around, revealing a purple palm strike on her fair, smooth back. It was a heavy blow that caused even her soul to seep out. This injury had been around for a long time now.","“Are you done looking? Hurry up and apply it,” the red-haired woman urged.","“All right.” Chu Feng quickly applied the ointment.","The red-haired woman quickly tidied up her clothes. She was surprisingly demure despite her indecorous attitude.","“Who wounded you, big sister?” Chu Feng asked.","“Why? Are you going to avenge me?” the red-haired woman asked.","“I’ll subdue him on your behalf once I become strong enough.”","“I’ll remember those words, but I don’t remember who wounded me. Let’s talk about it after I remember what happened.”","“You forgot about it?” Chu Feng was astonished.","“I have forgotten a lot of things. Something terrible must have happened to old folks like us who survived the Ancient Era.”","Chu Feng was fawning on her to gather information about the Ancient Era. Thus far, everyone he had spoken to had no idea what happened at the end of the Ancient Era. He didn’t expect this trail to end like that.","“But I still remember my name. Do you want to know what it is?” the red-haired woman asked with a smile.","“I do.” Chu Feng nodded.","“Long Zhuoyan.”","Indeed, she’s the Dragon Clan’s demoness that the Divine Deer mentioned.","“But keep it to yourself. Don’t mention me to anyone else. I have quite a few enemies out there,” Long Zhuoyan smiled.","“I understand, but it’s a pity that I can’t mention it. It’s such a pleasant name.” Chu Feng shook his head in lamentation.","“Is it?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","“It’s one of the nicest names I have heard. It is as intoxicating as your beauty,” Chu Feng replied.","“Cut the bootlicking; I don’t buy into that.” Long Zhuoyan was smiling radiantly despite her words. “So, do you have any wish? I won’t be making this offer twice. I’m not that generous. You should quickly tell me what you want while I’m in a good mood.”","“Big sister, I do have a wish. I wish to visit the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to save my mother,” Chu Feng said.","“I have heard about the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. There seems to be some kind of mysterious power there, right?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","“Yes, that place is protected by powerful formations,” Chu Feng replied.","“To be honest, the earlier battle might have appeared one-sided, but I had to expend almost the entirety of my energy to ensure nothing went wrong. I have only just regained my freedom after being wounded by that bastard, so my cultivation is still far from my peak.","“I might have subdued the Immemorial Concealment Flood Dragon, but that old thing is a sly one. He placed a seal on his bloodline. It’ll take me some time to decipher it.”","The light in Chu Feng’s eyes was slowly going out.","“But I’ll accept your wish. I am a world spiritist, after all. Let me see what the greatest world spiritist power in this era is capable of. They must think that my little brother has no backing to dare bully you!” Long Zhuoyan sneered.","Chu Feng suddenly found her more beautiful than ever."]},{"number":6294,"title":"Chapter 6294: Chapter 6292: The Sacred Mansion’s Ancestral Token","paragraphs":["Chapter 6292: The Sacred Mansion’s Ancestral Token","Having made up her mind, Long Zhuoyan took Chu Feng and the others onto her cloud and dashed for the sky. Upon reaching the highest point, she thrust her palm forth to smash open the formation.","Beyond the formation was not outer space. Rather, they found themselves in another realm.","This made Chu Feng realize that he had indeed been in a formation realm, and it was located in one of the Seven Realms Galaxy’s Upper Realms.","Chu Feng told Wang Qiang and the others that he was going to confront the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, and they expressed that they wanted to tag along. However, Long Zhuoyan refused to take them along.","This left Wang Qiang and the others with no choice but to return to the Totem Galaxy first.","With a wave of her hand, Long Zhuoyan placed them on a cloud that moved at an astonishing speed upon entering the teleportation formation.","Following that, Long Zhuoyan and Chu Feng got onto a similar cloud and entered the teleportation formation too. While its traveling speed was not on par with the Nine Heavens Secret Domain’s teleportation formation, it was still an incredible feat.","...","Meanwhile, Jie Tianran was traveling through a beautiful hidden realm in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion with a grim expression.","This hidden realm was the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s forbidden land. By right, he should have been the only one with the authority to access it.","Yet, he just received a summon notice from this hidden realm.","Soon, a floating palace appeared on the clouds ahead.","He pushed the doors open and found himself faced with seven familiar silhouettes. Five were the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Saint-tier elders and one was Ling Sheng’er’s grandfather, the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief.","“Lord Mansion Master.”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief and the Saint-tier elders bowed to Jie Tianran, but they looked a little uptight, for there was someone else in this palace aside from them—Jie Shanxian.","Jie Shanxian was from the same era as Jie Tianran’s master, the World Spiritist Immortal King.","“Lord Shanxian? How are you...”","Jie Tianran was taken aback, but it also explained why the other party dared to set foot in this forbidden land. Jie Shanxian was indeed qualified.","“Are you trying to ask why am I still alive?” Jie Shanxian asked.","“That’s not what I mean. Lord Shanxian, you have been away for so long, and we don’t have your life token in our mansion, so we don’t know how you have been faring. I thought you might have entered the Ninth Galaxy like my master. Since you are here, it would mean that you have been in the world of cultivation all along. May I know where you have been all this while?”","Jie Tianran took a humble tone, but his expression spoke otherwise.","“I don’t need to report my whereabouts to you, do I?” Jie Shanxian asked.","Jie Tianran fell silent.","Jie Shanxian’s tone made it clear that she wasn’t here to catch up with him, and the chances were that she had gathered the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s upper echelons here today to question them.","Thus, Jie Tianran smiled. “There’s no need for you to report your whereabouts to me, but I can’t help but notice that I’m not the first to learn about your return despite being the mansion master. May I know if there’s a reason behind your abrupt return?”","“Yes, I do have business here.” Jie Shanxian got straight to the point. “It’s about your daughter, Jie Ranqing.”","“About Ranqing?” Jie Tianran chuckled. He could already fathom a guess as to what was going on, but he asked anyway, “May I know what this is about?”","“I shall get to the point. I have gotten a grasp about the circumstances surrounding your daughter, so I’d like to ask why did you imprison a junior as outstanding as Jie Ranqing and plunder her bloodline? Also, why are you so opposed to Chu Feng? You have to give me a good explanation for these matters,” Jie Shanxian said as she took out a seven-colored token.","The token’s appearance caused the palace to shake and the natural energies outside to swirl, but what was more terrifying than the power it harnessed were the words on it.","Inscribed on the token’s front was ‘Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’ and on its back ‘Ancestor’.","Only two people in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion were known to be in possession of the Sacred Mansion Ancestor Token. One was the World Spiritist Immortal King, and the other was Jie Shanxian.","It symbolized authority superseding the Mansion Master.","“Jie Ranqing is my daughter; this is my family’s internal affair. Lord Shanxian, are you intervening in my family affair too?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Oh? I’m surprised you know she’s your daughter too. Even a vicious tiger doesn’t prey on his cubs. Jie Tianran, how can you do this to your own daughter? Even if she isn’t your daughter, her talent is outstanding enough for the mansion to nurture her.","“Also, why do you have to intervene in her marriage? I have never heard of our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion having a tradition where our bloodline must not be leaked outward. Our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion is made up of world spiritists from all over the world of cultivation. Our foundation is built on our flexibility in taking in talents!","“Other than that, why are you after Chu Feng’s life? There’s no grudge between you two, and he’s your grandson! You should be trying to bring him to our side instead of going after his life! Jie Tianran, you better give me a good reason here today, or else I won’t let things slip!”","Jie Shanxian was practically shouting in the latter half of her statements. That was how infuriated she was.","“I’m doing this for our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s future. Ranqing is indeed talented, but that’s also the result of my meticulous nurturing. She used to be obedient, but that bastard Chu Xuanyuan appeared out of nowhere to ruin her.","“Chu Feng is talented, but if only Ranqing married another formidable world spiritist instead of that Chu Xuanyuan, their offspring would have been far more talented. They are the ones who ruined Ranqing, as well as my unparalleled grandson! Chu Feng’s talent doesn’t belong to him but our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion, so I’m going to take his bloodline back,” Jie Tianran spoke with an exceedingly calm voice, not displaying any anger whatsoever.","But his words angered Jie Shanxian. “Are you out of your mind?! Those are not words a human should speak! I can’t understand how someone like you became the Mansion Master!”","“I don’t need your understanding. All that matters is that I know that I’m doing this for the Sacred Mansion,” Jie Tianran said.","“Jie Tianran, I shan’t argue with you. I order you to release Jie Ranqing right now and return her plundered bloodline to her. Otherwise...”","“Otherwise what?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Otherwise I’ll be exercising the Sacred Mansion Ancestor Token’s supervision authority. The ancestors have the right to punish the Mansion Master if he fails to maintain fairness.”","Jie Shanxian raised her Sacred Mansion Ancestor Token. The token swiftly released a seven-colored aura that passed through the palace walls and seeped into the realm. The world shook as if a formidable power was about to break free.","Seconds later, Jie Shanxian’s face darkened.","Her token was still releasing the seven-colored aura, but it was no longer communing with the formidable power that threatened to break free. The palace stopped shaking, and the natural energies outside fell still.","Shocked, she turned to Jie Tianran. The latter’s impassive expression said it all.","“You... You dare to dispel the authority of the Ancestor Token?!”"]},{"number":6295,"title":"Chapter 6295: Chapter 6293: Unfathomable","paragraphs":["Chapter 6293: Unfathomable","It was not just Jie Shanxian who was astonished; the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief and the others were astounded as well. Dispelling the authority of the Ancestor Token was the same as open defiance against the ancestors. It was an act of gross disrespect.","Such a feat shouldn’t have been possible in the first place, but Jie Tianran pulled it off.","“Now that I’m the Mansion Master, I won’t allow anyone else to intervene in the Sacred Mansion’s affairs,” Jie Tianran revealed his reason for dispelling the Ancestor Token’s authority. “Lord Shanxian, you have already chosen to leave, so why return now? Your return shows that you still identify as a member of the Sacred Mansion. If so, you shouldn’t defy me and side with an outsider. Are you planning to betray the Sacred Mansion?”","“Betray the Sacred Mansion? What a slander! Not only have you failed to act impartially as the Mansion Master, but you have also turned your back on your ancestors’ teaching by dispelling the authority of the Ancestor Token. You claim to be doing it for the Sacred Mansion, but all I see is selfishness. You are a tumor to the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion!” Jie Shanxian spat.","“Cursing the Mansion Master. That’s another line to your list of crimes,” Jie Tianran calmly replied.","“Jie Tianran, do you think I am helpless against you just because you dispelled the Ancestor Token’s authority? It’s not just based on seniority that I, Jie Shanxian, acquired the Ancestor Token. Even without the Ancestor Token, I’ll purge the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion of this tumor!”","Jie Shanxian stowed away her Ancestor Token and unleashed her spirit power, causing her robe to flutter.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief and the others were astonished. Her aura was far superior to theirs. She was a rank three Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist!","That was her original spirit power, and she had made a full recovery now. Factoring in her heaven-defying battle power, her fighting prowess was comparable to a rank four Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.","Yet, Jie Tianran showed not the slightest unease in the face of her power. He said, “Not only did you side with an outsider and curse me, but you’re even planning to attack me now. Your crimes warrant the death penalty.”","Knowing words were futile, Jie Shanxian formed a hand seal. Her spirit power morphed into massive dragons that lunged at Jie Tianran.","Jie Tianran smirked.","...","Boom!","The palace shook. Powerful shockwaves could be felt outside, but this commotion didn’t last long before the shaking stopped.","Color spirit power suffused the palace, but the clash had already ended.","Jie Tianran was unharmed, whereas Jie Shanxian collapsed on the floor, covered in blood.","Weapons and treasures emanating the Ancient Era’s aura were scattered around her. They were covered in a defensive layer of spirit power, but the spirit power was from Jie Tianran instead of her even though these were her possessions!","Jie Tianran walked up to Jie Shanxian and stomped on her thigh, crushing it.","But Jie Shanxian didn’t wail in pain. Her eyes were filled with anger and despair.","Her anger was because she couldn’t defeat the man before her. Her despair was because she knew it was only a matter of time before the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion crumbled under his leadership.","“Jie Shanxian, I’ll spare your life in view of the contributions you have made to the Sacred Mansion, but I cannot overlook your betrayal of the Sacred Mansion. As much as I wish to turn a blind eye to your deeds, I have to be impartial as the Mansion Master. Don’t blame me for this.”","A blood-red formation emerged from Jie Tianran’s palm. This formation appeared to be a living being as it had a ravenous mouth!","“Lord Mansion Master!” the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief and the Saint-tier elders exclaimed in astonishment.","“Are you going to speak up on her behalf?” Jie Tianran shot them a cold glance.","The Saint-tier elders hurriedly lowered their heads out of fright.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief hesitated, but he still spoke up with a quivering voice in the end, “Lord Mansion Master, Lord Shanxian is our senior, and she’s on close terms with Lord World Spiritist Immortal King. Now that we are facing a threat from the Ancient Era’s races, we need to be united more than ever. Lord Shanxian’s strength is indubitably a huge asset...”","His words trailed off at this point.","As the Ling Clan’s Clan Chief, he ruled the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s Ling Clan. His standing was above that of the Saint-tier elders, making him second to only the Mansion Master. He was someone who had weathered storms before.","But faced with Jie Tianran’s increasingly frigid gaze, he lost the courage to speak up for his senior. In the end, he lowered his head like the other Saint-tier elders before he could finish his piece.","Seeing that there was no more opposition, Jie Tianran pressed his formation against Jie Shanxian’s abdomen.","“GAHHHHH!”","Jie Shanxian’s face distorted. Her expression didn’t flicker when her leg was crushed, but the pain she was suffering now was so excruciating that she gritted her teeth and hissed. Sweat rained down her face. Eventually, her screams became hoarse.","A powerful energy was flowing from her body into Jie Tianran’s body.","In the end, there was a spatial distortion, and even her body was dragged into Jie Tianran’s palm formation too.","“It’s a waste to leave these treasures with you.”","Jie Tianran stood up. With a wave of his sleeves, he stowed the weapons and treasures scattered over the floor into his Cosmos Sack.","“Did you all know about Jie Shanxian’s return?” Jie Tianran asked.","“Lord Mansion Master, we only learned about it ourselves. Lord Shan... No, Jie Shanxian summoned us to question us about Jie Ranqing and Chu Feng’s affairs, so we told her what we knew. This is information that outsiders can easily acquire too. I swear that we didn’t exaggerate the story to paint you in a bad light!”","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief and the Saint-tier elders were extremely nervous. Even Jie Shanxian, whose fighting prowess was comparable to a rank four Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist, was no match for Jie Tianran.","This showed just how unfathomable their Mansion Master was.","“There’s no need to be so nervous. I’m merely asking a question. You’re core members of our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. I trust you. You may go now,” Jie Tianran said.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief and the others bowed to Jie Tianran before taking their leave.","Just as they were about to walk out, Jie Tianran suddenly added, “Don’t tell anyone about Jie Shanxian for the time being.”","“Rest assured, Lord Mansion Master. Our lips are sealed!” they promised.","“Go.” Jie Tianran waved his hand.","The Ling Clan’s Clan Chief and the Saint-tier elders felt their legs wobble as they left the palace. They didn’t expect Jie Tianran to be so brazen as to do this to a venerated elder of Jie Shanxian’s stature.","It was fortunate that Jie Tianran didn’t punish them for this.","After they left, Jie Tianran departed from the palace and headed deeper into the hidden realm, making his way to a place that even Jie Shanxian couldn’t reach."]},{"number":6296,"title":"Chapter 6296: Chapter 6294: Devourer Emperor","paragraphs":["Chapter 6294: Devourer Emperor","The hidden realm looked and felt perfectly ordinary.","But when Jie Tianran created a spatial rift with a wave of his sleeves, it revealed a different scenery on the other side. The terrain on the other side of the rift was still the same, but the sky was blood-red.","The difference was due to the ten-thousand-meter-tall formation that enveloped the earth. Its blood-red color was what caused the sky to appear blood-red as well.","The formation was translucent. A person could be seen sitting at the center of the formation.","Jie Tian.","The formation pulsated rhythmically like a heart. Each pulsation would cause energy in the formation to gush into Jie Tian’s body.","Jie Tianran spent a while looking at Jie Tian before the corners of his lips crept upward. He was satisfied with Jie Tian’s performance. He walked up to the formation core and opened his palm, revealing the eerie formation from before.","A surge of energy flowed from the eerie formation into the formation core.","This energy was bloodline power, but it was not just Jie Shanxian’s. There were two more powerful bloodline powers in it too.","The infusion of these three bloodline powers caused the formation to pulsate with greater frequency.","The three bloodline powers exploded inside the formation and suffused it. They initially clashed with one another, refusing to fuse while attempting to break out of the formation. However, they soon realized it was impossible to escape the formation. They could only follow the formation’s flow of energy and converge at Jie Tian.","Somehow, Jie Tian felt no discomfort whatsoever. As he assimilated these three individual bloodline powers, a phenomenon began to form in the sky.","Something black yet glowing was gathering in the sky. It was massive and dark, and it felt like it could devour everything. Its sudden appearance amid the blood-red sky was terrifying.","The phenomenon lasted till Jie Tian fully assimilated the three bloodline powers.","As Jie Tian absorbed the remaining energy in the formation, the formation slowly lost its blood-red color and turned transparent. In the end, the formation dissipated, and the sky reverted to normal.","Jie Tian opened his eyes.","His aura flowed out—he was a rank six True Dragon World Spiritist, but his fighting prowess was already comparable to a rank nine True Dragon World Spiritist!","Jie Tian was overjoyed. He hadn’t expected to make such a huge advancement within such a short time.","He was now the strongest junior in the world of cultivation, and it was by a huge margin by that. His face reflected his wild ambition. He was going to cleanse the defeats and humiliation he had suffered!","If the prophecy was true, God’s Era’s power would be his as well!","He would become the ruler of this era!","But before he could make any grand statements, he noticed Jie Tianran and hurriedly reined himself in. “Grandfather, you’re back.”","He quickly kneeled before Jie Tianran with a beaming smile. In this world, there was no one he felt closer to than his grandfather. He knew that his grandfather was the reason he could make such a huge advancement this time.","The latter had devoted all the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s resources to him.","His grandfather was the reason he could undergo this metamorphosis.","“How are you feeling?” Jie Tianran asked with a smile.","“I feel great, but I know it’s all thanks to you, grandfather. I felt powerful energy flowing into my body earlier. Grandfather, you must have brought something back for me. Is it something from God’s Era? Have you obtained God’s Era’s power?” Jie Tian asked.","“I have reaped huge rewards from God’s Era, but it’ll take more time to obtain its power. However, you need not worry. That power will be ours. The earlier surge of energy isn’t from God’s Era. You can consider it a bestowment from heaven.”","Jie Tianran walked up and pulled Jie Tian to his feet. He looked at the latter with doting eyes.","“Where did you obtain it from?” Jie Tian asked out of curiosity.","Jie Tianran had tossed all the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s best resources into the formation before entering God’s Era. Whatever the sudden surge of energy was, it must have been obtained afterward.","Instead of revealing the truth, he said with an enigmatic smile, “Tian’er, it’s time to tell you the truth. You... are not born with the Ruler’s Bloodline.”","“What?!” Jie Tian was horrified. “Grandfather, you must be teasing me, right? How could I not be born with the Ruler’s Bloodline?”","Jie Tian panicked.","From a young age, his grandfather had told him that he possessed the most powerful Ruler’s Bloodline in this world.","“Your body has the unique traits of the Ruler’s Bloodline. Back then, we found a treasure in an ancient remnant that imitates the Ruler’s Bloodline. I fused that treasure into your body right as you were born. However, you were only able to impeccably fuse with the treasure because you possess a unique bloodline too. Your bloodline is the legendary Devourer Bloodline,” Jie Tianran said.","“Devourer Bloodline?” Jie Tian’s eyes flickered.","“You can devour world spiritist bloodlines to strengthen your bloodline power. Your potential doesn’t pale in comparison to the Ruler’s Bloodline. You made a huge advancement because I fused three decent bloodline powers into the formation.","“They are highly talented individuals with decent bloodlines, just that they have reached a bottleneck. With their bloodlines and talents, they could have made a name for themselves in the Ninth Galaxy,” Jie Tianran said.","“Grandfather, is my bloodline truly on par with the Ruler’s Bloodline?”","Jie Tian couldn’t care less whose bloodline he had just assimilated. He was only concerned about how strong his bloodline was compared to Chu Feng’s Ruler’s Bloodline. He couldn’t accept his bloodline being weaker than Chu Feng’s.","“Of course. You have already displayed tremendous prowess just by absorbing an imitation of the Ruler’s Bloodline. If you devour Chu Feng’s bloodline too, you’ll obtain a power comparable to the Ruler’s Bloodline. If you continue walking down this path, it’s only a matter of time before you reach a level that no one has ever reached.”","That greatly consoled Jie Tian, though he still struggled to come to terms with this matter. He had always thought that he possessed the strongest Ruler’s Bloodline, after all.","Noticing Jie Tian’s worries, Jie Tianran opened his palm to reveal a black scepter.","This black scepter looked imposing. It was overflowing with the Ancient Era’s aura. Anyone could tell at a glance that it was an extraordinary treasure.","“There was a person in the Ancient Era who was born with the Devourer Bloodline, and he became one of the strongest world spiritists in his era. The world came to address him as the Devourer Emperor,” Jie Tianran said."]},{"number":6297,"title":"Chapter 6297: Chapter 6295: Prove It To Me","paragraphs":["Chapter 6295: Prove It To Me","“Devourer Emperor?” Jie Tian widened his eyes.","It was his first time hearing about the Devourer Emperor, but the latter sounded like a formidable figure.","“The Devourer Emperor is extremely powerful, but he was not well-known in the Ancient Era because of his ambitions. The world recognized the strongest world spiritist in the Ancient Era to be the World Spiritist Emperor. To surpass the World Spiritist Emperor, the Devourer Emperor searched the world for treasures that could make him stronger.","“In the end, the Devourer Emperor forged two treasures that allowed him to undergo a metamorphosis. One is the imitation Ruler’s Bloodline, which has already been fused into your body. The other is this Devourer Scepter, a treasure created for devouring bloodlines.","“Perhaps due to overexertion or some other reason, the Devourer Emperor died shortly after forging these two treasures. This ended up benefiting you. The imitation Ruler’s Bloodline was fused into your body from the moment you were born, and I have been gradually nurturing your ability to devour bloodlines over the years.","“Your starting point is far higher than the Devourer Bloodline, not to mention you have the Devourer Scepter forged specifically for devouring bloodlines. Your spirit power was previously too weak to withstand the backlash of using the Devourer Scepter, but you should be able to use it now that you have partially awakened your Devourer Bloodline and your fighting prowess is comparable to a rank nine True Dragon World Spiritist,” Jie Tianran said.","“This scepter is powerful! No True Dragon World Spiritist will be a match for me if I channel its powers!” Jie Tian exclaimed.","“Only True Dragon?” Jie Tianran chuckled. “Even when channeling the Devourer Scepter as a pinnacle True Dragon World Spiritist, you can obtain strength above that of an early Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist.”","Jie Tian’s eyes widened in shock. I will be stronger than even an early Heavenly Dragon World Spiritist? That practically makes me unrivaled in the world of cultivation!","“According to the Devourer Emperor’s records, you can only barely channel the Devourer Scepter with your current strength, and you will suffer a huge backlash as a result. You should only use it as a final resort,” Jie Tianran said before handing the Devourer Scepter over.","Jie Tian gleefully accepted the Devourer Scepter with excited eyes. “I don’t know how I can ever repay you, grandfather.”","“If you wish to repay me, achieve what the Devourer Emperor failed at and become this era’s strongest world spiritist. Help me bring the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion to the peak of the world of cultivation,” Jie Tianran said.","“I will not let you down!” Jie Tian tightly clutched the Devourer Scepter.","He was disappointed earlier that he didn’t possess the Ruler’s Bloodline, but he only felt relief now. Perhaps this Devourer Bloodline would bring him to a greater height instead.","“Tian’er, I don’t want to douse your enthusiasm, but you have to harden your heart if you have made up your mind to walk this path. Carve into your mind that the weak is nothing but fodder for you. Always weigh the pros and cons and choose the optimal choice,” Jie Tianran said.","“Rest assured, grandfather. I’ll not let you down. No one else in the world matters to me other than you,” Jie Tian said.","“Are you certain?” Jie Tianran asked.","“I swear to heaven it’s the truth.” Jie Tian raised two fingers into the air.","“What if that person is a close kin?” Jie Tianran asked.","“I will do it.” Jie Tian’s eyes were filled with determination.","“Good. I’ll let you know whose bloodlines you have just assimilated.”","Jie Tianran waved his sleeves, and an elder fell from his palm.","The elder was extremely weak, and his body was like a withered corpse. His eyes were rolled upward, and he was frothing. He was still conscious, but he was close to death.","“He is a fellow disciple of the World Spiritist Immortal King. The world knows him as Daoist Starseizer,” Jie Tianran said.","“Daoist Starseizer?” Jie Tianran was shocked.","There was no way he wouldn’t have known about Daoist Starseizer.","“He attempted to sneak into the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion in my absence to rescue Jie Ranqing, but he underestimated me. He was caught in the formation I prepared beforehand. Thus, I stripped him of his bloodline when I returned.”","Jie Tianran waved his sleeves, and Jie Shanxian fell from his palm.","Jie Shanxian’s injuries looked no worse than before, but she struggled as if she was in terrible pain.","“This is a senior from the same era as my master, Jie Shanxian. You should have heard of her.”","“Jie Shanxian?” Jie Tian’s astonishment deepened.","She was the true powerhouse compared to Daoist Starseizer, a legendary figure in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.","“Like Daoist Starseizer, she tried to rescue Jie Ranqing. She sided with Chu Feng despite being a member of our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. So, I took her bloodline too.”","Jie Tianran’s palm formation transformed, and another figure dropped out from it.","It was a woman. Her condition was no better than Daoist Starseizer’s—she was practically a withered corpse, making it difficult to discern her original appearance.","However, Jie Tian’s face morphed in shock when he saw her. He would recognize her no matter how much she changed. She was his mother, Jie Tiannian.","“M-mother?”","Jie Tian tried his best to suppress his emotions, but he was unable to conceal his shock. This was the person who gave birth to him, after all.","He knew that his mother loved him, just that Jie Tianran had taken him under his wing from a young age, leaving his mother with few chances to interact with him.","“Grandfather, w-what wrong did my mother do?” Jie Tian asked.","Even though he threatened his mother that he would tell Jie Tianran that she secretly helped Chu Feng, he didn’t do so in the end because he knew that Jie Tianran would harshly punish his mother for that.","What could his mother have done to deserve such treatment? No matter what, she was Jie Tianran’s daughter!","“Your mother went down the wrong path. She wanted to side with Chu Feng to deal with you. I planted a gu in them to command them to capture Chu Feng, but they tenaciously resisted with their might. They would rather deplete their life force than to be controlled by the gu. To think that they would display such loyalty to an outsider. Pathetic,” Jie Tianran replied.","Jie Tianran must have found out that Jie Tiannian helped Chu Feng escape.","“Tian’er, you said that you can kill anyone aside from me. Prove it to me now. Kill your mother,” Jie Tianran said."]},{"number":6298,"title":"Chapter 6298: Chapter 6296: You Are the Reason For This Sword Wound","paragraphs":["Chapter 6296: You Are the Reason For This Sword Wound","Despite feeling conflicted, Jie Tian tightly gripped the Devourer Scepter and slowly approached his mother one step at a time.","Jie Tianran stared intently at Jie Tian with deep, unreadable eyes.","As if she had sensed something, Jie Tiannian somehow mustered the strength to turn around and look at her son. Her eyes were vacuous, a huge contrast to how she was before. Her vitality had completely dried out, making her as good as a walking corpse.","Faced with his mother’s gaze, Jie Tian halted his footsteps. His lips quivered.","“Why? You can’t bear to kill her?” Jie Tianran asked.","Jie Tian’s breathing hastened. He tried his best to calm himself, but he couldn’t control his physical reactions and emotions. His eyes reflected his raging emotions—sadness, panic, and fear.","He tightly gripped the Devourer Scepter, but his flickering eyes and hastened breath made his hesitation clear. In the end, he gritted his teeth, turned to Jie Tianran, and said, “Grandfather, my mother gave birth to me. I want to know what wrong she has committed to deserve death.”","Jie Tianran replied, “Not only did she aid Chu Feng’s escape, but she also gave your cultivation resources to Chu Feng. Are those not enough reasons for you?”","“But...”","Jie Tian still wanted to say something, but Jie Tianran interjected, “All that matters when it comes to devouring bloodlines is your interests. You don’t need sentiments. You shouldn’t spare anyone who threatens your interests. Those who achieve great things are not bound by such cheap sentiments. Close kin are often the ones who are the greatest hurdles to your success, let alone those who turn their backs on you. How can I believe that you won’t let me down if you can’t even do this much? Tian’er, I have high hopes for you.”","Jie Tianran’s eyes began to flicker as if he was making a decision too.","Jie Tian understood the nature of his gaze. Thus, his flickering eyes slowly hardened as he killed his emotions one by one, leaving only determination behind.","He slowly raised the Devourer Scepter.","“Hm?” Jie Tian’s gaze suddenly narrowed.","“That bug dares to return here?” Jie Tianran was both angered and elated. He turned to Jie Tian and said, “Tian’er, this is your chance to surpass the Ruler’s Bloodline.”","With a wave of his sleeves, Jie Tianran vanished together with Jie Tian, leaving Daoist Starseizer, Jie Shanxian, and Jie Tiannian lying on the floor. Unfortunately, the three of them were incapacitated.","...","The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s forbidden land was protected by a powerful sealing formation. Even ordinary Heavenly Dragon World Spiritists would struggle to breach it.","Yet, two figures riding on a cloud were swiftly descending on the formation—Long Zhuoyan and Chu Feng.","Chu Feng looked grim and nervous.","His mother should be imprisoned here according to his intelligence, but he was afraid that his intel was wrong and his mother wasn’t here. He was also worried that his mother was here but had suffered a terrible plight.","In the end, a figure appeared in Chu Feng’s line of sight.","Countless chains extended from all directions to shackle a woman.","The woman was truly beautiful. She had an ethereal face that didn’t seem to belong to this world and an immortal-like disposition, but her face was pale and she was unconscious.","She was none other than Chu Feng’s mother, Jie Ranqing.","Chu Feng’s emotions were on the verge of running amok seeing his mother close up, but Long Zhuoyan said, “It’s a trap.”","“A trap? Big sister, can you save my mother?” Chu Feng asked.","Long Zhuoyan was unfathomably powerful.","He had once come here with Old Cat, but the latter couldn’t breach the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formation and was forced to escape. In contrast, Long Zhuoyan easily breached the formation and brought him to its most secure forbidden land.","In Chu Feng’s view, Long Zhuoyan had the power to rescue his mother.","“It’s all a trap, including your mother,” Long Zhuoyan said.","Chu Feng was confused.","“That’s a fake. Your mother isn’t here,” Long Zhuoyan clarified.","“It’s a fake?” Chu Feng was astonished, for he didn’t find anything amiss with his Heaven’s Eyes.","“Yes, it’s an extremely dangerous trap, a forbidden formation from the Immemorial Era. Did the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion obtain an Immemorial Era’s legacy?” Long Zhuoyan said.","“There’s no way to say for sure. Elder, is there anything beneath the formation?” Chu Feng asked.","“No, we are already at the deepest part of this forbidden land. Could your mother be imprisoned elsewhere?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","“That could be possible,” Chu Feng replied.","Long Zhuoyan suddenly narrowed her eyes. With a wave of her sleeves, she unleashed her spirit power outward.","A split moment later, a piercing explosion echoed.","By the time Chu Feng registered what was going on, countless thick chains had already extended from all directions to coil around Long Zhuoyan’s spirit power. The chains were so powerful that it warped her spirit power.","Long Zhuoyan clenched her jaws. She was struggling despite her overwhelming strength, and she looked to be in pain. That was how powerful the formation chains were.","Through the chains, Chu Feng saw two figures in the sky slowly approaching them. They were Jie Tianran and Jie Tian.","“Chu Feng, you have finally brought your backing here? It’s a foreign face. Someone from the Ancient Era? Hoh, to think that you would work with someone from the Ancient Era. It looks like you’re also an unscrupulous individual.”","Jie Tianran’s attention was on Long Zhuoyan, knowing that she was the greater threat here. However, his vigilance was quickly replaced with confidence as he became certain that Long Zhuoyan was not feigning it.","“Jie Tianran, where’s my mother?” Chu Feng questioned.","“How dare you question me in such a tone? Do you think I’ll let you leave? You couldn’t have escaped from the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion if not for the fact that I didn’t want to release the seal on my suppressed spirit power.”","Jie Tianran looked at Chu Feng with fire seething in his eyes. He felt humiliated just thinking about how the latter wrecked havoc in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion that day.","Worst of all, Chu Feng had utilized the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s formations against itself. That was the day he made up his mind to change all the formations left by the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s ancestors regardless of the cost.","He was determined to be in complete control of the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. Never again shall an outsider use the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s own powers to wreak havoc on its grounds.","“Chu Feng, you won’t have a third chance. I won’t let you leave this place. It’s time for you to return your Ruler’s Bloodline to its rightful owner,” Jie Tianran said.","“Where’s my mother?” Chu Feng continued asking as if he was deaf to Jie Tianran’s words.","“Hah...” Jie Tianran suddenly burst into laughter.","Looking at Chu Feng, he suddenly had an idea—an idea that could plunge Chu Feng deeper into pain","“Chu Feng, do you know what I fear the most? I don’t fear you coming after me. I’m only afraid that you would go into hiding, especially in the Ninth Galaxy. That would render me helpless against you. Fortunately, you aren’t predisposed for greater things. You are tied down by your emotions. All it took was a simple ploy for me to tie you down to the world of cultivation.”","Those words shook Chu Feng.","“I’m in a good mood today, so I’ll let you die a knowing death.”","Jie Tianran pulled up his shirt to reveal his upper body. Despite his advanced age, his body remained toned and muscular.","However, Long Zhuoyan and Chu Feng’s gazes were drawn to his left chest, where a sword wound lay. It had been there for many years, but it refused to heal.","“You are the culprit behind this sword wound.”"]},{"number":6299,"title":"Chapter 6299: Chapter 6297: An Expert Never Seen Before","paragraphs":["Chapter 6297: An Expert Never Seen Before","Anger blazed in Jie Tianran’s eyes as he spat through gritted teeth, “It’s you and that bastard father of yours. You drove my daughter, who I bore high hopes for, to attack her own father. You two ruined my everything.”","“That’s my mother’s doing?” Chu Feng asked.","He could tell that it was not that Jie Tianran didn’t want to heal that sword wound but that he was unable to do so. Whoever was behind the sword wound had to be stronger than him.","“Hahahaha!”","Jie Tianran suddenly burst into laughter, but his laughter was chilling. His boundless fury could be felt. He laughed for a while before turning to Chu Feng, “How sharp were my eyes? Ranqing could have become peerless. Were she still around, God’s Era’s powers would be hers to take. Those Ancient Era’s races would be mere ants. No one would be a match for our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. No one would be qualified to be our enemy!”","Long Zhuoyan glanced at Chu Feng as if asking ‘What’s with your mother?’","Jie Tian’s mouth opened agape.","Anyone could tell that Jie Tianran’s injury was inflicted by Chu Feng’s mother. This meant that Chu Feng’s mother was stronger than Jie Tianran, perhaps even by a huge margin.","“Our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion could have unified the world of cultivation a long time ago, but your father and you ruined it all. Your father made my filial daughter defy me, and your birth made her point her sword at me. All I said was that if you inherited her bloodline, I’ll reclaim the bloodline for her use.","“To protect you, she expended her life force to awaken her Ruler’s Bloodline. She shouldn’t have been able to do it at her age, but she pulled it off. But little did I know that her first target after awakening her bloodline would be none other than the father who doted on her the most! You beast, Chu Feng! This is all because of you!” Jie Tianran glared at Chu Feng with vile eyes.","This was humiliating to him. He had bottled up this pain for many years, but he was finally revealing them. He told the truth to Chu Feng because he thought that Chu Feng would fall into despair upon realizing that he had worried about his mother in vain.","“Where is my mother now?” Chu Feng asked once more.","He couldn’t care less about Jie Tianran’s anger. All he was concerned about was his mother.","“Do you remember what I said earlier? I’m not worried about you coming after me. My only fear is that you would enter the Ninth Galaxy,” Jie Tianran said.","Chu Feng widened his eyes in realization.","“My mother has entered the Ninth Galaxy?” Chu Feng asked.","“I knew from the moment your mother awakened her bloodline that I wouldn’t be able to do anything about you and your father, so I played a trick to mislead her into thinking that you and your father have entered the Ninth Galaxy, so that she would head there on her own accord.","“I’ll head to the Ninth Galaxy too once I obtain God’s Era’s power. With you in my hands, Ranqing would have no choice but to obey me. Chu Feng, do you finally understand how foolish you have been?” Jie Tianran looked at Chu Feng with frenzied eyes.","It delighted him to be able to inflict pain on Chu Feng. Even to this day, he could still remember Jie Ranqing’s resolute eyes when she pointed her sword at him.","He knew that Jie Ranqing did cherish her family ties with him, but he couldn’t accept the fact that her most important person had been shifted from him to Chu Feng.","Thus, he wanted Chu Feng to know that he could have long entered the Ninth Galaxy to reunite with his mother, but his foolishness had reduced him to a tool for him to control Jie Ranqing. He wanted Chu Feng to suffer in pain.","“So, my little brother’s mother is in the Ninth Galaxy?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","That question caused Jie Tianran’s expression to stiffen up. He instinctively realized that something was off.","The pained look on Long Zhuoyan’s face disappeared, replaced with a beaming smile.","Whoosh!","With a wave of her sleeves, the spirit power protecting Long Zhuoyan and Chu Feng morphed into a massive spirit power scythe that severed all of the surrounding spirit power chains.","“You... concealed your strength?” Jie Tianran gritted his teeth.","He was infuriated not merely because Long Zhuoyan hid her strength but also at his own carelessness. He was overconfident in his judgment.","“Who are you?” Jie Tianran began reassessing Long Zhuoyan.","“Who am I? If I was at my peak condition, I could have spared myself the trouble of coming here. All it would take is a glance from me in the neighboring galaxy to obliterate your Seven Realms Sacred Mansion.”","Long Zhuoyan narrowed her eyes.","Jie Tianran shuddered at the sight of her gaze. Jie Tian felt like his head had exploded, and blood spurted from his mouth and nose.","“Don’t look into her eyes!” Jie Tianran quickly covered Jie Tian’s eyes, but the latter’s face was already ghastly pale. “This is our Seven Realms Sacred Mansion’s internal affair. Why are you interfering in it?”","He tried his best to remain composed, but his airs had weakened tremendously.","Long Zhuoyan’s gaze made him realize that he had offended someone he shouldn’t have.","It was just a normal gaze, yet it harnessed such destructive prowess. Only the true powerhouses in the past commanded such power. On top of it all, her eyes were brimming with confidence.","This made him realize that she was not bragging; she was the real deal.","“You still don’t get it? Chu Feng is my little brother, and I have come today to redress his grievances. I might be nowhere near my peak at the moment and an earlier battle has greatly weakened me, but it’s still more than enough to deal with a small fry like you.”","Long Zhuoyan waved her sleeves as she remotely sent a slap over.","Jie Tianran quickly formed hand seals and instantaneously constructed multiple barriers around him. Each barrier resembled a shield, and each layer was stronger than the previous.","Yet, Long Zhuoyan’s palm strike was so powerful that it easily shattered the shields as if they were no more than tofu. In the end, the slap still landed squarely on Jie Tianran’s face.","By the time Jie Tian snapped out of it, Jie Tianran was already no longer beside him. The latter had been slapped out of view.","Even Chu Feng was astonished. He had known that his big sister was strong, but he didn’t expect her to be this powerful.","Jie Tian froze up in fear. He had never tasted such despair before. Without a doubt, the woman beside Chu Feng was the strongest person he had ever met!"]},{"number":6300,"title":"Chapter 6300: Chapter 6298: The Prowess of the Devourer Scepter","paragraphs":["Whoosh!","Several chains suddenly shot forth from where Jie Tianran was.","At the same time, the formation chains below that had been binding Jie Ranqing also shot toward Long Zhuoyan and Chu Feng. Jie Ranqing was released as a result, but her silhouette dissipated right after.","She was indeed a fake.","Both Jie Tianran’s chains and the formation’s chains were enveloped in three layers of spirit power. They were far stronger than the chains that had attacked Long Zhuoyan and Chu Feng earlier.","“Hmph!”","Long Zhuoyan harrumphed. The formation scythe that had severed the chains earlier began striking the incoming chains, causing sparks to flare.","The clash was so fast that Chu Feng couldn’t see it clearly, but he could sense that the formation scythe, despite having easily severed the chains earlier, could only barely stand its ground against this wave of chains. It was unable to sever them.","Whoosh!","More chains flew forth from Jie Tianran’s direction. These chains resembled massive dragons, and this time, they were enveloped with five layers of spirit power. The chains intertwined with one another as if the dragons were collaborating to form a massive formation.","It looked like an unstoppable force. The sheer pressure coming from these chains left Chu Feng with goosebumps all over his body.","“How did that darned grandfather of yours get this formidable?” Eggy exclaimed in horror.","It was fortunate that Jie Tianran wasn’t around when he came here with Old Cat, or else they wouldn’t have the chance to escape. Jie Tianran was much stronger than they had anticipated.","“He must have hidden his strength,” Chu Feng said.","Jie Tianran’s strength had reached an entirely new level compared to the last time Chu Feng wreaked havoc in the Seven Realms Sacred Mansion. It was at a level where Chu Feng could no longer reach at the moment.","Even if he risked his life to unleash his Heavenly Lightning Nine Slashes, he still wouldn’t be a match for Jie Tianran.","The chain formation soon took shape, causing its prowess to be amplified.","Even the formation scythe protecting Long Zhuoyan and Chu Feng shattered in its face.","Long Zhuoyan released another surge of spirit power to block the chains, but it didn’t last long before shattering. Fortunately, she seemed to possess boundless spirit power that allowed her to summon a continuous stream of barriers to stop the chains, even if they only lasted for a brief moment.","“Whoever you are and whatever stature you have in the Ancient Era, you should have never picked a fight with me, Jie Tianran.”","Jie Tianran’s voice echoed from afar, but his figure was nowhere to be seen. He sounded much more confident than before.","“You look down on the Ancient Era just because you inherited an Immemorial Era’s legacy? You little twat. The best treasures of the Immemorial Era have been monopolized by our generation. What you have in your hands is merely trash that failed to catch our eyes! Let me you show you the true means of the Immemorial Era today!”","Long Zhuoyan changed her hand seal, and an inferno manifested. The inferno not only stopped the incoming chains but also melted them. In the end, only the chains reinforced with five layers of spirit power remained.","“Is that all you can do?” Jie Tianran sneered in disdain.","He conjured even more chains, and the chains also intertwined to form a formation. This time, the chains were reinforced with six layers of spirit power.","“Hmph!” Long Zhuoyan sneered.","The inferno she conjured flared with even greater intensity, resulting in a standstill.","Despite her composed front, she sent a voice transmission to Chu Feng, “Damn it! If only I hadn’t expended the bulk of my energy on dealing with the Immemorial Concealment Flood Dragon, I could have vanquished that brat in a single breath!”","Chu Feng could tell Long Zhuoyan was struggling, so he quickly replied via voice transmission, “Big sister, this is my private affair. I am grateful for your help, especially since I was able to confirm my mother’s safety. That puts my mind at ease. You don’t need to go all out to kill him today. I can take care of him myself in the future. This much is enough.”","“Shall we retreat?” Long Zhuoyan asked.","“Yes, let’s retreat,” Chu Feng replied.","Boom!","A pitch-black energy suddenly flared.","Chu Feng and Long Zhuoyan were baffled. The chains had blocked much of their vision, but they could tell that the energy wasn’t from Jie Tianran.","It was from Jie Tian.","Black aura was puffing out from Jie Tian’s Devourer Scepter. The black aura seeped into his body, causing his eyes to turn pitch-black.","“Jie Tian? What is that he is holding in his hands?” Chu Feng was taken aback.","The energy emanated by Jie Tian didn’t pale in comparison to Jie Tianran and Long Zhuoyan’s means, and it was coming from the scepter in his hands.","“What else could it be? It must be a vile treasure. The Seven Realms Sacred Mansion has picked up quite a few treasures along the way. That thing would be an invaluable treasure even in the Ancient Era,” Long Zhuoyan remarked.","At the same time, Jie Tianran’s voice boomed, “Stop, Tian’er! I suffice against them. You don’t need to intervene! Stand down right now!”","Jie Tianran diverted a portion of his spirit power to stop Jie Tian, but he had expended too much spirit power on the chain formation that he couldn’t stop Jie Tian.","Jie Tian gritted his teeth. He was bearing a tremendous amount of power that shattered his physical body and cracked his soul, but he continued to channel the Devourer Scepter.","In the end, the Devourer Scepter’s energy became one with him.","He raised the Devourer Scepter, and a black aura gushed out from his body. The black aura rushed toward not Chu Feng and Long Zhuoyan, but Jie Tianran. It morphed into a black cage that sealed Jie Tianran off.","This sudden twist in the situation left Chu Feng, Long Zhuoyan, and Jie Tianran baffled.","It was only when Jie Tian turned to Chu Feng that Jie Tianran understood what was going on.","“Chu Feng, save my mother!”"]}]);
